window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4601,"title":"Chapter 4601: Chapter 4600: Struggle! IV","paragraphs":["Noah’s mind burned with the words Ul’moreth had spoken, the teaching that now felt more relevant than anything else.","It was not merely that THE classification entities were stronger than those below them. That would be simple to understand, a quantitative difference that could theoretically be overcome through sufficient accumulation of power.","No, the true terror was that they operated on a fundamentally different layer of Existence where normal rules did not constrain them the same way.","The First Tongue, Ul’moreth had explained with absolute conviction, could act as a bridge to cross that vast Depth. To equalize the fundamental imbalance. Because The First Tongue was the language that defined what reality actually was at a level deeper than even THE classification authority could easily override.","Those were the words of Ul’moreth!","Noah had thought his forming Foundation of The First Tongue would be sufficient to at least resist THE classification, to stand on his feet before he utilized The First Tongue externally itself.","He wanted to feel this weight. Ideally, he had to feel the true weight of THE so that he had a baseline for what to overcome.","Unless one actually felt the full oppression of THE classification pressing against them with crushing intent, they would never fully understand what it truly meant.","And being brought to his knees for the first time in his entire Existence, having his fundamental Quintessence questioned and violated, this truly allowed him to feel the genuine power of THE with visceral clarity.","But feeling that power also gave him understanding he had not possessed before.","From his kneeling position, staring at the smooth floor as commanded, Noah focused inward with desperate intensity.","He felt his Foundation, THE Foundation of The First Tongue , actively resisting the imposed Sovereignty even now.","He felt THE Organ of Civilization pulsing with rejection of the external authority trying to define him as THE Rudimentary Units of Everything burned.","They were fighting, struggling against the weight pressing down from all directions.","But the refinement they had received so far was simply too limited. Barely any time had passed since he began fortifying himself with the eighteen Phonemes.","They had not yet crossed the threshold necessary to be fully capable of resisting THE Civilizational Authority the way he wanted.","His Foundation was too young, too undeveloped, insufficient for the impossible task before him.","But The First Tongue itself was the bridge. The bridge to cross this vast chasm that separated THE from Pre-THE, the gap that many would fail to overcome their entire lives.","And Noah held The First Tongue not as a borrowed tool but as his fundamental Way.","His consciousness focused with laser precision on the eighteen Phonemes flowing continuously through his Existence.","Fire. Water. Earth. Air. Void. Light. Darkness. Life. Death. Time. Space. Order. Chaos. Unity. Division. Beginning. Ending. Paradox.","The complete alphabet of Existence itself resided within him, even if his mastery remained at Novice Speaker level.","Yes, Raijin Katsuro controlled all of Existence within this arena through his Civilizational Authority. That was the power of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","But Noah held The First Tongue itself. He held The Way of Mana, the undifferentiated source from which all specialization emerged.","So he held The First Tongue not as something external to channel but as something fundamental to his being.","And even though conventional Existence was under the control of another entity, was The First Tongue not asserting that all of Existence itself stemmed from this original language?","Was he not cultivating the very foundation from which even Civilizational Authority ultimately derived its power?","So he did not need to ask permission to stand. He did not need to beg for the right to speak or move or act.","He simply needed to speak The First Tongue and assert his own reality according to the original grammar that preceded all other rules.","HUUM!","Noah’s will crystallized with absolute determination as he began internally speaking the Phonemes with unprecedented intensity.","Fire erupted first within his Existence, not the physical phenomenon but the principle of transformation and refusal to be extinguished. Blue gold flames that represented his connection to Mana itself.","Then Earth manifested, providing foundational stability that refused to be moved. The principle that some things endure regardless of external pressure.","Air followed, the concept of freedom and movement, the assertion that restriction was not absolute.","One by one, all eighteen Phonemes activated with synchronized purpose, each one adding their voice to his rejection of the imposed reality.","They began to express themselves outwardly despite the Sovereignty pressing down from all directions.","Around Noah’s kneeling form, reality itself began to shimmer and distort as linguistic authority manifested visibly.","Characters of The First Tongue, glowing with multicolored radiance, began appearing in the air around his body. Each Phoneme took visible form as complex symbols that pulsed with concentrated meaning.","The Phoneme of Fire burned with blue gold flames.","The Phoneme of Water flowed with silver blue liquid light.","The Phoneme of Earth manifested as bronze geometric patterns...","All eighteen letters of Existence’s alphabet materialized around him, creating a sphere of linguistic authority that pushed back against the purple gold lightning imposing Raijin’s will.","The two realities collided with visible force.","Purple gold lightning crackled and sparked where it met the multicolored radiance of The First Tongue, neither completely overwhelming the other.","Raijin Katsuro’s eyes gradually opened wider with genuine somberness as he witnessed this unbelievable scene.","This Pre-THE entity, this being without any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, was somehow resisting his command to remain kneeling.","How?","The Phonemes surrounding Noah grew brighter as his internal utterance intensified. The linguistic symbols began rotating around his form in complex patterns, creating grammatical structures that asserted new truths.","I can stand.","I will stand.","I must stand.","Not requests. Not pleas. Simple declarations in the original language that created reality itself.","Noah felt his body responding to these linguistic commands even as Raijin’s Sovereignty tried to hold him down.","His muscles, which had been locked in place by external will, began to move according to his own intention once more.","Slowly, with tremendous effort, Noah’s hands pressed against the smooth floor.","The Phonemes surrounding him pulsed with concentrated authority, each one lending its particular principles to his struggle.","Fire giving him the will to resist. Earth providing stability. Air granting freedom of movement. Unity binding all his components together. Beginning initiating the action. Paradox allowing the impossible.","His arms trembled with exertion as he pushed upward against the crushing weight of THE Civilizational Authority.","The purple gold lightning intensified, trying to force him back down.","But the multicolored radiance of The First Tongue blazed brighter in response, creating visible cracks in the imposed reality.","Inch by inch, Noah’s body rose from the kneeling position.","The eighteen Phonemes spun faster around him, creating a vortex of linguistic power that carved out a space where his will could assert itself.","Raijin’s expression shifted from contempt to disbelief as he watched this entity that should have been completely helpless somehow finding the strength to defy THE itself.","Noah’s knees lifted off the ground as he transitioned from kneeling to crouching.","Then, with final tremendous effort, surrounded by the blazing alphabet of Existence itself, he stood fully upright!","BOOM!","The Phonemes arranged themselves in a glorious display around his standing form, creating visible barriers between him and the imposed Sovereignty attempting to crush him back down.","He looked directly at Raijin Katsuro with imperious gaze that refused to be diminished, his eyes blazing with blue gold radiance mixed with all eighteen colors of The First Tongue.","When he spoke, his voice carried the weight of linguistic authority that superseded conventional power hierarchies.","|I am Noah Osmont, and I kneel to no one. Not to THE, not to any authority, not to Existence itself. My Way demands that I stand.|","HUUM!","As if he was saying this never fucking happened. His momentary kneeling never fucking happened!","He paused, his gaze growing colder as he continued.","|I thank you genuinely for providing this challenge, Raijin Katsuro. But you will have to fall on your knees soon to rectify what has happened here. This I declare in The First Tongue.|","As those words left his mouth, new prompts erupted before his vision with crystalline clarity.","|UNFATHOMABLE EFFORT EXERTED|","|Quintessence is being reinstated and reinforced beyond previous limits.|","|Your fundamental nature has been challenged and has emerged stronger.|","|New absolute rule integrated: Never again can you be forced to kneel against your will.|","|Your very Existence demands it as inviolable truth.|","|Fight. FIGHT. FIGHT!|","BOOM!","The word echoed through his entire being as something fundamental shifted within THE Foundation of The First Tongue.","The eighteen Phonemes surrounding him blazed with unprecedented brilliance as his Foundation took on new depth from this struggle.","Across the vast arena, Raijin Katsuro’s expression had transformed completely from contempt to genuine seriousness.","His purple gold lightning crackled with renewed intensity!","What the fuck was this?!"]},{"number":4602,"title":"Chapter 4602: Chapter 4601: The First Lesson I","paragraphs":["He stood.","As the overwhelming pressure of THE Civilizational Authority bore down upon him from all directions, he stood.","This alone was a terrifying act of defiance that should not have been possible.","Noah could see the shocked gaze of Raijin Katsuro fixed on him, those purple gold eyes wide with disbelief.","This being looked like he desperately wanted to break into the usual dialogue of \"What is this? How is this possible? Did you hide your true power all along?\" or any other sort of predictable bullshit that entities always spouted when confronted with the unexpected.","But Noah was utterly tired of all the endless talking.","He needed to focus with absolute concentration, and he needed tangible results immediately.","What he was doing right now was only barely gaining the capability to stand against THE Civilizational Authority without being crushed. That was it. Nothing more.","He realized with crystal clarity how THE Foundation of The First Tongue was still in its earliest stages of emergence, how the process of his entire Existence being refined by The First Tongue and him mastering the Phonemes was proceeding slowly.","It was naturally a slow and grueling process. That was the nature of Existence itself. Slow, grinding, heavy.","Across his entire journey through cultivation, the one resource he always fundamentally lacked was time.","He had come to The Earliest Folds and now The Infinite Unfurling precisely because he did not have sufficient time in his original era.","But there was a place that could give him time. Vast amounts of accelerated time.","Time to practice The First Tongue extensively. Time to refine his being through concentrated effort.","At this moment, he found himself thinking of something he had not yet wished to fully commit to, but which would now be absolutely ideal and necessary for survival.","So he asked the question internally with decisive focus.","’What is the current state of THE Infinite Desmoterion being forged within THE Organ of Civilization?’","THE Infinite Desmoterion.","A Sovereign Prison Domain forged within him by taking direct reference from THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature.","His Organ had developed significantly since that construct was first initiated. Where was its advancement now?","Clean and crisp prompts materialized before his vision with updated specifications.","|The Infinite Desmoterion - Updated Status|","| THE Organ of Civilization Development: 18.00%|","|Temporal Dilation: 10,000x faster than external reality|","|Maximum Prisoner Capacity: 18 entities with established Sovereignties|","|Current Prisoners: 0/18|","|Maintenance Cost: 10 Rudimentary Units of Everything per 24 hours (inactive until prisoners held)|","|Domain Stability: Absolute|","|All other core features remain operational as designed.|","At such words revealing the current parameters, a decisive light flashed in Noah’s eyes as he spoke with absolute conviction.","\"I have a prisoner for The Desmoterion.\"","New prompts appeared immediately in response.","|Review of combat records indicates Master has not defeated any viable prisoners with established Sovereignties yet.|","|No entities meeting imprisonment criteria detected.|","Yet Noah’s reply came without hesitation as he clarified his intention.","\"I have. I have kept them inside my Existence this entire trip through time. They will not truly be a traditional prisoner as I want to make the first genuine prisoner this fucker standing before me. But at this moment, for this unique purpose, let The Infinite Hunger reside in a new home. Let Ozymandias enter THE Infinite Desmoterion as its first occupant, and let me buy myself the time I desperately need. Ten thousand seconds in The Desmoterion for every single second out here in reality. Time to practice The First Tongue extensively. Time to advance my Way at accelerated pace.\"","|...|","Ruination seemed stunned into complete silence at the audacity and implications of what he was proposing.","After several moments, her voice returned with warning.","|This action is irreversible once initiated. Your counterpart, Ozymandias will be permanently bound to The Desmoterion.|","\"Yes.\"","...!","Ruination said nothing more, recognizing that his decision had already been made with full awareness.","He had to be ruthless in order to overcome the challenges Existence placed before him.","He could be ruthless to others when necessary, but more critically, he needed to be ruthless to himself.","He needed time, so he would create time through whatever means available.","He had been contemplating this specific action for a while as Ozymandias had stayed peacefully within his Existence since he first arrived in The Infinite Unfurling. Now, he was simply pulling the trigger on a decision that had been forming for some time.","New prompts bloomed with official confirmation.","|Prisoner Designation Accepted|","|Subject: Ozymandias, The Infinite Hunger|","|Classification: Paradoxical Entity - Another body of yours that is simultaneously you and yet not you|","|Follows: The Way of Mana and Hunger|","|Civilization: The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger|","|Status: Deemed defeated and subordinate under your Weavings of Existence|","|Imprisonment Initiated|","|Transferring subject to THE Infinite Desmoterion...|","|Transfer complete.|","|Active Prisoners: 1/18|","|Maintenance Cost: Now active - 10 Rudimentary Units of Everything per 24 hours|","|Temporal Dilation: 10,000x operational|","|Special Notation|","|Subject Ozymandias represents a paradoxical part of yourself imprisoned for mutual advancement.|","|Resistance to Mana influence: None (identical Way and Civilization)|","|Cultivation cooperation: Perfect synchronization|","|All advancement made by Ozymandias in The Way of Mana and Hunger will reflect as direct enhancement to Master’s Way of Mana and Hunger.|","|Refinement efficiency: Unprecedented due to being essentially the same Existence.|","WAA!","Thereafter, Noah, while still surrounded by the blazing Phonemes of The First Tongue creating protective barriers around his standing form, closed his eyes with focused intention as he ignored the shocked Raijin Katsuro who had begun speaking again with demands for explanation.","But Noah did not listen to a single word.","After he closed his eyes, his consciousness focused inward on his mind where a certain magnificent Organ spun with concentrated authority.","THE Organ of Civilization.","And inside of it, in a space that existed beyond normal dimensions, THE Infinite Desmoterion manifested.","The domain possessed undeniable qualities of both Mana and Hunger woven into its fundamental structure.","The space itself was vast, stretching for what appeared to be endless Gigaparsecs in all directions. The sky above pulsed with blue gold radiance that represented pure Mana given visual form.","The ground below was formed from crystallized Hunger, dark obsidian surfaces that seemed to devour light itself.","At this moment, in a central region of this new prison domain, vibrant blue gold chains hung suspended in the air, binding nothing yet as they waited for true prisoners to restrain.","Ozymandias could be seen standing unbound in the center of the space.","His obsidian gold humanoid visage, formed from countless writhing tentacles that maintained coherent shape, turned slowly as he examined his new home with calm acceptance.","With expression showing no distress or complaint, only serene focus, Ozymandias began uttering the Phonemes of The First Tongue with methodical precision.","Fire. Water. Earth. Air. Void. Light. Darkness. Life. Death. Time. Space. Order. Chaos. Unity. Division. Beginning. Ending. Paradox.","The complete alphabet of Existence flowed from his being as the Phonemes began to manifest around him in visible form, creating the same multicolored radiance that surrounded Noah in the external arena.","Inside THE Infinite Desmoterion. Inside THE Organ of Civilization itself!","The cultivation of The First Tongue had truly begun at accelerated temporal flow.","BOOM!","As such a terrifying wonder unfolded in the space within his Organ, Noah opened his eyes back in the external arena.","Already, he could feel the difference immediately.","The Phonemes of The First Tongue surrounding his physical form seemed to shine noticeably brighter, pulsing with increased authority and refined structure.","New prompts materialized with extraordinary implications.","|Unprecedented Cultivation Age Initiated|","|An unprecedented era of accelerated cultivation has been ushered within THE Organ of Civilization.|","|The First Tongue is being actively utilized and practiced in a unique domain of extreme temporal dilation.|","|All advancements made by Ozymandias in The Way of Mana and Hunger will directly elevate The Way of Mana.|","|All refinements achieved in mastery of The First Tongue’s Phonemes will immediately reflect in Master’s capabilities.|","|Current Temporal Ratio: 10,000:1|","|Effective result: For every 1 second in external reality, 10,000 seconds (2.78 hours) of First Tongue practice occurs within The Desmoterion.|","|Mastery progression of all eighteen Core Phonemes accelerating exponentially.|","|Foundation Advancement Accelerated|","| THE Foundation of The First Tongue is being refined at unprecedented pace.|","|Your resistance to THE Civilizational Authority is continuously increasing.|","|Estimated time to reach Fluent Speaker classification: Dramatically reduced.|","|Synergistic Cooperation Detected|","|Ozymandias is practicing The First Tongue with perfect dedication.|","|Unique circumstance: Imprisoned entity is paradoxically part of yourself, creating perfect synchronization.|","|Result: Efficiency multiplied exponentially beyond normal Desmoterion parameters.|","|This configuration represents the ideal template - imprisoning aspects of yourself for accelerated mutual growth.|","...!","After Noah finished reading these profound prompts detailing the significance of what he had just initiated, he now fully turned his gaze toward the stern figure of Raijin Katsuro.","The warrior monk’s expression had grown increasingly dark with anger at being completely ignored during what should have been a critical confrontation.","Raijin’s voice erupted with genuine fury.","\"Did you fucking hear me?!\"","Noah looked at this being that he knew with absolute certainty would be unfathomably difficult to even stand against in genuine combat, much less actually defeat.","But even acknowledging that overwhelming power gap, he simply shook his head with calm dismissal as he spoke with voice carrying no fear whatsoever.","After all.","This was existence.","Existence was unfair. Existence was a struggle.","Existence...simply was.","\"No, I did not hear you, nor do I particularly care what you were saying. Let us get a move on with this battle. Let us see the full display of what THE classification can truly accomplish when unleashed without restraint.\"","His eyes blazed with multicolored radiance as the Phonemes surrounding him pulsed with building intensity.","Inside The Desmoterion, Ozymandias continued his relentless practice.","Outside, Noah prepared to face the full wrath of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","And every passing second gave him hours of advancement that would make the impossible merely difficult!"]},{"number":4603,"title":"Chapter 4603: Chapter 4602: The First Lesson II","paragraphs":["Each of the Phonemes of The First Tongue surrounding Noah’s body allowed him to feel a distinct sense of protection against THE Civilizational Authority of Heavenly Lightning pressing down from all directions.","Fire provided the will to resist being extinguished. Earth granted foundational stability that refused to be moved. Air represented freedom from constraint. Unity bound all his components together against external force.","Even now, Raijin’s overwhelming Sovereignty continued to be exerted onto his Existence with crushing intent, commanding him to kneel and submit.","And yet the surging Phonemes of The First Tongue denied this exertion of power, creating barriers of linguistic authority that operated on principles deeper than Civilizational Authority alone.","Raijin’s expression became noticeably heavy as he observed this continued resistance.","After several moments of contemplative silence, he nodded with what might have been grudging respect and spoke with voice carrying building intensity.","\"There are oddities everywhere in Existence, I suppose. You have managed to bear the mere expression of my Sovereignty without collapsing, which is noteworthy for someone with no Depth whatsoever. Very well. I will not be tied down fighting conservatively against an entity lacking Civilizational Authority, so let me show you what actual power looks like. Begone.\"","HUUM!","The moment that word left his mouth, booming drums began to play across the vast arena as if reality itself had become an orchestra.","A glorious symphony kicked off with building crescendo as the sky above transformed.","In the surroundings spanning Gigaparsecs in all directions, colorful lightning began descending like drops of rain to batter everything below.","Purple. Gold. White. Violet. Amber. Colors that should not exist in electrical phenomena cascaded down with beautiful and terrifying majesty.","And each tendril of lightning carried unique power, an undeniable brilliance that could be felt resonating through Existence itself at fundamental levels.","The moment this transformed lightning appeared and began its descent...","BOOM!","Half of the Phonemes surrounding Noah were instantly crushed and shattered as if they had never existed.","The protective barriers of linguistic authority simply could not withstand the overwhelming force being brought to bear.","The pressure Noah felt increased tenfold in a single instant as he struggled to maintain his standing position.","He kept his expression outwardly calm despite the internal alarms screaming through his Existence, his consciousness immediately moving to utter more Phonemes of The First Tongue to replace those that were shattered.","Fire. Earth. Air. Water. Void....","But as soon as they began forming around him...","CRACK!","Any newly formed Phonemes were immediately cracked and splintered under the overbearing pressure of the descending lightning before they could fully manifest their protective effects.","New prompts appeared with critical information.","|All currently expressed Phonemes around your form have the passive support of Grand and Singularity Principles from nearby Existence.|","|However, at this time, the grandeur of a Genesis Principle has manifested in the expression of Raijin’s Civilizational Authority of Heavenly Lightning.|","|Genesis Principle Detected: The Principle of the Unstoppable Storm|","|Classification: Genesis Principle combining concepts of Heavenly Authority, Elemental Dominance, and Purifying Destruction|","|Effect: All lightning manifested carries the weight of existential judgment and the authority of natural disaster elevated to conceptual absolute|","|Because a Genesis Principle itself is fundamentally composed of complex expressions of The First Tongue at the Logos level and beyond, even though it is being utilized crudely and without conscious understanding by Raijin, it still represents a form of more sophisticated linguistic construction than individual Phonemes.|","|Your own Phonemes will continue to be broken with increasing intensity if nothing changes in your approach.|","|Individual letters cannot withstand complete words backed by Genesis authority.|","If nothing changes.","Okay.","Noah’s mind processed this information with crystal clarity even as more Phonemes shattered around him.","He had not elected to fight a THE level entity first without having some semblance of a plan in mind.","He could have taken the safer route of fighting multiple Pre-THE entities, imprisoning them one by one in The Desmoterion, and working his way up gradually to face THE classification after extensive preparation.","But where was the Quintessence in such cautious progression? And more critically, he simply did not have the time for such methodical advancement.","If he wanted genuine pressure to forge himself stronger, here was pressure in abundance.","If he wanted to struggle in ways that would catalyze explosive growth, here was struggle of the highest order.","Here was Existence itself testing him!","Now, he simply needed to be forged and reborn anew in the fires of this impossible challenge.","While Phonemes continued to break around him in cascading failures, while he formed them continuously only to watch them shatter moments later, his eyes flashed with decisive determination.","He knew all eighteen letters of The First Tongue’s alphabet. He had personally practiced each Phoneme internally.","And he had seen a few complete words, the Logos of The First Tongue inscribed on the prisons and throughout this very arena.","He had observed their structure, their grammatical patterns, how individual letters combined into meaningful expressions.","And as the seconds passed here in external reality, Ozymandias inside The Desmoterion had already undergone hours of new understanding and practice of The First Tongue under extreme temporal dilation.","That knowledge flowed back into Noah’s own comprehension through their paradoxical connection.","Now, even if he was not a natural genius at The First Tongue, he had given himself time through Ozymandias.","And with enough time, one did not need to be a genius to eventually exceed.","So at this moment, Noah raised his right hand and focused his will with absolute precision.","On his fingertip, a Phoneme of Fire appeared, blazing with concentrated blue gold radiance.","As it manifested, he thought carefully about what Ul’moreth had mentioned regarding Inscription of The First Tongue.","The technique was mainly used on objects like weapons or armor, mostly on anything other than one’s own Existence.","Because forcing The First Tongue onto living beings who were not aligned with it risked catastrophic collapse.","But he was fundamentally different from other entities.","His Existence itself was perfectly aligned with the very letters he wanted to inscribe because his Way was Mana, which was The First Tongue in its undifferentiated form.","So even though he knew absolutely nothing about the formal techniques of Inscription of The First Tongue, even though he had not learned any proper methodology from Ul’moreth, why could he not simply decide for himself what method to use?","After all, he was Mana. His Way was Mana. His Way was The First Tongue itself.","Could he really not do something as conceptually simple as writing his own native language onto himself?","So at this critical moment, he made his decision.","He would use his finger as his pen . The Phoneme of Fire blazing on his fingertip would serve as his ink.","And he would write directly onto his own flesh.","Noah’s thought process crystallized with perfect clarity as colorful lightning continued raining down around him.","Since there was lightning threatening to collapse him, he needed to protect himself from electrical phenomena.","So he simply had to arrange the correct sequence and variations of Phonemes to spell out a complete word, a Logos that would provide the protection he required.","A word that most closely translated to the concept of Insulation .","Being protected from electrical flow. Being rendered immune to lightning’s destructive passage through matter.","His mind worked rapidly to construct the proper linguistic pattern.","He would need the Phoneme of Void, representing separation and the space between things that prevents interaction.","The Phoneme of Division, creating distinction between himself and external forces.","The Phoneme of Ending, terminating the flow of energy before it could affect him.","The Phoneme of Order, establishing the rule that electricity could not pass through.","And the Phoneme of Unity, binding these concepts together into coherent whole.","Five Phonemes arranged in specific grammatical structure to create... The Logos of Insulation!"]},{"number":4604,"title":"Chapter 4604: Chapter 4603: The First Lesson III","paragraphs":["Noah envisioned the complete word in his mind first, seeing how each letter connected to the next, how the grammatical flow created meaning beyond what individual components could express.","Then, with the blazing Phoneme of Fire serving as his writing implement, he began inscribing directly onto the back of his left hand.","His finger moved with deliberate precision, tracing the first character.","Void manifested as a circular pattern that seemed to contain infinite depth.","Then Division, represented by a line that separated the circle into distinct halves.","Ending appeared as a point of termination, the grammatical period that concluded expression.","Order took form as geometric patterns establishing consistent rules.","And finally Unity, flowing curves that bound all the previous characters into unified whole.","As Noah inscribed each component of the Logos onto his own flesh using fire as his medium, Existence itself began to vibrate with unprecedented intensity.","The arena floor hummed. The distant walls resonated. Reality trembled at what was occurring.","The Logos of Insulation , written in The First Tongue, seamlessly melded with his Existence as if it had always belonged there.","In the next moment, a unique eruption of brilliance unfolded and illuminated the entire vast region of the arena.","Noah’s body momentarily turned glass-like, becoming translucent as the inscribed Logos integrated at cellular and conceptual levels simultaneously!","Light blazed from within him as transformation occurred.","New prompts materialized with glorious implications.","|Unprecedented Achievement|","|A Logos has been correctly constructed and inscribed onto your Existence simultaneously.|","|An unfathomable effort worthy of even more unfathomable harvest.|","|No recorded precedent exists for this methodology.|","|Inscription Modus Operandi Established|","| The Somatic Inscription Method has been attempted successfully for the first time.|","|Mechanism: Using one’s own body as canvas and Phonemes as ink to inscribe Logos directly onto Existence.|","|Only viable for entities whose Way is perfectly aligned with The First Tongue.|","|Proceed with extreme caution for future inscriptions.|","|Logos Successfully Formed and Branded|","|The Logos of Insulation has been inscribed onto your left hand.|","|The simultaneous formation and Inscription has activated a complex mix of supporting Principles.|","|Supporting Framework: 10 Grand and Singularity Principles providing foundational structure|","|Passive Genesis Principle Support Detected: The Principle of Existential Boundary|","|Genesis Principle Effect: Establishes absolute barriers between distinct states of being, ensuring separation remains inviolable at conceptual level|","|New Capability Acquired|","|Due to the inscribed Logos of Insulation, you have gained complete Immunity to all lightning-based Principles and Sovereignties of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","|Electrical phenomena cannot affect you regardless of source or intensity.|","|Classification: Selective Elemental Immunity|","|This immunity is permanent as long as the Logos remains intact.|","|The Logos draws continuous power from supporting Principles rather than your personal reserves.|","...!","BOOM!","The prompts were unfathomably glorious in their implications.","And as a consequence of feeling their profound majesty, of experiencing the radiant Logos and the unique power it brought surging through his Existence, Noah’s concentration wavered for a critical moment.","The rest of the Phonemes of The First Tongue that had been protecting him from the descending lightning shattered completely.","He had nothing left to stop the radiant onslaught of THE Civilizational Authority of Heavenly Lightning filled with the overwhelming power of a Genesis Principle as it rained down toward him.","The attack crashed down with devastating force.","Time seemed to slow as the vibrant waves of colorful lightning descended.","Purple tendrils crackling with judgment. Gold streamers carrying the weight of THE authority. White bolts pulsing with purifying destruction!","Oh!","All of it converged on Noah’s standing form as Raijin watched with expectation of witnessing the beginning of total collapse.","The thick tendrils of Genesis Principle-enhanced lightning smashed into Noah’s body with tremendous impact.","The electrical force coursed through him, seeking to unmake his Existence from the inside out.","But then, impossibly, the lightning splashed outward onto the surroundings as if striking rubber or an impenetrable barrier.","Noah remained standing completely unharmed.","A full devastating attack from a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity wielding Heavenly Lightning backed by a Genesis Principle had crashed directly onto him.","And his left hand shone brilliantly as the inscribed Logos of Insulation pulsed with authority, supported by the light of The Genesis Principle of Existential Boundary.","The Genesis Principle backing his defense heavily denied and completely nullified the expression of Raijin’s overwhelming Sovereignty.","Noah’s eyes shone brightly with satisfaction as he remained utterly calm in the face of what should have been annihilation.","He flexed the hand bearing the inscribed Logos, watching it pulse with linguistic power.","When he spoke, his voice carried quiet triumph.","\" Now...we are getting somewhere meaningful.\"","HUUM!","Yes. This was the path forward.","Nobody else could accomplish what he had just done, combining formation and inscription of a Logos onto their own Existence in the midst of battle.","The First Tongue was indeed the bridge he could assemble to breach the impossible gap against THE classification.","At this moment, he felt like he was finally, truly building that bridge with his own hands.","The first successfully formed and inscribed Logos served as a glorious pillar of foundation for everything to come.","The Phonemes and the Logos of The First Tongue were the answer to surviving and eventually defeating THE.","He had constructed one word. Now he needed to forge more and ensure that in this battle, he could not merely defend but also meaningfully attack and breach THE classification’s defenses!","He needed to look at an entity of The Level One Scale of Existence standing impossibly high above him and prove himself capable of dragging that entity down to his level!","—","Outside of The Primordial Genesis Arena, in the space where hundreds of powerful Ginnu Lifeforms had gathered to observe the unprecedented battle, there were no shouts or bellows of excitement at how events were unfolding.","There was not a single entity screaming about the extraordinary fact that someone who had not attained THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty was actually standing up against someone who had.","There was just an immense and heavy silence blanketing the entire gathering as the Ginnu Lifeforms remained focused with laser intensity on Noah’s left hand where he had inscribed a Logos directly onto his own flesh.","They replayed the outrageous thing he had accomplished in their minds again and again, analyzing every component of what they had witnessed.","This was the reason for the profound silence in the surroundings.","No excitement. No celebration. Just stunned contemplation.","At this moment in the skies above the arena, watching this entire spectacle unfold with his own ancient awareness, floated Ul’moreth .","Suddenly, a THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity appeared beside him without warning.","The newcomer possessed the form of a crimson-skinned humanoid with outstretched horns curving backward from her temples. Her entire body radiated concentrated authority that marked her as one of the more powerful entities in this settlement.","When she spoke, her voice carried genuine confusion mixed with respect.","\" Sir Ul’moreth, was that just now a new form of Inscription of The First Tongue that we do not know about? Did Sir Ul’moreth design this innovative methodology and pass it on to your student? What exactly is it? How does it function?\"","The questions hung heavy in the air with tremendous weight.","And Ul’moreth, for perhaps the first time in eons, did not have a satisfactory answer to provide.","Because just like all the others gathered here, he was also witnessing all of this for the very first time.","His student had created something entirely new!"]},{"number":4605,"title":"Chapter 4605: Chapter 4604: The First Lesson IV","paragraphs":["Inside The Primordial Genesis Arena, lightning continued to fall all around Noah’s position like judgment made manifest.","But gloriously, the crushing immensity and overwhelming weight that should have been forcing him to his knees could no longer be felt pressing against his Existence.","The inscribed Logos of Insulation on his left hand pulsed with steady brilliance as it performed its function flawlessly.","However, the power descending still held a sense of tremendous weight that was being received and processed by the vibrant Logos.","Even though Noah now possessed complete immunity to all lightning-based Sovereignties and Principles, this protection was only fully applicable against THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities wielding electrical phenomena.","And even with that immunity functioning perfectly, if one stripped away the specific identity and elemental expression of The Way of Heavenly Lightning from Raijin’s attacks, the very Weavings of power from an entity at THE Surface Depth still held tremendous fundamental weight.","It was like being hit with a hammer that could release lightning. The lightning was nothing crazy, but there was still the weight and physicality of the hammer!","The sheer density of refined Civilizational Authority, the accumulated pressure of a higher Scale of Existence, these elements Noah still had to bear and withstand.","And in the moment that Raijin utilized any forms of attack that were not pure lightning phenomena, Noah would find himself back at square one facing potentially overwhelming force.","But it was still a glorious achievement worth celebrating internally!","The scene was so utterly incredulous that the figure of Raijin Katsuro stood looking at Noah while seemingly at a complete loss for words.","Then his eyes became firm and focused in the next moment as he sensed with absolute clarity the unmistakable aura of a Genesis Principle rotating around Noah’s inscribed hand.","The Principle of Existential Boundary supporting the Logos of Insulation.","Noah was also at this very moment getting accustomed to wielding this new power while simultaneously trying to fully grasp exactly what terrifying capabilities he had called down just from properly arranging words of The First Tongue.","So he did his best to analyze the situation while continuing to actively plan for how to actually take down this overwhelmingly powerful enemy standing before him.","When Noah spoke, his voice carried calm determination.","\"No need to express any shock or surprise or even ask how such things are possible. Just wait for me.\"","Wait for him.","Raijin absolutely did not want to do such a fucking thing as his expression became unfathomably serious with building intent.","Noah kept his gaze fixed on this terrifying being and prepared himself to respond to any incoming attack.","Because at this moment, he was not simply waiting passively.","His mind was actively working at maximum capacity.","He was taking all the gains and insights Ozymandias was continuously making regarding The Way of Existence and increasing proficiency with The First Tongue, then attempting variations of different combinations of Phonemes to form entirely new Logos.","And as he engaged in this linguistic construction, he was also becoming increasingly more perceptive to the structure of his own nurtured and established Principles.","He now felt like he could begin to actually read the underlying Weaving that formed them, the specific Logos composition whether it consisted of a single word or a very complex lengthy expression or even paired words working in grammatical harmony.","He felt like he was extremely close to fully deciphering the linguistic structure of his own Principles.","Of Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect.","And when he finally accomplished that breakthrough, he expected to become capable of modifying the potency and relevancy they held across Existence.","They would no longer remain static Grand or Singularity Principles once he could directly edit their linguistic code.","If he could tweak them the same way he was currently manipulating individual Phonemes, he would witness his Principles ascending to the elevated tier of Genesis Principles through conscious refinement!","But for now, he had more immediate concerns.","His eyes lit up with focused activity as he raised his right hand once more.","The Phoneme of Fire blazed brightly on his fingertip as he had already calculated another viable Logos variation in his mind that seemed entirely feasible to construct.","He began the process of designing it mentally and inscribing it simultaneously onto his body.","Since The First Tongue was the bridge allowing him to stand against THE classification, he had to continue building that bridge relentlessly.","He needed to forge more and more complete words until the linguistic construction was lengthy and sturdy enough for him to stand upon it and look at THE entities without feeling overwhelming trepidation, and he could look up and says...get the fuck down!","His finger moved with practiced precision as he inscribed his second Logos.","This one would provide general defensive capabilities beyond just electrical immunity.","He combined the Phonemes of Earth for foundational stability, Unity for binding his Existence together against fragmenting forces, Order for establishing consistent protective rules, and Ending for terminating incoming attacks before they fully manifested their effects.","The Logos of Fortification took shape on his right forearm, glowing with bronze and gold radiance.","|Logos Successfully Inscribed|","| The Logos of Fortification has been branded onto your right forearm.|","|Effect: Comprehensive defensive enhancement against all forms of attack of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Supporting Principles: 8 Grand and Singularity Principles|","|Passive Genesis Support: The Principle of Enduring Foundation|","|Your Existence gains significant resistance to all damage sources of THE Civilizational Authority|","Immediately after completing that inscription, Noah moved to his third Logos without pause.","This one needed to provide offensive capability, the ability to bypass defenses and deal meaningful damage to THE Surface Depth entities.","He combined the Phonemes of Fire for transformative destruction, Division for separating defensive barriers from their targets, Chaos for breaking established patterns of protection, Void for creating spaces where defenses could not exist, and Paradox for allowing attacks to be both resistible and irresistible simultaneously.","The Logos of Penetration manifested on his right palm, blazing with multicolored aggressive light.","|Logos Successfully Inscribed|","| The Logos of Penetration has been branded onto your right palm.|","|Effect: Offensive attacks bypass conventional defenses and resistances of THE Civilizational Authority|","|Supporting Principles: 12 Grand and Singularity Principles|","|Passive Genesis Support: The Principle of Inevitable Violation|","|Your attacks can somewhat, slightly, and meaningfully damage entities at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","For his fourth and final Logos in this initial construction phase, Noah needed something to help bridge the vast power gap more generally.","He combined the Phonemes of Beginning for initiating what should be impossible, Air for freedom from constraints, Light for clarity of purpose and execution, Space for manipulating the distance between power levels, and Unity for bringing disparate elements together into functional whole.","The Logos of Elevation took form across his chest, shining with radiant white-gold brilliance.","|Logos Successfully Inscribed|","| The Logos of Elevation has been branded onto your chest.|","|Effect: Temporary elevation of your effective power level when facing superior opponents|","|Supporting Principles: 10 Grand and Singularity Principles|","|Passive Genesis Support: The Principle of Aspirational Transcendence|","|The gap between you and THE classification entities is partially bridged during active combat. Partially.|","HUUUM!","Noah now stood with four distinct Logos inscribed across his body, each one pulsing with its own unique radiance and supported by Genesis Principles operating passively.","His left hand glowed with the defensive Insulation against lightning.","His right forearm shone with the general Fortification against all attacks.","His right palm blazed with the offensive Penetration to breach defenses.","His chest radiated with the power-bridging Elevation.","The brilliance surrounding him had intensified dramatically, creating a visual display of linguistic authority that rivaled even THE classification entities.","At this precise moment, his enemy across the vast arena had not been idle.","Raijin Katsuro had been undergoing his own transformation this entire time, his full Sovereignty now put on complete display without any restraint.","His body had grown to nearly twelve feet in height, muscles defined with purple gold lightning coursing through every fiber. His eyes burned with cosmic radiance. The rosaries around his neck floated independently, each bead pulsing with concentrated Genesis Principle authority.","When he spoke, his voice carried genuine respect mixed with self-recrimination.","\"I sincerely apologize for treating you like a mere Pre-THE entity. It seems I was actually facing a THE classification entity playing elaborate games with their apparent power level, and I did not take this battle seriously enough from the beginning. That ends now.\"","BOOM!","The weight of his fully manifested Sovereignty crashed across the arena with devastating intensity, no longer holding anything back!"]},{"number":4606,"title":"Chapter 4606: Chapter 4605: The First Lesson V","paragraphs":["How did one suppress a Way of Existence?","This was a fundamental question that entities across all eras and territories had grappled with when facing opponents whose power seemed insurmountable.","The answer, like most profound truths, was both simple and extraordinarily complex.","One could suppress a Way of Existence through overwhelming superiority in the same domain. Fire could be extinguished by greater Fire. Water could be absorbed by vaster Water. This was the brute force approach, requiring exponentially more power than the opponent possessed.","Or one could suppress a Way through opposing principles. Fire countered by Water. Chaos balanced by Order. Lightning grounded by Earth. This was the strategic approach, requiring deep understanding of fundamental interactions.","Or one could suppress a Way by denying it expression entirely. Not through opposition but through removal of the stage upon which it performed . A swordsman rendered ineffective not by superior swordsmanship but by being placed in a space where swords could not exist.","This final method was the most elegant and the most difficult to achieve.","It required understanding not just what the Way was, but what allowed it to function at all.","And then systematically removing those foundational permissions until nothing remained but potential without manifestation.","---","Inside The Primordial Genesis Arena, Noah’s body moved with building confidence as he became increasingly familiar with the four Logos inscribed across his flesh.","Raijin’s attacks came with devastating variety now that lightning proved ineffective.","The warrior monk had shifted tactics entirely, abandoning his signature element and instead wielding multiple Singularity Principles that had nothing to do with electrical phenomena.","He manifested the Singularity Principle of Crushing Gravity, and Noah felt his bones compress under impossible weight of THE Civilizational Authority until the Logos of Fortification on his forearm blazed brighter and bore the load.","He invoked the Singularity Principle of Spatial Severing, and reality itself tried to cut Noah into component pieces until the Logos of Elevation on his chest elevated his existential density to withstand the attack.","He called upon the Singularity Principle of Temporal Decay with his Civilizational Authority, attempting to age Noah’s Existence into dust across compressed centuries, but the combined defensive Logos held firm against even this assault.","Each attack pushed Noah backward across the vast arena floor, forcing him to give ground despite his inscribed protections.","The Logos absorbed tremendous punishment but could not completely negate the fundamental power differential between Pre-THE and THE classification.","But as Noah defended desperately against this onslaught, he moved to usher in a new wave of possibilities.","He had performed the difficult and nearly impossible task of Inscription first, writing Logos directly onto his own flesh.","But when it came to simply speaking Logos by arranging variations of Phonemes in proper grammatical patterns and uttering them aloud, that came even more naturally to him.","His Way was The First Tongue itself. Speaking it should be as instinctive as breathing.","So as another wave of Spatial Severing crashed toward him, Noah opened his mouth and spoke his first complete Logos in combat.","He combined the Phonemes of Unity, Order, Space, and Ending into the Logos of Coherent Wholeness.","The word left his mouth with concentrated authority, declaring that his Existence remained unified and could not be separated into pieces.","The Spatial Severing crashed against this spoken declaration and shattered.","Raijin’s eyes widened with shock as his THE Civilizational Authority was casually nullified by a single word.","Noah smiled as understanding flooded through him.","This was it. This was the bridge he needed to build.","Not just inscribed Logos for permanent enhancement, but spoken Logos for dynamic response to whatever the opponent attempted.","He felt like he was constructing that bridge between Pre-THE and THE with every word he spoke, every linguistic pattern he mastered through actual combat application.","Because so often, many entities were too scared to attempt something or convinced themselves they could never accomplish it.","But unless one actually attempted the impossible, they would never discover their true limits.","As Raijin manifested the Singularity Principle of Molecular Disintegration with his THE Civilizational Authority, Noah spoke the Logos of Structural Permanence combining Earth, Life, Order, and Unity.","His body refused to disintegrate because the language of Existence itself declared his structure permanent.","As Raijin invoked the Singularity Principle of Conceptual Erasure attempting to remove Noah from reality’s memory, Noah spoke the Logos of Undeniable Presence combining Light, Beginning, Fire, and Paradox.","Reality could not forget him because his presence was linguistically undeniable.","With each spoken Logos, Noah’s confidence grew exponentially.","And then, as he successfully rebuked another devastating attack from THE Surface Depth entity, his figure began moving forward with genuine purpose and building tyranny.","His mind raced with strategic calculation.","How could he actually suppress this THE entity rather than just defending indefinitely?","He did not necessarily need to somehow penetrate Raijin’s defenses and collapse his entire Way. That was far too difficult given the power differential.","But... had he not observed many prisons outside this very arena?","Had Ul’moreth not explained in explicit detail exactly how THE entities were imprisoned using specific Logos working in systematic harmony?","So what if Noah simply adopted that methodology of suppression and created his own personal cage specifically designed to contain THE classification entities?","It was not his personal power making any of this possible. It was the power of The First Tongue itself providing the bridge.","But wasn’t he The First Tongue made manifest? Wasn’t his Way fundamentally identical to the source language?","With this realization crystallizing into decisive action, Noah’s movements became purposeful and rapid.","He began forming the seven Logos that comprised the prison cages exactly as Ul’moreth had explained their structure and function.","The Logos of Absolute Separation combining Void, Division, and Space.","The Logos of Predetermined Failure combining Order, Unity, and Ending.","The Logos of Temporal Constraint combining Time, Beginning, and Order.","Even though these Logos seemed relatively simple with only three Phonemes each, they possessed their own difficulty in proper grammatical construction.","The Logos of Self-Destructive Force combining Fire, Death, and Chaos.","The Logos of Living Structure combining Life, Unity, and Water.","The Logos of Mutual Blindness combining Darkness, Void, and Paradox.","And the Master Keystone Logos combining all eighteen Phonemes in the specific pattern that bound everything together.","After he felt confident he could speak each one with proper pronunciation and grammatical flow, Noah raised his right hand with deliberate intent.","In his palm, something began to manifest.","A stick.","Simple. Unadorned. Wooden in appearance.","A stick.","The Goad . The implement connected directly to THE Creature’s First Lesson, the teaching method used to instruct and discipline those learning fundamental truths.","But at this moment, Noah’s eyes blazed with determination as he spoke aloud with voice carrying absolute conviction.","No longer would it have any connection with THE Creature .","\" This will be my First Lesson to a THE entity. My Goad. My First Lesson.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the stick transformed dramatically.","It became filled with his Way, shining with brilliant blue gold radiance that illuminated the entire vast arena.","It burned with pure Primus Mana, the undifferentiated source from which all specialization emerged.","It pulsed with Pure First Tongue, the language of Existence given physical form.","Thereafter, Noah began the process of Inscription.","Using the blazing Phoneme of Fire still active on his fingertip, he started writing the prison Logos directly onto the surface of The Goad.","The first Logos of Absolute Separation manifested along the stick’s length, glowing with deep purple radiance.","The second Logos of Predetermined Failure wrapped around it in silver white spirals.","The third Logos of Temporal Constraint pulsed with golden amber light.","But as Noah inscribed this third Logos, The Goad trembled violently as if the wooden implement could not sustain any additional linguistic weight without shattering.","Noah nodded with understanding. Three inscribed Logos seemed to be the maximum this manifestation could bear.","He proceeded to speak aloud the remaining four prison Logos that Ul’moreth had described and that he himself had observed on the actual cages.","His voice rang out across the arena with building authority.","|Logos of Self-Destructive Force!| The words manifested as crimson and black energy swirling around Raijin’s position.","|Logos of Living Structure!| Emerald green light formed barriers that adapted and flowed.","|Logos of Mutual Blindness!| Pale violet concealment wrapped around the target.","|Master Keystone Logos!| Prismatic radiance bound all seven Logos together into unified whole.","These rulings of The First Tongue, these declarations of how reality would function within their influence, began actively surrounding Raijin Katsuro despite his attempts to resist.","Despite his billowing THE Civilizational Authority!","And as the linguistic prison took shape, Noah raised The Goad high and swung it downward with purposeful force.","The stick enlarged dramatically as it descended, growing to become twice as massive as Raijin’s transformed twelve-foot form.","It had become a weapon of judgment, reality itself condensed into a tool for delivering The First Lesson!","Raijinn roared as the grandeur of a Genesis Principle burned all around him!","HUUUM!","The scene unfolded with terrible beauty.","Noah gradually cornered the THE entity through systematic application of The First Tongue, each spoken and inscribed Logos reducing Raijin’s capacity to express his overwhelming power.","The light of the Gensis Principle he was trying to express could not be fully called out!","The Logos of Absolute Separation prevented him from drawing upon external resources or receiving support from his Civilization.","The Logos of Predetermined Failure ensured any attempt to break free concluded in failure before it could fully manifest.","The Logos of Temporal Constraint locked his perception of time into linear flow, preventing temporal manipulation.","The Logos of Self-Destructive Force turned his own strength against him whenever he attempted to force his Way through the barriers that had begun forming and closing in around him!","His lightning...was becoming contained.","His Sovereignty was becoming suprressed by The First Tongue itself.","He was being told but his glorious Civilizational Authority that could impose itself on existence...could actually not impose itself here. Because an entity had been rewriting the very rulings of Existence to be completely against him. To be specifically against him to the point that he could not even express his authority.","When one stopped to worry whether they could or could not, and they simply changed how existence operated based on the enemy that they faced...the results that could unfold were unfathomably glorious.","The Logos of Living Structure adapted to counter whatever technique he deployed.","The Logos of Mutual Blindness isolated him conceptually from the outside arena.","And the Master Keystone Logos bound all these restrictions together into inescapable whole.","Into a glorious, unfathomable net of The First Tongue.","Until ultimately, after what felt like both an eternity and mere moments, Raijin Katsuro stood frozen.","\"...\"","His entire form surrounded by a radiant blue gold hazy prison formed from The Seven Logos of Imprisonment.","The containment felt eerily similar to the physical cage he had been confined in before, but this one was far more sophisticated because it existed as living language rather than static structure.","He could not see anything outside the linguistic barriers now containing him.","He could not express his Civilizational Authority beyond the boundaries defined by The First Tongue.","He could only stand with expression mixing rage and profound shock at what had been done to him.","At such a moment, the glorious scene played out as if in slow motion.","Noah stood before a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity who genuinely could not express their power at this moment because Noah himself had caused such suppression.","Time seemed to slow to a crawl as Noah lifted his First Lesson, his Goad, the stick burning with blue gold Mana and linguistic authority.","He moved it with deliberate precision to Raijin’s shoulder.","Using the implement’s end, he tapped it gently against the warrior monk’s form and then pushed downward with steady pressure.","Not tremendous force. Not overwhelming power.","Just gentle, inexorable insistence backed by seven Logos declaring how reality would function in this space.","Moments later, the impossible occurred.","Raijin Katsuro, THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity, The Monk of Ten Thousand Storms, slowly fell to his knees.","His body moved against his will, compelled by linguistic authority that superseded even his Civilizational power.","First one knee touched the smooth arena floor.","Then the other.","Until he knelt completely, trapped within a cage of words, forced into the same position he had earlier imposed on Noah.","...!","An immense silence reigned over the entire arena.","Existence itself seemed to hold its breath.","No prompts materialized before Noah’s vision.","No notifications appeared celebrating this achievement.","Everything was utterly, quintessentially silent, as if Existence itself had to bear witness to this in silence!","An entity that had not attained THE classification had forced a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty being to kneel, locked within a cage constructed entirely from Logos of The First Tongue.","The silence stretched.","And in that profound quiet, reality itself seemed to acknowledge that something fundamental had shifted.","That a bridge had been fully constructed where none should have been possible.","That the impossible... had become merely difficult.","Merely.","Merely!"]},{"number":4607,"title":"Chapter 4607: Chapter 4606: The First Lesson VI","paragraphs":["Far from The Primordial Genesis Shore, countless Gigaparsecs away within the chaotic expanse of Ginnungagap, two figures floated above an obsidian sea that crackled with visible instability.","Tor and THE Living Origin remained utterly still, their forms hovering motionless as if they had become statues carved from compressed authority.","The silence between them stretched with building tension until Tor finally spoke.","\" THE Barrier of Hunger I placed on him has faded. Cracked completely. The connection has been severed.\"","THE Living Origin remained silent initially, her white-gold eyes closing as she focused her awareness inward to sense through her own connection.","After several moments, she opened her eyes and spoke with a carefully measured tone.","\"I innately feel that his Origin has not been collapsed. He still exists somewhere within Ginnungagap. The fundamental thread connecting him to Existence remains intact.\"","Tor’s expression darkened as he processed this information, his mind racing through possibilities.","\"If a THE level entity attacked him and managed to overcome his defenses...\"","THE Living Origin considered his words before responding thoughtfully.","\"It is not always collapse. Ginnu Lifeforms at times take hostages rather than simply collapsing those who enter their territories. They have settlements, laws, customs. Some use prisoners for studying or as meals.\"","Tor’s eyes narrowed dangerously as he turned to face her directly.","\"Oh, so we need to locate a Ginnu Settlement and just walk directly in?\"","\"...\"","THE Living Origin met his gaze with calm assessment before asking the critical question.","\" How far are you willing to go for this? For him?\"","Tor did not even hesitate or look away as he replied with voice carrying absolute conviction.","\"As far as I need to go.\"","...!","He thought of The Little Devil. He thought of Khor as he sighed internally. Even if he collapsed in the future, he had to ensure she had a future.","Origin nodded slowly as if she had expected exactly such an answer.","\" Very well, then let us follow the flow of concentrated power. The most densely accumulated authority in Ginnungagap will mark the locations of major Ginnu Settlements. Let us pay them a visit and see what we find.\"","With such words carrying ominous promise, the two began heading in a different direction with renewed purpose, their forms cutting through the chaotic environment toward their destination.","---","In the distant Primordial Genesis Shore where Noah’s unprecedented battle had just concluded, Ul’moreth found himself surrounded by multiple Ginnu Lifeforms who seemingly wanted answers to questions they could barely formulate.","A THE Surface Depth Ginnu with crystalline protrusions covering their malformed body spoke first with voice mixing awe and confusion.","|Sir Ul’moreth, we all witnessed what occurred in the arena. But we need clarification... Most of us at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty can at most proficiently utter the eighteen Core Phonemes with reasonable consistency. We practice for years to achieve even that level of competency.|","A THE Intermediate Depth Ginnu whose body appeared to be formed from flowing liquid metal continued the thought.","|Forming complete Logos by combining multiple Phonemes together is extraordinarily dangerous and prone to catastrophic failure. Even those of us who have studied The First Tongue for countless ages sometimes make critical mistakes when attempting to construct words from individual letters.|","Another voice chimed in, this one belonging to an ancient Ginnu whose form shimmered with temporal distortion.","|The difficulty lies in the connections between Phonemes. Each letter must flow into the next with perfect grammatical precision. At any point during the process of forming a Logos, if the strokes and linguistic patterns do not connect effectively, it represents a violation of Existence itself. Everything explodes violently. The one forging the Logos becomes injured, sometimes severely enough to damage their foundation permanently.|","The crystalline Ginnu gestured toward the arena with clear disbelief.","|And yet the Anomaly in that arena, the entity we all just watched, formed multiple complex Logos in rapid succession. He strung together different combinations of Phonemes with perfect fluency. And not once, not a single time, did he make any connection errors. Not once did he fail or cause a linguistic detonation. Every single Logos he constructed manifested flawlessly.|","The liquid metal Ginnu’s voice carried profound weight.","| Even those of us at THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty cannot claim that we could always successfully form Logos with one hundred percent consistency. There is always risk, always the possibility of catastrophic error no matter how experienced we become. And moving beyond just formation, the difficulty of actual Inscription is exponentially greater!|","|The precision required to write The First Tongue onto objects or Existences without causing reality to reject the patterns is something that takes millennia to master even partially. And he inscribed multiple Logos onto his own flesh in the middle of combat without a single failure...|","All eyes turned to Ul’moreth with expressions demanding explanation.","|So how, Sir Ul’moreth? How was what we just witnessed even remotely possible?|","Some of the gathered Ginnu looked like they desperately wanted to voice another question entirely.","Please teach us the same methodology! Share this technique!","But Ul’moreth remained silent, his hairy form giving away nothing.","How could he possibly tell them the truth?","That he had only just met this Little Anomaly recently. That he had not even begun to teach him how to properly form Logos from combined Phonemes. That all he had done was provide the complete alphabet, the eighteen Core Phonemes of The First Tongue, and nothing more beyond basic explanations.","The entity had taught himself everything else through pure necessity and impossible talent.","\"...\"","Ul’moreth’s silence spoke volumes that he could not put into words.","Oh!","In this region of The Primordial Genesis Shore, a heavy and immense silence of profound shock settled over the assembled witnesses.","At the same precise time as all of this occurred, in the periphery of the settlement far from the central gathering, there sat a peculiar figure.","A humanoid Ginnu Lifeform perched casually on the branch of a tall obsidian tree, his position granting clear line of sight toward the arena where Noah had just accomplished the impossible.","This entity possessed a form that appeared almost perfectly human at first glance, lacking the extreme malformations common to most Ginnu.","His skin held a subtle iridescent quality that shifted between colors depending on the angle of observation. His eyes were completely black, no iris or pupil visible, just pure darkness that seemed to absorb light.","He wore simple robes of deep violet that somehow remained pristine despite the chaotic environment of Ginnungagap.","Most notably, he was filled with an aura of profound mystery, as if his true nature remained deliberately concealed beneath layers of misdirection.","In his hand, he held a fruit that pulsed with concentrated THE Civilizational Authority, each bite releasing waves of refined power into his system.","At this moment, as he observed Noah using a stick to cause a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity to kneel, he began speaking in whispers that were actually messages being transmitted across vast distances.","|Sir, I have just witnessed something that you may find genuinely interesting and worth your attention. I am compiling and sending over all observations relating to the incident now.|","His body pulsed with brilliant light as concentrated information began flowing outward in linguistic patterns, traveling through specialized channels toward a distant location.","The mysterious Ginnu continued eating his fruit calmly as he floated down from the obsidian tree branch, his form drifting closer to the arena.","His black eyes remained fixed on Noah’s position with unwavering focus, as if he wanted to observe even more of what this unprecedented entity might stand for, what else he might show from here.","In the shadows of The Primordial Genesis Shore, forces began to watch and move with immensity!"]},{"number":4608,"title":"Chapter 4608: Chapter 4607: The First Lesson VII","paragraphs":["How does one conduct themselves when they stand in a position of genuine superiority?","This was a question that revealed the true character of entities across all of Existence.","Many, when they achieved victory or accumulated power or wealth beyond their opponents, felt an overwhelming urge to express that superiority loudly and visibly. They needed others to witness and acknowledge their elevation.","The rich would throw gold coins at the poor in contempt, not to help but to humiliate.","The powerful would grind the weak into dust while laughing, not because it served any purpose but simply to demonstrate that they could.","These beings who expressed their superiority through such displays held immense arrogance and pride.","And more often than not, such beings were inevitably the first to collapse spectacularly and lose absolutely everything they had accumulated.","Because they mistook temporary advantage for permanent supremacy. They confused a single victory for eternal dominance.","No, the truly superior entities did not revel excessively in their gains or gloat over their elevated position.","They simply kept moving forward steadily because this was what they needed to do.","Not out of humility or false modesty, but out of understanding that superiority was not a destination to celebrate but merely a waypoint on an endless journey.","To keep moving forward without pause. This was the way.","---","At this moment, Noah was moving forward.","He looked down at the figure of Raijin Katsuro kneeling on the smooth arena floor, his tremendous power unable to be expressed despite his repeated desperate attempts.","The warrior monk’s body trembled with contained fury and shock as he tried again and again to break free from the linguistic prison surrounding him.","Noah felt the seven Logos of Imprisonment pulse and tremble under the constant pressure.","THE Civilizational Authority was so overwhelmingly powerful that even contained by The First Tongue itself, it continuously strained against the barriers.","Noah had to constantly smooth out and reinforce the connections between individual Phonemes that comprised each Logos, ensuring the grammatical links remained intact under impossible stress.","If it was not him specifically, if any other entity attempted to maintain this prison, Raijin would be able to exploit the smallest weakness and shatter the containment to continue the battle.","This was the terrifying nature of THE classification.","Even while completely surrounded by multiple Logos of The First Tongue working in perfect harmony, Raijin’s sheer existential weight was almost breaking apart the very links and linguistic locks that bound him.","Noah had to continuously monitor each connection, each grammatical flow, ensuring no critical links fractured while simultaneously preparing for the next phase.","Anyone else who did not possess his Way, anyone whose Existence was not fundamentally aligned with The First Tongue itself, would not be capable of maintaining such precise control.","So no, Noah did not stand on ceremony at this critical moment.","He did not gloat over his impossible achievement or waste time celebrating.","He had promised to bring this entity to his knees, and so he had done exactly that.","Now the noise of recognition and reward could begin.","BOOM!","Prompts erupted before his vision with concentrated significance.","|Unquantifiable Harvest Initiated|","|You have suppressed an entity of a fundamentally higher Scale of Existence.|","|Harvest being collected and amplified exponentially by Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect.|","|Resource generation has exceeded normal calculation parameters.|","|All gains multiplied by factors beyond conventional measurement.|","|Quintessential Declaration Recorded|","|Your Way of Existence has quintessentially exerted itself without question or doubt.|","|Your Way has declared itself supreme even against an entity of a higher Scale.|","|Quintessence permanently reinforced through this expression of absolute conviction.|","|Future challenges to your fundamental nature will face increased resistance.|","|Mastery Elevation Achieved|","|Your proficiency in The First Tongue has been elevated from Novice Speaker to Fluent Speaker.|","|Contributing factors: Extensive cultivation by Ozymandias within THE Infinite Desmoterion under extreme temporal dilation, and direct combat application forming multiple complex Logos under pressure.|","|The formation and successful deployment of functional Logos in genuine battle definitively establishes Fluent Speaker classification.|","|You can now consistently form Logos of 5-10 Phonemes with no error risk.|","|Inscription capabilities significantly enhanced.|","|Foundation Development Accelerated|","| THE Foundation of The First Tongue has experienced dramatic growth through combat refinement.|","|Resistance to THE Civilizational Authority elevated substantially.|","|Estimated time to Perfect Speaker classification: Significantly reduced through maintained practice.|","| THE Organ of Civilization - Developmental Growth|","|THE Organ of Civilization Development; 24.00%|","|Major advancement triggered by successful imprisonment of THE classification entity.|","|All derivative capabilities enhanced proportionally.|","|Maximum Prisoner Capacity: 18 to 27 entities|","|Temporal Dilation: 10,000x to 15,000x faster than external reality|","|Lineage Emergence Progressing|","|The identity of your emerging unique lineage is becoming increasingly clear.|","|The Distinction of The Early Creature, Osmont is being systematically dissolved and replaced.|","|Your heart continues seeking emergence of lineage directly from The First Tongue itself.|","|Bloodline formation: 47% complete|","|New fundamental identity crystallizing around linguistic supremacy.|","|New Distinction Acquired|","|Your unprecedented action of suppressing an entity of a higher Scale of Existence has earned you a unique Distinction.|","|Distinction Gained: THE Scale Breaker|","|Effect: When facing entities of higher Scales of Existence, the gap between your power and theirs is reduced by a fixed percentage.|","|The impossible becomes merely difficult when you confront those who should be unreachable.|","| This Distinction will grow stronger with each additional entity of higher Scale you suppress or defeat.|","Noah observed all of these prompts with outward calm, his expression revealing none of the satisfaction burning within.","After reading through the significance of what he had accomplished, he spoke aloud with voice carrying quiet finality.","\"I have the first true official prisoner of THE Infinite Desmoterion.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, reality shifted.","Noah’s head began to glow with terrifying intensity, brilliant light erupting from his skull as his consciousness connected directly to THE Organ of Civilization spinning within his mind.","Tendrils of blue and gold energy that resembled writhing tentacles burst forth from the light, extending outward with purposeful intent.","They wrapped around Raijin’s body with irresistible force, binding him even more thoroughly than the Logos already containing him.","Raijin’s Civilizational Authority defied and struggled violently against this new restraint, his entire being fighting desperately against imprisonment.","But Noah simply made the surrounding seven Logos of Imprisonment even tighter, reinforcing their grammatical structure and eliminating any possibility of escape.","In the next moment, Raijin Katsuro and his terrifying grandeur of power simply disappeared from the arena.","Vanished entirely as if he had never existed at all.","Noah stood there calmly in the vast empty space, still holding his stick.","Still gripping The Goad that had delivered The First Lesson.","He did not bellow out in triumphant fervor or scream his victory to the watching crowd.","This was simply Existence unfolding as it should.","And he was only just getting started on his path.","New prompts bloomed with extraordinary implications as consequences of imprisoning a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity.","| THE Infinite Desmoterion - Critical Update|","|First THE classification prisoner successfully imprisoned.|","|Active Prisoners: 2/27|","|Prisoner 1: Ozymandias (willing cooperation, perfect synchronization)|","|Prisoner 2: Raijin Katsuro, The Monk of Ten Thousand Storms (resistant, requiring containment)|","|Maintenance Cost: 20 Rudimentary Units of Everything per 24 hours|","|Unprecedented Cultivation Configuration Achieved|","|Two entities now cultivating within The Desmoterion under 15,000x temporal dilation.|","|Ozymandias continues perfecting The First Tongue and The Way of Mana and Hunger.|","|Raijin Katsuro will be compelled to refine The Way of Heavenly Lightning.|","|All advancement made by both prisoners reflects as enhancement to your Way of Mana and Hunger.|","|Synergistic effect detected: Having multiple prisoners accelerates overall cultivation efficiency beyond linear addition.|","|The Way of Heavenly Lightning - Integration Initiated|","|As Raijin cultivates and refines his Way within The Desmoterion, aspects of The Way of Heavenly Lightning will gradually become accessible to you.|","|His Singularity and Genesis Principles will be studied and potentially replicated.|","|Estimated time for meaningful integration: Variable based on Raijin’s cooperation level|","|Note: Resistant prisoners provide slower but still significant benefits.|","|Mana Influence Process Activated|","|Raijin Katsuro is now being gradually influenced by Mana as foundational authority.|","|His Way will slowly align more closely with The First Tongue over extended imprisonment.|","|Resistance expected but ultimately futile given temporal scale and environmental pressure.|","After reading through these significant updates, Noah closed his eyes and turned his awareness inward.","His consciousness descended into THE Organ of Civilization where THE Infinite Desmoterion existed as a vast domain.","---","Inside THE Infinite Desmoterion , the sky pulsed with blue gold radiance while the ground remained formed from crystallized Hunger.","Into this space, Raijin Katsuro descended surrounded by vibrant chains of Mana and linguistic authority.","Even more chains materialized from the environment itself, wrapping around his limbs and torso with irresistible binding force.","His vision returned abruptly as he looked around in absolute shock at his new surroundings.","This was not the arena. This was somewhere else entirely, somewhere that felt impossibly vast yet simultaneously confined.","His Civilizational Authority tried to erupt with full force, attempting to shatter these new restraints and escape this unknown prison.","But an unfathomable power wrapped around him immediately, crushing his attempted rebellion.","For Noah, internally voicing The First Tongue within his own Organ of Civilization was even easier than external expression.","Here, in this domain that was literally part of his Existence, The First Tongue flowed from him with perfect fluency.","At this moment, across the vast expanse of The Desmoterion, Ozymandias looked toward the figure of Raijin descending and struggling against his bonds.","From Ozymandias’s hand, a stick materialized with casual authority.","Another Goad, identical to the one Noah wielded externally.","And this one was already covered with inscribed Logos of Imprisonment, pulsing with concentrated linguistic power.","Even more Logos formed in the air around Raijin as Ozymandias approached with calm deliberation.","Seven additional layers of containment wrapped around the struggling prisoner.","Ozymandias spoke with voice carrying absolute finality.","\" Get down.\"","Instantly, the authority of The First Tongue spoken within this domain crashed against Raijin with overwhelming force.","BOOM!","Raijin’s figure was driven downward violently, crashing to the ground surrounded by multiplying chains as he looked toward Ozymandias with expression mixing shock and growing horror.","His voice erupted with desperate confusion.","\" What is this?! Who are you?! What do you Ginnu monsters want with me?! What are these twisted games you are playing?!\"","Ozymandias rose to his full height, the Goad in his hand pulsing with authority as he shook his head with what might have been pity.","\"Hush with all of that pointless questioning, and begin your cultivation immediately. You lost your battle because your Way was fundamentally weak and underdeveloped compared to what it could become. You now have an effective eternity in here under extreme temporal dilation to perfect your Way and advance beyond your current limitations, so get started without further delay.\"","He paused before adding with a voice carrying strange encouragement.","\" Mana will help you whether you want it to or not. The First Tongue will refine you. Eventually, you may even thank us for this opportunity.\"","BOOM!","A terrifying progression of accelerated cultivation bloomed within The Infinite Desmoterion as both prisoners began their eternal refinement.","---","In Existence, there were many paths to power and countless methodologies for advancement.","Some entities accumulated strength through patient cultivation across eons, building their foundations slowly and carefully.","Some stole power from others through violence and consumption, growing rapidly but unstably.","Some inherited power from ancient lineages or were born with advantages others could never possess.","But the rarest path, the one that defied all conventional understanding, was the path of those who built bridges where none should exist.","Who looked at the impossible gap between themselves and entities of higher Scales and decided that gap was merely an engineering problem to be solved through sufficient understanding and effort.","Noah had just demonstrated that The First Tongue could serve as such a bridge.","Not through overwhelming personal power, but through linguistic authority that operated on principles deeper than Civilizational classification.","The battle against Raijin had proven something fundamental: mastery of The First Tongue could allow those of lower Scales to stand against, suppress, and even imprison those of higher Scales.","The bridge had been built and tested.","And Noah stood upon it calmly, already looking toward the next impossible challenge.","Because truly superior entities did not stop to celebrate their achievements.","They simply kept moving forward.","Always forward.","Toward whatever came next."]},{"number":4609,"title":"Chapter 4609: Chapter 4608: Ginnungagap Festival I","paragraphs":["In Existence, if one could not fly, then they should at least run with everything they had.","If you could not run, then at least walk with steady determination.","If you could not even walk, then do every damn thing within your power to at least crawl forward.","Even if you lost your arms and legs, if your body was shattered and your foundation cracked, still find some way to keep moving forward through sheer force of will.","Whatever one did, however they accomplished it, they had to keep moving forward without pause.","This was not merely philosophical wisdom. This was survival imperative.","Because the moment you stopped moving forward, the moment you allowed yourself to believe you had reached a destination worth resting at, Existence would crush you under forces you were no longer prepared to face.","Stagnation was death. Complacency was collapse. Only forward motion, relentless and unceasing, offered any hope of enduring what came next.","---","Even though Noah had just made a ridiculous accomplishment that even he had not fully expected to achieve, he would continue moving forward without pause.","So he took a moment to consolidate his gains internally.","He closed his eyes, feeling the Logos inscribed across his body pulse with steady authority.","He opened them with renewed clarity.","And then he took a single step forward.","A moment later, the isolated vastness of The Primordial Genesis Arena began to fade as the spatial expansion deactivated.","The surroundings filled with hundreds of gathered Ginnu Lifeforms became visible once more.","Noah found himself faced with a heavy, profound silence.","The Ginnu Lifeforms were looking at him with eyes shining with complex emotions that mixed wonder, shock, calculation, and something approaching interest.","They observed him as if they were witnessing some unprecedented monster that had emerged from impossible circumstance.","An entity that should not exist, accomplishing what should not be possible.","The moment Noah’s figure was fully revealed standing alone in the now-normal-sized arena, The Goad still gripped casually in his hand while absolutely no trace of Raijin Katsuro remained anywhere, Ul’moreth’s presence expanded dramatically.","His hairy form rose high above all the assembled Ginnu Lifeforms as obsidian gold light radiated from him with crushing celebratory authority.","And at this moment, booming laughter erupted from THE Primeval Titan that shook the entire settlement.","| BAHAHA! ARE YOU NOT ENTERTAINED?!|","His voice thundered across the space with infectious enthusiasm.","|Look upon this glory! Witness this wonder! Pre-THE against THE classification, and what is the result before your eyes? The impossible made manifest!|","He paused dramatically before continuing with building fervor.","| Roar for his glory! Scream for his virtue! Scream for... err...|","Ul’moreth paused awkwardly in his grand pronouncement.","Noah could feel the ancient being’s smile through their connection as Ul’moreth whispered directly into his mind.","| Little Anomaly, what do you want to be referred to as publicly? What name should they chant?|","Noah shook his head calmly as he replied without hesitation.","| The Scale Breaker is fine.|","Ul’moreth’s laughter intensified with satisfaction as his voice bellowed out again with renewed grandeur.","| Roar for his glory! Scream for his virtue! Scream for THE SCALE BREAKER!|","The Ginnu Lifeforms nearby looked at each other with uncertain expressions before the excitement became infectious.","They began to roar out in The First Tongue, their voices creating linguistic patterns that made reality vibrate.","| THE SCALE BREAKER! THE SCALE BREAKER! THE ANOMALY! THE ANOMALY!|","The chant built in intensity as hundreds of powerful entities raised their voices in genuine celebration.","Noah listened to all of this while shaking his head with mixture of embarrassment and acceptance.","In the next moment, Ul’moreth’s laughter continued as he raised his voice even louder, a sense of pride evident in his voice.","|To mark this glorious occasion, I shall unleash my personal boons from THE Vaults of Ginnungagap! I shall usher in A Ritual Festival of Existence to commemorate what we have witnessed! And I hope the rest of you will not be cheap with your contributions! COME!|","The atmosphere transformed instantly, becoming booming and raucous with building celebration.","In the region above the core settlement of The Primordial Genesis Shore, Ul’moreth raised one hairy hand and caused a massive Logos to be written directly into the sky itself.","Noah looked up at it with analytical focus, his eyes immediately breaking down its component structure.","The Logos combined the Phonemes of Fire, Unity, Beginning, Life, and Light into a complex word that translated most closely to \"Eternal Celebration\" or \"Festival Without End.\"","In the next moment after the Logos fully manifested, the entire sky of this region flickered and transformed into brilliant, vibrant flames.","Not destructive fire, but celebratory radiance.","The heavens became painted in colors associated with ancient festivals across countless eras. Deep crimsons mixed with golden yellows. Emerald greens danced with sapphire blues. Violet purples intertwined with amber oranges.","It looked like vibrant flames formed entirely from visible Phonemes dancing above in complex patterns, creating a shifting aurora of linguistic celebration.","Down below on the ground, the Ginnu Lifeforms entered fully into the festive mood.","Some began making ancient music through their Weavings of Existence, creating sounds that resonated across multiple frequencies simultaneously.","Deep drumming that felt like heartbeats of reality itself. Melodic tones that seemed to come from instruments that did not physically exist. Harmonic chanting in The First Tongue that created layers of meaning beneath the celebration.","Others conjured Phonemes directly in the air around them, writing out variations and permutations that released ancient archaic melodies with their very existence.","A Ginnu formed the Phoneme of Air in twelve different variations simultaneously, each one producing a different musical note that harmonized with the others.","Another created the Phoneme of Water in flowing script that generated sounds like rushing rivers and cascading waterfalls.","The entire settlement transformed into a celebration of linguistic and existential wonder.","Then the Ginnu Lifeforms began thumping their chests with ritualistic fervor as their bodies released unique items that seemed to materialize from within their very beings.","Each treasure pulsed with concentrated THE Civilizational Authority.","|I shall contribute to the festival! | one THE Surface Depth Ginnu declared as they produced a crystallized fruit that glowed with internal radiance.","|I offer my boon as well!| another called out, releasing a jewel that seemed to contain compressed starlight.","Noah observed with fascinated attention as unique fruits, jewels, crystallized essences, metallic flowers, prismatic stones, and other naturally forming treasures began accumulating in the vibrant colorful skies above.","Each one filled with different expressions of THE Civilizational Authority.","Many Ginnu repeated the action of contributing their own treasures as a terrifying concentration of wonders began gathering overhead like a second sky made entirely from compressed value.","Noah activated his Lens of Civilization to examine what was being offered.","His gaze fixed on a particular jewel floating among the accumulating treasures.","|Treasure Analysis|","|Name: The Chaos-Edged Genesis Shard|","|Classification: Naturally Formed Civilizational Treasure|","|Composition: Pure undifferentiated unstable THE Civilizational Authority (Chaos-aligned)|","|Effect: Consumption increases Depth of Sovereignty by refining foundational authority|","|Warning: Authority contained within is highly unstable and will actively resist integration|","|Note: If one can correct or sufficiently handle the instability while devouring this treasure, significant advancement in Civilizational Depth can be achieved|","|Origin: THE Vaults of Ginnungagap|","He shifted focus to examine a vibrant fruit nearby.","|Treasure Analysis|","|Name: The Order-Touched Sovereign Fruit|","|Classification: Naturally Formed Civilizational Treasure|","|Composition: Pure undifferentiated unstable THE Civilizational Authority (Order-aligned)|","|Effect: Consumption increases Depth of Sovereignty by expanding authority foundation|","|Warning: Authority is unstable and requires careful refinement during absorption|","|Note: Entities capable of stabilizing the contained authority will experience dramatic growth in their Civilizational classification|","|Origin: THE Vaults of Ginnungagap|","Noah’s eyes narrowed as he continued scanning the accumulating treasures.","The vast majority of them, perhaps ninety percent or more, all shared the same origin notation.","THE Vaults of Ginnungagap.","So while Ginnu Lifeforms ushered in THE Ritual Festival of Existence under Ul’moreth’s enthusiastic direction, Noah found himself wondering with building curiosity.","What exactly were THE Vaults of Ginnungagap? And more importantly, where was it located?","It looked like a place someone with his particular appetites would very much enjoy exploring personally.","But even as all of this celebratory chaos unfolded around him, Noah shook his head internally.","As amazing as this festival was, as valuable as these treasures clearly were, he had actually wanted to keep his momentum going and jump directly into the next battle without pause.","To work his way systematically through imprisoned THE entities or even challenge THE Maelstrom Thundermane immediately!"]},{"number":4610,"title":"Chapter 4610: Chapter 4609: Ginnungagap Festival II","paragraphs":["He wanted to continue rapidly increasing the tally of his prisoners in THE Infinite Desmoterion.","Because more prisoners meant his Way would advance even faster. His progression in mastering The First Tongue would accelerate exponentially.","If he had twenty-seven THE Surface Depth entities all imprisoned and cultivating their Ways of Existence under extreme temporal dilation, all of their advancement feeding directly into his own growth, how rapidly would he reach THE classification even with his ridiculously demanding foundation requirements?","And part of the reason he wanted to keep moving at breakneck pace was a growing sense of unease.","Since arriving in Ginnungagap, he could objectively be considered to have experienced extremely and unfathomably glorious fortune.","Learning The First Tongue directly from THE Primeval Titan Ul’moreth . Successfully suppressing his first THE classification entity. Acquiring treasures and knowledge beyond measure.","This was all far too much concentrated luck and opportunity.","He half expected everything to collapse catastrophically at any moment!","Existence was fundamentally unfair. Existence would not remain on easy mode indefinitely.","If fighting a THE entity and nearly losing his Quintessence could even be considered \"easy mode.\"","He even looked around cautiously as if expecting some monstrous creature to emerge from nowhere at any second to fuck everything up spectacularly.","But instead of disaster, Ul’moreth was the only one who approached him.","The ancient being’s presence radiated amused understanding as he spoke.","|Haha, I can see a look of worry and impatience burning in your eyes, Little Anomaly. Did you want to continue battling immediately without rest? Are you worried that Existence will shatter in the next moment to ruin all your carefully laid plans?|","He paused before continuing with reassuring authority.","|While such catastrophic interruption may indeed be possible, I will tell you plainly not to worry excessively. Because I, your Teacher, am here beside you! I may be excessively hairy and difficult to look at, but I am actually somewhat powerful when circumstances demand it. Somewhat...|","His tone became more serious despite the underlying humor.","|Loosen up just a little bit, Little Anomaly. Even if Existence itself begins to fall apart around us, I will personally hold it together long enough for you to accomplish what you need. Now come and participate properly in the festival. You are the entire reason it began, after all. This is the first time since the weavings of THE Secretive Eon that someone has broken the Scales...|","WAA!","|This will also be an excellent opportunity for you to acquire treasures and boons that can significantly aid the progression of your Way. Some of what will be offered can even directly elevate your proficiency in The First Tongue itself beyond what normal practice could achieve.|","Ul’moreth said such words with genuine encouragement.","Noah’s eyes shone brightly with renewed interest at that final revelation.","His naturally cautious nature did not change fundamentally. He still fully expected and remained prepared for the absolute worst possible outcome.","But for now, he would focus on acquiring whatever treasures this festival offered.","And gathering critical information.","His thoughts formed into a direct question sent to Ul’moreth.","|What exactly are THE Vaults of Ginnungagap?|","Ul’moreth and Noah floated together toward the center of the festivities where Ginnu Lifeforms had shockingly begun performing ritual dances.","They moved in precise circles around massive flames formed entirely from the Phoneme of Fire written repeatedly in intricate patterns that resembled a bonfire.","The ritual had distinct structure. Ginnu danced in concentric circles around the central flames, their movements following ancient patterns that created secondary linguistic expressions through pure motion.","The swirling Phonemes of Fire blazed higher with each completed rotation of the dancers.","Archaic and melodic sounds echoed continuously from all directions, creating an atmosphere that felt timeless and profound.","In the midst of such celebration, Ul’moreth smiled beneath his obscuring hair as he began his explanation with voice carrying mysterious weight.","| Many entities do not know this truth, but Ginnungagap alone is actually even more vast than The Infinite Unfurling that contains it. The chaotic space between ordered reality extends farther than most can comprehend or survive exploring.|","|There exist countless Weavings of The First Tongue and concentrated expressions of pure Existence scattered throughout this vast expanse. Places and phenomena that none of us fully understand despite eons of study.|","|THE Vaults of Ginnungagap are specific locations that hold extremely concentrated Weavings of either The First Tongue in its purest form or raw undifferentiated Existence itself. These places naturally generate Civilizational Treasures that would be extraordinarily useful for entities at any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","His voice took on more serious tone.","|But these Vaults are not merely treasure repositories waiting to be plundered. They are genuinely dangerous places where reality operates according to rules that shift constantly. Where The First Tongue speaks itself without conscious direction, creating effects that can elevate or annihilate those who venture inside.|","|Some Vaults contain time that flows backward or sideways. Others hold spaces where all eighteen Phonemes manifest simultaneously in chaotic superposition. Still others are places where Existence itself is still deciding what it wants to become, making them fundamentally unstable at levels that even THE Intermediate Depth entities struggle to withstand.|","|I have found many profound things when venturing into various Vaults across the eons. Treasures, knowledge, understanding of The First Tongue that cannot be gained through any other method.|","He gestured toward the accumulated treasures floating in the sky.","| But the gift I will give you right now to commemorate your grand accomplishment will be treasures that even I have been personally enjoying and benefiting from. Items I will now pass down to you because I judge you capable of making better use of them than I can at this stage of my existence.|","After saying this with genuine generosity, Ul’moreth reached into the space near the ritual Phonemes of Fire and withdrew something extraordinary.","Vibrant obsidian Lotuses materialized in his hands, each one shaped in unique variations of different Phonemes rather than having normal petal structure.","One Lotus was formed entirely from the Phoneme of Light written in flowing script.","Another took the shape of the Phoneme of Time inscribed in crystallized moments.","A third embodied the Phoneme of Paradox in contradictory geometries.","Noah could sense terrifically potent Weavings of The First Tongue emanating from these strange flowers.","He immediately activated his Lens of Civilization to examine them in detail.","|Treasure Analysis|","| Name: The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Light)|","|Classification: Vault-Born Treasure of The First Tongue|","|Composition: Crystallized comprehension of linguistic fundamentals shaped by concentrated exposure to pure First Tongue expression|","|Effect: Consumption induces a unique state of profound comprehension in The First Tongue|","|Primary Function: Allows observer to perceive all variations of Phonemes and the infinite different Logos that could potentially be formed from various combinations|","|Note: Variations are truly endless - this treasure provides temporary access to perceiving that infinite possibility space|","|Secondary Effect: If consumed by an entity who has not yet learned The First Tongue, this item would place them in an elevated state where they could potentially learn one or more variations of Core Phonemes directly|","|Comprehension state is temporary but insights gained are permanent|","|Duration: Variable based on consumer’s affinity with The First Tongue|","| Origin: THE Vaults of Ginnungagap - Vault of Infinite Expression|","Noah observed the detailed analysis of such an extraordinary treasure.","Instantly, his eyes pulsed with building majesty and barely contained tyranny.","This...looked unfathomably glorious!"]},{"number":4611,"title":"Chapter 4611: Chapter 4610: The Discovery","paragraphs":["Enjoy the little things.","This alone was something that very few truly understood over the years as they continued to work and struggle endlessly.","Noah understood this principle a while ago as even amidst apocalypses and existential struggles, he made conscious effort to enjoy the little things.","He had a side profession as a farmer and chef after all as he even had a Cooking Sovereign Spire of Osmont, and he kept the company of multiple vibrant entities that formed his family across realities.","He enjoyed the small moments of peace amidst the constant struggle because if one only struggled and did nothing else, by the time their life was done they would inevitably ask themselves a terrible question.","What was all that struggle for if I spent eons doing it and nothing else?","So for now, even though he still half expected and remained prepared for something obscene to occur at any moment, he loved to be proven wrong as he looked at the festival unfolding around him.","The feel of the celebration carried weight that went beyond simple enjoyment.","There was ancientness here, ritual wonder that spoke of traditions older than most realities.","The Ginnu Lifeforms danced around the flames of Phonemes with movements that had been perfected across countless eons. Their steps created secondary linguistic patterns in the air, their rhythm generating waves that resonated with fundamental frequencies of Existence itself.","After completing particular sequences of the dance, individual Ginnu would reach up into the swirling cluster of treasures circling overhead in the vibrant sky.","They would pluck a fruit or jewel, take a bite or absorb a portion of its concentrated authority, revel in the sensation of power flooding through them, and then return seamlessly to the dance.","It felt surreal to witness.","These were entities with their own complete Weavings of Existence and their own complex lives stretching across unfathomable timespans.","And here they were, celebrating together with genuine joy rather than the usual cold calculation that dominated interactions between powerful beings.","As Noah looked at all of them participating in this timeless ritual, something in his expression shifted slightly as he missed his family.","Ul’moreth noticed immediately.","|What is that nostalgic look I see crossing your face, Little Anomaly? Come on, live in the present moment! Here is my gift to you, take it all. I’ll let you continue your relentless struggle in a little bit since I understand your impatience well enough, but participate properly in the festival just to have it marked across Existence that one day, in Ginnungagap, The Scale Breaker was here. The Anomaly was here. Dance, eat, celebrate!|","The words boomed with infectious enthusiasm.","Right after Ul’moreth spoke, Noah felt all the radiant Lotuses flowing toward him as if drawn by irresistible gravity.","Clean prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Festival Boon Acquired|","|The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Light) x3|","|The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Time) x3|","|The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Paradox) x2|","|The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Water) x2|","|The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Fire) x2|","|The Primordial Comprehension Lotus (Phoneme Variation: Void) x2|","|Total Primordial Comprehension Lotuses Acquired: 14|","Noah looked at all of them with eyes shining with profound satisfaction before immediately putting them away into secure storage.","He sent half of the total directly toward THE Infinite Desmoterion.","Part of the reason he could even convince himself to take a moment to live in the present and participate in this festival was simple calculation.","Another part of him was currently inside THE Infinite Desmoterion continuing to advance his Way and deepen his study of The First Tongue at fifteen thousand times temporal dilation.","So Noah was still working hard in that space. Fifteen thousand times as hard, in fact!","Or more accurately, he was making progress at such a multiplied rate that it justified taking brief moments to exist normally in external reality.","So he would participate properly in the festival and see about obtaining more treasures from the swirling cluster circling above.","Because The Primordial Comprehension Lotuses alone represented extraordinary opportunity.","He could give these to his people.","How glorious would it be if Khor quickly gained the capability to utilize The First Tongue? If Moiraine, Malphas, Riya, and all the others acquired this fundamental linguistic authority as well?","His eyes brightened with expanding possibilities as he looked toward the distant cages where THE Maelstrom Thundermane remained imprisoned alongside other captured entities.","His gaze sharpened as he sent them a silent message.","Wait for me. I’m coming for all of you soon enough.","...!","---","While a festival of linguistic wonder unfolded in Ginnungagap, reality continued its relentless motion elsewhere.","In the current Era, on the other side of The Veil that continued breaking down piece by piece, deep within The Lands of The Dead, The Great Usurper known as Eckert continued his idle existence.","He continued passively expanding his Derivative Civilization of Idle Existence in the most grand manner possible.","By doing absolutely nothing.","But sometimes, this approach alone was more terrifying than any active conquest or violent expansion.","His existence spread exponentially across The Lands of The Dead while remaining completely unobservable by any other entities who might wish to detect or interfere with his growth.","His entire Weaving of Existence had expanded to cover such a vast area that at this particular moment, something unexpected occurred.","\"Hmm?\"","Eckert blinked, in his formless state anyways, with mild surprise as he felt his existence extend into a region spanning several Gigaparsecs of seemingly empty murky obsidian space.","But there was something unusual here.","There seemed to be a point of concentrated singularity where his passively spreading existence suddenly spilled into something hidden within this apparently vacant region.","And as more of his Idle Existence flowed into this concealed space, his awareness expanded to encompass what lay within.","His expression shifted to genuine shock.","He could feel an extremely exuberant cluster of concentrated power residing in this hidden location.","This was a veiled pocket of existence, a deliberately concealed space folded away from normal observation.","The pocket itself measured perhaps a few hundred thousand kilometers across, small by cosmic standards but densely packed with authority that made Eckert’s senses sharpen immediately.","The space had strange properties. Reality here felt different, as if it operated according to rules that predated current Existence.","And at the center of this veiled pocket, Eckert’s spreading awareness encountered three circular bubbles of brilliant radiance.","Each bubble was approximately a kilometer in diameter, suspended in perfect equidistant formation from each other.","Inside each bubble, he could sense a distinct presence.","Three Early Creatures, their forms visible but completely inactive.","They appeared to be in some form of suspended animation or deep stasis, their existences preserved but not actively functioning.","And wrapped around each bubble was unique scripture written in a language Eckert could not understand despite his vast knowledge.","The writing pulsed with authority that felt impossibly ancient, and it held power that exceeded any of the Guiders of Order he saw!","As he looked at all of this with growing fascination, prompts materialized before his awareness.","| Your Idle Existence has passively spilled into a Veiled Pocket of Existence belonging to THE Creature|","|Classification: Hidden Storage Space|","|Contents Detected: The Inactivated Disciples of THE Creature|","|Status: Three Early Creatures in suspended stasis|","|Preservation Method: Unknown linguistic containment beyond current comprehension|","|Security Level: Extreme - designed to remain hidden from all observation|","|Note: Your unique method of passive expansion through Idle Existence has bypassed standard detection barriers since...it is a Derivative Civilization stemming from Existence itself. Otherwise. you would have not been able to enter.|","|Critical Decision Point|","|Current Mode: Passive Observation through Idle Existence|","|Your presence remains undetected due to nature of Idle Existence|","| Question: Would you like to switch to Active Mode?|","Eckert stared at the prompts with expression mixing curiosity and calculation.","Three disciples of THE Creature itself, hidden away in suspended stasis within a veiled pocket of existence.","Preserved by linguistic scripture that even he could not decipher!"]},{"number":4612,"title":"Chapter 4612: Chapter 4611: Bloody Peace!","paragraphs":["Would he like to switch to active mode?","Was this even a question worth asking?","Eckert laughed internally as he didn’t even bother answering the prompt, simply looking curiously at the massive Early Creatures that seemed simultaneously Dead and not Dead.","As he observed them with growing fascination, his existence continued spreading calmly.","It flowed around the protective bubbles containing each Disciple like water finding every gap and crevice.","And since his Idle Existence was fundamentally no different from the surrounding ambient reality itself, it permeated effortlessly into the bubbles without resistance.","Even the radiant strokes of ancient language covering the protective barriers didn’t activate or respond.","Why would they when effectively, there wasn’t any foreign influence nearby?","Just existence being existence, flowing where it naturally would.","But his spreading awareness permeated through the barriers until it covered the Early Creatures themselves, wrapping around their suspended forms like invisible threads.","And then something extraordinary occurred.","BZZT !","Prompts materialized with significant implications.","|Integration Protocol Detected|","|Due to the Sealed State of The Inactivated Disciples of THE Creature, their Weavings of Existence currently hold no prevailing identity or consciousness|","|Your Weavings of Existence have begun flowing into their dormant forms|","|Additional Information Being Obtained as your existence flows into and integrates with their Weavings of Existence|","|Process: 17% Complete|","Eckert felt genuine surprise as he faced an unexpected influx of information flooding into his awareness.","Information that felt far too grand and complex for his current mental framework to fully process, but it made the situation significantly more clear despite the overwhelming volume.","New prompts bloomed with extraordinary detail.","|Information Database Updated|","|The Inactivated Disciples of THE Creature have been protected inside barriers preserved by the Phonemes of The First Tongue|","|Barrier Function: Maintain stasis while preventing external corruption or interference|","|Critical Discovery: Due to their completely inactive state with no prevailing consciousness, your Idle Existence is now filling up their empty Weavings of Existence|","|Projection: You will gain full control of their physical bodies momentarily|","|Classification: If and when successful, these three entities can be considered Secondary Extensions of your will|","|Authority: They can be commanded by you to perform whatever actions you wish|","|Control Method: Direct consciousness integration through passive existence overlay|","Eckert’s metaphorical eyes opened wide at this unfolding reality.","The First Tongue? What the hell was that? Did Osmont know about this?","He couldn’t help but laugh with genuine amazement at the absurdity and opportunity of what was occurring.","He loved being idle, yes. That was his entire fundamental nature.","But he also wanted to help the big guy, the monstrous Osmont, if he possibly could so that he wasn’t struggling against the weight of Existence completely alone.","It was hard to bear that crushing burden without any support.","And if all the information he had been receiving about Existence, about THE Loom and The Fallout and the conflicts tearing reality apart, if all of it was actually true rather than exaggeration, then he wouldn’t be able to enjoy his peaceful Idle Existence if everything collapsed around him anyway.","These Disciples of THE Creature felt monumentally more powerful than any Guiders of Order he had previously encountered.","Additional prompts confirmed his assessment.","|Sealed Weaving Analysis|","|Within the dormant Weavings of The Disciples of THE Creature, complete structures of Singularity Principles can be sensed|","|Additionally, fragments of a Genesis Principle are detectably present within their foundations|","Unique prompts continued blooming one after another as Eckert brought himself to sharper focus.","Already, he could sense the hands of The Disciples beginning to twitch slightly as his consciousness filled their empty vessels.","He would gain full control over them very soon.","After that happened, well, maybe he might actually be a little bit more active in how he engaged with Existence.","After all, there had to be beautiful and intact Weavings of reality remaining if he wanted to properly enjoy an Idle life in the future.","Sometimes protecting the conditions for idleness required brief moments of action.","---","On the other side of The Veil, in The Lands of The Living, where the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds used to exist but were now just a vast region of spatial collapse and distorted reality, Alexander Asmodeus stood with one hand pressed against his chest.","He could feel The Shattered Part of THE Heart of Law pulsing there.","Well, really THE Heart of Law itself, or at least a fragment of it.","A piece of the heart belonging to an entity of a fundamentally higher Scale of Existence.","He was thinking deeply at this moment while he watched the forces of Osmont’s people defend desperately against overwhelmingly powerful enemies.","He saw The Infiniverse surging with brilliant authority as she went directly against a terrifying Disciple of THE Creature that shone with the light of a Principle even Alexander could not yet fully grasp or comprehend.","He saw Khor charging forward with absolute lividity toward Schrodinger, whose eyes looked extremely eerie and unsettling at this moment as if something fundamental had shifted in that being’s nature.","He saw the millions of Primus Inevitabilities fighting alongside The First Farmer and countless others as this battle raged across collapsed dimensions.","And throughout all of this observation, he had been asking himself a critical question.","What was his role in all this conflict?","It was a question he had been toiling with since his conversation with THE Living Law.","A question that continued haunting him even after he obtained this piece of their Heart.","And at this moment, watching everything unfold with sharp clarity, he came to a final decision.","He closed his eyes and spoke internally with genuine emotion.","’I am truly sorry.’","BOOM !","He meant those words with complete sincerity.","And they were directed at none other than the fragment of THE Heart of Law glimmering with concentrated Civilizational Authority within his chest.","A reply echoed through his consciousness with unexpected warmth and understanding.","\"Haha, what could you possibly be sorry for? Paradox collapsed my entire Civilization, yes, but it will rise again eventually through other means. Do what you must with some of its remnants. I give you permission freely. Use it well. Through your Peace, there may be Law and Order.\"","The voice of THE Living Law resonated in his mind with genuine encouragement rather than reproach.","Alexander nodded with grim determination.","And in the very next moment, he acted.","CRACK!","He deliberately shattered the already Shattered Part of THE Heart of Law further, breaking it down into its fundamental components.","It began dissolving directly into his own Weaving of Existence.","And then he set it ablaze, burning it as fuel under his conscious direction to forge something entirely new.","His voice rang out with calm and glorious conviction as he spoke his truth to reality itself.","\"Peace is a fortress that must be built upon the broken spine of Chaos itself. Existence is a ravenous tide seeking only to drown all of us in endless entropy and dissolution. To survive against the consuming void, one does not negotiate diplomatically with the storm. One breaks the storm completely until it learns absolute submission.\"","\"Sometimes, Peace has to be brutal and dominating in order to ensure it remains stable. Sometimes, Peace can only be bought with a river of necessary blood flowing from those who would shatter it. I will not follow The Way of Law as it currently exists, but I will enact a bloody path toward Peace. A Way of Peace that will ensure lasting prosperity for those who deserve it, no matter how many must die to achieve that outcome.\"","With such words carrying absolute conviction, a silver-white brilliance began overflowing from Alexander’s entire being.","At this moment, he took a tiny piece of a Heart that had belonged to a THE entity who may have reached THE Intermediate or even Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","And he dissolved it completely to forge his own unique Way. His own emerging Civilization.","It was an action of profound significance.","A choice that, once made, could not be unmade.","A choice that caused the previously calm and silent figure of Schrodinger to suddenly shift his eerie gaze toward Alexander for a long moment of complete silence!"]},{"number":4613,"title":"Chapter 4613: Chapter 4612: A Period of Quintessential Progress! I","paragraphs":["THE Ritual Festival of Existence in The Primordial Genesis Shore unfolded with tremendous glory, and Noah was a full participant in it all.","He observed with fascinated attention all the unique ways that these lifeforms touched by The First Tongue acted and expressed themselves.","How they utilized the individual letters of The First Tongue to manifest and produce sounds and melodies completely unique to their particular Weavings of Existence.","Dances and rituals unfolded next to a swirling storm of Phonemes combining Fire, Light, and Darkness into a constantly shifting vortex of linguistic celebration.","He experienced it all for more than an hour of external time.","And was actually profoundly appreciative of this seemingly brief hour.","Because it allowed him to get a direct glimpse of just how terrifying the utility of THE Infinite Desmoterion would truly be going forward.","This single passing hour in external reality equated to fifteen thousand hours cultivating inside THE Infinite Desmoterion.","More than six hundred days of accelerated advancement.","Prompts bloomed before his vision detailing the extraordinary collective progress.","|THE Infinite Desmoterion - Temporal Progression Report|","|External Time Elapsed: 1 hour, 14 minutes|","|Internal Time Elapsed: 18,525 hours (772 days)|","|Prisoners Currently Cultivating: 2/27|","|Maintenance Cost Paid: 20 Rudimentary Units of Everything|","|Mastery Advancement - The First Tongue|","|Your proficiency in The First Tongue has experienced dramatic growth through intensive practice|","|Current Classification: Fluent Speaker (Advanced)|","|You can now freely form Logos of 8+ Phonemes with minimal concentration required|","|Complex grammatical structures containing multiple Phonemes can be constructed with careful effort|","|Inscription speed increased by 340%|","|Error rate when forming Logos under pressure: Reduced to near-zero|","|Phoneme Comprehension Deepened|","| You have extrapolated and internalized the different variations of each Core Phoneme|","|Understanding achieved: A single Phoneme can carry dozens of subtle meanings depending on context, inflection, and combination|","|Example: The Phoneme of Fire can mean destruction, transformation, purification, passion, or creation depending on how it is expressed|","|This multilayered comprehension allows for more sophisticated Logos construction|","|Foundation for Perfect Speaker classification being systematically built|","|Prisoner Cultivation Report - Ozymandias|","|Days Cultivating: 772|","|Primary Focus: Perfecting The First Tongue and refining The Way of Mana and Hunger|","|Progress: Ozymandias has achieved near-perfect fluency in basic Logos construction|","|Advancement: His insights into The Way of Mana and Hunger have deepened your own understanding proportionally|","|Prisoner Cultivation Report - Raijin Katsuro|","|Days Cultivating: 772|","|Initial Status: Extremely resistant and defiant|","|Current Status: Disciplined and fully focused on The Way of Heavenly Lightning|","|Transformation: After 347 days of constant containment and Mana influence, Raijin ceased resistance and began genuine cultivation|","|Progress: The Way of Heavenly Lightning is being systematically influenced and enhanced by The Way of Mana|","|Notable Incident: On day 189, Raijin attempted rebellion and was subjected to thrashing and additional Logos of Imprisonment by Ozymandias. Resistance ceased entirely afterward.|","|Raijin now meditates precisely 18 hours per day and has developed what Ozymandias describes as \"an unhealthy obsession with perfecting his lightning manifestation to prove his Way wasn’t fundamentally weak.\"|","|Current Relationship: Professional prisoner with excellent work ethic|","|The Way of Heavenly Lightning - Integration Complete|","|You can now express The Way of Heavenly Lightning through your own Existence|","|Authority Level: 67% of Raijin’s original mastery|","|This percentage will continue increasing as Raijin refines his Way further within The Desmoterion|","|Principle Analysis - Records Studied|","|The complete records of Raijin Katsuro’s Singularity Principles have been thoroughly analyzed|","|The Genesis Principle contained within his foundation has been examined|","|Understanding Achieved: The structural difference between Singularity and Genesis Principles and The First Tongue has been mapped|","| Projection: After approximately 2,000 additional days of study within The Desmoterion, alteration of Complex Logos representing Principles will become possible|","|Application: This will allow the systematic elevation of your current Singularity Principles toward Genesis classification|","|Timeline: Achievable within 5-6 hours of external reality at current temporal dilation|","|Exponential Advancement - Way of Mana and Hunger|","|The combined cultivation of yourself, Ozymandias, and Raijin within The Desmoterion has created synergistic effects|","|Your Way has expanded across multiple dimensional expressions|","|Stability increased by 410%|","| Authority density increased by 890%|","|Foundation depth reinforced beyond previous projections|","| THE Organ of Civilization - Development Surge|","|Current Development: 31.00%|","|Maximum Prisoner Capacity: 27 to 36 entities|","|Temporal Dilation: 15,000x to 18,000x faster than external reality|","|Note: Each additional prisoner will continue accelerating overall development|","|THE Foundation of The First Tongue - Critical Advancement|","|THE Civilizational Authority Resistance: Increased to 50%|","|Effect: When facing THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities, your Foundation will innately filter out and resist approximately half of their authority pressure|","|This resistance applies passively and does not require conscious effort to maintain|","Oh!","The advancements made were absolutely glorious.","With such exponential progress, Noah truly felt like the seemingly far-away stage of achieving THE classification himself could be reached much sooner than he originally anticipated.","At this moment, he reached up into the swirling cluster of treasures overhead and plucked a jelly-like quartz that pulsed with internal radiance.","He took a bite, and his eyes immediately flashed with brilliant obsidian light.","|Treasure Consumed|","|Name: The Void-Touched Essence Quartz|","|Classification: Naturally Formed Civilizational Treasure|","|Composition: Crystallized Void authority mixed with pure THE Civilizational Authority|","|Effect: Permanently enhances capacity to manipulate void and empty space|","|Secondary Effect: Increases resistance to spatial collapse and dimensional distortion by 15%|","|Tertiary Effect: Grants instinctive understanding of how to hide one’s presence within spatial folds|","|Origin: THE Vaults of Ginnungagap|","|Note: Synergizes exceptionally well with The First Tongue’s Phoneme of Void|","As Noah absorbed the treasure’s benefits, Ul’moreth floated beside him with visible joy radiating from his hairy form.","The ancient being spoke with earnest sincerity.","|Ginnu Lifeforms rarely celebrate like this, you know. We tend to be solitary and focused exclusively on our individual advancement. But I wish for all of them to collectively succeed and find genuine happiness in their existence. It saddens me that across all of Existence, the strongest entities seem to have completely forgotten that happiness is even possible. Most seem intent only on covering all of reality under their particular Way and controlling absolutely everything they can reach.|","He shook his head with what might have been melancholy before turning to Noah with renewed energy.","| Alright, I’ve made you enjoy the festival long enough! You are partly still like The Others in nature. Like THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, or THE Secretive Eon and similar entities. I know your fundamental nature is not to sit still for extended periods. So go ahead. While the festival continues to unfold, we can also enjoy dancing and singing and eating while observing another battle for entertainment. I’ve already placed the one you had your eye on in the arena.|","Noah blinked and looked toward the distant arena.","Surely enough, THE Maelstrom Thundermane could be seen standing in the expanded space, looking around with a somber and heavy expression as if contemplating what was about to occur.","Noah smiled as he looked back toward Ul’moreth and nodded with genuine appreciation before beginning to walk steadily toward the arena.","As he moved, he replied to Ul’moreth’s words.","| Sometimes, one needs to have a precise balance of both approaches. To maintain that insane drive and ambition to place all of Existence within one’s palm and control, while also finding one’s own belonging and genuine happiness within that same Existence. Because sometimes, if you dont have Existence in your palm...you happiness can easily be taken away...|","At these words, Ul’moreth’s hairy figure radiated satisfaction as he responded with amused warmth.","| You don’t always have to have the last word in every exchange, my student. Go on now, let us see how you deal with someone who has a slightly stronger Depth of Absolute Sovereignty than your previous opponent. Even though their Ways are similar in expression, this should prove a little more difficult. Because some THE entities will not simply sit there politely and wait for you to speak The First Tongue at them. And remember, all THE classification entities are inherently faster than you currently are!|","Noah nodded at such accurate warnings as he opened his palm.","A vibrant blue-gold stick materialized with familiar weight.","The Goad, ready once more to deliver lessons.","He jumped directly toward the arena, and Gigaparsecs of space expanded dramatically all around him as the battlefield prepared for another impossible confrontation.","---","Far from The Primordial Genesis Shore, outside of Ginnungagap entirely, deep within The Infinite Unfurling where reality operated according to different fundamental rules, a titanic humanoid entity moved with terrifying purpose.","Multicolored flames of raw Existence itself surrounded this being completely, making their actual form completely unobservable beneath the blazing corona.","One could only see pressurized steam blowing continuously out of what appeared to be a nose, creating visible distortions in surrounding space.","Billowing waves of crushing heat poured out of what seemed to be a mouth with each breath.","The steam emanating from this entity’s existence alone melted and healed the surrounding fabric of reality in a continuous cycle.","If a THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity faced even the passive steam radiating from this being, they would be systematically melted alongside their entire Way and Civilization!","Dissolved completely by ambient heat alone.","The entity moved forward with measured steps that covered impossible distances.","Behind them, multicolored chains swung with rhythmic motion.","When one followed those chains backward, a horrifying sight became visible.","Seven completely bound THE classification entities were being dragged along like captured prisoners.","Each one held eyes filled with sheer existential terror as they barely dared to even look at the entity who pulled them along so effortlessly.","As for the entity themselves, their barely discernible eyes behind the flames of Existence were currently focused ahead on something specific.","Illusory screens floated in the space before them, displaying past scenes with perfect clarity.","Scenes from inside a Primordial Genesis Arena.","A battle showing a Pre-THE Existence wielding a simple stick.","Causing a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity to kneel through linguistic authority alone.","This titanic entity watched the recorded scene with complete calm, their expression unreadable behind the consuming flames.","After several moments of observation, they waved one hand casually and caused the illusory screens to disappear entirely.","And then they continued moving forward.","Calmly.","Gloriously.","Unfathomably!","Pulling seven terrified THE entities behind them like trophies."]},{"number":4614,"title":"Chapter 4614: Chapter 4613: A Period of Quintessential Progress! II","paragraphs":["Noah stepped into the vastly expanded arena with calm deliberation, his blue-gold Goad held loosely in one hand.","Across from him, Astrape, THE Maelstrom Thundermane , stood with a heavy expression carved into features that seemed perpetually surrounded by crackling white lightning.","The entity’s eyes blazed with fury and profound resentment.","When Astrape spoke, his voice carried the rumbling quality of distant thunder as he looked at him up and down.","\" All of this. Every single consequence that has befallen me. All of this happened because of YOU. And now, after everything you’ve caused, you have the audacity to step into a cage with me?\"","HUUM!","White lightning began crackling more intensely around his form as killing intent solidified into almost physical pressure.","\" Regardless of what The Ginnu Lifeforms do to me afterward, regardless of what punishments they devise, I will kill you today. Your existence ends here, Anomaly. I swear it upon my Way.\"","The arena trembled with the weight of that vow.","Noah looked at the enraged entity with complete calm, his expression revealing nothing.","And then he spoke with quiet finality.","\"You should not have given me time to utter.\"","THE Maelstrom Thundermane’s expression shifted to confusion.","What could that possibly mean?","In the very next instant, he understood with horrifying clarity.","Multiple Logos descended onto his position from positions all around the arena where Noah had already inscribed them while walking forward.","Seven Logos of Imprisonment, identical in structure to those that had bound the cages of captured THE entities, wrapped around Astrape’s form with irresistible authority as he found this power familiar!","Additional Logos designed specifically to weaken and suppress lightning-based authorities activated simultaneously.","Shock exploded across Astrape’s features as he realized Noah had prepared the battlefield before even beginning the confrontation.","The battle that unfolded was less a clash of pure power and more a deadly dance between opposing forces.","Above the arena, Ginnu Lifeforms continued their ritual celebration, dancing around the massive flames of Phonemes with building fervor.","Their movements seemed to mirror and accentuate what occurred below.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane erupted with his full authority, his Way of Fulmination expressing itself in overwhelming fashion.","Bursts of brilliant white lightning exploded outward, each discharge containing enough concentrated power to annihilate entire realities.","The lightning smashed against the descending Logos with devastating force, shattering several of the linguistic constructs instantly.","But Noah simply reformed them faster than Astrape could destroy them, his Fluent Speaker mastery allowing rapid reconstruction.","Then Astrape released something far more terrifying.","A Genesis Principle.","The Genesis Principle of Absolute Conduction!","The moment he unleashed this profound authority, everything within the arena transformed fundamentally.","The ground, the air, the very fabric of space itself, even the Logos Noah had constructed, all of it converted instantly into tendrils of pure white lightning.","Existence itself became an ocean of electrical discharge under Astrape’s complete authority.","Noah’s body was smashed backward violently as reality itself pressed down with crushing force.","The four Logos inscribed across his form flared with protective authority, filtering out approximately half of the devastating pressure.","But even with that resistance, every ounce of transformed reality around him sought to force his existence to convert into pure lightning under Astrape’s Genesis Principle.","Astrape came to float above Noah like a titan formed entirely from condensed electrical fury.","At that moment, this enraged being chose not to speak or waste breath on declarations.","He simply wanted to kill.","What happened next seemed to play out in slow motion, each instant stretched to painful clarity.","Astrape raised both hands high above his head.","For Gigaparsecs behind him, stretching to the very edges of the expanded arena space, absolutely all of existence turned into vibrant white lightning under his authority.","A sea of electrical annihilation waiting to be released.","He brought his hands down with finality, seeking to thunder all of that accumulated devastation directly onto Noah’s position and erase him from Existence entirely!","At such a critical moment, the scene continued playing in that strange slow-motion clarity.","Noah simply raised his stick with calm precision and spoke words that carried quiet satisfaction.","| Thank you for coming so close.|","Even though the might and Depth of Astrape was so terrifying that his Genesis Principle had transformed absolutely everything in the arena, even the Logos Noah had constructed, into white lightning, there remained one fundamental truth.","That Genesis Principle itself was ultimately a complex form of Logos written in The First Tongue.","And even though the visible Logos Noah had utilized were transformed into lightning alongside everything else, his Way could sense every single Phoneme comprising those linguistic structures.","All around him, hidden within the ocean of white lightning that now permeated the entire space, Noah had reformed the seven Logos of Imprisonment.","He had masked them perfectly to appear identical to the lightning surrounding them, making them completely undetectable.","At this moment, where Astrape’s descending hands would bring annihilation crashing down to ensure Noah’s death, Noah activated the veiled Logos that were now mere inches away from the thundering entity.","HUUM!","The terrifying waves of pressure and overwhelming power that Astrape was releasing instantly began to dwindle and be systematically repressed.","The seven Logos of Imprisonment activated simultaneously, wrapping around the shocked entity with binding authority.","Additional Logos manifested in rapid succession.","Multiple Logos of Absolute Separation cut Astrape off from his Civilization and Way.","Logos of Predetermined Failure ensured that any attempt to draw upon external Existence or utilize his Way would conclude in immediate collapse.","Because of the extreme closeness and proximity, Noah’s mastery expressed itself with devastating efficiency.","Tendrils of white lightning that had surrounded Astrape instantly transformed back into visible Logos and began binding him with multiplying restraints.","Noah himself took his Goad and began striking with serpentine speed.","The stick lashed out multiple times in rapid succession, each strike landing on different points across Astrape’s massive form.","With each precise impact, another portion of Astrape’s power was locked away and sealed.","The strikes looked like an intricate dance of Existence itself.","In the surroundings, the vibrant music of the festival permeated even into this expanded arena space.","The rhythm of drums, the melodic tones of Phoneme-based instruments, the harmonic chanting of The First Tongue all created an atmosphere that transformed violence into performance!","Above, the Ginnu Lifeforms were dancing with even more fervor as if everything had reached a critical precipice.","Their movements became faster, more passionate, more celebratory.","The more times Noah struck Astrape with his Goad, the dimmer and dimmer the authority of this once-terrifying being became.","No matter how desperately Astrape tried to express his Way of Fulmination, the Logos already binding him made such expression impossible.","And even when he managed to break through individual Phoneme connections in the linguistic chains through sheer force, Noah reformed them even faster than Astrape could shatter the links.","For the final strike, Noah took a batting stance with his Goad held in both hands.","He swung upward with explosive force, the stick connecting with Astrape’s bound form and launching the massive entity high into the air.","Noah’s figure flickered and appeared far above at the precise trajectory where Astrape would arrive.","He swung downward with equal devastating power, smashing the helpless entity back toward the arena floor with meteor-like velocity.","BOOM!"]},{"number":4615,"title":"Chapter 4615: Chapter 4614: A Period of Quintessential Progress! III","paragraphs":["The moment this occurred, the dance reached its conclusion.","Noah crashed down alongside Astrape like a falling star, his Goad positioned perfectly to drive into the massive chest of the defeated THE entity.","BOOM !","The impact shook the entire arena as Noah landed standing directly on the prone body of a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity.","Astrape looked up at him with eyes filled with pure incredulity and absolute shock.","This could not be happening. This should not be possible!","And yet...","Noah simply raised his Goad one final time and swung it down to strike Astrape’s head with measured force.","The instant the blow connected, Astrape’s entire form disappeared.","He was deemed defeated.","And now he was drawn directly into THE Infinite Desmoterion as its third official prisoner.","Only now did the dance truly end.","Outside the arena, the Ginnu Lifeforms dancing around the ritual flames howled out in celebration, their voices creating linguistic harmonics that made reality vibrate.","The Phonemes of Fire surrounding them exploded upward and formed into towering pillars of glorious multi-colored flames that reached toward the transformed sky.","Noah stood in the center of the arena with eyes shining brightly as he breathed out slowly, processing what had just occurred.","And glorious prompts began descending before his vision.","|Unquantifiable Harvest Initiated|","|You have suppressed and imprisoned a second entity of fundamentally higher Scale of Existence|","|Harvest being collected and amplified exponentially by Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect|","|Resource generation continues exceeding conventional calculation parameters|","|All gains multiplied by factors beyond standard measurement|","|Sequential THE entity defeats are creating compound amplification effects|","|THE Scale Breaker - Distinction Evolution|","|Your Distinction has grown stronger through additional THE entity suppression|","|Effect Enhancement: Gap reduction when facing higher Scale entities increased from base level to amplified tier|","|THE Infinite Desmoterion - Prisoner Acquisition|","|Second THE classification prisoner successfully imprisoned|","|Active Prisoners: 3/36|","| Prisoner 1: Ozymandias (willing cooperation, perfect synchronization)|","|Prisoner 2: Raijin Katsuro, THE Monk of Ten Thousand Storms (disciplined cultivation)|","|Prisoner 3: Astrape, THE Maelstrom Thundermane (newly captured, status: resistant)|","|Maintenance Cost: 30 Rudimentary Units of Everything per 24 hours|","|Two THE entities now cultivating within The Desmoterion under 18,000x temporal dilation|","|Ozymandias continues perfecting The First Tongue and The Way of Mana and Hunger|","|Raijin Katsuro refines The Way of Heavenly Lightning under Mana influence|","|Astrape will be compelled to cultivate The Way of Fulmination under containment|","|The Way of Fulmination - Integration Initiated|","|As Astrape cultivates and refines his Way within The Desmoterion, aspects of The Way of Fulmination will gradually become accessible to you|","|His Genesis Principle of Absolute Conduction will be studied and potentially replicated|","|Estimated time for meaningful integration: Variable based on cooperation level|","|Timeline for elevating your own Singularity Principles to Genesis tier: Somewhat accelerated|","|THE Organ of Civilization - Development Surge|","|Current Development: 31.00% to 38.00%|","|Major advancement triggered by second THE prisoner acquisition|","|Maximum Prisoner Capacity: 36 to 45 entities|","|Temporal Dilation: 18,000x to 21,000x faster than external reality|","| THE Foundation of The First Tongue - Ongoing Growth|","|THE Civilizational Authority Resistance: 50% to 62%|","...!","Oh!","The prompts were numerous as he needed to condense them somewhat.","But...","Noah absorbed all of these notifications with deep satisfaction.","Two THE Surface Depth prisoners now cultivating at twenty-one thousand times temporal dilation.","His progression was accelerating at rates that defied reasonable expectation!","And he was only just beginning to fill THE Infinite Desmoterion with captured entities who would fuel his advancement.","The dance continued.","Always forward.","He looked up and said with a smile.","|Teacher, this student wants more enemies...so send more THEs down!|","...!","Teacher.","Never did he think a day would come where he would say this, but Ul’moreth had given him far too much as saying this distinction at least should be nothing much. After all, he didn’t think of himself to be so arrogant that he could not learn from another!","So he had called out above.","And truly, moments later...","He saw a distant cage be opened, an obsidian gold light pull something from inside it and chuck it down to the Arena!","A THE entity who looked around with shock and confusion landed in the Arena right after.","And Noah raised his stick!","But...","Every THE entity held their own unique Way.","The words of Ul’moreth remained absolutely true that regardless of how much control Noah gained over The First Tongue, THE entities were inherently faster than him.","So he had to prepare multiple things in advance when he came to face them.","Astrape had talked in the beginning and given him critical time to set things in motion.","The next monster that he faced was an extremely cautious one.","The moment this entity landed and found itself in the setting of the expanded arena with an enemy it sensed was merely Pre-THE classification, it moved with ridiculously terrifying speed.","Speed that exceeded light by margins that made conventional measurements meaningless.","Well, even light couldn’t be used as an accurate comparison for what THE entities were capable of.","What they moved past could at most be accurately described by Planck Speed.","Planck Speed represented the theoretical maximum velocity at which any causality or information could travel through Existence.","It was the speed limit of reality itself , beyond which the very concept of \"movement\" ceased to have coherent meaning.","To move at Planck Speed meant crossing a Planck Length in a single Planck Time unit. In practical terms, it meant traversing the smallest possible meaningful distance in the smallest possible meaningful moment.","And even those words were hard to grasp as one might scratch their head!","For entities operating at this velocity, conventional space became irrelevant. Distance was no longer an obstacle but merely a suggestion that could be ignored.","In the context of their current reality where Existence itself was woven from linguistic authority and Civilizational power, Planck Speed represented movement so fast that it occurred between the individual Phonemes of a spoken Logos.","You could begin forming a word, and a THE entity moving at such velocity would cross the entire arena, strike you, and return to their starting position before the second Phoneme left your mouth.","THE entities seemingly moved even faster than this theoretical maximum.","The moment this particular entity arrived in the arena was the exact same moment it arrived directly in front of Noah with one hand already wrapped around his throat.","It was fucking terrifying!"]},{"number":4616,"title":"Chapter 4616: Chapter 4615: Choices I","paragraphs":["No transition. No visible movement. Just instant displacement from one position to another as if space itself had been deleted between the two points.","The entity’s hand clenched with crushing pressure, THE Civilizational Authority flooding through that grip with intent to shatter Noah’s existence immediately.","Its only mistake was not moving to crush Noah’s existence or attempting annihilation in that very first instant.","Because the moment its hand made contact, the moment Noah’s existence was grabbed in close proximity, Noah used his own body as the direct conduit to layer multiple Logos of Imprisonment onto this entity’s form.","The linguistic constructs erupted from his skin where contact was made, wrapping around the shocked entity’s arm and spreading rapidly across its entire body.","While the entity processed what was happening with dawning horror, Noah began using his Goad to strike its body with rapid precision.","Each impact locked away more authority, bound more of its Way, suppressed more of its capacity to resist.","Only after seven strikes had landed and seven layers of containment were active did Noah have enough breathing room to act further.","He brought his other hand up and began manually moving the fingers of this terrifying entity, forcing them to unclasp from around his neck one by one.","The strength required was immense even with the entity suppressed, but eventually Noah extracted himself from the deadly grip.","Every single THE entity was genuinely dangerous.","Even though he had now suppressed two successfully, this third one had actually come extremely close to heavily injuring or even killing him in the opening instant.","When they stopped posturing and talking so much, when they acted with pure killing intent and maximum efficiency, THE entities were utterly dreadful opponents.","Suppressing two or three would not mean he could definitively and easily suppress others going forward.","Each one would present its own unique challenge based on their particular Way and combat approach.","But as Noah sensed this entity continuing to desperately try expressing its Way of Existence to shatter the Logos and break apart the individual Phonemes that comprised them, his eyes squinted with dangerous focus.","He utilized his Goad to continue delivering lessons with methodical brutality.","Thrashing this THE entity with strike after precise strike.","Inscribing additional containment with each blow!","Until finally, the entity’s resistance crumbled completely.","And it disappeared in the next moment, drawn directly into THE Infinite Desmoterion as the fourth prisoner.","Noah breathed heavily and stretched his neck with careful rotation.","Burning marks could still be felt across his throat where the entity’s hand had gripped him, only now beginning to heal under his regenerative capabilities.","After he confirmed through internal sense that everything was stable, he silently deployed multiple Logos of Imprisonment all around the arena in concealed positions.","Preparation for whoever came next.","Then he looked upward toward where he knew Ul’moreth observed and spoke with voice carrying determined hunger.","| Again!|","He didn’t even glance at the multiple prompts descending before his vision.","He simply wanted more opponents!","—","Outside The Primordial Genesis Arena, Ul’moreth gazed down at Noah as his student prepared to face yet another opponent.","The hairy Primeval Titan smiled beneath his obscuring hair as he turned toward a THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity standing beside him.","His voice carried casual authority as he gestured toward a specific figure below.","| Take that little fox outside of Ginnungagap and into The Infinite Unfurling. My student is extremely paranoid by nature, and while such paranoia can be exhausting, it can also be beneficial sometimes. Anomalies more often than not possess senses and instincts that the rest of us simply don’t have access to.|","He paused before continuing with thoughtful consideration.","| He says she is an investment he’s making that might pay off substantially over time, so just keep her company in The Infinite Unfurling for now while events unfold here. Take some treasures from my personal stores with you to aid her growth and advancement. Consider it my contribution to whatever my student is planning.|","Ul’moreth said all of these words while pointing toward none other than Lumivara, the nine-tailed fox who had followed Noah’s Way.","Noah had taken her out of his inner existence during the festival and spoken his final words to her with characteristic bluntness.","He wanted to continue exploring Ginnungagap and all the profound mysteries it held.","But if anything catastrophic happened during his journeys through this chaotic realm, he would be forced to utilize temporal traversal to escape immediately.","And he would not be able to take her with him if such emergency evacuation became necessary.","Since she was a follower of his Way and had sworn herself to his path, he would see what advancements she could make if she managed to survive whatever unfolded in The Infinite Unfurling on her own merit.","Lumivara had been teary-eyed but she nodded with understanding and acceptance.","At this moment, as she looked around with amazement at the ongoing battle between her Master and another THE entity, at the glorious festival continuing to unfold with ritual wonder, a Ginnu Lifeform materialized beside her.","The entity gently took her arm to whisk her away toward whatever destiny awaited beyond Ginnungagap’s borders.","While such arrangements occurred, at the distant edge of The Primordial Genesis Shore where reality began transitioning into the chaotic void, THE Fisherman sat calmly continuing his endless task.","His fishing line extended into the murky waters of Ginnungagap with patient stillness.","But his eyes pulsed occasionally with visible caution, and he sighed every few moments with increasing frequency.","As if his Weavings were tense and filled with profound worry about something he could not quite identify.","He pulled his line in once again and it came up completely empty.","No catch. Not even a nibble.","He sighed once more with building frustration.","And in that exact moment, a voice spoke from directly beside him.","|What’s got you so stressed, big guy?|","BOOM!","THE Fisherman’s eyes became unfathomably grim as he whipped his head to the right.","An entity sat there casually, as if they had been present the entire time.","An entity that had somehow been here without THE Fisherman sensing their presence until after they chose to speak.","And they had spoken using The First Tongue with perfect fluency!"]},{"number":4617,"title":"Chapter 4617: Chapter 4616: Choices II","paragraphs":["THE Fisherman’s eyes flashed with alarm as he immediately began to-","| Come on now, don’t do any of that.|","Before Ains could even fully perceive what was happening, faster than even Plank Speed, dozens of silent Logos flashed into existence throughout the surrounding area.","The light of at least nine distinct Genesis Principles erupted simultaneously.","This entire region turned eerily quiet, reality itself seeming to hold its breath.","The urgent warning information that THE Fisherman was desperately trying to send to alert Ul’moreth did not even leave his existence before it was completely stopped and contained.","His eyes filled with genuine trepidation as he looked over at this being who had appeared from nowhere.","The mysterious entity seemed deceptively simple by all visual accounts.","A humanoid figure adorned in flowing robes that were perfectly split between absolute black and pure white, the division so precise it seemed to cut through the concept of color itself.","His eyes crackled with vibrant purple light that seemed to contain compressed infinity within each pupil.","His bearing felt unfathomably grand despite his relaxed posture, as if the weight of countless eons and infinite possibilities rested comfortably on his shoulders.","His eyes alone, as they gazed at everything around them with detached curiosity, held a natural superiority that would cause even weak THE entities to falter and question their own worth.","When facing such an entity, THE Fisherman felt like...a child! As if he would be powerless regardless!","Ains stared at this being as the first words that left his mouth carried desperate need for identification.","| Which one of them are you? THE Creature? THE Primordial Chaos? THE Primordial Paradox? THE Secretive Eon? THE Tongue Whisper? THE—|","The entity laughed with genuine amusement, waving one hand dismissively.","| Relax with all those grandiose names and titles. Me, THE Creature? That brutish fucker who solves everything through raw consumption and violence? Haha, no, no. Nothing like that monstrous approach at all.|","He smiled in a manner that seemed friendly on the surface but carried unfathomable depths beneath.","| You can refer to me as THE Arbitrium. What I am is someone who seeks to learn absolutely everything about Existence and all its infinite permutations. I am also a devoted student of choices and the consequences they create. I love choices more than anything else.|","His purple eyes gleamed with building intensity.","|I consider flashy battles to be quite boring and ultimately a waste of potential. Watching the process of a choice being made, especially profoundly difficult ones where every option carries terrible cost, entertains me far more than any combat ever could. So for you, right now, there is a choice to be made.|","HUUM!","As THE Arbitrium said such words, he smiled in an overtly friendly manner and came to sit casually beside Ains as if they were old companions sharing a peaceful moment.","His voice carried terrifying weight despite the conversational tone.","|I know that your buddy Ul’moreth passed through here recently with someone unusual. I know they are currently enjoying that delightful festival inside The Primordial Genesis Shore. Which fucking sucks that you can’t even go and participate yourself, right? Stuck out here fishing endlessly while everyone else celebrates. But regardless, I know exactly what’s happening in there.|","He paused to let that sink in before continuing.","| Instead of doing some insane things that would be terribly destructive and wasteful, I want to give you a choice. A fairly simple one, all things considered. I...won’t lift a single finger to harm anyone directly. But if you choose to collapse your own Depth of Absolute Sovereignty voluntarily, if you take it all the way down from THE Fundamental Depth to merely THE Surface Depth through self-imposed destruction, if you make that choice of your own free will right now, I promise you that absolutely no harm will come to Ul’moreth.|","HUUM!","The words hung in the air with ominous finality.","This entity sat beside Ains with complete calm while delivering such a horrifying ultimatum.","Ains became even more somber as the implications crashed through his mind.","His voice emerged carefully controlled.","| What of the one that Ul’moreth traveled with?|","THE Arbitrium’s smile widened as purple light danced in his eyes with building amusement.","| Ah, good question! I appreciate someone who thinks about all the variables before committing. If you go one step further in your sacrifice, if you completely dismantle your entire Civilization rather than merely suppressing your Depth, if you drop yourself down to before you even held any classification at all, down to just Pre-THE existence, then I won’t touch the unusual one that Ul’moreth traveled with either.|","He leaned in slightly as if sharing a secret between friends.","| And this choice I can actually help you execute if you wish to go through with it. I can ensure the process is clean and complete, no lingering fragments or hidden anchors. A true return to lesser existence. So tell me, THE Fisherman...|","His purple eyes locked onto Ains with crushing focus.","| What will it be? What will be the choice you make?|","The mysterious entity remained unfathomably calm after delivering those terrifying words.","As if they were having the most casual conversation imaginable rather than presenting Ains with a choice that would shatter his entire existence.","THE Arbitrium swung his legs with childlike playfulness as he spoke with conversational ease.","|All those years ago, you found those despicable Ginnu Lifeforms who had discovered a loophole in your community’s laws. They knew that if they outright killed any of their own kind, they would be persecuted and punished severely. So they didn’t kill. They simply slowly ate away at the existence of other Ginnu Lifeforms, keeping their victims perpetually on the edge of death and complete collapse while continuing an endless cycle of harvest on their own kind for an untold number of years.|","His purple eyes gleamed with something that might have been admiration.","| They were respected leaders in your community, trusted authorities that everyone looked up to. When you finally discovered what they were doing, you rightly and decisively collapsed every single one of them without hesitation. And in the end, you chose to keep the secret of their horrifying actions so that all Ginnu Lifeforms would not lose their fundamental faith in their leadership structure.|","He nodded with genuine appreciation.","|It was something genuinely valiant to watch unfold. Which makes it such a shame that now you have to make this new choice. Ah, the irony of Existence...|","The words caused Ains to tremble visibly as profound emotion crashed through him.","His voice emerged somber and heavy.","| Who are you really? What entity holds such knowledge of events that were buried and forgotten?|","THE Arbitrium waved one hand dismissively, his smile never faltering.","| My specific identity is not the point here. You are missing the point entirely. The point is your choice and nothing else. So what will it be? You defended your juniors last time when it cost you dearly. Will you defend Ul’moreth and an Anomaly this time?|"]},{"number":4618,"title":"Chapter 4618: Chapter 4617: No longer capital!","paragraphs":["THE Arbitrium leaned forward with building interest.","| Your buddy and longtime friend, I can absolutely understand why you would make that sacrifice for him. But the anomaly that he came with? You don’t really know this entity at all. You have no deep attachments or shared history. Would you truly choose to go even further, to break your entire Civilization down past THE Surface Depth and into complete Pre-THE existence, for someone you barely know?|","The words hung in the air with crushing weight.","They were followed by an immense silence that seemed to stretch across eternity.","A sense of profound power mixed with deep melancholy wrapped around THE Fisherman as he sat there processing everything.","At this moment, he calmly took his fishing rod and cast out another line into the murky waters.","His movements were practiced and serene despite the trembling in his hands.","His gaze held utmost serenity and terrible power as he spoke with voice carrying absolute conviction.","| Your type continues to play with Existence as if everything lies perfectly under your fingertips. Always so arrogant and prideful, as if you could do absolutely anything with zero repercussions or consequences. One of these days, entities like you and The Others will find yourselves in the exact same positions that you keep putting the rest of us in. One of these days, you will have your due. Existence always balances itself eventually.|","THE Arbitrium smiled with genuine amusement at these words.","His carefree nature radiated outward as he nodded with easy agreement.","| You are absolutely right. Existence is vast and unfathomable beyond anyone’s complete comprehension. Who knows what will happen seconds or years from now? I may just find myself in the exact same terrible position as you currently occupy. But right now, at this specific moment, I am on the other side of this equation. So I will enjoy it thoroughly while it lasts.|","After these words, a heavy and profound silence descended.","It carried a sense of inevitable loss and mourning.","THE Fisherman spoke calmly despite the tremor in his voice.","|I will make the choice of collapsing my Civilization all the way down before even THE Surface Depth classification. If you can help me execute this, that would be appreciated. Because inherently, my Sovereignty will resist its own collapse with everything it has. I do not think I have it within my heart to carry it out completely by myself.|","The moment he said these words with finality, THE Arbitrium smiled with expression suggesting this entire situation brought him unfathomable joy.","His eyes flashed with a sense of immensity and terrifying power, as if the wonder and satisfaction within had grown even stronger.","He spoke with voice carrying genuine curiosity.","| What a fine choice of sacrifice that is. I can understand making it for your longtime friend Ul’moreth. But why the anomaly? Why make the choice to collapse everything even further for an entity you barely know? What drives such selflessness?|","At such a direct question, THE Fisherman did not answer immediately.","He continued holding his fishing rod with both hands, his posture unchanged.","His arms trembled slightly, visibly shaking as if his entire Sovereignty was mourning what was about to occur.","His voice emerged with quiet dignity.","| Someone like you and how you view Existence would never be able to truly understand my reasoning. Let’s not waste any more time with pointless questions. The delay of the action is only torturing me further. Do what you must.|","At such words, an extremely sad and grand scene unfolded.","THE Fisherman raised his hand and plunged it directly into his own chest.","His fingers wrapped around his heart, the core of his Civilization and Sovereignty.","And he decisively crushed it.","A massive storm of Civilizational Authority sought to erupt outward in violent rejection of this self-destruction.","But THE Arbitrium simply waved his hand with casual authority and caused the explosion to disappear entirely, contained before it could manifest.","He then adopted a calm expression as if wanting to help out a dear friend in need.","A past friend.","| Ah, let me assist you with the more difficult part of erasing even THE Surface Depth classification. This requires precision.|","With such words spoken gently, he tapped out with one finger toward THE Fisherman’s form.","Ains trembled violently as crimson-gold blood instantly spurted from his eyes, nose, and mouth.","Every single ounce of his Civilization was systematically dissipated and erased.","Existence itself wailed around him in mourning, reality crying out at the loss of such profound authority.","The mysterious entity let out a calm and satisfied sigh as he observed the completion of this sacrifice.","| Ah, what a choice. What a magnificent choice indeed!|","As he said this with genuine appreciation, something else occurred behind them.","From the inner depths of The Primordial Genesis Shore, Lumivara was being led by a Ginnu Lifeform.","They flew outward together, their figures passing by and seeing only the backs of THE Fisherman and the mysterious entity sitting side by side.","THE Arbitrium turned toward them with perfect timing and smiled warmly.","He waved his hand as if to say a friendly hello.","Both the Ginnu Lifeform and Lumivara immediately bowed deeply toward him with instinctive respect.","The Ginnu Lifeform also looked toward Ains and nodded with visible respect and acknowledgment.","In their eyes, they saw no blood or desolation at all. Just two entities sitting peacefully side by side as if enjoying casual conversation.","The Ginnu Lifeform gently pulled Lumivara away as they disappeared into an obsidian river passageway leading out of Ginnungagap.","THE Arbitrium watched this departure as if it was of absolutely no consequence to him whatsoever.","He stood up and carefully wiped imaginary dust from his black and white robes.","|Ah, alright then. Thank you genuinely for the choice, THE Fisherman... oh, nope, my mistake. Just \"the fisherman\" now. No capital letters for you anymore. Ah, very sad indeed, my friend.|","He paused before continuing with voice carrying binding authority.","|But do not worry unnecessarily. I keep my end of every bargain I make. I will not personally move to harm a single hair on Ul’moreth or the Anomaly he brought here. For now, you simply continue fishing here as per normal and don’t ruin my fun by doing anything dramatic.|","...!"]},{"number":4619,"title":"Chapter 4619: Chapter 4618: Imagine It!","paragraphs":["After he delivered these final words, this entity tapped out with his finger once more.","Immense waves of The First Tongue erupted outward with terrifying complexity.","Dozens of Phonemes came together with perfect precision, forming into multiple complete words.","The words combined further to form an entire sentence, a sentence that wrapped around this entire region before becoming invisible and disappearing from normal observation.","A binding constructed from linguistic authority that would ensure compliance absolutely!","This entity then hummed pleasantly to himself as he smiled with satisfaction, nodded once, and took a single step directly into The Primordial Genesis Shore.","Behind him, a desolate scene remained.","The fisherman still sat there with his fishing line cast out into the murky waters.","A smiling expression remained fixed on his face, serene and peaceful.","But bloody tears fell continuously from his eyes and nose, crimson-gold streams running down his cheeks.","His heart was destroyed.","His Civilization was completely erased.","His very being, built across eons of struggle and advancement, was just collapsed down to nothing.","And he sat there fishing, still protecting those he cared about even as everything he was dissolved into memory.","On the other end...","The mysterious entity known as THE Arbitrium delved deeper into The Primordial Genesis Shore.","As he moved through the chaotic space, his form began to subtly change. An aura of a unique Way of Existence manifested.","A rough obsidian robe materialized around him, replacing the pristine black and white garment.","His hair enlarged dramatically, becoming wild and unruly, pulsing with contained power.","His facial features shifted and transformed, taking on a different structure entirely.","But his eyes maintained their same infinite purple depth, crackling with that same unfathomable intensity.","He appeared at the heart of The Primordial Genesis Shore and observed the ongoing festival with genuine appreciation.","A smile crossed his transformed features as Phonemes erupted around him in joyful expression.","He actually moved forward and joined directly into the circle of dancing Ginnu Lifeforms surrounding the massive bonfire of Fire Phonemes.","He danced with them, his movements creating patterns that generated melody even grander and more complex than what the others produced.","His presence felt unique among the gathered entities, carrying weight that transcended simple classification.","Moments later, the distant Ul’moreth floating above while observing the Weavings unfolding in the arena below noticed this particular dancer.","His eyes flashed with sharp recognition before he laughed with warm familiarity and voiced out with booming enthusiasm.","|Haha, Mammon, you actually made it!|","The words carried the tone one would use greeting a longtime friend arriving at a celebration.","Down at the bonfire, THE Arbitrium , now known as Mammon to those gathered, looked over and smiled warmly.","He took a single step and appeared instantly beside Ul’moreth in the space above the festival.","His smile remained as he spoke with conversational ease.","|I just came by to see what all the commotion was about. I caught up with Ains before arriving here as he seems a little...down. He sends his regards. But...it seems you have taken in something quite dangerous to this settlement.|","As he said this, he looked down toward the arena below.","What unfolded there was another impossible scene.","Multiple Logos spun around a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity who erupted with verdant leaves and tremendous storms swirling in all directions.","The entity’s Way of Nature expressed itself with overwhelming force, attempting to transform the entire arena into a primordial forest of crushing authority.","But the Logos were gradually suppressing this tremendous power, containing and binding it piece by piece.","Opposing this THE entity was a Pre-THE Existence, none other than Noah, who moved with focused intensity.","He was gloriously forming even more complex Logos with rapid precision while simultaneously striking out with his blue-gold Goad.","Each strike locked away more authority as he steadily closed the distance toward his opponent.","Ul’moreth looked at the scene below and sighed with mixture of pride and concern.","| Not any more dangerous than anything else in Existence. Just like you and me, he is simply someone trying to pioneer his own unique Way through this vast reality.|","Mammon looked over with expression carrying deeper understanding than anyone could imagine!","He sighed with what might have been genuine worry.","| You were always like this, Ul’moreth. Hopeful to a fault. Idealistic even when reality demands cynicism. How can you say such words when you are watching what he is currently doing? When you know exactly what something like that represents?|","His purple eyes gleamed with intensity.","|You know that The Others would inevitably come for him if they learned of his existence and capabilities. I know you understand this with absolute clarity. So why are you doing this? Why take such a monumental risk?|","The words hung heavy in the air between them.","Ul’moreth kept his gaze fixed on the arena below as he became immensely calm and somber.","When he spoke, his voice carried the weight of decisions already made.","|The Ginnu Lifeforms are not so weak that we cannot defend what we choose to protect. We fight collectively and move collectively when threats arise. And I am not merely an idiotic idealist who thinks nothing can possibly go wrong. I know many things can go catastrophically wrong. I know the substantial chance of those involved in The Oldest Paradox of Existence having dangerous interest if they knew of him and what he represents. I know all of this.|","He paused before continuing with building conviction.","|Because of that knowledge, I have taken extensive countermeasures. I have reached out to the other Leaders of Primordial Genesis Shores scattered throughout Ginnungagap. You were actually next on my list to contact, but you at times go silent for eons. But since you are already here, you can simply join in with what I am planning.|","He could simply join in?","Mammon smiled mysteriously at such casual words.","He maintained his calm demeanor as he spoke with deceptive lightness.","|You think gathering entities like me will be of any substantial help against those disastrous beings if they decide to act? That seems optimistic even for you.|","He said such words casually, as if discussing weather rather than potential conflict with the most powerful entities in all of Existence.","Ul’moreth’s expression revealed that he had already made a heavy choice!","|I have been thinking extensively that maybe... I should throw my full weight behind him. Completely and without reservation.|","BOOM!","The declaration carried crushing significance.","He continued with voice building in passionate conviction.","|He is young, yes. Inexperienced by our standards. But what he represents is genuinely grand and unprecedented. Rarely do entities like me or you elect to choose our own Ways to fully support another being’s advancement. We are too proud, too invested in our own paths. But doing so with him? Combining our collective strength and knowledge behind his potential?|","His eyes blazed with possibility.","|We could allow him to become just like them. Like THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, THE Secretive Eon, and the others who stand at the absolute apex. But better than them in crucial ways. Not filled with that same baleful ambition of trying to stomp brutally over all others just to claim the top position. Imagine someone achieving the same standing of power as those monstrous entities, but without their destructive tendencies.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4620,"title":"Chapter 4620: Chapter 4619: Imagine It! II","paragraphs":["Ul’moreth leaned forward with building intensity.","|Imagine the possibilities that would open for Ginnu Lifeforms across all of Ginnungagap. For the advancement and protection of The First Tongue itself. For reshaping how power operates at the highest levels of Existence.|","The words carried tremendous weight and dangerous implications.","Mammon smiled internally at hearing such bold declarations, though his expression remained carefully neutral.","|Mm, I can imagine such outcomes. I can absolutely imagine them. But the words you are saying right now are profoundly dangerous, old friend. If THE Creature, who actively seeks to encompass all of Existence under his authority, ever hears you speak like this about elevating a potential rival...|","He shook his head with what seemed like genuine concern.","|You have to be more careful, Ul’moreth. You never know who might be listening to conversations like this one. But setting that aside for the moment, you say you will throw your full weight behind him, and you expect to convince me and the other settlement leaders to do the same? Not everyone shares the same beliefs and values as you. Many would see this as foolish risk.|","At these words, Ul’moreth smiled with absolute confidence.","|Once they see him in action, they will believe. Once they witness what he can accomplish with proper support, doubt will transform into conviction. I mean, just look at him right now.|","He gestured down toward the arena.","The scene below showed the THE Surface Depth entity with The Way of Nature becoming fully suppressed by Noah’s relentless assault.","Multiple Logos wrapped around the defeated entity as resistance finally collapsed.","And in the very next moment, the entity disappeared entirely, drawn into THE Infinite Desmoterion as another prisoner.","Thereafter, Noah’s valiant shout could be heard echoing across the space.","| Again!|","Without resting for even a moment, demanding the next challenge immediately.","Ul’moreth smiled brilliantly at this display of relentless drive.","He waved his hairy hand with casual authority.","In the next instant, another distant cage opened as his brilliant obsidian-gold light reached inside, plucking the entity contained within before throwing them directly into the expanded arena.","Ul’moreth had spoken freely and openly to Mammon because to him, this was similar to when he conversed with Ains.","A friend he had known for an unfathomably long period of time across countless eons.","To Ul’moreth , that was simply what Mammon represented. Nothing more, nothing less.","A trusted companion he could share his thoughts with openly!","---","Outside The Primordial Genesis Shore, at the very edge where reality transitioned into chaotic void, a desolate scene continued to unfold.","Ains sat there with his fishing line cast out into murky waters, his posture unchanged from before.","The smile remained fixed on his face, serene and peaceful.","But crimson-gold tears continued falling from his eyes and nose, staining his features with the evidence of profound loss.","His existence felt diminished, weak in ways that should not be possible for one who had once held such tremendous authority.","Moments later, two powerful figures materialized at the edge of The Primordial Genesis Shore.","THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin appeared with cautious deliberation, their senses extended outward to assess potential threats.","They observed the figure of Ains fishing with growing confusion.","Tor, THE First Hunger, spoke first with voice carrying genuine puzzlement.","\"My Hunger says this place holds the most promise for finding what we seek. It is a Ginnu Settlement, and there sits a Ginnu. Though why do his eyes seem so profoundly sad when he is merely fishing? And why does he feel so terrifyingly weak for one of his kind?\"","The questions hung in the air as they approached cautiously.","And when they came within a certain distance, they both stopped instantly in shock.","A terrifying type of power wrapped around this entire region, invisible but absolutely present.","Bindings constructed from authority that transcended normal classification.","THE Living Origin’s expression shifted to alarm as she spoke with a voice holding dawning horror.","| This type of power...is something that only someone like THE Creature himself could produce! Or perhaps one of the other entities operating at that same unfathomable caliber!|","She left the rest of the words unsaid, but the implications were clear.","If there were bindings like this present, constructed with such overwhelming mastery, it meant either THE Creature or someone of equivalent power was here at this very moment.","Or had been here recently enough that their work remained active.","But why would they bind this particular Ginnu?","What purpose could such an action serve?","Tor’s expression became heavy with determination as he made his decision.","\" Let us find out what has occurred here.\"","In the next moment, decillions of obsidian jaws manifested around him as he began to actively devour the bindings wrapping around the fisherman.","His Way of Hunger expressed itself with full force, attempting to consume the unique weavings of a language through sheer hunger!","HUUUM!","An eruption of tremendous power crashed against Tor as he was knocked backward heavily.","A deep gash opened across his mouth, blood seeping from the wound.","But he did not relent, continuing to hunger for and devour whatever power was binding this region.","His jaws multiplied exponentially, attacking the bindings from countless angles simultaneously.","His eyes shone brighter and brighter with knowledge as he did so!","\" The...First Tongue!\"","...!","As he systematically dismantled the linguistic prison, he and THE Living Origin began to see the true state of Ains beneath the concealing authority.","The blood running down his face became visible.","The complete absence of Civilizational Authority within him became apparent.","The utter devastation of his existence revealed itself.","And finally, they could hear his words, repeated over and over in desperate loop.","\"Warn Ul’moreth. Warn the Anomaly. Warn Ul’moreth. Warn the Anomaly...\"","...!","Tor and THE Living Origin’s faces both went pale with shock.","Anomaly?","It had to be him!","He was here, inside this settlement.","But an entity of the caliber of THE Creature had actually arrived here before them and done this to a guardian of the settlement.","What did this mean for what was occurring inside?!"]},{"number":4621,"title":"Chapter 4621: Chapter 4620: Hello! I","paragraphs":["Inside The Primordial Genesis Shore, as the festival continued with building fervor, another glorious battle reached its conclusion.","The Ginnu Lifeforms cheered with tremendous enthusiasm, watching yet another THE Surface Depth entity disappear under the relentless might of The Scale Breaker.","In the arena, Noah stood calmly with his Goad still gripped in one hand.","He was about to raise his fist to call out for another opponent when Ul’moreth’s voice arrived directly in his ears.","| Haha, take a brief breather and come out of the arena for a moment. There is someone I want you to meet.|","Someone Ul’moreth wanted him to meet?","Noah raised his brows at this unexpected development as he gave a light nod of acknowledgment.","He had been fighting nonstop with singular focus to imprison as many THE entities as he possibly could in rapid succession.","Because frankly, he did not feel comfortable at this moment.","Whenever things went unfathomably well for him without interruption, he instinctively waited for the other shoe to drop.","Things had gone ridiculously well for far too long as he constantly expected Existence to come crashing down catastrophically in the next second.","He was currently operating in full caution mode, with the intricate workings of The First Tongue burning continuously across his existence in defensive configurations.","And he had even held back from observing the accumulating prompts.","But at this moment, with a brief pause granted, he called forth the full collection of notifications.","|THE Infinite Desmoterion - Comprehensive Status Update|","|Total Prisoners Contained: 15|","|Prisoner 1: Ozymandias (willing cooperation, perfect synchronization)|","|Prisoners 2-15: THE Surface Depth entities (various cooperation levels)|","|Maintenance Cost: 150 Rudimentary Units of Everything per 24 hours|","|Prisoner diversity creating exponential synergistic effects|","|Time Elapsed Within Desmoterion: More than 1,283 days |","|All prisoners have been cultivating continuously under maximum temporal dilation|","|Collective advancement creating compound acceleration effects|","| THE Organ of Civilization - Exponential Development|","|Current Development: 38.00% to 59.00%|","|Major advancement triggered by reaching 15 total prisoners|","|Critical Threshold Crossed: Development acceleration has entered exponential phase|","|Maximum Prisoner Capacity: 45 to 63 entities|","| Temporal Dilation: 21,000x to 27,000x faster than external reality|","|THE Foundation of The First Tongue - Mastery Approaching Perfect Speaker|","|Mastery Classification: Fluent Speaker (Peak) - approaching Perfect Speaker threshold|","| THE Civilizational Authority Resistance: 62% to 81%|","|Logos Formation: Can now construct 12+ Phoneme Logos with zero error risk|","|Inscription Speed: Increased by 940% from baseline|","|Way Integration - Multiple Paths Consolidated|","|The Way of Heavenly Lightning: 67% to 89% integration|","|The Way of Fulmination: 41% integration achieved|","|The Way of Nature: 23% integration initiated|","|Ten Additional Ways: Various integration levels (8%-67%)|","|Your Way of Mana and Hunger are expanding to encompass aspects of all imprisoned Ways|","|Genesis Principle Analysis - Critical Milestone Approaching|","|Total Genesis Principles Observed: 14 distinct variations|","|Structural Analysis: 97% complete|","|Understanding of structure of Genesis-tier authority construction: Exceptional|","|After approximately 15 minutes of external time, enough Weavings of Genesis Principles will have been collected and analyzed to allow for the systematic alteration and elevation of current Principles to Genesis Principle classification|","|Unquantifiable Harvest - Compound Accumulation|","|Resource generation from 15 THE prisoners has exceeded all projection parameters|","|Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect creating multiplication effects that defy calculation|","|All fundamental aspects of your existence growing exponentially|","|Bloodline Formation - Accelerated Crystallization|","|Lineage Emergence: 47% to 98% complete|","|The Distinction of The Early Creature, Osmont continues systematic dissolution|","|New fundamental identity crystallizing rapidly around linguistic supremacy|","|Estimated Completion: Soon? Soon.|","...!","The prompts were glorious.","THE Foundation of The First Tongue, THE Organ of Civilization, His budding Lineage...as there was even the fact that after 15 minutes, he would be able to effectively modify his Principles into more complex Logos.","Just 15 Minutes.","After the prompts finished rolling down with their extraordinary implications, Noah kept his eyes closed to observe THE Infinite Desmoterion directly.","His consciousness descended into that vast internal space.","The scene that greeted him was one of tremendous organized activity.","The sky pulsed with intensified blue-gold radiance, the color deeper and richer than before.","The ground formed from crystallized Hunger had expanded dramatically, now covering what felt like continental scale.","Throughout this vast space, fifteen distinct regions had formed, each one containing a prisoner.","Ozymandias occupied the central and largest region, his form radiating authority as he continued perfecting The First Tongue with methodical precision.","Around him in a circular arrangement, fourteen THE entities each occupied their own designated cultivation zones.","Some remained resistant, their forms wrapped in additional layers of Logos to ensure containment.","But most had entered states of focused cultivation, either through genuine cooperation or simple acceptance of their situation.","Raijin Katsuro sat in meditation with disciplined posture, lightning crackling around him in controlled patterns as he refined his Way with obsessive dedication.","Astrape occupied another zone, still radiating defiance but unable to express it meaningfully through the containment.","The entity with the Way of Nature had transformed their entire region into a miniature forest ecosystem, using their imprisonment as opportunity to deepen understanding of growth and cycles.","Others exhibited similar adaptations, each prisoner finding ways to advance despite or perhaps because of their confinement.","And overseeing all of this with absolute authority, Ozymandias moved between regions offering guidance, corrections, and occasionally additional suppression when resistance flared.","The atmosphere felt like an academy of existential cultivation, with the most reluctant students gradually becoming the most dedicated once they accepted their circumstances.","Noah observed the flow and workings of this space with deep satisfaction.","Everything operated with beautiful efficiency.","His Way advanced with every moment that passed within this accelerated time.","He smiled with genuine appreciation for what he had built.","Then he took a single step and appeared outside the arena, back in the festival space.","Who exactly did Ul’moreth want him to meet?","Outside the arena, the festival had reached its precipice and seemed to be slowly wrapping up as Noah made his way toward Ul’moreth.","Everywhere he passed, the Ginnu Lifeforms cheered him on with genuine enthusiasm.","Some reached out to hit his body jovially in celebration, their hands thumping against his shoulders and back with friendly force.","He simply nodded back at them with quiet acknowledgment, appreciating their genuine warmth while maintaining his focus.","When he arrived before Ul’moreth, he saw that his teacher was not alone."]},{"number":4622,"title":"Chapter 4622: Chapter 4621: Hello! II","paragraphs":["The figure of another powerful Ginnu Lifeform stood beside him.","A being that Noah immediately noted carried a heavy sense of oppression similar to Ul’moreth’s presence.","If not slightly denser and more profound.","This being looked toward him with calm observation, purple eyes studying him with interest that felt both curious and calculating.","Ul’moreth waved his hand to form an isolated domain of obsidian-gold light around the three of them.","As if he didn’t want what he was about to discuss to be overheard by everyone at the festival.","He looked toward Noah and nodded with visible appreciation as he spoke with building enthusiasm.","|It seems THE Surface Depth classification is not far from your grasp at this rate of advancement. I was just telling this old friend here that I have come to a profound decision after watching your performances. To give you my complete support and backing, and to lobby actively on your behalf to others like me across Ginnungagap.|","His voice carried weight of genuine conviction.","|If multiple entities of our caliber throw our full weight behind you, if we combine our resources and authority to support your advancement, then with what you already represent and your mastery of The First Tongue, what would possibly stop you from wielding the same level of power as THE Creature or any of The Others who stand at the apex?|","Ul’moreth’s words were tremendously heavy.","Noah’s eyes shone brightly at the implications.","The full support of multiple THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities?","Such a terrifying boost seemed almost too good to be true.","He had been wondering how much longer he would even be able to remain in Ginnungagap.","His timeline was to attain THE classification in the next few hours at the exponential rate that things were currently progressing.","And after grasping that level of power, he could move with genuine confidence to explore THE Vaults of Ginnungagap and claim whatever treasures they held before making his way back to his current time.","If he also had the backing and support of beings like Ul’moreth, entities who stood at the very peak of what Existence produced...","His eyes flashed as his paranoia returned with full overwhelming bloom.","That would mean things continuing to go ridiculously smooth without interruption.","The sense of profound unease in his existence grew even stronger as he looked around cautiously.","He raised his head upward as if literally expecting the fabric of Existence to shatter in the next moment and bring catastrophe crashing down.","When he did this, Ul’moreth smiled wryly at his student’s excessive caution.","Beside him, the one he had introduced as a friend looked at Noah with growing amusement and spoke with a voice of genuine curiosity.","|After being told of such grand possibilities and offered tremendous support, why is the very first thing you do looking upward with such extreme caution? Most would be celebrating.|","Noah brought his eyes down to focus on this being and Ul’moreth before he replied with calm seriousness.","|Fortune and disaster come hand in hand throughout Existence. There has been so much concentrated fortune falling upon me that my intuition is screaming warnings about potential disaster arriving to balance the scales.|","At these words, Ul’moreth laughed jovially as he clapped Noah on the shoulder.","|Being careful and cautious is genuinely good practice! But this entity here is Mammon, an old friend of mine. As long as you have him as another backer alongside a few others with our Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty supporting you directly, entities like THE Creature will not be a genuine danger to you in the future!|","After Ul’moreth made this introduction, the being known as Mammon stepped forward with a warm smile.","He raised his hand casually toward Noah in offer of a handshake.","His voice carried friendly warmth as he spoke.","|I go by many names across different eras and regions. Ains knows me by one particular name, Ul’moreth knows me by another. Mammon is a longtime name of mine that I’ve grown quite fond of...|","As he said this, Noah looked at this being with close attention.","Toward the outstretched hand, he returned the handshake as their two hands made contact.","While this physical connection occurred, Noah also activated his Lens of Civilization to examine whether this being was veiled like Ains had been or freely displaying their true capabilities.","A status sheet materialized before his vision.","|Analysis Report|","|Name: Mammon (?)|","|Classification: ???|","|Depth of Absolute Sovereignty: ???|","|Way of Existence: ???|","|Civilizational Authority: ???|","|True Nature: ???|","|Additional Title freely left unveiled: The Eldest of The Oldest Paradox of Existence|","Noah blinked as his eyes became razor sharp.","His mind buzzed with accelerating thoughts as his heart beat faster, and THE Organ of Civilization began to howl!","The Eldest of The Oldest Paradox of Existence?","The Oldest Paradox of Existence referred to the fundamental question of what came first in the origin of reality.","The chicken or the egg. Existence or The First Tongue.","Which preceded which, and how could either exist without the other already being present?","The paradoxical nature of this question gave Paradox itself tremendous power as a concept.","If someone was deemed The Eldest of The Oldest Paradox of Existence, that would mean...","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with unfathomable somberness and building intensity!","His entire existence howled with alarm as realizations struck at Planck Speed.","The Logos branded across his body began lighting up with defensive brilliance.","In front of him, the one whose hand he was shaking smiled brilliantly as he continued speaking with voice carrying building revelation.","His words carried imposing and terrifying weight as the truth emerged.","|I go by many names, yes. So many names accumulated across eons. Mammon works perfectly well for casual interactions. THE Arbitrium serves for certain purposes. But the name I personally like the most, the one that represents what I truly am...|","He paused for perfect dramatic effect.","|...is Chaos.|","HUUM!","Everything seemed to shift into slow motion as reality itself struggled to process what was occurring.","Noah’s expression transformed to heavy somberness as his entire existence buzzed with alarm.","Every instinct screamed danger at maximum intensity.","Mammon’s face held a brilliant, devilish smile as if everything unfolding was profoundly amusing to him.","As if this entire situation brought him tremendous entertainment.","He finished his words with that devilish smile spreading even wider.","|Chaos. THE Primordial Chaos. Hello there, Anomaly. It is so, so very nice to finally meet you properly.|","BOOM!","The words held such tremendous weight that it felt like all of surrounding Existence had literally shattered.","In this glorious scene where everything continued moving in impossible slow motion, Ul’moreth’s expression transformed through multiple stages in rapid succession.","From confusion, to shock as he processed the words being spoken, to explosive lividity as realization struck, to absolute horror as the full implications crashed through his mind.","And Noah could only gaze back with eyes blazing with brilliant, utterly defiant Quintessence.","His hand was held tightly in the grip of an unfathomable entity.","One of The Others who stood at the absolute apex of all Existence.","THE Primordial Chaos himself.","Oh.","Oh!","OH!!!","The other shoe had dropped. And it was a fucking heavy of drop!"]},{"number":4623,"title":"Chapter 4623: Chapter 4622: End of The Line I","paragraphs":["In Existence, more often than not, entities believed themselves to be infallible.","They accumulated power and authority and began thinking they would live forever, that nothing could truly threaten what they had built.","Many did not understand the fragility of their own mortality until the moment it was stripped away.","They moved through reality with confidence that bordered on arrogance, certain that their preparations were sufficient and their foundations unshakeable.","Then there were others who understood their own mortality with painful clarity.","Who recognized that things could and did always go wrong, regardless of how careful one was.","These entities prepared for all eventualities and considered all possibilities with paranoid thoroughness.","They did everything they absolutely could and remained as cautious as possible at every moment.","But sometimes, even after such exhaustive preparation, even after accounting for every variable and planning for every contingency, even after being as careful as an entity could possibly be...","Sometimes things just happened anyway.","Shit happened.","That was Existence, and Existence simply was.","No amount of preparation could fully protect against the truly unexpected.","---","Before Noah, shit had truly happened in the most catastrophic way possible.","He gazed into the eyes of this terrifying being holding his hand as nearby, Ul’moreth’s body began trembling violently.","THE Primeval Titan’s hair rose up with explosive power as shockingly, his authority seemed to be surging even within THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty and climbing higher.","His hidden eyes held a devastating mixture of lividity, shock, and profound feelings of betrayal all compressed into a single moment.","But before anything could be done by him, before he could act on the rage and horror flooding through his existence, Noah faced the entity before him.","And uniquely, he didn’t feel any fear.","Even though this was arguably the single most dangerous moment in his entire existence across all his life, he remained utterly calm.","His existence lost all other thoughts except singular focus on survival .","His eyes turned immensely cold and crystalline calm as he looked directly at this being and spoke with a voice carrying absolute conviction.","|You are unfathomably faster and stronger than me in every measurable way. But you are not faster than my own thoughts. You are not faster than my own tongue. You are not faster than The First Tongue itself when spoken from within my existence.|","His words carried building intensity.","|Should you move to do anything hostile to me in the next moment, my thoughts will move instantly. The First Tongue will move. And with it, I will initiate something irreversible that will doom all of Existence to collapse. Not just you or me, but everything.|","BOOM!","His words emerged without any trace of fear! He made a bold claim that he could initiate the doom of all of Existence!","His eyes shone with the brilliance of pure Quintessence, with tyranny and absolute defiance even when facing this apex entity.","This being who continued holding his hand in what was unquestionably the longest and most dangerous handshake in all of Existence.","And toward Noah’s bold declaration, this entity actually had his purple eyes shine with tremendous brilliance.","He smiled with what seemed like genuine delight as he responded.","| Why would I do anything bad to you? I came here purely because I was curious. And my friend Ul’moreth, pipe down and do not ruin my curiosity with your explosive temper. I’ve already grabbed hold of his existence, and I could do...many things.|","His smile widened.","| Even though you do not truly know me personally, you should understand at least a glimpse of my power from reputation alone. So why don’t we all just relax and have a pleasant conversation? Haha...|","Ul’moreth’s body continued showing surging Weavings of Existence and overwhelming emotion.","His entire form trembled with contained power that wanted desperately to erupt.","But at this moment, he remained frozen in place, unable to move despite his tremendous authority.","Held perfectly still by power that transcended what even he could resist.","The eyes of THE Primordial Chaos shone with unfathomable depth and concentrated power.","Within those purple depths, endless Weavings of pure Chaos churned and shifted in patterns that defied comprehension.","Before Noah’s vision, terrifying and ominous prompts materialized.","|CRITICAL EXISTENTIAL CHALLENGE|","|Your Way of Existence and all aspects of your being have come across an unstoppable force of Existence itself|","|Your Way is being fundamentally tested at its deepest level|","|At this moment, the entirety of your existence and your Way is being challenged by The Oldest Paradox of Existence itself|","|","|Question Posed:|","|Before THE Primordial Chaos, what are you?|","|This question demands answer not through words but through the fundamental structure of your existence|","| Failure to maintain coherent answer will result in existential dissolution|","WAA!","What was he?","Before THE Primordial Chaos , what was Existence itself, and what was The First Tongue?","Which came first, and how could either exist without the other?","The sensation Noah felt in this moment was utterly indescribable.","He felt every single atom and cell of his existence working in absolute overdrive.","As if every single component part of what made him real was being questioned again and again in rapid succession.","Before THE Primordial Chaos, what was he?!","What defined his existence when confronted with the living embodiment of paradox?","The questions boomed through his mind with crushing weight as the entity in front of him continued smiling pleasantly during all of this existential pressure.","THE Primordial Chaos spoke with voice carrying both amusement and genuine fascination.","| What an enigma you are, truly. You do not belong here in Ginnungagap and yet you absolutely do. You should not be here by any logical progression and yet you undeniably are. You are weak by classification and yet you are also profoundly strong in application. You have so many paradoxes surrounding your entire existence that I would have genuinely thought you were THE Living Paradox in a different form if I didn’t know better.|","He paused before continuing with building interest.","| But no matter. I am not here for anything too crazy or destructive. I am here simply to ask a few specific people to make choices. I asked Ains to make a choice a little bit earlier at the edge of this settlement, and he made it decisively. What a selfless individual he was, choosing sacrifice over safety.|","His purple eyes gleamed.","|I will now ask you what choice you will make when presented with options. Nothing wild and nothing unreasonable. You spoke of me potentially doing something hostile or even expecting destruction from my presence, but I find such direct violence tedious and profoundly boring most of the time.|","His smile took on deeper significance.","|I find Existence to be vastly more interesting when everything is based on choices made freely. On the glorious Primordial Chaos that blooms naturally as a result of endless choices intersecting and creating unpredictable outcomes. Force is simple. Choice is beautiful.|","The words hung in the air with tremendous weight.","What choice would THE Primordial Chaos demand from him?"]},{"number":4624,"title":"Chapter 4624: Chapter 4623: End of The Line II","paragraphs":["What choice would THE Primordial Chaos demand from Noah?","As his very existence remained under constant crushing pressure, as he continued facing the immensity of the fundamental question of who he was before Primordial Chaos, this entity continued speaking as if it did not even matter what Noah was experiencing right now.","Even though no one could know with complete certainty whether this entity understood exactly what Noah’s existence was currently facing.","And at such a critical point, he was also posing something else entirely.","Noah did not have to look around to perceive that at this moment, there was an immense silence spreading throughout the entire region.","Every single Ginnu Lifeform had formed a circle of profound silence and somberness as each one now felt the oppressive aura of THE Primordial Chaos radiating outward.","His presence spread like a suffocating blanket across all of reality.","To experience the aura of an entity on the same unfathomable level as THE Creature was to feel utterly crushed.","It felt as if all of Existence was constantly pressing down on top of you from every direction simultaneously, compressing your very being into an infinitely small point.","At this moment, every single entity that did not possess any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty seemed like they were struggling desperately for their lives.","Their consciousness threatened to simply turn off and be forcibly put to sleep in the next instant, overwhelmed by pressure too great to endure.","And yet the Ginnu Lifeforms stood.","They were somber and they felt the despotic weight crushing them.","But they still floated all around Ul’moreth in a protective circle.","As if regardless of what happened here, regardless of what this apex entity demanded, they would stand with their leader and their fellow Ginnu Lifeforms until the end.","THE Primordial Chaos continued as if none of this solidarity was of any consequence to him.","His eyes remained fixed solely on Noah with unwavering focus.","|I don’t like to ramble unnecessarily, so I will present you with the choice directly and simply. Ul’moreth here took you into Ginnungagap when you needed refuge. He saved you from whatever you were fleeing. He seemingly taught you The First Tongue with tremendous generosity. He brought you into his home, his settlement filled with his people.|","His voice carried casual authority.","|There are many Ginnu Lifeforms gathered here. Before you came, they were living perfectly fine lives in relative peace. And if you had not come here, it would have continued to be this way. But now that you’re here...|","He paused for perfect effect.","|I will tell you plainly that every single life on this Primordial Genesis Shore will perish, including Ul’moreth himself, unless you make a choice. A simple choice to declare with conviction that before Primordial Chaos existed, The First Tongue was nothing. That Existence itself, The First Tongue, that Mana, that all of it rose directly from Primordial Chaos as the true origin.|","His smile remained pleasant.","|Just say those simple words with genuine conviction, and all those gathered here will be saved. Refuse, and they all die. Simple.|","The words were devastatingly heavy and terrifying.","Noah kept his gaze utterly calm upon this being even as all of his existence continued vibrating with immense pressure.","The effort he was exerting to maintain coherence was monumentally heavy and vibrant.","Even though he couldn’t even begin to care about potential Harvest at this moment.","What Harvest could there possibly be when the next few seconds of continued existence were not even guaranteed?","And this entity had posed a question of choice that was actually identical to the existential question he was already facing.","This entity was telling him exactly how to answer the paradox.","To make the choice to abandon the immensity of Mana as fundamental origin.","To claim that before Primordial Chaos and Existence, Mana was nothing!","This was the choice THE Primordial Chaos wanted him to make in exchange for the lives of Ul’moreth and all the others gathered here.","It was absolutely ridiculous.","The pressure Noah felt became even more crushingly intense as he looked down at his hand still holding onto THE Primordial Chaos.","It felt like he was gripping something that, if it exerted even slight pressure, could begin systematically crushing every ounce of his existence into nothingness.","This was a type of feeling he never wanted to experience in his existence.","A feeling of complete helplessness.","A feeling of being utterly at the mercy of others.","Because if the disposition of THE Primordial Chaos had been even slightly different, if he did not genuinely care about choices as he presented himself right now, then whether Noah’s threat about being able to induce something irreversible in Existence if harmed was true or not would be completely meaningless.","Everything would simply be over regardless.","It would be the absolute end of the line.","This was something Noah had fought constantly for days and weeks and months to never be in a position like this.","And yet here he was anyway.","Because this was Existence.","Existence was not fair. Existence was not benevolent. Existence was not malicious.","Existence simply was.","And now he simply had to find a way forward in the face of impossible odds!","So he turned his gaze toward THE Primordial Chaos , who at this time shook his head while looking at Noah with deep understanding.","THE Primordial Chaos then turned toward Ul’moreth and all the other gathered Ginnu Lifeforms.","His voice carried casual cruelty.","| You all do not even need to wait for his answer. I already know exactly what it will be. This man here that you brought so generously into your home, that you were planning to put your full backing behind, to sell short your own Way of Existence and make it unfathomably harder for yourselves to ever advance further... this man will never sacrifice himself for any of you.|","His smile widened.","|Regardless of all you have done for him, regardless of the kindness shown, he will choose himself. Every time.|","THE Primordial Chaos turned to look directly at Noah.","His gaze carried the weight of someone looking at another that they considered to be fundamentally the same as themselves.","He continued with voice carrying absolute certainty.","| Did you think it would be different with him compared to me or THE Secretive Eon or THE Creature? I tell you now with complete confidence that he is one and the same as us. People like us have this particular complex where we somehow believe that we are above all others. Not necessarily in terms of raw power, but in a sense of fundamental entitlement.|","He paused thoughtfully.","| Even that word does not fully do it justice, but entitlement is about right. Beings like him and I live our entire existence as if our lives are somehow more existentially important than others. As if other entities can die or lose absolutely everything, and that would be more than acceptable, but not us. Never us.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4625,"title":"Chapter 4625: Chapter 4624: End of The Line III","paragraphs":["His purple eyes gleamed.","| We don’t sacrifice our foundations for others. We don’t willingly die. People can die for us, we may close our eyes afterward and solemnly swear we will avenge them... but we will never give up our Way for others’ survival. It is a type of entitlement, hubris, and fundamental arrogance that none of you can truly understand.|","He gestured toward Noah.","| But our Anomaly here understands this feeling very well, because he and I are exactly the same at our cores.|","BOOM!","The atmosphere turned incredibly heavy and profoundly silent.","Noah stared at this being with extremely cold eyes that held no warmth whatsoever.","He realized this entity was genuinely dangerous and constantly attacking even though he was not utilizing any direct existential authority.","His words alone were enough to achieve a tremendous number of terrible things.","Sowing doubt, creating division, undermining trust.","But at this time, in this immense silence where THE Primordial Chaos had been completely controlling the stage and narrative, Noah finally opened his mouth to speak.","His voice emerged with tyrannical calm and devastating concision.","| You speak of entitlement and arrogance as if they are unique to beings like us. But every entity across all of Existence believes their life matters more than others’. The difference is that some have the power to make that belief reality, and others do not. You are not special for valuing your own existence. You are simply powerful enough that no one can force you to pretend otherwise.|","His eyes blazed with cold fire.","|And you mistake conviction for arrogance. I will not abandon my Way because you demand it. Not because I believe I am entitled to survival, but because my Way is true regardless of what any entity claims.|","WAA!","Then Noah addressed the fundamental question directly.","The answer to The Oldest Paradox of Existence.","Before Primordial Chaos, what was The First Tongue? What was Mana?","His voice rang out with profound authority.","|Before Primordial Chaos, before Existence itself took recognizable form, there was not nothing. There was potential. There was the capacity for reality to manifest. And that capacity, that fundamental potential for anything to exist at all, is what Mana represents. Not as what came after, but as the inherent possibility that preceded others.|","His existence began illuminating with unfathomable waves of blue-gold brilliance.","|The First Tongue is not something that emerged from Chaos. It is the language through which potential becomes actual. The mechanism by which possibility collapses into reality. Chaos may have shaped Existence, but the capacity for Chaos itself to exist required something prior. Required the fundamental substrate of possibility.|","The light intensified dramatically.","|So before Primordial Chaos, before Existence, before even the concept of ’before’ held meaning, there was Mana. There was The First Tongue as the Infinite Potential for anything to be real. The First Tongue is how that potential expresses itself into manifestation. Neither created Chaos. Both simply are, making Chaos possible rather than being products of it.|","His words carried absolute conviction.","|This is my answer. This is my Way. And I will not abandon it regardless of consequence.|","BOOM!","Glorious prompts descended before his vision as his entire being blazed with triumphant radiance.","|Existential Challenge - Resolution|","|Your answer to The Oldest Paradox of Existence has been evaluated|","| Verdict: Adequate|","|Note: Your answer is not perfect or complete, but it is coherent and defensible|","|You have successfully defended your position and standing regarding The Way of Mana, The Way of The First Tongue|","|Your existence has proven resilient enough to maintain identity even when questioned by THE Primordial Chaos itself|","|Critical Threshold Achieved|","|Your existence has built sufficient foundation to step into THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of The First Tongue in the near future|","|All prerequisites have been met through this existential trial|","|Lineage Formation - Final Component Obtained|","|The last ingredient for your emerging Lineage has been secured through this confrontation|","|Bloodline Crystallization: 100% Complete|","|Your new fundamental identity is ready to manifest|","| The Distinction of The Early Creature, Osmont has been completely dissolved|","|New Lineage: Pending Emergence|","...!","Such extraordinary prompts descended before Noah’s eyes.","At this moment, as his gaze shone with unfathomable luminosity, he stared directly into the eyes of THE Primordial Chaos.","Who was actually smiling brilliantly at this moment with what seemed like genuine satisfaction.","As if everything had unfolded exactly as he hoped.","And this entire time, through everything that had occurred, this terrifying entity had never once released Noah’s hand from his grip.","As THE Primordial Chaos continued gazing at Noah after he finished answering The Oldest Paradox of Existence, in the span of less than an instant, Noah’s thoughts moved rapidly faster than even Planck Speed itself.","His existence buzzed with unprecedented intensity as he felt something unfathomable emerging as a direct result of his declaration.","He felt his lineage crystallizing into reality!","Within his heart, something fundamental shifted.","The organ that had been The Heart of The Early Creature, Osmont began transforming with devastating finality.","But this was not destruction. This was metamorphosis.","His heart, which had served as the foundation for so much of his power across countless Weavings, was being reforged entirely.","The Distinction of The Early Creature dissolved completely, the identity that had defined him for so long finally being replaced by something that belonged wholly to his current path.","In its place, something new began to manifest.","A heart that pulsed with blue-gold radiance so intense it seemed to contain compressed Infinity.","A heart that beat with rhythm that spoke The First Tongue with every contraction.","A heart that embodied the answer he had given to THE Primordial Chaos.","Prompts descended with overwhelming significance.","|Lineage Emergence Underway|","|Your new fundamental Lineage has manifested in response to your declaration against The Oldest Paradox of Existence|","|Lineage Name: THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, THE Potentate|","|The emerging lineage disdains any Distinction less than THE as it has given itself capital T, H, E|","HUUM!"]},{"number":4626,"title":"Chapter 4626: Chapter 4625: End of The Line IV","paragraphs":["The name reverberated through his existence again and again as a glorious symphony surged within his being.","And all of this was happening in a fraction of an instant as he processed these prompts and underwent these changes in that impossible span of time.","But as of this moment, he was no longer The Early Creature.","Every cell within him began to scream with new identity.","THE! Genesis! Monarch! Of! Infinite! Lexicons!","THE Potentate!","It burned within his Weavings of Existence gloriously, branding itself onto every component of what he was.","|Classification: Unique Primordial Lineage tied to The First Tongue|","|Origin: Born from the conviction that Mana represents infinite potential and The First Tongue is the mechanism of manifestation|","|Heart Transformation - New Distinction Acquired|","|Your heart has been completely reforged and elevated|","|Former Identity: The Heart of The Early Creature, Osmont (dissolved)|","|New Identity: THE Heart of Infinite Lexicons |","|Distinction Gained: THE Potentate|","| Effect: Your heart now generates a unique form of blood that carries both Mana and Fragments of Phonemes of The First Tongue in every drop|","THUMP! THUMP! THUMP!","His heart beat like an ancient drum awakening from primordial slumber.","It had woken with power when he first attained the status of an Early Creature, yes.","But the way it beat right now was entirely different.","It was akin to the beating of drums from the earliest times of Existence.","From times when Mana ran wild and untamed across reality.","From times when The First Tongue was freshly spoken and everything was still being named.","He felt as if each beat echoed outward not just through space but through time itself.","The rhythm flowing backward through Ginnungagap where he currently traversed.","Flowing forward through eons to that distant blue planet where he would eventually be born.","It was indescribably glorious, this sensation of his heart connecting past and future through pure potential.","| THE Heart of Infinite Lexicons begins pumping Glorious Genesis Blood of Potential throughout your existence|","|This blood carries the fundamental nature of your Lineage to every aspect of your being|","|Transformation Status: In Progress|","Noah’s entire existence began to shine with unfathomable blue-gold brilliance as the new blood pumped outward from his transformed heart.","It spread through every vein, every cell, every atom of his being.","Where it flowed, transformation followed.","His body began restructuring itself at the most fundamental level, integrating the new Lineage into every component of his existence.","Additional prompts bloomed with extraordinary detail.","| THE Heart of Infinite Lexicons - Core Properties|","|Primary Function: Generates Glorious Genesis Blood of Potential that enhances all aspects of existence|","|Secondary Function: Serves as anchor point for The First Tongue within your being|","|Tertiary Function: Allows instant conversion between Mana and Phonemes of The First Tongue|","|Quaternary Function: Grants instinctive understanding of how Potential becomes actual|","|Lineage Capabilities - Foundational Features|","| Feature One: Lexical Genesis|","| Your Lineage grants the profound capability to create new Phonemes of The First Tongue|","|Maximum New Phonemes: Nine (9) unique creations|","|Requirements: Deep understanding of the concept, sufficient Civilizational Authority, and conviction in the Phoneme’s necessity|","|Potential Phonemes Identified Based on Your Way:|","|- Phoneme of Quintessence|","|- Phoneme of Infinity|","|- Phoneme of Tyranny|","|- Phoneme of Fortune (Loot)|","|- Phoneme of Advantage (Cheats)|","|- Phoneme of Narrative (Protagonist)|","|- Phoneme of Harvest|","|- Phoneme of Hunger|","|- Phoneme of Potential|","|Note: These Phonemes will be recognized as valid by The First Tongue itself if and when created|","|Warning: Creating new Phonemes is an act of tremendous significance and will allow those proficient in The First Tongue across Observable Existence to sense a change|","BOOM !","A ridiculous capability bloomed within his awareness at this moment.","Mind you, all of this was happening as Noah still held the hand of THE Primordial Chaos .","But it remained contained within that fraction of an instant as his thoughts moved faster than Planck Speed itself.","It was because he was rapidly processing all the emerging Weavings of his power and lineage.","To ensure he had potential solutions against an entity so overwhelmingly superior that he could be crushed in a moment.","His emerging lineage was one possible answer.","The attainment of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty was another.","But all of it remained Potential until actualized.","And as THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, his mind buzzed with comprehension of Infinite Potential itself.","Even this moment right here, these Weavings of Existence playing out right now, they were filled with potential that could be actualized into something grand.","He simply had to determine how to do it.","The first glorious possibility when it came to this infinite potential was the capability to forge his own Phonemes.","It was grand and unfathomable.","There were only eighteen core Phonemes in all of Existence, each with their own countless variations.","And yet he would get to create his own?!","The prompts continued descending in that fraction of an instant.","| Feature Two: Resonance of The First Tongue|","|Your Lineage shares profound connection with all aspects of The First Tongue|","|Effect: Learning new Phonemes is 900% faster|","|Effect: Forming Logos requires 70% less concentration|","|Effect: Inscription speed increased by 1,200%|","|Effect: Error rate when working with The First Tongue reduced to effective zero|","|Effect: Can sense when others speak The First Tongue within vast distances|","|Effect: Instinctively understand the grammatical structure of any Logos encountered|","| Feature Three: Mana Supremacy|","|Your Lineage declares Mana as fundamental origin and Infinite Potential|","|Effect: All Mana-based abilities enhanced by 500% for your entire Civilization|","| Effect: Mana regeneration is functionally infinite for the strongest in your Civilization - granting them Infinite Potential. When you attain THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger, this capability will be fully actualized|","|Effect: Can convert any form of energy or authority into Mana with 89% efficiency|","|Effect: Your Mana naturally influences and gradually converts other forms of power|","|Effect: Resistance to non-Mana authorities increased by 340%|","BOOM!","A terrifying set of capabilities bloomed as they detailed the usage and exertion of infinite potential.","For those in his Civilization to essentially have Infinite Mana regeneration.","Infinite Mana!"]},{"number":4627,"title":"Chapter 4627: Chapter 4626: Collapse I","paragraphs":["This was potential. This was Infinite Potential filled with a terrifying assortment of possibilities!","Even though to fully apply it, he would need to elevate his Civilization to the next level.","|Feature Four: Advancement Through Linguistic Mastery|","|Your Lineage directly aids progression through Depths of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Mechanism: Each new level of mastery in The First Tongue accelerates Civilizational development|","|Current Boost: Approaching Perfect Speaker provides 670% acceleration to reaching THE Surface Depth|","|Projection: Achieving Perfect Speaker may grant automatic elevation to THE Surface Depth|","|Long-term: Mastery beyond Perfect Speaker will continue providing exponential advancement benefits|","|Feature Five: Propagation of Lesser Lineage|","| Your Lineage can be shared in diminished form with those who follow your Way|","|Classification: Lesser Distinction of THE Potentate|","|Bestowal Method: Requires willing acceptance and genuine alignment with your Way|","|Limitation: Can only be granted to entities who have sworn themselves to your path|","|Lesser Distinction Benefits:|","|- 200,000% increase to Mana capacity and regeneration|","|- 15,000% increase to learning speed for any Mana-based abilities|","|- Instinctive resistance to authority suppression (30% reduction)|","|- Enhanced Quintessence stability|","|- Accelerated advancement through lower classifications|","|- Passive regeneration enhancement|","|Feature Six: Greater Distinction for Entangled Weavings|","|Those with deepest connections to you can receive enhanced Lineage benefits|","|Classification: Greater Distinction of THE Potentate|","|Eligibility: Family members, closest companions, entities with profound existential entanglement|","|Examples: Barbatos, Adelaide, The Infiniverse, Khor, Henry, Moiraine, Riya, and others with deep bonds|","|Greater Distinction Benefits:|","|- All Lesser Distinction benefits amplified to 5,000,000%|","|- Granted potential to comprehend and utilize The First Tongue directly|","|- Deep connection to Mana allows instinctive understanding of its nature|","|- Can draw upon your authority in moments of extreme need (limited)|","|- Advancement speed increased by 800% when cultivating near you|","|Feature Seven: Atlas Integration - Foundation Transformation|","|Your previous Atlas has been elevated and integrated into THE Foundation of The First Tongue|","Oh?","What was this now?","| The Nine Mundis of Power have been transformed into Lexical Pillars within The Early Atlas of the Folds|","|New Classification: The Nine Pillars of Infinite Expression|","|Transformation Details:|","| First Pillar: Conceptual Lexicon (formerly Conceptual System)|","|- Allows formation of Logos that embody pure concepts|","|- Grants ability to speak reality into existence through conceptual authority|","| Second Pillar: Outerversal Lexicon (formerly Outerversal Descent)|","|- Enables Logos construction that transcends conventional dimensional limitations|","|- Grants Transcendent linguistic abilities|","| Third Pillar: Ingenious Lexicon (formerly Ingeniare)|","|- Focuses on creative and innovative Logos construction|","|- Allows rapid prototyping of new linguistic structures|","|Fourth Pillar: Kuklos Lexicon (formerly Kuklos)|","|- Specializes in Logos involving cycles, repetition, and Infinite existential return|","|- Grants increased mastery over temporal and cyclical linguistic patterns|","| Fifth Pillar: Megalos Lexicon (formerly Megalos System)|","|- Enables construction of Logos of tremendous scale and scope|","|- Grants ability to speak words that affect Existence across vast distances|","| Sixth Pillar: Singed Lexicon (formerly Singed System)|","|- Allows formation of Logos combining The First Tongue with primordial flame|","|- Grants increased ability to inscribe with fire that cannot be extinguished|","| Seventh Pillar: Paradoxical Lexicon (formerly Ordo Ab Chao)|","|- Specializes in Logos that embody paradox and contradiction with increased Infinite Potential|","|- Allows speaking truths that should be impossible|","| Eighth Pillar: Eldritch Lexicon (formerly Eldritch Expanse)|","|- Enables Logos construction using incomprehensible or maddening concepts|","|- Grants ability to speak words that defy conventional understanding|","| Ninth Pillar: Veridical Lexicon (formerly Veritarch)|","|- Focuses on Logos of absolute truth and certainty|","|- Allows speaking words that cannot be denied or contradicted|","|Pillar Synergy Effect:|","|All Nine Pillars work in concert to support your mastery of The First Tongue|","|Each Pillar provides specialized linguistic capabilities|","|Combined, they create foundation strong enough to support Perfect Speaker classification and beyond|","|The Pillars actively accelerate your progression toward THE classification|","Noah felt nine distinct points of singularity rotating within THE Heart of Infinite Lexicons.","Each one formed a core component of his terrifying Foundation.","From his Atlas they had emerged, and now they aided in expanding and elevating the infinite potential he held over The First Tongue.","In what he could now say and do with linguistic authority.","It deserved tremendous further exploration.","|Feature Eight: Potential Manifestation|","|Your Lineage embodies the principle that potential precedes actuality|","|Effect: Can temporarily manifest potential futures as if they were real|","|Duration: Variable based on complexity|","|Limitation: Cannot manifest impossibilities, only unrealized possibilities|","|Application: Can briefly wield abilities you could potentially develop in the future|","Oh.","Everything stopped.","Noah felt like all of Existence paused.","Potential Manifestation.","Could this be an answer? Could this be what he was searching for to escape the current impossible situation?","His mind raced through possibilities at speeds that transcended comprehension.","If he could manifest potential futures, then theoretically he could manifest a future where he had already achieved THE Surface Depth.","Manifest a future where he possessed power sufficient to stand against THE Primordial Chaos.","Manifest a future where he had already escaped and was safe.","The limitation stated he could not manifest impossibilities, only unrealized possibilities.","But was a future where he survived this encounter impossible?","No. It was merely improbable. Unrealized. But not impossible.","The issue was his current power level.","The potential he wanted to manifest might be deemed impossible by the mechanism simply because the gap between his current state and that desired future was too vast.","If he tried to manifest himself as a THE Fundamental Depth entity, the power requirement would likely collapse the manifestation instantly.","But what if he was more strategic?","What if he manifested not overwhelming power, but the perfect timing?","The perfect moment of distraction?","The perfect confluence of events that would allow escape?","What if he manifested a potential future where THE Primordial Chaos simply chose to let him go?","That future existed as a possibility, slim though it might be.","Or what if he combined Potential Manifestation with his other capabilities?","Manifested a future where he had already formed one of his nine unique Phonemes?","The Phoneme of Advantage, perhaps, which could tilt probability itself in his favor?","Or the Phoneme of Narrative, which could reshape the story being written?","His eyes pulsed with building brightness as he catalogued these possibilities for immediate or future usage.","Even if they were impossible potentials given his current limitations, they represented tools he could refine and develop."]},{"number":4628,"title":"Chapter 4628: Chapter 4627: Collapse II","paragraphs":["As he contemplated these possibilities, the remaining prompts descended.","| Feature Nine: Lexical Sovereignty|","|Your Lineage grants increasing authority over The First Tongue itself|","|Effect: Your spoken Logos carry additional weight and authority|","|Effect: Can overwrite or modify Logos spoken by others (requires sufficient power difference)|","|Effect: Can sense when your name is spoken in The First Tongue anywhere in Existence|","|Effect: Grants immunity to linguistic bindings below your classification level|","| Feature Ten: Civilizational Resonance|","|Your Lineage resonates with THE Civilizational Authority structure|","|Effect: Advancement through Depths of Sovereignty is 450% faster|","|Effect: Can sense the Depth of other entities instinctively|","|Effect: Your Civilization develops automatically as your mastery of The First Tongue increases|","|Effect: Prisoners in THE Infinite Desmoterion benefit from your Lineage’s passive influence|","The transformation continued as billowing waves of blue-gold blood flooded through Noah’s existence.","His skin began glowing from within as if he had become a living embodiment of compressed potential.","His eyes blazed with intensity that seemed to peer directly into the fabric of reality itself.","His very presence began carrying weight that made nearby space tremble.","Final prompts descended.","|Lineage Manifestation - Complete|","| THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons has fully integrated into your existence|","|All features active and operational|","|Your fundamental nature has been elevated beyond what you were|","|The Early Creature, Osmont no longer exists as a meaningful identity|","|You are now: THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, THE Potentate, The Nascent Master of The First Tongue|","|Immediate Effects:|","|- THE Foundation of The First Tongue: Reinforced to Absolute tier|","|- THE Civilizational Authority Resistance: 81% to 95%|","|- Mastery Classification: Fluent Speaker (Peak) to Threshold of Perfect Speaker|","|- Time to THE Surface Depth: Minutes. Minutes. Minutes!|","|- Bloodline Power: Increased by 3,400%|","|- Existential Weight: At THE classification despite current Pre-THE status . Could your Existential Weight exceed most THE Surface Depth entities without you attaining THE?|","Noah’s transformation reached completion as the last of the Glorious Genesis Blood of Potential finished circulating through his existence.","He stood there shining with unfathomable radiance.","Still holding hands with THE Primordial Chaos.","Who continued smiling brilliantly.","Noah’s mind raced through potential solutions as he faced this overwhelming force.","He needed unpredictability. He actually needed chaos amidst all of this.","Because only in chaos would he find opportunity to make his exit.","He had grand ideas and possibilities of exploring THE Vaults of Ginnungagap and other potential Weavings.","But with entities possessing excessively greater power than him moving about, he would have to cut his temporal traversal short.","Because of his paranoia and extreme caution, he had already made certain preparations that had not yet revealed themselves. He had left behind Sparks.","They would likely only activate after he left Ginnungagap entirely.","So at this moment, even if they represented impossible potentials, he prepared to unleash Potential Manifestation as a last resort.","But in the next instant, something unexpected occurred.","\" Stop!\"","The voice rang out with desperate authority.","At this moment, the figures of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin arrived with expressions of shock and determination.","Their gazes were stern as they took in the scene before them.","THE Primordial Chaos holding Noah’s hand.","Both surrounded by the scattered encirclement of Ginnu Lifeforms and the frozen form of Ul’moreth.","Noah’s gaze became even more somber as he sensed Tor and THE Living Origin’s arrival.","Because the entity whose hand he currently held was one who seemed to genuinely enjoy playing games of sacrifice.","Of forcing others to make impossible choices.","Something Noah absolutely detested.","And now even more people had arrived who might be forced to make such sacrifices.","As if THE Primordial Chaos could perfectly infer his thoughts, he smiled brilliantly while looking directly at Noah.","| Okay. It seems like you won’t really answer my question after all. And by not answering, that is also a choice in itself. What a shame. What a shame.|","HUUM!","The words carried ominous finality.","As THE Primordial Chaos made such an ominous statement, Tor and THE Living Origin roared out with desperate determination as they rushed forth.","Their combined authority erupted with building intensity, seeking to intervene in whatever was about to occur.","And off to the side, the figure of THE Primeval Titan, Ul’moreth , finally made his move.","He began slowly floating toward Noah and THE Primordial Chaos with deliberate purpose.","His voice emerged carrying the weight of eons and absolute conviction.","|In Existence, a teacher has a few fundamental responsibilities that cannot be shirked or delegated. The first responsibility is to impart knowledge without holding back what the student needs to know. The second responsibility is to correct errors and guide the student away from paths that lead to collapse. The third responsibility is to push the student beyond what they believe themselves capable of achieving.|","His hairy form continued advancing as obsidian-gold light began radiating from him with building power.","|The fourth responsibility is to recognize when the student has surpassed the teacher and to step aside with grace. The fifth responsibility is to never claim credit for the student’s achievements, as their success belongs to them alone. And the sixth responsibility, the one that supersedes all others...|","He paused as his entire existence began to tremble.","|...is to ensure the safety of my student at any cost. This responsibility I will complete without fail, or my Civilization will collapse and my Way will dissolve into nothing!|","The words were devastatingly heavy.","In the next moment, the power that Ul’moreth radiated shockingly spilled past THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","It headed toward an unfathomable direction beyond normal classification.","His entire existence became surrounded by scintillating obsidian-gold light as multiple Genesis Principles manifested around his form.","He was THE Aeon-Strand Keeper. THE Primeval Titan.","And at this time, he moved!","When Noah first met him and examined his status, among the details revealed was a philosophy that stated: All things flow from The First Tongue and return to it eventually.","His Way was The Way of Primordial Continuity.","The understanding that Existence moved in grand cycles, that all authority ultimately originated from and would return to The First Tongue in endless progression.","And at this moment, Noah could sense with horrifying clarity that this being was burning his very Primordial Continuity itself.","Consuming the fundamental essence of his Way to generate power beyond his normal limits.","Yet another sacrifice. Something Noah hated above almost all else.","Yet he couldn’t do anything to prevent it in the next moment.","THE Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana flashed brilliantly across Ul’moreth’s entire body.","Everything seemed to shift into slow motion as reality itself struggled to process what was occurring.","This Genesis Principle expanded outward with irresistible authority, covering everything in the immediate vicinity.","Where Noah stood clasping the hand of THE Primordial Chaos, Ul’moreth instantly manifested in his exact position as if there had been a perfect replacement.","A seamless exchange of spatial coordinates and existential positions.","And where Ul’moreth had been standing moments before, Noah now found himself!","It was the work of The Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana!"]},{"number":4629,"title":"Chapter 4629: Chapter 4628: Collapse III","paragraphs":["The Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana operated on a profound but elegantly simple concept.","It declared that at the most fundamental level, before differentiation into distinct forms and identities, all Mana was identical and interchangeable.","Before Mana became fire or water, light or darkness, creation or destruction, it existed in undifferentiated potential.","And beings themselves, at their deepest core, were expressions of that same undifferentiated potential.","Ul’moreth had leveraged this truth to perform an exchange that should have been impossible.","Even with the overwhelming power of THE Primordial Chaos, even with his hand physically clasped around what he thought was Noah, the exchange succeeded.","Because Ul’moreth had burned his Way of Primordial Continuity to temporarily exceed his normal scope of power.","And because Noah represented The First Tongue itself in living form. Represented Mana itself in its purest expression.","Undifferentiated potential made manifest.","So when Ul’moreth invoked THE Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana, declaring that he and Noah were fundamentally identical at the level of pure potential, reality accepted that declaration.","And enacted the exchange regardless of THE Primordial Chaos’s grip.","It was simultaneously the most complex and most simple maneuver imaginable.","Complex in the metaphysical understanding required to execute it.","Simple in the fundamental truth it exploited.","At the exact moment of the exchange, Noah felt an influx of tremendous authority and compressed information flow directly into his existence.","A prompt materialized before his vision.","|Emergency Transmission Received|","| THE Primeval Titan has imparted THE Farewell of Ginnungagap unto your existence|","|This represents the collective accumulated knowledge, treasures, and final gifts of a Primeval Titan|","|Content: Sealed until safe activation conditions are met|","|Warning: Opening prematurely may draw unwanted attention|","Noah felt a radiant obsidian-gold box of concentrated Weavings being pushed deep into his existence for safekeeping.","In the next moment, he heard Ul’moreth’s voice resonating directly in his mind with desperate urgency.","|Please do not let the burning of your teacher be for nothing. Go, and go now. Do not look back. Do not hesitate. Just GO!|","The glorious and terrible scene unfolded in that stretched moment.","THE Primordial Chaos stared directly into the hairy obscured eyes of THE Primeval Titan.","And he actually smiled brilliantly before beginning to laugh with genuine amusement.","As if this entire development was the most entertaining thing he had witnessed in eons.","In this moment where Existence itself seemed to move with painful slowness, Noah felt his entire being buzzing with overwhelming emotion.","His eyes locked onto Ul’moreth , taking in every detail of the being who had taught him so much.","Then his gaze shifted to the figures of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin rushing desperately forward.","And further behind them, he could see the slowly walking crippled figure of Ains, The fisherman who had sacrificed everything.","He saw all of them clearly.","He gave each one a single final look, burning their images into his memory.","Then he closed his eyes and uttered the words with absolute conviction.","| Temporal Traversal.|","He ended his time in this era, concluding his temporal traversal.","His existence burned with profound defiance at the way it was ending.","It burned with rage that another entity had to step in on his behalf and consume their very Way of Existence to give him a chance to escape.","But since it was done, since the sacrifice had been made, he would not allow it to be for nothing.","He did not tarry. He did not hesitate or second-guess.","His Early Atlas of the Folds activated at once as his figure began being funneled backward across the rivers of time.","The reality of The Primordial Genesis Shore began to fade.","THE Primordial Chaos, Ul’moreth , and all the others started becoming distant and indistinct.","And then-","| Haha, I have finally caught you! And you are even using time itself at this very moment. Just where are you returning to, friend? Do you know how much your reckless actions across time can affect Existence? Do you understand the Loops of Time?!|","BOOM!","Just as he was leaving. Just as temporal traversal was nearly complete and about to return him to his current era!","Everything became frozen in time itself.","The figures of THE Primeval Titan and THE Primordial Chaos and all others that had been fading away became actualized and very real again.","Noah turned around in shock as the endless rivers of time that had been flowing smoothly around him became violently unstable.","Behind him, he could now see a new entity.","Surrounded by brilliant purple waves of temporal authority.","Time itself seemed to bend and flow around this being’s form.","The figure appeared humanoid but with features that seemed to shift and age and regress simultaneously.","Their skin held a quality that made it impossible to determine if they were ancient or newborn.","Their eyes contained infinite depth, as if one could peer through them and see every moment that had ever existed layered upon itself.","Purple light emanated from them in cascading waves that made reality itself tremble.","They wore robes that seemed woven from compressed moments, each thread a frozen instant of time.","Noah did not have to think long before realizing with defiance that this was THE Living Temporal.","On the cusp of him leaving and returning to his current era, after THE Primeval Titan Ul’moreth had burned his very Way of Primordial Continuity to give him this chance, another entity at the same level as THE Primordial Chaos had actually arrived to stop everything!","And one could definitively say THE Living Temporal operated at the same unfathomable tier as THE Primordial Chaos.","The allure of undeniable power emanating from them far exceeded any other entity present.","It bordered on the exact same wavelength of authority as THE Primordial Chaos himself.","The situation had turned from hopeful to unfathomably worse in an instant.","This profound chaotic progression caused the distant figures of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin to pale even further.","At this moment, THE Living Origin roared with desperate fury.","\" Temporal, what are you doing?! Why are you interfering now?!\"","Her eyes carried profound lividity as her own body began erupting with a type of power she had never unveiled before.","Authority that had remained hidden throughout all their previous encounters.","And yet THE Living Temporal did not even turn toward her.","His gaze remained fixed on Noah as if observing the most fascinating specimen in all of Existence.","His voice emerged carrying terrifying weight.","|I have been searching for you across time for longer than you can comprehend. Someone jumping around back and forth through the eras, causing subtle changes here and there that ripple forward and backward as you didn’t truly change anything...but causality was tested. To have finally found you is a stupendous occasion beyond measure. Come.|","...!"]},{"number":4630,"title":"Chapter 4630: Chapter 4629: Collapse IV","paragraphs":["THE Living Temporal extended his hand with casual authority, as if Noah’s capture was already inevitable.","Noah’s eyes burned with absolute lividity and defiance.","His entire existence began shining with endless waves of blue-gold light.","What was this?!","Was Existence itself set on trying to collapse him here no matter what?!","Regardless of how much he prepared, regardless of how cautious he was, when temporal traversal had already activated successfully, another monstrous being had to appear at the worst possible moment?!","He looked like an imperious Emperor about to stake absolutely everything on one final stand.","His lineage began spilling outward with tremendous grandeur.","The full physical manifestation of his lineage that he had not yet expressed externally due to the ongoing chaos of events finally began to reveal itself.","An imperious blue-gold robe formed from actual Fragments of Phonemes of The First Tongue erupted around his body.","It descended and wrapped around him with majestic authority, each thread a compressed word of power.","More Fragments of Phonemes surged and spun over his body in complex patterns.","They began forming a radiant blue-gold crown that materialized above his head, floating there with regal magnificence.","The crown itself was constructed from interwoven Phonemes that spelled out concepts of sovereignty, infinite potential, and linguistic supremacy.","And yet, even as his lineage manifested with such unique power, even as he emanated waves of authority that made nearby Ginnu Lifeforms tremble, he could only hear the mocking laughter of THE Primordial Chaos.","That apex entity grasped the hand of Ul’moreth , who had already turned to see the figure of THE Living Temporal and howled with desperate fury.","And yet THE Primordial Chaos kept his hand clasped onto Ul’moreth so tightly that THE Primeval Titan could not move to intervene.","The situation was unfathomably dire.","At this time, THE Living Temporal thrust his massive hand outward to capture Noah directly.","Purple temporal authority wrapped around those fingers with concentrated power.","At such a critical moment...","HUUM!","Existence itself began to tremble violently.","The skies of The Primordial Genesis Shore shook as if reality was tearing.","An aura of immense proportions and unfathomable wonder bloomed above the settlement.","The mere eruption of this presence cascaded downward and caused every single entity that had not achieved a Depth of Absolute Sovereignty to have their consciousness immediately flicker and shut down.","They became unconscious and dropped from the skies like flies, unable to withstand even the passive pressure.","Even some weaker THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty Ginnu Lifeforms lost consciousness entirely and fell.","The laughter of THE Primordial Chaos ceased abruptly.","The movement of THE Living Temporal stopped mid-motion.","Noah’s gaze became even more fiercely defiant as he looked upward to witness the emergence of an unfathomably massive and titanic outline of a humanoid entity.","This being’s entire body was surrounded and obscured by multicolored flames of pure Existence itself.","The flames burned in impossible colors that should not exist, shifting between hues that had no names.","Heat and steam and additional flames emanated continuously from what appeared to be a nose and mouth.","They were melting and healing the surrounding fabric of Existence in constant cycles.","Where the steam touched reality, it would dissolve momentarily before reforming instantly.","An air of profound ancientness surged around this entity.","An aura of immensity that suggested this being had existed since before time itself took coherent form.","The moment this titanic figure appeared, everything nearby turned utterly silent.","Even THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Temporal ceased all movement and sound.","Prompts materialized before Noah’s vision.","| You have glimpsed Immensity|","|You have glimpsed THE Creature|","|Warning: Prolonged observation may result in existential damage|","HUUM!","The moment this massive titanic entity appeared in full manifestation, the figure of THE Primordial Chaos that had been laughing throughout this entire ordeal stopped completely.","His gaze turned upward toward THE Creature.","His entire existence began illuminating with tremendous defensive power.","His expression became razor sharp as he spoke with voice carrying challenge.","|Oh no you don’t!|","Purple and chaotic authority erupted from him as he moved to counter whatever THE Creature intended.","Noah’s eyes burned with absolute defiance as his awareness registered three entities of unfathomably terrifying power all focused on this single moment.","THE Living Temporal behind him had stopped momentarily when THE Creature appeared.","But now his massive hand extended once more, burning with crackling waves of temporal authority to capture Noah.","Meanwhile, Noah could feel the influence of THE Primordial Chaos surging toward both himself and THE Creature simultaneously.","Attempting to lock down all variables and control the outcome.","And this massive titanic entity that he now stared at with unwavering defiance...","Its face could not be clearly observed as it burned with far too much concentrated flame of Existence.","But Noah could absolutely feel the eyes of this being staring straight at him through that inferno.","His defiance burned even greater.","Was this what Existence wanted?!","Did they truly want to test him and force him to make good on his threats?!","Because he genuinely felt like he could do something absolutely irreversible to The First Tongue if he wished.","Something that would cause unknown cascading effects throughout all of reality.","If no solution presented itself, if things really continued heading toward this disastrous direction, if he and all those depending on him were put in mortal danger...","He would willingly flip the entire board and accept whatever consequences followed.","In this moment of unfathomable defiance, burning with determination to survive no matter the cost, he felt something shift within his existence.","A semblance of a Depth he had been approaching.","THE .","It was calling out to him with greater intensity than ever before.","The threshold was right there, tantalizingly close.","But when it came to beings who moved far faster than even Planck Speed, would any advancement be capable of changing anything in this frozen moment?!","Everything moved in terrible slow motion.","At this time, the massive titanic form of the immensity above The Primordial Genesis Shore raised one hand.","And simply clenched his fist.","A mere clench of a fist. Such a simple gesture.","And yet in the next moment, the figure of THE Living Temporal showed a face of immense shock and genuine surprise.","The figure of THE Primordial Chaos roared out with what sounded like frustrated familiarity.","| You ugly bum!|","And in the next instant...","BOOM!","The terrifying and imposing temporal restrictions that had appeared the moment THE Living Temporal arrived and stopped Noah’s traversal from proceeding...","They disappeared instantly as if they had never existed.","The sensation of Existence fading all around Noah, which had been interrupted, resumed immediately.","The figures of Ul’moreth, Tor, THE Living Origin, THE Primordial Chaos, and THE Living Temporal all began fading away once more.","Noah’s defiant gaze remained locked on THE Creature above.","His eyes fumed with blue-gold Mana as they showed profound shock!"]},{"number":4631,"title":"Chapter 4631: Chapter 4630: Why?!","paragraphs":["As his weavings burned with glory and shock, in the next moment...","BOOM!","Temporal Traversal freely and fully activated without further interference.","His figure became funneled backward across space and time with irresistible momentum.","THE Creature had arrived at the critical moment and made a single decisive move.","Breaking off the restraints of THE Living Temporal with such overwhelming authority that even that apex entity could not maintain them.","It had allowed Noah to complete his Temporal Traversal successfully.","THE Creature had saved him.","Why...","Why had THE Creature saved him?!","With eyes still burning with defiance and infinite potential, Noah felt himself being pulled completely away from that era.","He concluded a terrifying traversal and returned to the current time.","---","In Existence, there are certain truths that transcend power and authority.","One such truth is this: every action creates debt, whether acknowledged or not.","When an entity extends their hand to help another, they create a bond that resonates across time and causality.","Not because the helper demands repayment, but because Existence itself recognizes the imbalance and seeks equilibrium.","Some entities accumulate vast debts without ever recognizing them.","They take and take, believing themselves entitled to what they receive, never understanding that Existence keeps perfect accounting.","Others recognize every debt immediately and feel its weight crushing them.","These entities often become paralyzed, unable to move forward because they cannot bear the thought of owing anyone anything.","But the wisest entities understand a deeper truth.","That debt and sacrifice are not burdens to be avoided but rather the fundamental currency through which meaningful connections are forged.","When a teacher burns their Way to save a student, they are not creating obligation.","They are expressing the ultimate form of their teaching: that some things matter more than personal advancement.","When an apex entity who should be completely indifferent makes a single move that changes everything, they are not acting randomly.","They are acknowledging something they see that others have missed.","Real power is not the ability to take without consequence.","Real power is the ability to give without expectation, to sacrifice without regret, to intervene without demanding gratitude.","Those who can do this reshape Existence itself through their actions.","They create ripples that echo across eons, influencing events they will never witness.","And sometimes, in moments of desperate crisis, the accumulated weight of all those small interventions crystallizes into a single perfect action.","A clenched fist that shatters temporal bindings.","A burning Way that creates space for escape.","A choice to step into danger so another can step away.","These are not transactions. They are expressions of something deeper than power.","They are expressions of the conviction that Existence matters, that individuals matter, that the struggle to survive and grow and become more than you were is sacred.","And those who have received such gifts carry them forward.","Not as debts to be repaid to specific entities, but as obligations to Existence itself.","To become the kind of being who would make the same choice when the moment arrives.","To burn what must be burned.","To intervene when intervention seems impossible.","This is the true progression that matters.","Not the accumulation of authority or the climbing of classifications.","But the willingness to give up everything you have accumulated when the moment demands it.","Because in the end, all things flow from The First Tongue and return to it eventually.","All power is temporary. All advancement is transient.","But the choice to stand between danger and those who cannot yet defend themselves...that echoes eternally.","It echoes with the same defiant refusal to accept impossible odds.","The same determination to flip the board rather than accept defeat.","The same Infinite Potential waiting to be actualized.","This is how Existence balances itself across impossible scales.","And those who understand this truth carry it forward, becoming the intervention for the next desperate soul.","Ensuring that no defiant existence burns out alone.","—","In the current era, in the region of collapse that used to be The Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, a desperate battle continued to unfold.","The First Farmer moved with methodical precision across the devastated landscape, his weathered hands reaching down to harvest a Seed from the corpse of the Avatar of Ambessa.","The Seed pulsed with residual authority, still carrying traces of the tremendous power that entity had wielded.","He placed it carefully into his collection, his expression grim as he observed the ongoing conflict around him.","Alexander Asmodeus floated above the battlefield, his entire form shining with unfathomable silver-white light.","The radiance of Peace emanated from him in crushing waves, his Way fully expressed and burning with conviction.","The Shattered Part of THE Heart of Law had been completely consumed and transformed into fuel for his new path.","His eyes held absolute certainty as he prepared to enforce Peace through whatever violence proved necessary.","The diminutive figure of Khor surged forward with explosive momentum, her small form surrounded by trillions of obsidian jaws that manifested from her Way of Hunger.","Each jaw snapped and hungered, seeking to devour absolutely everything in their path.","She moved like a living storm of consumption, her eyes blazing with fury as she charged directly toward Schrodinger.","All around them, rings of Primus Inevitabilities of different Specializations floated in defensive formations.","They created overlapping fields of authority that sought to contain and suppress their opponents.","And at the very center of this chaotic battle, The Infiniverse blazed with tremendous power.","Surrounding her form was a dazzling letter that very few entities in all of Existence could recognize.","A Phoneme of The First Tongue, written large and burning with concentrated authority.","Blue-gold flames seethed around her entire being as this linguistic symbol enhanced her capabilities beyond normal limits.","Her figure moved like a primal beast unleashed, pure instinct and power combined.","Her feet stomped toward The Disciple of THE Creature with earth-shaking force, each step leaving cracks in the already devastated reality.","At such a critical time, everything shifted.","HUUM!","The figure of Schrodinger adopted an extremely saddened expression.","His eyes, which had been eerie and unsettling throughout this entire conflict, now held genuine grief!","Behind him, the collapsed space fractured even further as something profound began to manifest.","A paradoxical rift tore open in reality itself.","This was not a normal spatial tear or dimensional gateway.","It was a rift that existed and did not exist simultaneously, that opened while remaining closed, that connected to everywhere and nowhere at once.","Looking at it directly caused perception to fracture, as the mind struggled to comprehend something that violated fundamental logic.","The rift pulsed with colors that contradicted themselves. Light that was simultaneously bright and dark. Emptiness that was simultaneously full.","From this paradoxical rift, nine entities began to emerge with terrible majesty.","Each one radiated profound waves of overwhelming power.","At first assessment, they felt like entities at the level of Pre-THE classification.","But the actual power they emanated was suffocating and crushing, exceeding even The Disciple of THE Creature by substantial margins!"]},{"number":4632,"title":"Chapter 4632: Chapter 4631: Infinite Potential I","paragraphs":["Around each of these nine entities, the unmistakable allure of a complete Genesis Principle surrounded them like halos of compressed authority.","Not Singularity Principles, but full Genesis Principles related to Paradox itself.","They all looked exactly identical to one another, as if cast from the same impossible mold.","Each entity stood approximately fifteen feet tall with powerfully built humanoid frames.","Their bodies appeared to be constructed from smooth metallic material that gleamed with obsidian-gold coloration.","No faces were visible, only smooth featureless surfaces where heads should be.","Their forms radiated an aura of absolute indestructibility, as if they were forged from the concept of permanence itself.","Massive obsidian-gold wings extended from their backs, each wing inscribed with intricate patterns of paradoxical geometry.","Tendrils of pure paradox surrounded them, writhing and coiling like living things.","These tendrils existed in states of constant contradiction, simultaneously solid and ethereal, moving and still, there and not there.","As they floated behind Schrodinger in perfect formation, Khor and all the other combatants felt a profound sense of suffocation crash over them.","The pressure these entities exerted simply by existing made it difficult to maintain coherent thought.","But the most shocking detail revealed itself as they drew closer.","On the chest of each entity, prominently displayed and burning with terrible power, was an inscribed Phoneme.","The Phoneme of Paradox, written in The First Tongue itself.","It blazed with authority that made reality tremble, granting these entities connection to linguistic supremacy that should not be possible.","They radiated terrifying might and complete indestructibility, weapons forged from paradox itself and empowered by The First Tongue.","At this moment, Schrodinger spoke with voice carrying profound despondency.","\"I am to be a harbinger. I am to let you know that the Agents of The Fallout have descended from THE Loom. That as of this moment, we are twenty-five seconds to midnight.\"","HUUM !","The words were devastatingly heavy.","As if sensing that those gathered did not comprehend what he truly meant, Schrodinger continued with voice mixing grief and resignation.","\"Twenty-five seconds to midnight is a measurement of how close Existence stands to complete and total collapse. Midnight represents the moment when The Fallout becomes irreversible, when THE Loom unravels completely, when everything that is ceases to be. We measure our proximity to this end not in years or eons, but in seconds. And we have just moved from thirty seconds to twenty-five.\"","His expression became even more anguished.","He paused, trembling.","His entire being began shaking as rage mixed with his despondency.","\"Why did you all not listen?! Why could Osmont not give a single life to save countless others?! Is he so important that one individual him is worth everything in Observable Existence perishing?! One entity versus the survival of all reality, and you chose to protect the one?!\"","When he said those last words, his entire existence trembled violently with mixture of fury and profound grief.","As if he knew with absolute certainty that it was all too late.","That the choice had been made, and the consequences were now inevitable.","That these nine Agents of The Fallout standing behind him were merely the beginning of what was to come.","And that twenty-five seconds to Midnight might as well be zero, because nothing they could do now would stop the unraveling.","After Schrodinger’s words finished echoing across the devastated landscape, the nine Agents of The Fallout rose higher into the air.","Their metallic bodies seemed to emanate no emotion whatsoever.","Only immense paradoxical coldness radiated from them, a chill that went beyond temperature into something fundamental and existential.","Each of them turned with perfect synchronization toward The Infiniverse and Khor.","As if their targets had already been predetermined before they even emerged from the paradoxical rift.","As if the outcome had been calculated and the execution was merely a formality.","It was a moment that could induce immense despair in even the strongest entities.","With the power that these nine entities possessed, how could they possibly be faced when their very existence emanated Weavings of The First Tongue inscribed directly onto their indestructible bodies?!","The First Farmer moved to stand behind The Infiniverse, his expression carrying the weight of one who had seen civilizations rise and fall countless times.","Alexander Asmodeus floated into position, his silver-white light of Peace burning with defiant conviction despite the impossible odds.","Khor positioned herself with jaw set in determination, trillions of obsidian jaws still manifesting around her small form.","Millions of Primus Inevitabilities of various Specializations formed ranks alongside them.","All of them lined up as if preparing to make their final stand against an unstoppable force.","As if they knew with crushing certainty that these enemies were so unfathomably powerful that many of them here would not survive what was about to unfold.","But they would stand regardless, because that was what remained when all other options had been exhausted.","Schrodinger observed all of this with expression mixing grief and frustration as he shook his head slowly.","Because among all those gathered here in their battle formations, among those adorned in Civilizational Armors and preparing for certain death, he could see her.","Leonore Rureaux stood among the defenders, her stance resolute despite the hopelessness.","He had wanted to save her and so many others like her.","But now it was all too late for salvation.","His voice emerged with despotic weight as he spoke words meant to make them understand the futility.","\"These Agents of The Fallout are Pre-THE Existences that approach the power of genuine THE entities despite not having achieved that classification. Since Existence itself suppresses THE classification, since no THE can manifest currently outside THE Loom due to these suppressive mechanisms, these Agents represent essentially the most powerful creatures that can exist outside THE Loom’s boundaries.\"","He gestured toward the nine metallic figures with trembling hand.","\"Not at THE level technically, and yet they can almost exhibit this level of power through their unique construction and empowerment. They are weapons forged specifically to bypass the restrictions. As of this moment, there isn’t even a theoretical idea of resistance that would work. All of this catastrophe, all of this despair, could have been avoided!\"","His words were enough to induce immense hopelessness in those who heard them.","He made it devastatingly clear just how terrifying and indestructible these nine Agents truly were.","They were essentially killing weapons that could never be harmed or stopped outside of THE Loom itself!","Oh!"]},{"number":4633,"title":"Chapter 4633: Chapter 4632: Infinite Potential II","paragraphs":["And just as the nine Agents were about to move forward to execute their predetermined targets, just as despair was settling over all the defenders...","HUUM!","Existence itself vibrated violently throughout this entire region of collapse.","Directly in front of The Infiniverse, a blue-gold tear opened in the fabric of reality itself.","And from it emerged a figure of unfathomable and glorious presence.","An entity adorned in an imperious blue-gold robe that seemed woven from compressed potential itself.","A spinning blue-gold crown materialized above his head, rotating slowly and radiating linguistic authority.","His entire existence appeared ethereal and untouchable, as if he existed slightly out of phase with normal reality.","His aura felt pure and true, carrying the weight of Infinite Potential waiting to be actualized.","And yet his eyes at this moment shone with terrifying concentration of defiance and glory that burned like compressed stars.","The moment he appeared, everything seemed to shift into slow motion.","Many existences opened their eyes in profound shock and disbelief.","Because this was the man in question that so many had been discussing and debating.","The visage of Osmont himself!","He had never appeared throughout this entire catastrophic conflict.","And now, when things had achieved what seemed an irreversible state, when despair had settled over all, he finally showed himself?!","Schrodinger felt immediate lividity surge through him.","He wanted to bellow toward Osmont for his recklessness and cowardice that had driven events to this terrible point.","To demand why he had hidden while reality crumbled around them.","But the moment Schrodinger locked his gaze onto Noah, the moment their eyes met across the devastated space, something unexpected occurred.","Schrodinger saw into those defiant blue-gold eyes.","And he actually trembled and froze completely as if he had just glimpsed a terrifying primordial beast barely contained within human form.","What he saw in those eyes was not fear or regret or shame.","Only absolute defiant conviction and something far deeper. Something that transcended normal classification.","In the next moment, the glorious scene unfolded with devastating swiftness.","Noah, who still held that defiant light burning within his eyes, turned his gaze toward the nine Agents of The Fallout.","The entities that had been rushing forward to execute The Infiniverse and Khor.","The supposedly indestructible weapons that nothing outside THE Loom could face.","And in the next instant, he raised his hand with casual authority.","A radiant blue-gold stick formed in his grip, The Goad manifesting with familiar weight.","And with speed that others present could not even begin to fathom or track, he struck downward with this simple stick.","It enlarged explosively as it descended, expanding to instantly cover every single region of this collapsed space.","It looked like a massive blue-gold pillar had manifested above all nine of the newly appearing Agents of The Fallout.","A stick the size of continental landmasses, blazing with compressed authority.","The manifestation thundered down with force that made reality itself scream.","And shockingly, impossibly, the seemingly indestructible Agents folded like fragile paper under its weight.","Their obsidian-gold metallic bodies that should have been immune to all damage crumpled and were nearly flattened completely by the overwhelming pressure.","The allure of The First Tongue shone unfathomably bright from the stick, from Noah himself, as linguistic authority crushed physical indestructibility through sheer superiority.","In the next moment, Noah waved his hand with simple gesture.","The crumpled metallic figures of all nine Agents of The Fallout began flowing uncontrollably toward him.","Drawn by irresistible force toward his open palm.","He closed his hand decisively, and they all disappeared entirely into his grip.","Vanished as if they had never existed at all.","The indestructible entities that had just appeared moments ago with such terrifying fanfare.","The entities that Schrodinger had stated would find nothing capable of defeating them outside of THE Loom due to their power approaching THE classification itself.","Yet now, in less than a nanosecond after a single entity appeared, after he struck down with a simple stick in one devastating blow, all nine of these supposedly unstoppable weapons had been taken down and captured in a single stroke!","Oh!","Every single thing in nearby Existence instantly turned unfathomably silent.","The wind stopped. The residual energy discharges ceased. Even the ambient sounds of collapsing reality faded to nothing.","Complete and absolute silence descended as every entity present tried to process what they had just witnessed.","The First Farmer stood frozen with eyes wide.","Alexander Asmodeus’s silver light flickered with shock.","Khor’s millions of obsidian jaws had stopped moving entirely.","The Primus Inevitabilities hung motionless in formation.","And Schrodinger stared with expression that had transformed from livid fury to absolute incomprehension.","Because what had just occurred should not be possible.","Could not be possible.","And yet it had happened before all their eyes.","Noah stood there calmly, his blue-gold robe settling around him, his crown still spinning slowly above his head.","And his eyes continued burning with that same defiant glory, as if crushing nine Agents of The Fallout was merely the beginning of what he intended to accomplish.","Noah had made his return with temporal traversal proceeding as rapidly as the mechanism allowed.","He did not tarry within the chaotic temporal Weavings of space for even a fraction longer than necessary.","His Early Atlas of the Folds simply returned him to his current era at the fastest speeds possible.","Because there could be no additional surprises or complications after what he had just experienced.","The past that he’d left behind had three terrifying titans converging in a single location where he had been standing.","THE Primordial Chaos, THE Living Temporal, and THE Creature had all arrived at The Primordial Genesis Shore within moments of each other.","And yet the appearance of THE Creature was the one that left one of the more pronounced impressions burning in his mind.","That massive titanic being covered by multicolored flames of Existence all around its form had clenched a single fist.","And that simple gesture had actually allowed Noah to complete his Temporal Traversal successfully.","Which caused the question of why to buzz in his mind again and again during his journey back.","He knew with absolute certainty that everything was done on purpose at that level of power.","That there could be no mistakes or accidents when entities like THE Creature acted.","So there had to be a deliberate purpose behind THE Creature’s actions.","He just could not see what that purpose was yet."]},{"number":4634,"title":"Chapter 4634: Chapter 4633: Infinite Potential III","paragraphs":["The pieces did not fit together into a coherent picture in his understanding.","And yet the moment he arrived back in his current era, he appeared directly in the region of collapse where an ongoing battle was occurring.","Nine creatures burning with paradoxical authority and inscribed with the Phoneme of Paradox had been attempting to suppress and induce despair in his Civilization.","So he had struck down with his Goad.","But his Goad now held multiple Phonemes arranged within its structure in complex linguistic patterns.","And when paired with his current level of power, his new lineage as THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, and his terrifying Foundation reinforced by the Nine Pillars of Infinite Expression...","These entities at the Pre-THE Existence level were absolutely nothing before him.","Even if they were approaching the power of a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity through their unique construction.","After all, he had faced genuine Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities in direct combat!","He had battled and imprisoned 14 of them in THE Infinite Desmoterion.","So nine paradoxical weapons, however impressive their construction, could not stand against what he had become.","His action had caused immense silence to descend across the battlefield.","He didn’t pay attention to the shocked reactions rippling through all the gathered entities.","Instead, he turned around to face his people directly.","The moment he did so, he came face to face with none other than The Infiniverse.","Her figure was majestic and commanding, adorned in a blue-gold battle dress that seemed woven from compressed reality itself.","The dress was filled with and surrounded by countless Omniverses and Folds, each one orbiting her form like satellites around a planet.","Her radiant multicolored hair cascaded down her shoulders in waves that seemed to contain flowing information itself.","Each strand appeared to shift through different hues depending on the angle of observation.","Her eyes seemed filled with infinite information and possibilities, containing depth that suggested she processed reality at speeds beyond normal comprehension.","They typically held a type of analytical coldness, the gaze of one who viewed Existence as data to be understood and optimized.","And yet at this moment, as she looked at Noah and saw the defiance and lingering lividity within his eyes, something shifted in her expression.","The Infiniverse floated forward with deliberate movement.","And shockingly, she embraced Noah directly.","She actually placed her head against his chest and closed her eyes, her arms wrapping around him in gesture that seemed utterly foreign to her normally emotionless demeanor.","She spoke only for him to hear, her voice carrying warmth that few would believe she possessed.","\" Welcome back, Master.\"","Welcome back.","They were simple words, only three syllables combined.","But they were filled with immense relief and genuine warmth that transcended her usual analytical nature.","Because she was actually one of only two beings who had been watching what happened to Noah in Ginnungagap in real time.","The Infiniverse and Ruination had observed through their deep connection to him.","They watched as THE Primordial Chaos appeared and things turned horrendous.","They watched as THE Living Temporal arrived and the situation seemed to deteriorate beyond hope.","They watched as THE Creature manifested and the future became utterly unclear.","The outcome had been uncertain at that terrible moment.","Ruination and The Infiniverse were the only ones who lived through the terror of that convergence alongside Noah himself.","So at this moment, the normally emotionless Infiniverse actually embraced her Master and welcomed him back with genuine feeling.","The burning glory and defiance within Noah’s eyes lessened somewhat as he held the head of The Infiniverse gently.","He patted her hair with careful affection.","\"I’m back,\" he said simply. \"I’m back.\"","The words were straightforward enough, carrying weight of reassurance.","In the next moment, glorious and terrifying prompts bloomed before his vision as time itself seemed to freeze around him.","|Temporal Traversal - Final Resolution|","|The grandest Temporal Traversal you have undertaken so far has ended|","|Total Duration: Traversal to The Infinite Unfurling and return|","|Temporal Displacement: Eons backward, then return to present|","|Critical Understanding - The Nature of Unchanging Past:|","|The past is the past and the past will not change|","|What occurred in The Infinite Unfurling has already occurred and is set|","|No alteration to established events is possible through temporal mechanics|","|HOWEVER: The exertion of your efforts and the Infinite Potentials that you represent have made it possible for Infinite Potentials to bloom from your actions|","....!","|Actualization of Infinite Potential: |","|Since the past cannot be changed, the potential of your actions will instead be expressed in the current Weavings of Existence|","|You have no control over the exact manner of their exertion|","|Their implementation may potentially benefit you OR harm you depending on the potential results of your actions|","|Your actions and choices have consequences that ripple forward through time|","|The causality of all actions in The Infinite Unfurling is being measured and calculated|","|Seeds of Your Way:|","|During the Festival at The Primordial Genesis Shore, you left Sparks of Your Way|","|Due to leaving seeds of your Way of Existence in The Infinite Unfurling, in Ginnungagap, Weavings of boundless potential were created|","|Entities Significantly Influenced: Lumivara, THE First Hunger, THE Living Origin, Ul’moreth, Ains, and numerous others|","|Your Way was picked up and influenced the Weavings of many entities eons ago|","...!","|The Set Past:|","|The set past did not change through your influence|","|Those that died in established history still died|","|Those that lived in established history still lived|","|Events played out exactly as they were always going to play out|","| Understanding the Closed Temporal Loop:|","|Your Temporal Traversal has created what is classified as a type of a Closed Time Loop with some discrepancies and anomalies|","|Definition: A self-contained causality cycle where time travel to the past does not change history because the traveler’s actions were ALWAYS part of that history|","|Your presence in The Infinite Unfurling was not an alteration, it was always meant to be there|","|Everything you did in the past had already happened from the perspective of linear history|","BOOM!"]},{"number":4635,"title":"Chapter 4635: Chapter 4634: Infinite Potential IV","paragraphs":["Waves and waves of prompts cascaded down one after another, each one giving off grander waves of information compared to before!","| Fixed Timeline Principle:|","|Time flows as an unchangeable line where all events, including time travel, are set in stone|","|The timeline is fixed because your traversal was part of what created the timeline you remember|","|Causality Loop Mechanics:|","|The traveler’s future knowledge or presence in the past is what creates the past they remember|","| You influenced Lumivara, Ul’moreth, and others eons ago, this influence was always part of their history|","|They did not experience a timeline without you and then a timeline with you|","|They experienced only one timeline, and you were always in it|","| This forms a self-contained loop where cause and effect circle back on themselves|","|Again, due to your anomalous weavings, these rulings of time may not always be entirely accurate.|","|No Change Possible - Paradox Prevention:|","|Any attempt to alter the past is fated to fail OR to cause the very events you remember|","|You could not have saved Ul’moreth from imprisonment because his fate was already set|","|You could not have prevented the convergence because it was always meant to happen|","|The loop is closed.|","|Bootstrap Existence:|","|Some elements of your current power may have no true origin|","|Did you develop your understanding of The First Tongue on your own, or did the seeds you planted in the past circle back to influence your present?|","|The knowledge and power flowing through the loop may be self-creating|","|This is the nature of closed causality, origin points become meaningless|","|The Unchangeable Cycle:|","|You have become your own cause|","|Your future self traveling to the past is what created continuing conditions for your present self to exist|","|The past you visited has already happened from history’s perspective|","| The future you will live has already been influenced by what you did in that past|","|The cycle is complete and cannot be broken|","|BUT: The Infinite Potential of your actions and weavings now manifests in the present|","|Lumivara - Manifestation of Potential:|","|The Infinite Potential of Lumivara is manifesting in current Weavings|","|Historical Record: Lumivara, having been escorted by a Ginnu Lifeform away from The Primordial Genesis Shore during the convergence, survived the encounter|","|She lived in The Infinite Unfurling and cultivated following the influence of your Way of Mana and Hunger|","|She ascended through the Depths of Absolute Sovereignty over eons|","| Her advancement and the advancement of all those she influenced is now being actualized in your current era|","Noah’s eyes shone with brilliant intensity as he felt everything around him freeze completely.","Time itself seemed locked in the span of an instant as countless prompts cascaded down before his vision!","He continued holding The Infiniverse in his embrace while processing this overwhelming information.","|Comprehensive Manifestation - All Influenced Entities:|","| The Infinite Potential of all entities significantly affected by your presence is manifesting simultaneously|","|Calculation Status: Complete for major Weavings|","|The Convergence - Outcome Assessment:|","| The full results and unfolding of the convergence between THE Primordial Chaos, THE Living Temporal, and THE Creature remains partially unknown|","|Many variables exist beyond current observation capacity|","|HOWEVER: Through your connection to The First Tongue, the fates of those directly connected to you have been ascertained|","|Tor (THE First Hunger) - Fate Determined:|","| The collapse of Tor at the hands of THE Creature in The Earliest Folds has been ascertained|","|This occurred even after his deep connection with THE Living Origin|","|THE Living Origin’s intervention made it so THE Creature initially excluded Tor from imprisonment in The Infinite Unfurling|","|However, eventual collapse was inevitable and has been confirmed|","|Ginnu Lifeforms - Survival Confirmed:|","|The Fisherman Ains: Survival ascertained, Weavings continuing|","| Ul’moreth (THE Primeval Titan): Survival ascertained, Weavings continuing|","|All other Ginnu Lifeforms significantly influenced by your Way: Survival ascertained|","|Their Weavings have continued throughout The Infinite Unfurling|","| THE Prison - Discovery Through First Tongue:|","|Through your connection to The First Tongue, critical information has been ascertained|","| All significantly complex entities in Ginnungagap and The Infinite Unfurling were locked under THE Primordial Unfurling Nodes of Existence|","|Prison Structure: THE Northern, Southern, Eastern, and Western Nodes of Existence of THE Creature|","|Prison Name Ascertained: The Belly of Existence|","|Function: An unknown number of entities within The Infinite Unfurling were placed under the influence and shadow of THE Creature|","|Mechanism: Their Weavings and advancement continuously empower His Way and the Way of a select few who aided THE Creature|","|Result: Empowering Existence itself through their contained cultivation|","|Manifestation of Your Actions - The Harvest:|","|The Infinite Potential of your actions is now manifesting across all affected Weavings|","|Your influence on the Ginnu Lifeforms, on Lumivara, and on the Civilization she forged around Mana principles has been calculated|","|All these entities remain locked in The Belly of Existence to this day|","|Their Ways became grander due to your influence|","|In turn, THE Creature siphoned off vastly more Weavings of The First Tongue and Mana from them across eons|","|Nothing of the established past was changed|","| BUT: The Infinite Potential of all accumulated advancement is being actualized NOW|","| Comprehensive Benefits Analysis:|","|The First Tongue became even grander and more refined due to your actions in the past|","|Existence itself has become fundamentally stronger due to your influence|","|Paradox has become even more paradoxical through the ripples you created|","|Chaos has run more rampant due to your presence influencing established patterns|","|All of this infinite potential manifests simultaneously in current Weavings|","|Your Personal Harvest:|","|Your Way of Existence has obtained an unfathomably incalculable harvest|","|Source: Eons of cultivation by Lumivara, Ains, Ul’moreth, and others influenced by your Way|","|Magnitude: Beyond normal calculation parameters|","|Estimated Effect: After receiving and integrating all the harvest, it may be sufficient to elevate you to THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, and may even exceed THE Surface Depth and approach THE Intermediate Depth even with your astounding potential|","|Fair Distribution - The Oldest Paradox:|","|The changes and consequences apply fairly and equally|","|All components within The Oldest Paradox of Existence experience corresponding changes|","|The Way of Existence (THE Creature’s domain): Massive benefit|","|The Way of The First Tongue: Massive benefit|","|The Way of Paradox: Substantial benefit|","|The Way of Chaos: Substantial benefit|","|All other Ways: Variable benefits based on involvement|","|Final Assessment:|","| Out of all entities and concepts involved, it has been deemed that The Way of Existence and The Way of The First Tongue benefitted the most from your temporal actions|","| THE Creature’s gain is estimated to exceed your own by multiple orders of magnitude|","|However, your gain remains unprecedented for an entity of your current classification|","...!"]},{"number":4636,"title":"Chapter 4636: Chapter 4635: Infinite Potential V","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes buzzed with intensity as he processed all of this while still holding The Infiniverse in his embrace.","This frozen instant stretched as information flooded his consciousness.","Why had THE Creature saved him? He had asked himself this question repeatedly during his return.","The answer became devastatingly clear now.","Oh, it was so clear now.","THE Creature had not saved him out of benevolence or mercy.","THE Creature had saved him because Noah’s survival and return maximized the harvest for all involved.","If Noah had been captured or collapsed by THE Living Temporal , the Infinite Potential would have been lost or redirected.","But by allowing Noah to return to his current era, by ensuring the loop completed properly, THE Creature ensured that all the accumulated potential across eons would manifest.","And since THE Creature held Lumivara, Ains, Ul’moreth, and countless others locked away in The Belly of Existence, siphoning from them constantly across all those eons...","THE Creature arguably gained vastly more than anyone else from this actualization.","Noah felt the unfathomable harvest waiting within his existence like a dam ready to burst.","Ready to rush out and transform every aspect of his being.","At the same time, the others who had benefitted from his actions across time also attained their corresponding harvest simultaneously.","And THE Creature , who had countless entities locked away in The Infinite Unfurling, with those connected to Noah’s Way being especially potent sources that he had siphoned from for eons...","THE Creature had gained monumentally more than before.","And since nothing of the past would change, since events had unfolded exactly as they always had, all of that infinite potential of accumulated possibilities manifested NOW across current Weavings.","An instant later, as time resumed its normal flow, Existence all around began to shimmer and transform.","Whether in this region of collapse where Noah stood.","Or in the distant Wandering Territories where entities pursued their own advancement.","Or in the Transcendent Folds where reality took different forms.","Or in the Lands of the Living where most entities dwelled.","Or in the Lands of The Dead where collapsed existences gathered.","All of surrounding Existence began shimmering with multicolored brilliance .","Reality itself gave off a sense of unfathomable immensity and grandeur as fundamental changes rippled outward.","The very fabric of what was real became denser, more refined, more potent.","Oh, Existence had benefitted tremendously from the closed temporal loop!","And that massive benefit, that fundamental strengthening of reality itself, would have unfathomable and entirely unintended consequences!","Consequences that even THE Creature might not have fully anticipated.","Because when you strengthened the foundation of all reality, when you made Existence itself more potent and refined...","Everything built upon that foundation changed as well.","And not always in predictable or controllable ways.","Noah stood there holding The Infiniverse as the shimmer of transformation spread across all of reality.","His eyes still burned with defiance, but now mixed with growing understanding!","Existence burned with glory.","And because it did so...","Within THE Loom , in a sea of endless paradox that had been seated over Existence itself, reality began to tremble and vibrate.","The sea of paradox churned violently, waves of impossible contradictions crashing against each other with building intensity.","And standing at the center of this churning chaos, the visage of THE Living Paradox rose to his feet with eyes shining with profound interest.","He raised his hand slowly as he felt an unfathomable emergence of paradox alongside an even grander emergence of Existence itself.","The two forces surged simultaneously, their growth perfectly synchronized.","Sometimes, coincidences existed in reality.","But more often than not, everything was fundamentally connected in ways that transcended surface observation.","THE Living Paradox thought about what he had just witnessed through his connection to the Agents he had sent forth.","How Osmont had arrived and eliminated the nine Agents of Paradox like they were nothing.","Crushed them with contemptuous ease and captured them in a single devastating strike.","And then, less than a second later, his own Way and Existence itself began burning with unprecedented immensity.","Both growing stronger simultaneously.","Coincidence?","No.","No, this was no coincidence at all.","\"Osmont, is it? Are you actually a weapon of THE Creature, or something else entirely?\"","THE Living Paradox actually smiled at this moment as he spoke the question aloud.","Even though such a development had occurred, even though his Agents had been neutralized and Existence itself had grown stronger, he remained prepared.","After all, he knew precisely what monster he was fighting.","He understood that THE Creature had countless entities locked away in his Belly.","His Belly of Existence. His Belly of THE Beast.","And THE Loom would strike that Belly wide open and spill everything contained within.","All those from The Infinite Unfurling would be released.","All those from Ginnungagap would emerge.","After THE Loom struck, after The Fallout descended fully, nothing would remain the same.","In the previous eons, THE entities had been rare and exceptional.","This would not remain the status quo.","The Fallout would reveal it all. The Fallout would show the fundamental truth.","And then, his true battle with THE Creature would fully and genuinely begin!","THE Living Paradox smiled brilliantly as he spoke with voice carrying across the churning sea.","\" Well, regardless of who you truly are, regardless of whether you’re a tool or an independent actor, your actions are taking us infinitely closer towards Midnight. Existence thrashing like this with all this concentrated power... hah. I will also let you know something, Osmont. If you are indeed a tool being used by THE Creature, you at least deserve to know what your role is accelerating.\"","Seas of Paradox churned even more violently as he spoke.","And in the next moment, the hands of a massive paradoxical clock manifested in this space.","The clock itself seemed to exist and not exist simultaneously, its face showing contradictory times that somehow all remained true at once.","The hands turned with ominous finality.","They moved from twenty-five seconds.","And rotated inexorably toward zero.","The hands of the clock turned closer and closer toward Midnight!","Until...they were 5 Seconds to Midnight!"]},{"number":4637,"title":"Chapter 4637: Chapter 4636: Actualization I","paragraphs":["In the region of collapse, Noah’s existence remained in that unique state.","There was unfathomable potential for him to tap into, a harvest beyond normal calculation waiting to be claimed.","But at this moment, as The Infiniverse emerged from his embrace with hardened expression returning to her features, a howl of someone in immense pain echoed out from behind them.","Noah’s gaze became stern as he turned to look.","The Disciple of THE Creature had a somber expression as his entire existence was actually shining with increased power from the surge affecting all of reality.","But the wailing came from someone else entirely.","The beggar.","Schrodinger.","At this moment, he had a crazed look consuming his features as from his body, a sea of obsidian-gold paradox surged outward.","It formed into a manifestation of a clock.","This ancient and paradoxical timepiece appeared constructed from compressed contradictions, its face showing impossible geometries.","The numbers seemed to shift and rearrange themselves constantly while somehow remaining fixed.","The hands moved with jerky, unnatural motion that defied smooth progression.","And at this time, those hands could be seen moving with terrible swiftness.","From twenty-five.","To twenty.","To fifteen.","To ten.","And then, horrifyingly, to five!","FIVE!","Schrodinger’s wailing words emerged with desperate intensity.","\"The clock has moved from twenty-five seconds to five seconds! FIVE SECONDS TO MIDNIGHT ! Osmont, what have you DONE?! What have you done to accelerate this so catastrophically?! Your actions have brought us ever closer to Midnight! Ever closer to The Fallout! THE Living Paradox wants you to know this! He now displays this clock for all to witness so we know exactly when the bells will ring for Midnight! You are the doom of us all! You are-\"","BOOM!","Noah clenched his hand and punched outward with casual violence.","The Phoneme of Paradox flashed brilliantly on his knuckles.","A manifestation of a massive golden fist appeared directly below Schrodinger and smashed into him with devastating force.","His body was flung upward like a rag doll.","Additional manifestations of fists burning with the Phoneme of Paradox appeared in the exact direction he was thrown.","They smashed into him again and again.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Multiple fists pounded his figure from different angles with brutal efficiency.","Until he looked like nothing more than a bloody mass of pulverized meat barely maintaining coherent form.","Thereafter, a blue-gold prison began forming around his ruined body.","The prison shone with silent Logos of Imprisonment inscribed across its crystalline walls.","Multiple layers of containment wrapping around each other in complex linguistic patterns.","The ever-manipulative figure of Schrodinger was locked up completely!","In the distance, Noah’s gaze remained exactly the same.","The light of glory and defiance in his eyes burned brighter than ever before.","Five seconds to Midnight? Five seconds to The Fallout?","Okay!","They wanted to play games with countdowns and threats?","After this Temporal Traversal, after everything he had experienced and survived, he was fucking ready to tear the entire board apart rather than play by their rules.","So he moved with absolute dominance as he turned his gaze toward The Disciple of THE Creature.","He also saw the shocked Guiders of Order standing far behind in formation.","Order.","His eyes flickered with deadly light as he raised his stick again.","He flung the Goad outward toward The Disciple of THE Creature with devastating intent.","The Disciple raised his sword desperately, the blade shining with the power of a Genesis Principle.","But Noah thrashed him with the same contemptuous ease as the fists had thrashed Schrodinger.","His stick enlarged and descended repeatedly, each strike crushing through the Disciple’s defenses.","The Genesis Principle proved utterly insufficient against Noah’s current level of authority.","After the Disciple was thoroughly thrashed and beaten into near-collapse, Noah locked him within another cage as well, and the Guiders of Order...they didn’t even deserve more than a sentence as a worse version of this occurred to them simultaneously.","And everything in this region of collapse turned unfathomably silent.","Alexander Asmodeus stood frozen, his silver light flickering with disbelief.","Khor stared with millions of obsidian jaws hanging motionless.","The First Farmer’s weathered expression showed profound shock.","Elyndra, Riya, Moiraine, and the others looked toward Noah with expressions mixing shock and awe.","All entities present gazed at him with the same fundamental question burning in their minds.","Just what had happened to him?!","What had occurred during his absence to transform him so dramatically?!","As they all sought answers, the immense Infinite Potential within Noah churned and shifted.","He felt another influx of information flooding his consciousness.","All around them, Existence itself felt even more immense and concentrated than moments before.","New prompts descended before his vision.","| Infinite Potential - Additional Sources Identified|","|Boundless Infinite Potential still remains within the Collapsed Primordial Civilizations of Hunger and Origin|","| Both Civilizations were significantly influenced by your Way during your time in The Infinite Unfurling|","|THE Living Origin - Critical Development:|","| Instead of fully aligning with THE Creature as expected, THE Living Origin leaned more toward your Weavings of The First Tongue|","|After whatever occurred during the conflict between THE Primordial Chaos, THE Living Temporal, and THE Creature in Ginnungagap, critical events unfolded|","| Ul’moreth gave both THE Living Origin and Tor one of the Sparks of your Way that you left behind during the Festival|","|This Spark influenced their development across eons|","|Preservation in The First Tongue:|","| The Infinite Potential of both Tor and THE Living Origin has been preserved within The First Tongue itself|","|Their essence remains encoded in linguistic authority|","| The Seed of Tor and the Seed of THE Living Origin can now be actualized from Infinite Potential|","|This will allow the emergence of their Weavings in your current era|","|Records and Influence:|","|Records of their Primordial Civilizations remain in Existence as historical fact|","|BUT: Their influence toward your Way allowed their records to also remain encoded in The First Tongue|","|There is sufficient Infinite Potential from their actions toward you that helped you survive|","|And from your actions toward them that helped them advance|","|This mutual benefit has created a resonance strong enough for actualization|","|Actualization Query:|","| Shall the Infinite Potential of Tor and THE Living Origin be actualized in current Weavings?|","| Estimated Result: Emergence at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty classification|","|Both entities will manifest with full memory and weavings they held before collapse|","BOOM!"]},{"number":4638,"title":"Chapter 4638: Chapter 4637: Actualization II","paragraphs":["The prompts were devastatingly heavy with implications.","They were grand. But they should be. Because he was THE Potentate. THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons!","Noah’s expression remained unfathomably tyrannical as he spoke with absolute conviction.","\" Let the Infinite Potential be actualized.\"","In the next moment, reality itself responded to his command.","An obsidian-crimson singularity of pure Hunger bloomed a few meters away from Noah.","Simultaneously, a white-gold singularity of absolute Origin manifested beside it.","Each singularity was shockingly surrounded by all eighteen Core Phonemes of The First Tongue.","Linguistic authority wrapped around them in protective cocoons.","They began growing larger and pulsing with unfathomable Weavings of life and concentrated immensity.","The Singularity of Hunger instantly caused the nearby Khor to tremble violently.","She looked toward Noah with eyes wide with shock and desperate hope.","\"Outsider, what have you done? What IS this?!\"","What was it indeed?","Noah’s expression remained vibrant with barely contained power as he replied with calm certainty.","\" The Infinite Potential of Tor, THE First Hunger. Keep him company as best you can. In a little while, you’ll be able to say hello to him again.\"","BOOM!","His terrifying words struck Khor like physical blows.","Her entire visage began trembling as tears she didn’t know she could still produce formed in her eyes.","Noah observed all of this as the fire in his eyes remained just as vibrant and defiant.","He had Infinite Potential ready to elevate his existence toward THE classification.","Enough accumulated power to potentially reach THE Surface Depth or even exceed it.","But he now instinctively understood that THE was not the complete answer.","Not the true path to survival against what was coming.","The First Tongue was the answer. His Mana was the answer.","Even if he achieved THE Intermediate Depth or THE Fundamental Depth, it wouldn’t matter against The Fallout.","His survival and eventual supremacy were tied fundamentally to Mana and The First Tongue.","So he would invest everything there instead.","His internal dialogue crystallized into decisive command.","\"Begin the distribution of all Infinite Potential toward THE Foundation of The First Tongue. Direct everything toward the design and formation of my own Core Phonemes. Allow my Foundation alone to exceed any THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity. Without even grasping that Depth classification myself, I will surpass those who have.\"","After these words resonated through his existence...","BOOM !","Brilliant blue-gold waves of concentrated light surged from Noah’s body in expanding ripples.","His entire form blazed with linguistic authority made visible.","As this monumental process began, he turned to The Infiniverse and spoke with absolute certainty.","\"Prepare yourself. You have access to all my accumulated knowledge of The First Tongue through our connection. Paint the Walls of The Infiniverse with that knowledge. Make it the foundation of your entire structure. Proceed immediately with the forging of THE Infinite Loom.\"","Her glorious figure shone with unfathomable light as comprehension and determination flooded through her.","\"Yes, Master.\"","Then Noah closed his eyes and felt his Weavings of Existence burning upward exponentially.","He looked internally at the transformation occurring within.","There was tremendous activity happening simultaneously and much to be accomplished.","Tor and THE Living Origin would soon undergo Emergence from their singularities.","He was elevating his own Weavings beyond previous limitations.","The Fallout approached with only five seconds remaining on that ominous clock.","Multiple viable solutions swam through his mind with crystalline clarity.","Some were already being implemented as he stood here.","In the midst of all this tremendous upheaval, there remained some loose ends.","Some matters that needed to be resolved before The Fallout arrived and changed everything.","He now moved decisively to take care of them!","---","In a space between spaces, in the manifested Weavings of Order where a veil lay between The Living Order and THE Dead Order, reality shifted.","HUUM!","This space had normally only held Sigrid as she siphoned rivers of Order from THE Dead Order across the veil.","But at this moment, Noah’s figure appeared within this space once more!","The manifestation of Sigrid looked at him with breathless gaze as he materialized mere inches from her position.","She threw herself toward him without hesitation and hugged his body tightly.","She whispered with voice carrying immense relief.","\"I missed you.\"","The scene resembled the reunion of long-lost lovers who hadn’t seen each other in millions of years.","And yet ridiculously, absurdly, it had been at most a few hours since they last met.","On the other side of the veil, THE Dead Order stood in her white robe that seemed woven from pure compressed authority.","Her hair now pulsed with white-gold streams of Order flowing through each strand.","She looked toward this intimate scene with expression of profound revulsion twisting her features.","\" You survived the curse of THE Living Elemental? How were you able to do what you did against a Disciple of THE Creature? Just what did you DO during your absence?!\"","Her gaze seemed livid with barely contained fury.","She had witnessed through the eyes of her Guiders of Order, however briefly, what had transpired.","Noah looked toward her calmly before turning his attention back to Sigrid.","He kissed her deeply, taking her lips into his with passion that had been building during their separation.","He whispered against her mouth.","\"Wait just a little while longer for me, and I’ll make up for every lost hour. Okay?\"","Sigrid appeared breathless as she nodded with flushed expression.","\"Mmm.\"","THE Dead Order witnessed this scene as she shook her head with utter incredulity. As if she was asking...what the fuck Bro?!","She began roaring out with building rage.","\" You sacrilegious savages! You would plan to profane Order right before my presence?! You would dare to- You... what are you doing?!\"","As she was speaking, Noah’s figure floated toward the veil separating their spaces.","The barrier that THE Dead Order could not cross to reach him or Sigrid.","And he shockingly passed through the veil as if it didn’t exist.","He came to float directly before THE Dead Order as she was shocked into complete silence!","In that profound silence, Noah activated Lens of Civilization.","A status sheet materialized before his vision.","|Entity Analysis - THE Dead Order|","|Name: [Redacted by Authority]|","|Classification: THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Way of Existence: The Way of Order|","|Civilization: Primordial Civilization of Order (Fractured)|","|Civilizational Authority: THE Civilizational Authority of Order|","|Current State: FRACTURED DEPTH|","|Note: Her Way exists at THE Surface Depth but has been fundamentally fractured|","|Distinction: Protected by THE Creature|","|Distinction: Former Apex of Order|","|Weakness: Foundation unstable due to fracturing|","...!"]},{"number":4639,"title":"Chapter 4639: Chapter 4638: Actualization III","paragraphs":["An entity at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","But her Depth was fractured, compromised, fundamentally weakened.","Noah gazed at the details with calm analytical focus.","At this moment, THE Dead Order finally reacted to his intrusion.","Her body exploded with terrifying power as her eyes burned with glory and grace.","\"Do you think it will be the same as last time you came here?! You have no flames of THE Living Elemental to protect you now! You are now fully within my domain, my space of absolute authority! This time you will NOT leave! I thank you for your utter stupidity and hubris to think that after defeating a few Pre-THE entities and metal constructs of Paradox that you would somehow be ready for the power of a genuine THE entity! I thank you for delivering yourself to me!\"","As she spoke, her Way erupted with devastating force.","THE Civilizational Authority of Order surged from every direction to surround Noah completely.","White-gold light flooded the space as authority sought to lock him down from all angles.","The veil behind him became utterly covered and sealed to ensure he could not retreat back to Sigrid’s side.","\" You are now locked in here with me, and I will take my time with you. Slowly. Methodically. Until there is nothing left.\"","At such words, THE Civilizational Authority of Order thundered down onto Noah to bind his existence completely.","And yet shockingly, the crushing authority seemed to stop mere inches away from his skin.","As if striking an invisible barrier it could not penetrate.","He raised his hand calmly and formed a single simple stick.","The Goad.","The First Lesson.","THE Potentate’s First Lesson , which had mainly been used to discipline THE entities.","THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons’ First Lesson!","Before its authority, what was a THE entity with a fractured Depth?","Noah’s voice emerged with grand certainty that filled the entire space.","\"I am not locked in here with you, O Order. You are locked in here with me. And what a terrible place it is for you to be trapped.\"","The next scene unfolded in glorious slow motion.","The eyes of THE Dead Order opened wide in mounting shock as she witnessed her authority accomplishing absolutely nothing.","And then Noah struck his stick outward.","The movement appeared slow and deliberate, each increment of motion visible and trackable.","Yet paradoxically, the speed exceeded Planck Speed by incomprehensible margins.","The moment he completed the strike, the stick arrived before THE Dead Order’s head.","It enlarged explosively as it approached.","Time seemed to stretch impossibly as the Goad made contact.","Multiple Logos of The First Tongue flashed brilliantly along the stick’s surface with the impact.","The Phonemes of Beginning, Division, and Ending arranged themselves in declarative structure of Logos that most closely translated to: \"What begins whole becomes divided and ends fractured.\"","The stick smashed into the forehead of THE Dead Order with devastating precision.","Her skin, which should have been inviolable for an entity of her classification, ruptured instantly.","The flesh tore open as bone beneath fractured audibly.","White-gold blood began seeping from the wound as her entire head rocked backward from the force.","Then Noah took a single step forward.","His glorious body adorned in that imperious blue-gold robe moved with fluid grace.","The spinning crown above his head blazed with Fragments of Phonemes as he moved.","He appeared instantly above the split forehead of THE Dead Order.","And with calm deliberation, he sat directly on her head.","His expression remained utterly cold and analytical as both hands reached down.","His fingers gripped both sides of the torn forehead firmly as Logos began manifesting across his arms in intricate patterns.","The Phonemes of Earth and Division combined to grant tremendous physical strength and the ability to separate what should be unified.","Solid bronze radiance reinforced his muscles and bones.","Silver fractures of Division ran along his fingers, creating cutting edges that could tear through conceptual bonds.","The Phoneme of Void opened within his palms, creating spaces that pulled matter apart.","The Phoneme of Ending manifested as deep violet dusk energy that concluded the integrity holding her skull together.","These Logos glowed with blue-gold radiance as they enhanced his capability exponentially.","Using the power of these combined Phonemes, he held THE Dead Order’s struggling form completely still.","And then he pulled with both hands.","To further split her torn head apart.","The bloodied eyes of THE Dead Order showed utter horror and complete disbelief.","Her entire majestic presence seemed to be getting literally torn apart by this Pre-THE entity.","She tried to scream but found her voice trapped by the Logos binding her.","She attempted to unleash her Civilizational Authority but found it suppressed by linguistic superiority.","She sought to call upon her protection but discovered it took time to manifest.","And through all of this, Noah continued pulling steadily and methodically.","The terrible ripping sound echoed through the space as her skull began separating.","White-gold blood flowed more freely as the wound deepened.","In the next moment, Noah truly split the head of THE Dead Order completely.","Her skull separated down the middle as he tore it open like breaking fruit.","And the moment the split was complete, he formed another complex Logos using multiple Core Phonemes.","The Phoneme of Water for adaptation and flow.","The Phoneme of Beginning to initiate transfer.","The Phoneme of Unity to connect what was separated.","The Phoneme of Division to separate what should not remain together.","The Phoneme of Space to create proper distance and channel.","These Phonemes wove together into a Logos of tremendous complexity that most closely translated to: \"What flows from one beginning divides from unity and unites across space with another.\"","THE Civilizational Authority of Order contained within THE Dead Order’s fractured existence surged outward like a white-gold tsunami.","It flowed across the space toward the distant Sigrid in unstoppable waves, following the channel created by Noah’s Logos.","Prompts descended before Noah’s vision.","|Authority Transfer - In Progress|","|25% of the total Weavings of THE Civilizational Authority of Order flowing into The Living Order, Sigrid|","|Sigrid’s Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Order is being constructed|","|Foundation: Rapidly stabilizing|","|Authority Transfer - Accelerating|","| 50% of the total Weavings of THE Civilizational Authority of Order flowing into The Living Order, Sigrid|","|Construction Speed: Exponential|","|Sigrid’s existence expanding to contain transferred power|","|Authority Transfer - Critical Mass|","|60% transferred... 70% transferred... 80% transferred... 90% transferred|","| THE Dead Order’s classification rapidly declining|","|Sigrid approaching THE Surface Depth threshold|","...!"]},{"number":4640,"title":"Chapter 4640: Chapter 4639: Actualization IV","paragraphs":["In this surreal scene, Noah was shockingly transferring the entire Depth of THE Dead Order toward Sigrid at impossible speed.","To the extent that within mere femtoseconds, nearly ninety percent of her accumulated authority across eons was siphoned away completely.","Additional glorious prompts manifested.","|Emergence Assessment - Sigrid, The Living Order|","|Sigrid has built sufficient foundation due to your influence of Mana and the siphoned Civilizational Authority of Order|","|Her Foundation is stabilizing rapidly|","| Her establishment of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Order has been deemed INEVITABLE|","|Timeline: Imminent|","|Outcome: Through her and under your guidance, the true Primordial Civilization of Order shall bloom once more|","At this moment, as the last remnants of Order were about to be completely extracted from THE Dead Order’s collapsing existence, her torn face managed to roar out with utter horror and desperate rage.","\"O CREATURE! SAVE ME! SAVE ME! I USE ONE OF THE PROMISES!\"","BOOM!","The moment those words left her ruined mouth, Noah felt an undeniable force descend from outside this space.","It pulled his arms forcibly from her split head.","Her figure became instantly covered and preserved in multicolored flames of Existence.","Vast distances manifested between them as space itself expanded.","He watched as she breathed raggedly with expression mixing horror, shock, and absolute rage toward him.","Her figure appeared weak and feeble and filled with profound misery.","She looked at him while her split forehead attempted desperately to heal.","But when she sensed the extent of her lost power, when she felt the hollow emptiness where her authority had been...","She wailed with voice that shattered the remaining composure she possessed.","\" MY ORDER! MY GLORIOUS ORDER! YOU HAVE TAKEN EVERYTHING FROM ME! EVERYTHING! ALL MY EVERYTHINGS! I WANT YOU DEAD! I WANT YOU COLLAPSED INTO NOTHINGNESS!\"","Tears of white-gold blood streamed down her face.","\"O CREATURE! FOR THE LAST PROMISE! FOR MY FINAL WISH! I WISH FOR THE COMPLETE AND TOTAL COLLAPSE OF OSMONT! IN THIS EXISTENCE, IN YOUR EXISTENCE, HE CANNOT BE ALLOWED TO REMAIN! COLLAPSE HIM! COLLAPSE HIM! COLLAPSE HIM NOW!\"","Her screams echoed with desperate finality as she spent her last protection.","The words of THE Dead Order seemed like the ravings of a mad woman.","But she had lost absolutely everything as she had nothing else left to cling to.","Noah’s expression was heavy as he remembered the unstoppable force that had pulled him away from her just moments ago.","Just when he had been about to extract the last remaining waves of authority from her fractured existence.","That unstoppable force and momentum was none other than Existence itself.","It had felt like the very structure of reality around him flared with overwhelming power.","Even musings of The First Tongue had surged to cause absolute and undeniable separation between him and THE Dead Order.","If that was the result of a single wish from this being, and she now wished for his complete collapse...","His eyes burned with a sense of defiance and lividity once more.","His entire existence became covered by defensive Logos of The First Tongue as he prepared for what might come.","The Phonemes of Void, Darkness, and Paradox wove together to create conceptual shields.","The Phonemes of Unity and Division combined to make his existence both unified against attack and divided enough to survive fragmentation.","The Phoneme of Beginning prepared rapid regeneration if needed.","In the distance, the raving figure of THE Dead Order wailed and cried with voice breaking.","She kept her tear-streaked gaze fixed upon him, desperately waiting to witness his collapse.","Beside Noah, the figure of Sigrid, soon to be THE Living Order in full manifestation, moved to stand protectively at his side.","THE Civilizational Authority of Order flowing through her newly empowered existence began spreading outward.","White-gold streams of authority covered Noah as well, creating additional layers of protection around him.","Her expression showed fierce determination to defend what was hers.","As they all waited with mounting tension for the terrifying response from Existence itself...","No response came.","Silence descended across the space.","The Weavings of THE Dead Order began shining with a maddening light of pure lunacy as the silence stretched.","She roared out again with voice cracking from strain and desperation.","\"I SAID FOR MY LAST WISH I WISH HIM TO BE COLLAPSED! YOU PROMISED THIS TO ME! WHEN I FELL TO PARADOX, WHEN I LOST EVERYTHING THE FIRST TIME, YOU PROMISED ME! WILL YOU NOT KEEP YOUR PROMISE?!\"","Her voice became even more desperate and broken.","\"YOU PROMISED ME INFINITY! YOU PROMISED ME HAPPINESS! YOU PROMISED ME RESTORATION! WILL YOU NOT EVEN GIVE ME THAT AMIDST ALL THIS MISERY?! AFTER EVERYTHING I HAVE LOST?! AFTER ALL I HAVE SACRIFICED?!\"","She wailed and cried as she spoke the last few words, her entire being trembling with grief and rage.","Tears of white-gold blood continued streaming down her fractured face.","And yet, shockingly, there was still no response from Existence itself.","No force descended to collapse Noah.","No power manifested to fulfill her wish.","Only profound silence answered her desperate pleas.","Moments later, amidst her teary face and wailing Weavings of existence, a different power descended.","Multicolored flames of Existence wrapped around THE Dead Order’s broken form.","And this unique power began taking her away from this space entirely like cradling a broken child.","Removing her to some unknown location.","It was a unique scene to observe.","Because shockingly, impossibly, THE Creature did not accomplish the wish of THE Dead Order to collapse Noah!","Her final promise, her last desperate request, went unfulfilled.","Why?","The eyes of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons pulsed with Fragments of Phonemes of The First Tongue as he contemplated many possible answers.","Had THE Creature decided Noah was more valuable alive than dead?","Had the closed temporal loop made Noah’s existence somehow essential to maintain?","Had THE Creature gained too much from Noah’s actions to risk collapsing him now?","Or was there some other game being played that Noah could not yet perceive?","The questions swirled through his mind as he analyzed the implications.","THE Dead Order had not fully collapsed by his hands as he had intended.","But he had obtained all that he truly needed from her.","Ninety percent of her Civilizational Authority now resided in Sigrid.","Enough to forge THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty for The Living Order.","Enough to restore the true Primordial Civilization of Order under his guidance.","So at this moment, Noah put his hands gently around the waist of Sigrid.","He pulled her close as he spoke with quiet certainty.","\" Let’s go.\"","A moment later, their manifestations in this space between spaces disappeared.","And this manifested space itself, no longer sustained by THE Dead Order’s presence and authority, began crumbling and folding into nothingness.","The veil that had separated Living and Dead Order dissolved.","The entire constructed reality collapsed back into the fundamental Weavings from which it had been formed.","Leaving only scattered traces of what had occurred here.","And the unanswered question of why THE Creature had refused THE Dead Order’s final wish."]},{"number":4641,"title":"Chapter 4641: Chapter 4640: Actualization V","paragraphs":["Nobody knew the future.","Not truly.","Even those who believed they knew, even those who fooled themselves into thinking they could predict what was coming with certainty, they were only looking at possibilities and potentials.","In Existence, nobody absolutely knew the future with complete certainty.","It was so terrifying and unpredictable that if an entity from the future traveled back and told someone in the past a few specific things that would be happening later on, they would shake their heads in disbelief.","As if they were listening to the words of an absolutely insane person.","If days ago, if a few weeks ago when Noah first met Moiraine in a certain prison after his Weavings led there from being embroiled with Little Bobby’s schemes, when he had only just begun learning about THE Living Existences from her and started listening to the Stories of The Earliest Folds, about THE Creature and how he supposedly met Origin, Concept, and Paradox in grand encounters...","Which all turned out to be utter bullshit now that he knew the truth.","But if at that time, someone had come to him and said:","\"Oh yeah, days from now, you will actually glimpse THE Creature in person. You’ll talk with THE Living Order and form a connection. You’ll be nearly caught by THE Living Temporal during temporal traversal. And then somehow, your actions across time will actually cause Infinite Potential to bloom from a closed temporal loop and allow THE Living Origin, who was collapsed eons ago, to be coming back to existence. And oh, there’s even THE First Hunger returning alongside her.\"","If someone had approached Noah back then and told him all of this with complete seriousness, he would have looked at them as if they were absolutely nuts.","As if to ask: how the hell would things somehow evolve and progress to that level of insanity in a matter of mere days or even weeks?","It would have seemed impossible. Utterly incredulous.","Nobody knew the future with certainty.","Nobody knew how things would fully unfold or what paths reality would take.","But the one constant that remained, the one truth that endured, was that the future would unfathomably be glorious in ways that nobody would ever come to understand until they lived it in the present moment.","Things that would have been deemed utterly incredulous and completely unfathomable mere weeks ago were happening right now, in this very instant.","And who knew what things that were considered impossible at this moment in time would be occurring days or weeks from now?","What new impossibilities would become reality?","Noah did not know and could not say with absolute surety.","But at this time, he opened his eyes in that region of collapse once more.","From his people gathered among the armored Primus Inevitabilities, Sigrid took a step and instantly appeared beside him.","Her body continued radiating increasingly grand levels of power.","The aura of THE was slowly building within her existence, becoming more defined and concentrated with each passing moment.","Khor, The First Farmer, Alexander Asmodeus, and all the others couldn’t help but turn to stare with shock.","Such a sudden eruption of power represented far too much immensity to ignore.","But at this time, Noah acted with decisive purpose.","He began weaving together a complex Logos using multiple Core Phonemes of The First Tongue.","The Phoneme of Void to create conceptual emptiness that could not be perceived through.","The Phoneme of Darkness to conceal what occurred within from outside observation.","The Phoneme of Space to establish proper dimensional boundaries.","The Phoneme of Division to separate inside from outside completely.","The Phoneme of Unity to bind all the concealment effects together seamlessly.","The Phoneme of Order to maintain the structure’s integrity.","The Phoneme of Beginning to initiate the isolation.","These seven Phonemes wove together into a Logos of tremendous complexity that most closely translated to: \"In void and darkness, space divides and unites with ordered beginning to conceal.\"","The Logos flowed outward from Noah’s position, expanding rapidly to surround the entire region of collapse.","A blue-gold veil wrapped around this entire area like a crystalline dome.","It ensured that everything happening within would not be visible to entities observing from outside.","It isolated the space entirely so that any authorities erupting here would not be detected by other powers.","Not by THE Living Paradox observing from THE Loom.","Not by any other entities watching for signs of unusual activity.","Even the jailed figures contained in prisons formed with blue-gold bars were moved.","Schrodinger with his broken body.","The Disciple of THE Creature in his cage.","The captured Guiders of Order.","All of them were placed outside of this veiled domain so they could not witness what was about to unfold.","Noah accomplished all of this with immense calmness and methodical precision.","Then he focused his attention on the vibrant trembling singularities of Hunger and Origin floating before him.","He was watching the power of Infinite Potential that his lineage represented begin to show itself fully.","He was witnessing what it truly meant to be THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons.","The First Tongue held countless possibilities and wonders as it was the answer to The Fallout and all other existential problems.","And even as THE Living Paradox deemed that it was now five seconds to midnight, Noah’s gaze contained profound defiance.","He would be ready for whatever came.","He WAS ready.","He had himself, who could take down THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities before he even officially grasped this classification himself.","And he could be considered to have fifteen such entities contained within THE Infinite Desmoterion as prisoners contributing to his power!","And to top it all off at this very moment...","Prompts descended before his vision.","|Emergence Sequence - Initiating|","| The Seed of THE First Hunger is actualizing from Infinite Potential|","|The Seed of THE Living Origin is actualizing from Infinite Potential|","|Source: Closed Temporal Loop completing causality cycle|","|Mechanism: Your influence on their Weavings in The Infinite Unfurling preserved in The First Tongue|","|Timeline: Immediate manifestation|","| THE First Hunger - Tor|","|Classification Upon Emergence: THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Memory Status: Complete retention of all experiences|","|Loyalty Assessment: Strong positive connection to your Way|","| THE Living Origin|","|Classification Upon Emergence: THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Memory Status: Complete retention of all experiences|","|Loyalty Assessment: Strong positive connection to your Way|","At this moment, the cocoons of singularities surrounded by all eighteen Core Phonemes of The First Tongue seethed with unfathomable and infinite potential.","The aura of a terrifying entity began blazing outward from within them with building intensity.","The cocoons trembled and pulsed as the Phonemes glowed brighter and brighter.","Alongside the eruption of these overwhelming auras, a voice suddenly echoed out.","\" Oh, what the shit is this now? I was sleeping in endless Hunger so soundly and peacefully...\"","The voice was unique and ancient, carrying weight of eons and a casual irreverence that seemed utterly out of place given the circumstances.","The moment it emerged, the figure of Khor began trembling violently.","Her eyes went wide as tears started forming and streaming down her small face.","Her millions of obsidian jaws froze in place as her entire being focused on that voice.","The cocoon surrounded by radiant Weavings of The First Tongue began breaking apart.","Cracks of brilliant light spread across its surface as the singularity within reached critical manifestation.","And from it, the visage of Tor walked out with casual confidence.","He had an ancient and wild appearance that spoke of primordial power barely contained.","His long obsidian hair danced wildly on his head as if each strand possessed independent life.","Shadowy weavings of pure Hunger wrapped around his muscular figure like living tattoos.","His body radiated raw physical power, muscles defined but not bulky, lean and dangerous.","He looked like a primordial beast that had been sleeping for eons and had now returned to Existence with full might.","He blinked slowly as he looked around, taking in his surroundings with curiosity.","His gaze swept across the veiled domain before coming to lock onto Noah specifically.","His jaw opened in shock as recognition flared in his eyes.","\" Little Anomaly? What... how are you...\"","Before his words could even finish, the diminutive figure of Khor threw herself into his chest with desperate velocity.","She crashed into him and wrapped her arms around him as tightly as she could manage.","Tor looked down at her with expression softening immediately.","He spoke with natural affection as if no time had passed at all.","\" Ah, Little Monster. I was going to come take a look at you soon regardless. Relax! I’m here now.\"","He wrapped his arms around her small form and held her as she sobbed against his chest.","Two embodiments of Hunger embraced as eons of separation finally ended.","At the same time, from the second cocoon filled with white-gold Weavings of Origin, another emergence began.","The structure broke apart with graceful inevitability.","And THE Living Origin stepped forth with unfathomable majesty that made reality itself seem to pause.","She was unfathomably beautiful in ways that transcended simple physical appearance.","Her white-gold hair flowed like liquid light down past her shoulders.","Her skin was fair and seemed to glow with inner radiance.","Her golden eyes held endless depth, as if one could peer into them and see the origin point of all things.","She wore robes that seemed woven from the concept of beginnings themselves.","Her terrifying power at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty pulsed outward in waves.","She took a single step forward as her eyes looked around Existence with analytical gaze.","Taking in the veiled domain, the gathered entities, the state of reality.","Before her gaze finally locked onto Noah with focused intensity.","THE Living Origin. THE First Hunger.","Infinite Potential had been actualized into concrete reality.","This represented one of the first terrifying actions that THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons was taking.","Beside Noah floated THE Living Order, Sigrid, her own power still building toward THE classification.","And at this moment, a surreal reality existed within this contained domain of space.","Surrounded by veiled Weavings of The First Tongue.","Three THE Surface Depth entities stood within arm’s reach.","All connected to Noah’s Way.","And uniquely...THE was not suppressed by Existence!"]},{"number":4642,"title":"Chapter 4642: Chapter 4641: Half My Weight!","paragraphs":["In Existence, many believed connections with others weren’t important.","That they could accomplish everything themselves through sheer individual will and power.","That bonds were weaknesses to avoid rather than strengths to cultivate.","While this approach could work in some cases, the truth was simpler: connections ruled Existence at the deepest levels.","Consider Ains, The Fisherman.","He’d formed connections with Ul’moreth and the other Ginnu Lifeforms across countless eons.","When THE Primordial Chaos arrived to test him with impossible choices, those connections meant Ains chose sacrifice over self-preservation.","He gave a warning. He tried to protect those he’d bonded with across time.","Or Ul’moreth himself, THE Primeval Titan.","He’d forged a teaching bond with Noah in Ginnungagap.","When the moment of crisis arrived, when THE Primordial Chaos held Noah’s hand in that terrible grip, Ul’moreth burned his very Way of Primordial Continuity to switch places with his student.","The connection between teacher and student proved stronger than survival instinct.","Or examine THE Creature’s own actions.","He’d allowed Noah to complete his Temporal Traversal not out of mercy, but because of the connections Noah had forged.","Those connections meant Noah’s influence had spread to entities who would be locked in The Belly of Existence. THE Belly of Existence!","Entities whose enhanced cultivation across eons would benefit THE Creature himself through the connection of imprisonment.","Even THE Living Origin’s collapse by THE Living Paradox had come about because of connections.","Her backing of THE Creature had created chances that Paradox exploited.","Connections shaped outcomes at every level of power.","While you didn’t absolutely need bonds or connections to succeed in Existence, they certainly made the path easier, more stable, and stronger.","Isolation wasn’t strength. It was just isolation.","---","In the isolated region of collapse where Noah had layered waves of Logos to create a veiled domain, the air hummed with building power.","His existence was being reinforced by waves of boundless harvest and Infinite Potential stemming from his actions and their cascading consequences, and he stared at another manifestation of that same Potential made flesh.","Tor and THE Living Origin.","Two entities who shouldn’t exist in this era, now standing before him because of the closed temporal loop he’d created.","Tor had his attention taken by Khor, who still clung to him with desperate relief.","Meanwhile, THE Living Origin stared straight at Noah with a gaze mixing confusion and deep serenity.","This was an entity who’d been collapsed by THE Living Paradox himself.","One of those who should have enjoyed the Weavings of The Belly of Existence, of THE Prison where THE Creature locked everything within The Infinite Unfurling.","That alone should have made her incredibly powerful across the eons.","And yet THE Living Paradox had still managed to collapse her even with all the accumulated power that THE Creature’s prison had granted her.","That single fact said a lot about the true power and schemes of THE Living Paradox.","At this time, THE Living Origin finally made her move.","She looked at Noah with those endless golden eyes and spoke. Eons weighed down every word.","\" Existence is filled with mysteries beyond counting. But there are only a select few entities who are truly capable of fighting against and controlling the flow of Existence itself. By doing what you’re doing, by bringing us back from Infinite Potential, by challenging the established order, you’re placing yourself among the ranks of those who seek to hold Existence in their palms.\"","She paused before continuing with building intensity.","\" THE Creature. THE Living Paradox. THE Primordial Chaos. THE Living Temporal. THE Secretive Eon. THE Tongue Whisper. You would be seeking to climb to the ranks of these supreme beings who shape reality itself. Are you that type of being? Are you HIM?\"","Was he HIM?","The question carried serious weight in the context of Existence.","To be HIM meant more than simple power or classification.","It meant having the conviction that you could reshape reality according to your vision.","It meant believing with absolute certainty that your Way was correct and worth any sacrifice.","It meant standing against impossible odds and refusing to yield regardless of consequence.","It meant being the type of entity around which Existence itself would have to bend and reorganize.","Noah thought about the question for a brief moment before responding with calm certainty.","\"I am HIM.\"","HUUM!","He said this with unwavering confidence that allowed no room for doubt or hesitation.","His eyes blazed with absolute conviction as the words emerged.","THE Living Origin nodded slowly a moment later, as if his response confirmed something she’d suspected.","\"In the past, I listened to another entity tell me the exact same thing with the same conviction. I followed him with complete loyalty. I believed him without reservation. And yet despite all that belief and backing, I was still collapsed by Paradox. Perhaps I should have never followed another’s vision. Perhaps I should have trusted only my own Way. But now, it’s far too late for such regrets. I’ve become cautious now through painful experience.\"","Her expression became more guarded.","\"Even though I understand that every action has a reaction, that causality demands equal exchange, I still have to be careful. I still have to be absolutely certain before committing fully. So for now, as gratitude for bringing my Way and Existence back to bloom in this era, I’ll give half of the Weight of my Way towards your brilliance. Towards your vision and your Way.\"","She held up one hand as if making a formal declaration.","\"If you allow me to observe your actions for a while longer, if you demonstrate that your vision truly differs from what came before, then I’ll decide whether to completely give my full weight and backing to you without reservation.\"","HUUM!","The words were heavy with implication.","An immense brilliance erupted around Noah as reality responded to her declaration.","Prompts descended before his vision.","|Backing Received - THE Living Origin|","| THE Living Origin has placed half of her backing, half of the Immensity of her Way, in support of your vision|","|Classification: Partial Backing of THE Surface Depth entity|","|Weight Added to Your Existence: Tremendous|","|Effects of Partial Backing:|","|- Your Existential Weight increased quintessentially|","|- Your Civilizational Authority enhanced quintessentially|","|- Your Way of Mana and Hunger resonates with her Way of Origin|","|- All entities in your Civilization receive 120% boost to advancement speed|","|- Your Foundation stability increased by 890%|","|Lineage Integration:|","| THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons has recognized the significance of this backing|","|The meaning and importance of this action is being transformed into Infinite Potential|","|This Potential flows toward your Foundation and Way of Existence|","...!"]},{"number":4643,"title":"Chapter 4643: Chapter 4642: Crossing A Line","paragraphs":["The Prompts continued with an unending momentum!","|Historical Context - WARNING:|","| THE Living Origin previously gave her backing to THE Creature before her collapse|","|The effects of her backing toward THE Creature across eons were substantial|","|It is unknown what cascading effects will bloom now that her backing is directed toward you|","|Even though this backing is currently partial (50%), it may draw attention from interested parties|","|Additional Note:|","|When/If THE Living Origin grants full backing (100%), the effects will exceed current parameters by orders of magnitude|","As Noah watched these prompts cascade down before his vision, his eyes maintained their heavy brilliance.","He simply nodded with calm acceptance and spoke with measured certainty.","\" My Way is mine, and I’ll move as I see fit according to my own vision. If you agree with my actions and choices, that’s good for both of us. If you don’t agree at some point, that’s also fine. But I do have a lot of questions for you about what happened in The Infinite Unfurling and what you know of THE Creature’s true plans.\"","As he said all this, off to the side, Tor finally pulled Khor away from his chest.","He held her at arm’s length with both hands, examining her with a critical eye.","The obsidian skin and wild hair of this ancient being danced with shadowy Hunger as he spoke with a booming voice.","\" What is all this official diplomatic bullshit?! When you commit to something, Origin, just do it completely! What’s the need for all this righteous posturing of ’ooh, I have to carefully watch you first and cautiously decide, ooh!’ Do it simply! Do it easily and directly!\"","He turned his gaze toward Noah.","\" The Little Anomaly has allowed my Hunger to bloom once more in this era and protected Little Monster here while I was gone, even though she seems disappointingly weak after all the potential I left her with. When you commit to something, Origin, commit FULLY like you used to! I always told you this back in the old days!\"","He raised his voice with passionate intensity.","\"Say it simply and clearly like this: I give the FULL weight of my Way towards the Little Anomaly without reservation! I’ll witness what his unique vision of Existence will become! Because the vision that THE Creature and Paradox and Chaos are pushing fucking SUCKS and leads only to collapse and imprisonment!\"","HUUM!","THE First Hunger said such provocative words with complete conviction.","THE Living Origin calmly stared at him. She’d clearly heard such passionate speeches many times before.","And Tor only smiled and laughed with booming sound.","Right after his declaration, an eruption of even grander waves of brilliant blue-gold light bloomed around Noah!","New prompts descended with overwhelming significance.","|Full Backing Received - THE First Hunger|","| Tor, THE First Hunger, has given the complete weight of his Way of Hunger in support of your vision|","|Classification: Full Backing of THE Surface Depth entity|","|Weight Added to Your Existence: Monumental|","|Effects of Full Backing:|","|- Your Existential Weight increased quintessentially|","|- Your Way of Mana and Hunger resonates PERFECTLY with his Way of Hunger|","|- Your Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect principles amplified by 890%|","|The backing is contributing to the emergence of more harvests of Infinite Potential.|","|Combined Backing Assessment:|","|You now possess:|","|- Full Backing (100%) from THE First Hunger|","|- Partial Backing (50%) from THE Living Origin|","|Combined Effect: Your Existential Weight has crossed critical threshold|","|CRITICAL MILESTONE ACHIEVED:|","|The immense concentration of Infinite Potential from multiple sources has reached critical mass|","|Sources:|","|- Harvest from Temporal Traversal causality (Lumivara, Ains, Ul’moreth, and countless others across eons)|","|- Full Backing from THE First Hunger|","|- Partial Backing from THE Living Origin|","|- Your Lineage as THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons|","|All Infinite Potential flowing into:|","|- THE Foundation of The First Tongue (primary destination)|","|- Formation of your unique Core Phonemes (primary destination)|","|- Reinforcement of your Way of Existence (primary destination)|","|UNPRECEDENTED ACHIEVEMENT:|","|The weight and immensity of your existence has crossed the threshold of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|DESPITE not having officially claimed THE distinction or classification|","| Your Existential Weight at Pre-THE classification can now rival genuine THE Surface Depth entities|","|This is deemed: Paradoxical and Unprecedented|","|Current Status:|","|Immense concentrations of Infinite Potential from all sources continue flowing|","|Your Way is being refined continuously|","|Your Foundation is being reinforced beyond theoretical limits|","|Your unique Core Phonemes are being forged|","|Core Phoneme Formation Progress:|","|The Core Phoneme of Quintessence: 94% complete|","|Estimated Time to Completion: Minutes|","|Note: This will be the first entirely new Core Phoneme created in Observable History|","|Warning: Creation will be noticed by all masters of The First Tongue across Existence|","BOOM!","Noah felt the transformation happening within his existence at the most fundamental level.","The sensation was hard to describe, yet he tried to understand what was happening.","It felt like crossing an invisible threshold into an entirely new way of seeing.","His vision began slowly changing as the weight of THE Surface Depth settled into his being.","He started seeing everything differently.","Not as solid objects or separate entities, but as waves and strings vibrating with their own unique frequencies.","Each entity, each piece of matter, each expression of authority appeared as complex patterns of vibration.","These countless individual vibrations came together, harmonizing and interfacing, to form what made up Existence itself.","He could perceive... the fundamental frequency of Mana underlying everything.","He could sense the linguistic resonance of The First Tongue structuring reality.","He could observe how different Ways created different vibrational patterns that either harmonized or clashed with each other.","It was as if a veil had been lifted from his perception, allowing him to see the true machinery of reality operating beneath the surface appearance.","This was what it meant to approach THE.","To perceive Existence not as it appeared, but as it fundamentally was.","And he’d achieved this perception without even officially grasping THE classification yet.","What would happen when he actually crossed that final threshold?"]},{"number":4644,"title":"Chapter 4644: Chapter 4643: And Then There Was You I","paragraphs":["As Noah acclimated to the new sense of power coursing through him, Tor and THE Living Origin seemed to sense the shift.","The former continued with casual interest as he spoke.","\" You and others like you always like to do things with flair and fashion. You haven’t truly grasped any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, and yet the immensity of your existence seems to have reached it anyway. I used to take you to fight weak little things that had just laid a claim on their Sovereignty, but do you think you could fight against me now, Little Anomaly?\"","Tor asked such a question in a completely carefree manner.","Noah looked back at this entity that had given him his backing and nodded calmly.","\" That is among the many things that we can do. And there’s a lot to be done.\"","Tor blinked at this reply.","He looked around at Noah and all the others gathered in this veiled space.","In the next moment, his expression shifted to confusion.","\" Why all the sense of doom and gloom here? What’s happening right now?\"","What was happening right now?","Noah took this question in calmly as he answered.","\" THE Living Paradox and others formed THE Loom, a shelter and weapon, that’s going to collapse all external Existence and Civilization in what they call The Fallout at some indeterminate time. It could be hours or days or weeks or years from now. Survival against The Fallout was a serious question a few days ago, but now... I have a level of confidence towards it. I just need to make sure that all my preparations are ready.\"","BOOM!","He said such words with calm certainty.","THE First Hunger looked at him with mounting incredulity before gazing at Khor as if he wanted her to confirm this insanity.","Khor nodded with a cloudy face and seemed about to say something else when, at this moment, THE Living Origin calmly inserted herself into the conversation.","\" Well... THE Loom is actually a Key. A key that THE Living Paradox designed to unlock THE Belly of Existence, the prison under the warden of...THE Creature that holds countless entities from The Infinite Unfurling. Its full scope of action will be unknown. But its eruption would mean that THE Living Paradox is ready to begin his fight against THE Creature with this weapon, to tear across The Belly of Existence to do whatever it was designed to do. And likely all of those imprisoned in The Infinite Unfurling will also be released.\"","BOOM!","She paused before continuing with heavy words.","\" But it was made with my Heart of Origin and Weavings of others that supported THE Creature. And of course... the Heart of Hunger.\"","BOOM!","Terrifying words were uttered from her mouth.","Noah looked at her closely before he spoke.","\" Alright, this is why we need to have a proper talk. Let’s- \"","Before Noah’s words could finish, THE First Hunger interjected.","His expression turned cloudy as obsidian crimson light began dancing around his frame.","The shadows of Hunger writhing across his skin intensified into something more volatile.","His voice came out flat and dangerous.","\" What do you mean the Heart of Hunger was utilized in its forging?\"","Silence came.","When this entity asked this question, Noah reserved answering it himself.","He turned his attention towards the one that THE First Hunger called Little Monster.","Khor.","At this time, this diminutive figure of the ancient entity looked towards Tor with a cold gaze.","As if she was laying out her grievances to an older member of her family.","As if she’d been waiting eons to say these words.","\" THE Living Paradox collapsed my Way and Civilization as he used my Heart of Hunger, my Primacy of Hunger, to fuse and mutate all the countless Inevitabilities into the walls of his Loom. For the past eons, Inevitabilities have been forced to hunger and hunger endlessly , never keeping any of the authority that they take in as it all goes towards supporting THE Loom . Every single Inevitability without question was mutated and forced to experience this endless sense of unsatisfied hunger.\"","Her voice was steady but cold as ice.","\"My emergence was made possible by the Outsider here, and the current Inevitabilities that you see around us are the product of what we’ve managed to achieve as we forge a new Civilization of Hunger from the ruins.\"","Her words got to the core of the issue.","The body of THE First Hunger trembled.","An unfathomably dangerous aura radiated from him as it looked like he would explode at any moment.","The air itself seemed to warp around him as crimson shadows pulsed outward.","But then, moments later, he reached out towards Khor again and held her.","He stroked the hair on her head with surprising gentleness despite the rage building in his frame.","His eyes had turned pure crimson when he turned to look at Noah.","The carefree demeanor from just moments ago was completely gone.","In its place was immense coldness and barely contained fury.","\" You said you needed to prepare. What needs to be done so that sometime in the future, I can look at the face of THE Living Paradox and peel the skin from his existence? Slowly. Piece by piece. Until there’s nothing left but his screaming Weavings.\"","A sense of wildness and contained rage pulsed within THE First Hunger as he asked such a thing.","Even though they all knew how impossibly hard it would be to accomplish.","Even though THE Living Paradox was one of the supreme beings who controlled the flow of Existence itself.","Even though he’d collapsed both Origin and Hunger in the past and walked away unscathed.","But Noah nodded lightly.","He looked towards THE Living Origin as he spoke.","\" The first thing we need to do is get a good grasp of exactly what’s happening around us. Information. Knowledge. We need to understand the full scope of what we’re facing and what resources we actually have. \"","He turned his gaze fully to her.","\" Are you able to help us with this, Origin?\""]},{"number":4645,"title":"Chapter 4645: Chapter 4644: And Then There Was You II","paragraphs":["Noah wanted THE Living Origin to provide whatever knowledge she had.","He continued to come across the reality that you could do a whole lot more when you had the correct type of required knowledge.","Consider what he’d learned from Ul’moreth about Mana and The First Tongue.","That knowledge had allowed him to answer The Oldest Paradox of Existence and trigger his Lineage emergence.","Those eighteen Core Phonemes had become the foundation of his power and allowed him to accomplish feats that shouldn’t be possible at his classification.","Knowledge was power in the most literal sense, and he needed more of it.","So at this time, he and many others were looking at the famous figure of THE Living Origin.","Noah felt the hands of Sigrid grasping onto his as she looked towards THE Living Origin.","Her eyes shined brilliantly as if she was observing a living legend.","After all, even though at this moment Sigrid was THE Living Order , she was the one who’d been born in the Transcendent Origin Folds as a Living Origin.","She revered the stories and legends of THE Living Origin herself.","The sense of slight nervousness and anticipation in Sigrid’s eyes as she looked at THE Living Origin allowed Noah to ease somewhat from his serious state of mind.","It reminded him that even in the case of an apocalypse, he didn’t need to be so high-strung and serious.","He was HIM , right?","He moved with glorious quintessence and tyranny as he currently held a sense of confidence when it came to The Fallout.","So he would simply move accordingly and continue to live Existence as he wished to. As he normally would.","Because even as all of this was happening, he needed to make up for the lost time with many in The Infiniverse.","And of course, ensure that there would be more time with them after The Fallout.","But for now, he needed to continue getting back to his baseline Weavings of Existence.","The events of the Temporal Traversal were truly too heavy as he was still acclimating from them.","As he thought about this, the figure of THE Living Origin rose up.","Many eyes focused on her as she waved her hands to manifest an illusory white-gold diagram.","It depicted an 8-cube octeract hypercube with intricate geometric patterns.","She began to speak with measured clarity.","\" In The Infinite Unfurling, THE Creature had grand designs and ideals. He could see Existence was continuing to unfold with boundless Chaos, with no structure. At least this was what he told us. He wanted to form a structure, and one of the major issues was that there were too many damn THE entities. Each one sought to find and establish their Way of Existence. Each one essentially fighting for supremacy. It caused a tumultuous Existence with constant battles and conflict, not to mention the conflicts of The Oldest Paradox of Existence that included THE Creature and others.\"","She paused before continuing.","\" And so he gathered some of us. Those who he knew and those he didn’t. Apart from THE Creature, we took on the distinctions of THE Living Existences. THE Living Origin, THE Living Concept, THE Living Dimensional, THE Living Order... we all held grand ideals. And to be on the same page, we all held the distinction of Living apart from THE Creature. The solution that we eventually implemented was THE Prison. THE Unfurling Nodes of Existence. THE Belly of Existence that would contain all the countless entities seeking supremacy in their Civilizations... to usher in an extended period of Order where a select few would focus on their Civilizations and actually have a chance of ascending the scales of Existence.\"","The words from THE Living Origin were heavy.","Noah and the others listened with shining eyes.","And as if THE Living Origin could see into the brilliance of Noah’s eyes and what he was thinking, she continued right after.","\" Yes, how arrogant it was for us to think that way. What hubris we had to believe ourselves to be grander and that we had more right than others to elevate our Civilizations while imprisoning everyone else. But THE Creature was a convincing being. THE Creature was an undeniable being. Many of us convinced ourselves that those who would be contained in this prison wouldn’t be harmed as they would continue to follow their Ways of Existence in a contained space, and we would simply benefit from their advancements. So The Belly of Existence was formed. And all of Observable Existence became quieter. There were only a few glorious Civilizations moving across Existence...\"","As she said all of this, she turned to look towards THE First Hunger.","He had a cloudy expression while gazing at her.","She continued with a softer tone.","\" Because of me and Hunger coming together in The Infinite Unfurling due to your existence, I grew a soft spot for the buffoon there. I sought permission from THE Creature to exclude him from the imprisonment. Thus, Hunger was free. I just didn’t expect all that followed. The golden age of cultivation and elevation of Civilizations that we were all envisioning did start. We did make tremendous advancements as we benefited from The Belly of Existence. THE Creature ushered in an entire new lineage under his name... Early Creatures. There was a propagation of Hunger as Inevitabilities multiplied, and Living Existences bloomed in our image as we forged our Civilizations.\"","Her expression became darker.","\" But of course, inevitably, something happened. Everything began to break down the moment that THE Living Paradox collapsed THE Living Order.\"","THE Living Origin looked like she was about to continue when at this time, Noah spoke up.","\" Hold on, hold on.\"","He felt like he was missing some critical piece of information there.","He wanted to backtrack a little bit.","\" What of THE Primordial Chaos, THE Secretive Eon... were these entities that are seemingly on the same caliber as THE Creature also locked in The Belly of Existence?\"","It was a question that deserved an answer.","And at this time, THE Living Origin looked towards him and said simply.","\"I don’t know.\"","What?","\" What do you mean you don’t know? \" Noah couldn’t help but ask.","Once more, THE Living Origin shook her head and replied calmly.","\"I don’t know.\"","Noah’s eyes became even sharper.","He turned his gaze up and looked around the veiled space as his mind worked through the implications.","Does this mean that monstrous entities on the same level as THE Creature could actually be outside of the prison? Suppressed somewhere in Existence or hiding in the gaps of reality? Or were they still contained within The Belly of Existence but... they were strong enough that THE Creature couldn’t siphon off any of their power?"]},{"number":4646,"title":"Chapter 4646: Chapter 4645: And Then There Was You III","paragraphs":["There were far too many unknowns.","At this time, Noah shook his head as he motioned for THE Living Origin to continue.","She nodded simply as she spoke.","\"I don’t know what triggered it. I don’t know why Paradox rebelled. Maybe being at the same stature as THE Creature and enjoying part of the boons of The Belly of Existence was a trigger. Maybe due to their nature, this was always bound to happen. But regardless, conflict began to bloom. Civilizations were collapsed, and in secret THE Loom was forged. Emotive, that fucking bitch...\"","Woah woah woah.","Noah had to almost stop THE Living Origin from destroying her image there as she revealed some emotion.","She had Sigrid and others that were big fans of hers, and seeing the veil of majesty and power crack slightly as she expressed her emotions here was unique!","THE Living Origin seemingly calmed herself before she continued with more measured tones.","\"A lot happened, but the gist of it... I was collapsed, and THE Living Law was collapsed... some survived, some joined THE Living Paradox and Emotive... I don’t know the full history as many of them moved in secret. But in the end, it seems that THE Living Paradox somehow succeeded in going against THE Creature as his preparations are nearly finished. All of these eons should just be the preparations of THE Living Paradox as he needs to face off against THE Creature. Because THE Creature is terrifying and THE Creature is not something that anyone can overcome.\"","She paused with heavy emphasis.","\"And yet, paradoxically, THE Living Paradox lives up to his name. To overcome THE Creature. After all, they are all part of The Oldest Paradox of Existence. Of what came first. And Paradox is right there in the name. The rest of us were bound to be mere casualties in all of this. But now there is you. Or... there was you.\"","BOOM!","THE Living Origin looked towards Noah as if she was also trying to understand him.","As if he held his own oddities that couldn’t fully be explained!","Her golden eyes studied him with intense focus.","\" Because you appeared in the past, and you are here in the future. You are also a part of The Oldest Paradox of Existence. You were there... before The Belly of Existence which locked everyone away was made. You were also there before THE Loom was formed. You... are like The Others in this regard. Anomalies.\"","She said such ridiculous words.","In the next moment, many eyes turned towards Noah.","Khor, Sigrid, Moiraine, Henry, and many others adorned in Civilizational Armors in the ranks of Primus Inevitabilities all looked towards him with shining eyes.","As if he was some legendary figure.","Noah shook his head.","THE Living Origin was making him seem like some crazy big bad or scary entity when she said things like this.","He couldn’t even begin to explain the capability that allowed him to go back so far in time.","And the idea of closed temporal loops that even he had to read over a few times just to tell himself that he fully understood it.","He was just someone with a little bit of Mana.","If he was left alone and didn’t have to worry about the collapse of Existence ruining his life, he would be perfectly content to be a farmer in a remote region of Observable Existence.","He would be more than happy to tend to an Early Veiled Shore, plant Sacred Herbs, delve into unique Depths, and enjoy the company of his family.","But no.","THE Primordial Chaos had to do what he did.","THE Living Paradox had to do what he was doing.","And THE Creature had to do what he was doing.","So at this moment, Noah had to also do what he was doing.","Until a future came where he could look upon the endless Observable Existence and not have to worry about what could happen in the next moment.","Until he could actually live the quiet life he’d prefer.","So at this time, he nodded towards the figure of THE Living Origin before she could say anything else too crazy to make him seem grander than he was.","\" Okay. There may be a few smaller details here and there that I’ll ask you about, but for now let’s prepare. Let’s go to my own little Belly of Existence. My own Loom.\"","He said such words casually.","He began to emanate waves of Logos in the surrounding region, sensing his connection to The Infiniverse as he started forming a doorway.","Blue-gold light carved through space itself as The First Tongue structured reality according to his will.","The Phonemes of Space, Beginning, and Division wove together to create a passage.","There was much to be done, especially with THE Living Paradox stating that Existence was five seconds to Midnight.","He had Core Phonemes to design and complete.","A box from Ul’moreth to open that contained something important.","The Infiniverse needed continued development.","Sigrid required support as she approached THE Surface Depth.","Tor and THE Living Origin needed to be integrated into his Civilization properly.","The prisoners in THE Infinite Desmoterion needed evaluation.","His family and allies deserved time and attention after all that had happened.","And beyond all of that, he needed to forge a response to The Fallout that would ensure survival and perhaps even victory.","A lot more. So much more!","The doorway completed itself with a pulse of blue-gold radiance.","On the other side, many things awaited.","His Civilization. His people. His foundation for whatever came next.","Noah stepped forward as Sigrid’s hand remained clasped in his.","Tor followed with Khor still held protectively.","THE Living Origin moved with measured grace.","And one by one, the others began to file through.","Entering the domain that Noah had built, entering the space where preparations would be made...entering the future that he was forging with his own hands!","---","In Existence, many believed that fate was inescapable.","That the paths laid out by those with greater power couldn’t be deviated from.","That entities like THE Creature, THE Living Paradox, and THE Primordial Chaos moved pieces on a board where others had no agency.","This belief was comforting in a way.","If you had no choice, then you bore no responsibility for the outcome.","If the game was rigged from the start, then you couldn’t be blamed for losing.","But the truth was more complex and far more terrifying.","Fate existed, yes. But only as grand designs that were laid by supreme beings across eons.","Yet within those designs, choices remained.","Ains chose to save his friends even knowing it would cost him everything.","Ul’moreth chose to burn his Way to save a student he’d known for mere hours.","THE Living Origin chose to exclude Tor from imprisonment because of a soft spot.","THE Living Paradox chose rebellion against the established order.","And Noah chose to keep moving forward rather than accept the roles others tried to assign him.","Anomaly. Casualty. Pawn in games between existential entities.","These were labels others placed on him, but labels only had the power you gave them.","Every being in Existence, from the weakest to THE entities themselves, possessed the fundamental capability to choose.","To act according to their own vision rather than accept the vision imposed by others.","The question was never whether choice existed, the question was always whether you had the courage to make it.","Whether you had the strength to bear the consequences.","Whether you had the will to keep choosing even when every choice led to more complexity, more danger, more responsibility.","Noah had made his choice.","Not to be a farmer tending Sacred Herbs in peaceful obscurity. Not to accept the role of casualty in conflicts between supreme beings. Not to wait passively for The Fallout to determine his fate.","He chose to be HIM.","To forge his own path using The First Tongue and Mana, and some ridiculous cheats here and there to build something that could stand against The Fallout.","To protect those he cared about regardless of what entities at THE Surface Depth or beyond decided.","Was this arrogance? Perhaps.","Was this hubris? Possibly. Quintessentially! Majisterially!","Was this the only choice he could live with? Abso-fucking-lutely.","In Existence, fate was real. But so was choice. And the interplay between the two was where legends were born! The interplay between the two was where THE Genesis Monarch could move with interminable glory."]},{"number":4647,"title":"Chapter 4647: Chapter 4646: THE Farewell of Ginnungagap I","paragraphs":["Noah delved into The Infiniverse while thinking of the many things that had to be accomplished.","The idea of The Fallout was something he could look at in different ways.","If he looked at it like a blade hanging over his neck that could fall at any moment, he might never get anything done.","Others might feel a sense of pressure to the extent that things would feel suffocating.","But he put it in the back of his mind as he got ready to do the countless things that needed to be done.","Because why worry when he had no control of when Midnight came?","So for now...","HUUM !","His body flickered and divided into multiple bodies, each one disappearing into different domains.","One pulled back to the region of collapse with the imprisoned Schrodinger and The Disciple of THE Creature and others.","Others went elsewhere.","Moments later, he appeared with everyone in The Early Veiled Shore that was now unfathomably vast!","The brows of THE Living Origin rose as she looked at Noah up and down while staring at The Early Veiled Shore before she spoke.","\" Are you sure you aren’t THE Creature?\"","Noah didn’t even glance at her as he moved forward while speaking.","\" I’m sure I’m not THE Creature. Welcome to my Osmontian Shore. The bastion that will eventually stand against THE Loom. Settle in for now and acclimate. There are Sacred Herbs and Sacred Mead for everyone to enjoy. I have a few things to look at first. Malphas, can you take care of everyone?\"","The moment he finished speaking, the butler-like figure of Malphas appeared and bowed as he took over care of the new entrants!","Sigrid also sent a message that she would momentarily keep THE Living Origin company.","Noah nodded at this as he turned his gaze towards the visage of Elyndra and The First Farmer, who was currently gazing around with shining eyes!","The entity who planted Seeds of Principles.","He wanted to see what would happen if he actually had knowledge that he was playing with The First Tongue without knowing it.","Noah approached Elyndra and The First Farmer, who both turned their gazes towards him with shining eyes.","He put his hand around Elyndra’s waist and gave her a kiss on her forehead as he spoke softly.","\" Let me borrow your father for a second.\"","Elyndra smiled shyly while nodding with her head down.","The First Farmer had his mouth twitching as light wrapped around him and Noah.","And the two of them disappeared.","They reappeared far from The Early Veiled Shore, inside a budding Transcendent Helios Fold filled with crimson-gold plasma and lemniscate singularities.","Energy pulsed around them in rhythmic patterns.","In this space, The First Farmer scrubbed the image of Elyndra and Noah from his consciousness as he calmly spoke.","\"It seems much has changed since we last talked. I didn’t know you were a farmer as well.\"","Noah nodded lightly as he looked at this being while raising his hand.","He formed a concentrated bundle of knowledge regarding The First Tongue and the eighteen Core Phonemes.","Blue-gold light coalesced into a perfect sphere of information.","\" Causality is a unique thing. In the past, you forged the Seed of The Principle of Perpetual Harvest and failed. I completed that Seed for you. And now, I will expand your knowledge as I infuse you with understanding of The First Tongue that makes up all Principles. All the workings of Existence. The equations that explain how Existence flows the way it does. The fundamental linguistic structure underlying reality itself.\"","As he said this, The First Farmer’s eyes opened wide in shock.","But Noah moved swiftly to throw the singularity of knowledge forward.","It flowed into The First Farmer’s existence!","The eyes of The First Farmer trembled with shock, then recognition, then pure ecstasy.","His entire body began to glow with building radiance.","His breathing became rapid as eons of effort and failure suddenly made sense.","BOOM!","From his body, a Phoneme of Fire began to be constructed!","Brilliant green-gold flames erupted around him as linguistic structures manifested in the air.","The ancient patterns of The First Tongue bloomed from his Weavings.","Prompts descended before Noah’s vision.","|Anomalous Factor of Existence Detected|","|Entity: The First Farmer|","| Anomalous Factor Classification: THE SEED|","|Definition - Anomalous Factor of Existence:|","|Unique configurations within an entity’s Weavings that grant exceptional potential beyond normal parameters of Existence|","|These factors remain dormant until specific conditions trigger their awakening|","|Once awakened, they provide exponential advancement in specialized domains|","| The First Farmer’s Anomalous Factor - THE SEED: Innate capability to perceive, nurture, and cultivate abstract concepts as if they were living organisms|","|This factor has remained partially dormant for eons|","|The First Farmer has unknowingly been manipulating Logos of The First Tongue through his factor|","|Without understanding the linguistic foundation, his success rate was minimal|","|Condition Met: Exposure to complete knowledge of the 18 Core Phonemes|","|AWAKENING SEQUENCE - COMPLETE|","|The Weavings of The First Farmer bloom after eons of failure and effort|","|After associating with Weavings of The First Tongue for countless ages without recognizing it|","|After failing and succeeding in nurturing abstract Logos of Principles|","|All this accumulated potential has now been culminated and unleashed|","|Harvest Assessment:|","|A Harvest of significant Infinite Potential has been collected from The First Farmer due to the effect of your actions|","|This Potential flows toward your Foundation and Core Phoneme development|","...!","Noah watched the scene before him with shining eyes as he thought about the information regarding Anomalous Factor of Existence.","Would him awakening to Infinite Mana all those years ago be considered his Anomalous Factor?","Or could he not even put himself on the same scale as others?","He couldn’t say for sure.","But at this time, he sat down while watching the dazed First Farmer erupt with ridiculous talent to design his first Phoneme.","The ancient entity’s body blazed with green-gold flames as linguistic structures formed and reformed around him.","And while The First Farmer did this, this body of Noah here would have a simple job.","\" Focus the Infinite Potential on getting my own personalized Phonemes completed and finalize the analysis of which connected Logos make up my Principles so we can take them to Genesis level.\"","BOOM!","|Understood, Master.|","The reply from Ruination came swiftly as his body began to explode with power.","At the same time, his chest began to shine as he pulled out THE Farewell of Ginnungagap!","The glorious obsidian-gold box materialized in his hands.","It was filled with unfathomable Weavings of ancientness and majesty.","Complex patterns covered every surface, pulsing with preserved power.","The craftsmanship alone spoke of mastery that transcended normal understanding.","Noah looked at it with shining eyes.","The farewell gift from his teacher.","He sighed as he moved to open it, wondering just what might be packed within.","What would Ul’moreth, THE Primeval Titan, consider important enough to give as a final gift?"]},{"number":4648,"title":"Chapter 4648: Chapter 4647: THE Farewell of Ginnungagap II","paragraphs":["Who didn’t love opening gifts?","Ever since entering dungeons on the Blue Planet and opening treasure chests, obtaining the Concept of Loot and gaining access to Loot Crates, Loot Caches, and other wondrous forms of treasure, Noah felt giddy whenever opening any box of rewards.","The anticipation of what might be inside never got old.","The possibility of something extraordinary always made his heart race just a little faster.","And this particular gift was uniquely special as it stemmed from THE Primeval Titan, Ul’moreth himself!","The one who’d taught him The First Tongue.","The one who’d sacrificed his Way of Primordial Continuity to save Noah from THE Primordial Chaos’ grasp.","Obsidian-gold light shone from the top of this chest as Noah placed his Primus Mana into it.","And shockingly, the box began to react with building radiance.","The light intensified as complex Weavings activated across its surface.","Gradually, an illusory obsidian-gold image began to emerge.","The form solidified into the towering figure of THE Primeval Titan himself, Ul’moreth!","WAA!","Eight hundred meters tall even in this manifestation, his body constructed from living hairy stone and pulsing with ancient power.","His eyes glowed with the same warm intensity Noah remembered.","Noah looked at him with shining eyes as this manifestation looked back and smiled sadly.","The expression held both pride and regret.","|I wish I could have given you the rest of the lessons in person, but... circumstances must have proven to be impossible, so here we are.|","The manifestation’s voice resonated in The First Tongue directly, each word a pulse of structured Mana.","|I talked with you a great deal about Phonemes and a bit about Logos during our brief time together, but I didn’t really get a chance to delve into Philology. I taught you the letters and the words of The First Tongue, but I didn’t teach you the sentences. I didn’t teach you the grammar that allows those sentences to reshape Existence itself.|","Ul’moreth’s manifestation raised one massive hand as blue-gold light began gathering around it.","|Let me explain what Philology truly is. You’ve learned the eighteen Core Phonemes. You’ve formed Logos by combining those Phonemes with intent. But Philology... Philology is the deepest grammatical structure that governs how Logos themselves form.|","The manifestation began pacing as if this were still a classroom lesson.","|Think of it this way. Phonemes are individual letters. Logos are words formed from those letters. But Philology...Philology is the syntax. The underlying rules that determine what is possible within The First Tongue. Not individual words, but the fundamental structure that allows words to exist and have meaning.|","Noah listened with absolute focus as his teacher continued.","|I won’t ramble on too much but...when you form a Logos, you combine Phonemes in a specific order with specific intent. But the order matters tremendously. The same Phonemes arranged differently create entirely different effects. This is syntax. The relationship between the Phonemes determines the ultimate meaning.|","Ul’moreth manifested several Phonemes in the air.","Fire, Water, and Beginning floated before Noah’s vision.","| Watch closely. If I arrange these as: Beginning, Fire, Water...|","The Phonemes aligned and pulsed with specific rhythm.","A small flame appeared that gradually transformed into steam.","| The meaning is: ’What begins as fire becomes water.’ A transformation from one state to another.|","Then the Phonemes rearranged themselves.","| But if I arrange them as: Fire, Beginning, Water...|","The same Phonemes now pulsed with different rhythm.","Steam appeared first, then condensed into water, which erupted into flame.","| Now the meaning is: ’Fire initiates water’s beginning.’ The causal relationship has completely reversed. Same components, entirely different effect. This is the power of syntax.|","Noah’s eyes widened as he absorbed the lesson.","|Logos can also be conjugated to change their properties. You can modify tense to make effects occur in past, present, or future. You can adjust intensity to make them weak or devastatingly strong. You can alter scope to make them affect a single target or the entire scope of Existence.|","BOOM!","The manifestation demonstrated by taking a simple Logos of Fire and showing how subtle variations in the pulse patterns changed it from a small flame to an inferno, from a current blaze to a future ignition, from a localized effect to an existential one.","| And just as words combine into sentences, Logos can combine into compound structures. Multiple Logos woven together create complex ’sentences’ that achieve sophisticated effects impossible with single words alone.|","Ul’moreth’s expression became more serious.","|What you need to understand is that each Sovereignty you’ve encountered - Storm, Hunger, Order, Chaos - these are essentially dialects of The First Tongue. Specialized vocabularies optimized for specific expressions but inherently limited in versatility. You...someone like you and what you stand for as master of The First Tongue...can speak all dialects fluently and even create new ones.|","He paused before continuing.","|Ginnu Lifeforms like myself instinctively know The First Tongue because we emerged when it was being formed. We’re native speakers. Others must consciously learn it like a foreign language. But you, Noah... you can surpass all of us. You could reach the same heights as...them.|","The manifestation’s eyes glowed brighter.","|The progression path is straightforward. First, you must recognize that Mana is language, not just energy. You’ve already accomplished this. Second, you learn Phonemes by understanding individual Mana pulses as distinct units. You’ve mastered all eighteen Core Phonemes. Third, you form simple Logos by combining Phonemes with intent. You’ve been doing this.|","Ul’moreth raised four massive fingers.","|Fourth, you master Logos structure to achieve what we call Singularity Principles. These are refined expressions that embody complete concepts. Fifth, you comprehend Philology to fully access Genesis Principles. This is what I’m teaching you now. And finally, sixth, you learn to speak in complete sentences to reshape Existence at its most fundamental levels.|","The manifestation gestured grandly.","| Genesis Principles are different from Singularity Principles. A Singularity Principle is a perfected expression of a single concept. But a Genesis Principle... a Genesis Principle is the underlying structure that allows entire categories of concepts to exist. It’s the difference between understanding fire and understanding the nature of transformation itself.|","Noah felt his mind expanding as he processed this information.","|I will now teach you the Philology of my three Genesis Principles. I will pass down what I hold to you. Watch carefully and listen with your entire existence, not just your ears.|","The manifestation of Ul’moreth raised both hands as THE Civilizational Authority of Primordial Continuity blazed around him.","He began writing in the air with blue-gold light.","Complex Logos formed, far more intricate than anything Noah had seen before!","Oh!"]},{"number":4649,"title":"Chapter 4649: Chapter 4648: THE Farewell of Ginnungagap III","paragraphs":["Multiple Phonemes woven together in elaborate syntax with conjugations and modifications layered throughout.","The complexity was staggering.","| The first Genesis Principle is: Undifferentiated Mana. This is Mana before it specialized into any particular form. The primordial potential that precedes all actualization.|","The Logos Ul’moreth wrote was unlike anything Noah had seen before.","It wasn’t just a few Phonemes arranged together.","It was a complete Philology - a full grammatical structure containing multiple Logos woven into a coherent sentence.","The Phoneme of Beginning pulsed first, establishing initiation.","Then Void bloomed to represent the emptiness before differentiation.","Unity threaded through to show wholeness before separation.","Paradox wove in to express the contradiction of being everything and nothing simultaneously.","But the structure didn’t stop there.","Chaos entered the syntax to represent the undirected state before Order imposed form.","Life and Death intertwined to show the potential for both creation and dissolution existing equally.","Fire, Water, Earth, and Air all manifested together - the classical elements in perfect equilibrium before any specialized.","Light and Darkness balanced each other, showing awareness and mystery coexisting.","Time appeared not as flow but as stillness - the moment before temporal sequence began.","Space manifested as infinite potential rather than defined dimension.","Order touched the edges to suggest the possibility of structure without actualizing it.","Division hovered at the periphery, representing the capacity to differentiate without yet doing so.","Ending paired with Beginning in a loop, showing that potential contains both initiation and conclusion.","All eighteen Core Phonemes were present in this single Genesis Principle.","But more than that, they were arranged into three distinct Logos that formed a complete sentence.","The first Logos combined Beginning, Void, Unity, and Paradox with specific conjugations that expressed: | What initiates in emptiness.|","The second Logos wove together Chaos, Life, Death, Time, and Space with syntax that declared: | Contains all possibilities without distinction.|","The third Logos unified Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Light, Darkness, Order, Division, and Ending in a structure that completed: | Until differentiation imposes form upon formlessness.|","Together, the three Logos created the full Philology:","| What initiates in emptiness contains all possibilities without distinction until differentiation imposes form upon formlessness.|","HUUM!","The complexity was breathtaking.","Each Phoneme pulsed with precise timing relative to the others.","Each Logos connected to the next through careful grammatical bridging.","The entire structure resonated with fundamental truth about the nature of Mana itself.","Ul’moreth’s voice resonated with profound depth as he spoke the complete Philology in The First Tongue.","The Logos pulsed with rhythm that felt older than time itself.","| This is the foundation of all Mana manipulation. Before Mana becomes fire or water, storm or hunger, it exists in this undifferentiated state. Understanding this Philology allows you to work with Mana at its most fundamental level. To reshape it before it takes any particular form. Once you grasp it, its full capabilities will show themselves to you.|","The manifestation allowed Noah a moment to absorb the first Genesis Principle before continuing, throwing this bundle of light to him be branded into his existence!","| The second Genesis Principle is: Temporal Perpetuity. This is Time as continuous flow rather than discrete moments. The understanding that past, present, and future are all one unbroken stream.|","The new Philology Ul’moreth wrote was equally complex.","Time appeared first, establishing the temporal foundation.","Unity wove through to show the unbroken nature of temporal flow.","Beginning and Ending intertwined in a loop, each containing the other.","Space manifested to show dimension across which time flows.","Order structured the sequence while Chaos introduced variation within continuity.","Life pulsed forward while Death pulled backward, creating tension that generated flow.","Paradox threaded throughout to express how past, present, and future exist simultaneously despite appearing sequential.","Void represented the gaps between moments that aren’t really gaps at all.","Light illuminated what was, is, and will be, while Darkness concealed the mechanisms of temporal progression.","Fire drove change forward as Water adapted to temporal currents.","Earth provided temporal stability while Air allowed temporal movement.","Division separated moments conceptually while Unity bound them into single stream.","Once again, all eighteen Core Phonemes appeared, but arranged into three distinct Logos.","The first Logos combined Time, Unity, Beginning, Ending, Space, and Order with conjugations expressing: | What flows without cease through all dimensions.|","The second Logos wove together Chaos, Life, Death, Paradox, and Void with syntax declaring: | Contains every moment within eternal now.|","The third Logos unified Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Light, Darkness, and Division in structure completing: | While appearing sequential yet remaining unified whole.|","The full Philology resonated:","| What flows without cease through all dimensions contains every moment within eternal now while appearing sequential yet remaining unified whole.|","Noah felt something shift in his perception as he absorbed this understanding.","The way he saw reality itself was changing.","Time wasn’t just a river flowing in one direction.","It was an ocean where past, present, and future existed as one body of water and one simply needed to swim in different areas. He already swam in different areas!","Ul’moreth gestured to the temporal Philology with reverence.","| This understanding is why temporal manipulation is possible. Time isn’t actually divided into separate moments. Those divisions are constructs we impose to make sense of existence. But the underlying reality is perpetual flow - one continuous stream. When you master this Philology, you don’t manipulate discrete moments. You work with the unified whole of temporal existence. You have been traversing through time in a way only you understand...|","...!","The manifestation’s form began to dim slightly, its remaining energy focusing on the final lesson.","| The third Genesis Principle is: Existential Foundation. This is the bedrock upon which all reality constructs itself. The fundamental substrate that allows many things to BE.|","This final Philology was the most dense with meaning.","Earth appeared first as the core concept of foundation. Beginning established that foundation must exist before anything else can. Order provided the structure that foundation requires....","Unity, Space, Time, Life, Death, Fire...each added to it.","Air allowed foundation to remain permeable rather than rigid. Light revealed the foundation’s presence while Darkness protected its mysteries.","Void, Chaos, Division...","Ending paired with Beginning to show foundation supports both inception and conclusion.","All eighteen Core Phonemes wove together into three Logos of tremendous density.","The first Logos combined Earth, Beginning, Order, Unity, Space, and Time with precise conjugations expressing: | What grounds all being in structured persistence.|","The second Logos interwove Life, Death, Fire, Water, Air, and Void with complex syntax declaring: | Supports transformation and stillness equally.|","The third Logos unified Light, Darkness, Chaos, Division, Paradox, and Ending in architecture completing: | While permitting all contradictions to coexist upon bedrock of reality.|","The complete Philology pulsed with overwhelming weight:","| What grounds all being in structured persistence supports transformation and stillness equally while permitting all contradictions to coexist upon bedrock of reality.|","...!","This final Genesis Principle seemed to vibrate with such fundamental truth that reality itself resonated in response!"]},{"number":4650,"title":"Chapter 4650: Chapter 4649: THE Farewell of Ginnungagap IV","paragraphs":["Ul’moreth stepped back as all three complete Philologies floated in the air before Noah.","Each one was a masterwork of linguistic architecture.","Each one contained more than fifteen Phonemes arranged into at least three Logos that formed complete sentences.","Each one represented a fundamental truth about reality that transcended simple concepts.","| These are my Genesis Principles. The deepest understanding I achieved during my existence. Each one required eons to fully comprehend and construct. Each one represents the culmination of countless attempts, failures, and refinements. I give them to you now freely. Study the Philology. Reproduce the syntax. And they will become part of your own Weavings of Existence.|","The manifestation began to fade more rapidly now, its time clearly running short.","| You’ll notice that each Genesis Principle uses all eighteen Core Phonemes. This isn’t coincidence. A Genesis Principle must be complete - it must incorporate the full spectrum of fundamental concepts. Anything less is merely a Singularity Principle, no matter how refined.|","Ul’moreth’s eyes locked onto Noah’s with fierce intensity.","| The arrangement matters. The conjugations matter. The way the Logos connect into complete sentences matters. Change even one element and the entire meaning shifts. This is why Philology is so difficult to master.|","The manifestation raised one hand in final blessing.","| Remember. The First Tongue is not just power. It’s understanding. It’s the ability to perceive and reshape the fundamental structure of Existence itself. Use it well. Use it wisely. And perhaps... use it to create a better Existence than the one we failed to protect.|","The illusory form of Ul’moreth smiled one last time before dissolving completely into motes of obsidian-gold light.","The light flowed into Noah’s body as the chest itself crumbled to dust.","But the three complete Philologies remained floating in his consciousness.","Each one a sentence of tremendous complexity.","Each one using all eighteen Core Phonemes in precise grammatical arrangement.","Each one containing multiple Logos woven into unified meaning.","Prompts descended before Noah’s vision.","|Genesis Principles Glimpsed|","|You have been taught the Philology of three Genesis Principles:|","|1. Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana - Mana before it specialized|","|2. Genesis Principle of Temporal Perpetuity - Time as continuous flow rather than discrete moments|","|3. Genesis Principle of Existential Foundation - The bedrock upon which all reality constructs itself|","|Integration Status:|","| The Philology has been recorded within your Weavings of Existence|","|Each Genesis Principle contains 18 Phonemes arranged into 3+ Logos forming complete sentences|","| As long as you can reproduce the Philology of these Genesis Principles, they will be available for use|","|Current Mastery: 0% (Knowledge acquired, practical application pending)|","|Practice Required: Extensive|","|Complexity Assessment:|","|Each Genesis Principle requires precise reproduction of 18 Phoneme arrangements|","|The conjugations, timing, and grammatical structure must be exact|","|A single error in syntax will result in failed activation or unintended effects|","|Estimated time to achieve Basic Mastery (10%): Months. Or for you...Minutes?|","|Estimated time to achieve Perfect Mastery (100%): Years...or maybe just days|","|Genesis Principles operate at a fundamentally different level than Singularity Principles|","|They reshape reality at the substrate level rather than manipulating existing structures|","|Misuse or imperfect execution may result in catastrophic unintended consequences|","Additional prompts bloomed with even greater significance.","|New Understanding Achieved - Existential Resistance of Genesis Principles|","|Through comprehension of Genesis Principle Philology, you have glimpsed a deeper truth|","|Existential Resistance of Genesis Principles:|","| Classification: Advanced form of THE Civilizational Authority Resistance|","|Function: Passive defense granted by understanding reality’s fundamental structure|","|When you comprehend the Philology that underlies Genesis Principles, you’re learning the grammar of existence itself|","|This understanding creates inherent protection because you’re aligned with reality’s fundamental rules|","|Attacks against you must first overcome the structure of existence to reach you|","|Resistance Levels:|","|Basic Understanding (10% Philology Mastery): Minor passive deflection of lower-tier attacks|","| Intermediate Understanding (40% Philology Mastery): Moderate passive defense against most THE Surface Depth attacks|","|Advanced Understanding (70% Philology Mastery): Strong passive defense; THE Intermediate Depth attacks may not pass through|","|Master Understanding (95% Philology Mastery): Supreme passive defense; THE Intermediate Depth attacks can be nullified without conscious effort|","| Perfect Understanding (100% Philology Mastery): Absolute passive defense; The First Tongue itself defends on your behalf|","|Current Calculation:|","|Your Existential Resistance: 5%|","|You have glimpsed the Philology but not yet practiced it|","|Estimated time to Basic Understanding: Probably seconds|","|Advanced Mechanics:|","|At higher mastery levels, you won’t need to consciously defend yourself|","|Existence itself will seemingly be passively defending you|","|But it’s not existence acting independently - it’s The First Tongue applying inherent protection|","|Your understanding of the grammar creates automatic defensive responses|","|At Master and Perfect levels and beyond:|","| Eventually, THE Fundamental Depth entities can attack you with full force, and you won’t need to lift a finger as all attacks are automatically parsed and defended against|","|The Philology you’ve mastered essentially tells reality: \"This attack violates proper syntax and is therefore invalid\"|","|Beyond this, The First Tongue may begin to attack on your behalf|","|Entities that threaten you will find their own Weavings restructuring against them|","|Reality itself becomes your weapon and shield simultaneously|","|This is the true power of linguistic mastery over existence|","|Be mindful- This level of defense is not invincibility|","|Entities with superior Philology mastery can override your defenses|","| Absolute power does not exist - only relative advantage|","Noah sat in stunned silence as he absorbed these prompts.","The implications were booming!","Ul’moreth had given him a lot.","He looked at the three Genesis Principle Philologies still floating in his mind’s eye.","Each one containing all eighteen Core Phonemes arranged into at least three Logos forming complete sentences.","Each one representing years, perhaps decades of practice to truly master.","But the potential...","At Perfect Understanding of Philology, he could stand before THE Intermediate Depth entities and not even need to raise a hand in his own defense.","Reality itself would defend him because his understanding of its structure would be so complete that attacks would simply fail to parse correctly.","He thought about The First Farmer currently designing his first Phoneme nearby.","About Sigrid approaching THE Surface Depth.","About the countless entities in his Civilization all advancing in their own ways.","And now he had this.","The deepest lesson from THE Primeval Titan .","Noah closed his eyes and began to practice the first Philology in his mind.","Undifferentiated Mana.","All eighteen Phonemes had to align in his consciousness in precise sequence.","Beginning, Void, Unity, Paradox, Chaos, Life, Death, Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Light, Darkness, Time, Space, Order, Division, Ending.","He pulsed them in the exact rhythm and syntax Ul’moreth had demonstrated.","First forming the initial Logos: |What initiates in emptiness.|","Then the second: |Contains all possibilities without distinction.|","Finally the third: |Until differentiation imposes form upon formlessness.|","The complete sentence emerged:","| What initiates in emptiness contains all possibilities without distinction until differentiation imposes form upon formlessness.|","Reality shivered.","For just a moment, he felt it.","The sensation of Mana in its undifferentiated state.","Pure potential before it became anything specific.","The foundation of all existence.","It was...","This was...","This was... fucking easy?!","Undifferentiated Mana, was his Mana! His Primus Mana!","Existence shivered as a Genesis Principle was accessed on Noah’s first try!"]},{"number":4651,"title":"Chapter 4651: Chapter 4650: Glorious! I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the complex Philology floating in his mind with amazement!","All eighteen Core Phonemes arranged into three Logos forming a complete sentence.","|What initiates in emptiness contains all possibilities without distinction until differentiation imposes form upon formlessness.|","It felt so seamless and so easy as...","He raised his hand and began to inscribe the Philology in the space before him.","His fingers moved with practiced grace as blue-gold light followed their path.","Beginning, Void, Unity, Paradox...","The Phonemes manifested one after another with increasing ease.","Chaos, Life, Death, Fire, Water, Earth, Air...","And then something remarkable just like before happened!","The inscription became shockingly easy.","Not because the Philology was simple - it was devastatingly complex.","But because Undifferentiated Mana was just","...his Mana.","This entire Genesis Principle wss just his Mana.","The fundamental potential that preceded all specialization.","The primordial state before form imposed itself upon formlessness.","This was what he’d been learnign since Ginnungagap.","This was what he’d shown Lumivara.","He just hadn’t known the elevated immensity of The First Tongue that described it.","Light, Darkness, Time, Space, Order, Division, Ending.","The final Phonemes fell into place as the complete Philology blazed before him.","And then pure blue brilliance erupted all around him.","Not blue-gold like his Primus Mana usually manifested.","Just pure, pristine blue .","The color of Mana itself in its most fundamental state.","The brilliance formed into flower-like patterns that bloomed and spread.","Rivers of blue light branched outward across existence like living tributaries.","Each river pulsed with undifferentiated potential seeking form.","The branching rivers spread across the Transcendent Helios Fold, touching everything they encountered.","And then they began flowing back.","All these rivers joined into a single pillar of brilliant blue light that flowed directly into Noah.","The sensation was overwhelming.","His entire body became surrounded by the Philology of Undifferentiated Mana.","The complete sentence spun around him like a hymn being sung by reality itself.","| What initiates in emptiness contains all possibilities without distinction until differentiation imposes form upon formlessness.|","The words pulsed with each rotation around his body.","Each Phoneme resonated with perfect clarity.","Each Logos connected seamlessly to the next.","The full Philology created a symphony of linguistic power that restructured his very existence.","Prompts descended before his vision in cascading brilliance.","|GENESIS PRINCIPLE GRASPED|","|Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana - ACHIEVED|","| Mastery Level: 50% (Instant Comprehension)|","|Classification: Your innate nature aligned perfectly with this Philology. You have exceeded Basic Mastery and attained Intermediate Mastery instantly.|","|Explanation:|","|This Genesis Principle describes the fundamental nature of Mana before specialization|","|You have been teaching and embodying this concept since your emergence|","|The Philology simply provided the elevated grammatical structure to express what you already understood|","|Result: Instant mastery. The only reason it is not 100% is because The First Tongue itself still holds many complexities and intricacies|","|EXISTENTIAL REFINEMENT INITIATED|","|The innate passive existential refinement of your existence has begun by an authority of The First Tongue|","|Your Weavings are being restructured at the substrate level|","|All aspects of your being are being optimized according to proper linguistic grammar|","|DEPTH REFINEMENT IN PROGRESS|","|Your Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger which have not been declared officially|","| Yet you hold the immensity of THE Surface Depth equivalent weight|","|Both are now under refinement with the Philology of The First Tongue|","|FOUNDATION REINFORCEMENT|","| THE Foundation of The First Tongue is being refined by Genesis Principle comprehension|","|Your Foundation now incorporates Genesis-level understanding|","|This creates compound effects with all other abilities|","|All Logos you form will carry traces of Genesis Principle architecture|","|All Mana you manipulate will reflect undifferentiated nature before specialization|","|CIVILIZATIONAL IMPACT|","| Your Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger resonates with this achievement|","|All entities within your Civilization receive passive benefit|","|Mana manipulation efficiency: +340% for all members|","|Way development acceleration: +450% for all members|","|These effects persist as long as you maintain Genesis Principle mastery|","Additional prompts bloomed with tremendous significance.","|The Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana grants the following capabilities:|","| Feature 1 - Way Manifestation:|","| You alone, due to your nature, can exhibit any Way of Existence through this Genesis Principle|","|By accessing undifferentiated potential, you can temporarily specialize into any form|","|Duration: Variable based on complexity of Way|","|Limitation: Cannot permanently adopt Ways that conflict with your core nature|","|Application: Allows you to demonstrate, teach, or utilize any Way as needed|","| Feature 2 - Way Alteration (Benevolent):|","| You can change the Ways of others in non-harmful manner through this Principle|","|By returning their Way to undifferentiated state, you can help them reshape it|","|This requires their willing cooperation and cannot be forced|","|Applications:|","|- Correcting flaws in another’s Way development|","|- Helping entities transition between Ways safely|","|- Optimizing Way efficiency by rebuilding from foundation|","|- Removing harmful influences or corruption from Ways|","|Limitation: Cannot alter Ways against the entity’s will or nature|","| Feature 3 - Pedagogical Amplification:|","|When you teach Ways or aid in the progression of others, you receive amplified returns|","|The more effectively you teach, the greater the harvest|","|Students’ breakthroughs generate Infinite Potential that flows back to you|","|This creates a cycle of teaching and advancement|","|Harvest Multipliers:|","|- Basic teaching (sharing knowledge): +200% harvest|","|- Active guidance (personalized instruction): +500% harvest|","|- Breakthrough facilitation (enabling major advancement): +1,200% harvest|","|- Genesis comprehension (student grasps Genesis-level truth): +3,000,000% harvest|","| Feature 4 - Existential Resistance Enhancement:|","|50% Mastery of this Genesis Principle immediately grants Intermediate Understanding (40% Philology Mastery equivalent)|","|Your passive defense against attacks has increased substantially|","| THE Surface Depth attacks are now significantly weakened before reaching you, and may find it hard to harm you|","| Feature 5 - Mana Primacy:|","| All Mana-based attacks you perform now carry Genesis-level authority|","|Your Mana operates at the substrate level beneath specialized forms|","|This allows your attacks to bypass resistances based on specialized Sovereignties|","|Example: An entity immune to fire cannot fully resist your Mana-based fire because you’re working with the potential that precedes fire|","| Feature 6 - Way Evolution:|","|You can now guide the evolution of your own Way with unprecedented precision|","|By returning aspects of your Way to undifferentiated state, you can reshape them optimally|","|This allows continuous refinement rather than being locked into early development choices|","|Your Way of Mana and Hunger can now evolve dynamically based on need|","Oh!","Oh!!!","Noah smiled as he processed all of these prompts.","He could exhibit any Way of Existence by accessing undifferentiated potential.","He could help others reshape their Ways safely and benevolently.","And most importantly, when he taught others, he received amplified returns.","Pedagogical Amplification.","He thought about Ul’moreth teaching him.","Did Ul’moreth gain tremendous returns from that teaching?","He hoped the Infinite Potential there was immense.","Ul’moreth deserved as much as he needed, especially since he was locked in THE Belly of Existence this whole time.","The thought made Noah’s smile grow wider.","If teaching generated such powerful returns, then Ul’moreth’s sacrifice to save Noah from THE Primordial Chaos would have created even more.","The causality there was profound.","A teacher saves his student by burning his Way.","The student later brings the teacher’s Genesis Principles to full comprehension.","The loop completes itself with both parties benefiting from the connection.","The blue brilliance surrounding Noah began to stabilize.","The Philology of Undifferentiated Mana had fully integrated into his Weavings.","His Foundation was reinforced beyond what should be possible at his current classification.","His Depths of Mana and Hunger Sovereignty were being refined to absolute purity.","And he’d gained capabilities that would allow him to exhibit any Way, reshape others’ Ways, and harvest tremendous potential through teaching.","All from grasping a single Genesis Principle.","He still had two more to master from Ul’moreth’s teachings.","Temporal Perpetuity and Existential Foundation.","And beyond those, he had nine Core Phonemes of his own to create as THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, and Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect to take to Genesis.","The path ahead was clear.","And with the Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana now fully grasped, that path had become significantly more achievable!","Noah looked over at The First Farmer, still blazing with effort as he constructed his first Phoneme.","He considered using Way Manifestation to demonstrate the process more clearly.","Or using Way Alteration to help optimize The First Farmer’s approach.","But he held back.","The First Farmer needed to achieve this himself for now for the harvest to be meaningful.","Teaching was most effective when the student struggled and overcame.","Easy answers created shallow understanding.","So Noah simply sat and observed, ready to offer guidance if truly needed.","While around him, the pure blue rivers of Undifferentiated Mana continued to flow.","He was thinking that maybe, before The Fallout...he needed to take the role of a Teacher...and teach on The First Tongue to all those in The Infiniverse.","...!"]},{"number":4652,"title":"Chapter 4652: Chapter 4651: Glorious! II","paragraphs":["Noah put the idea of teaching on his to-do list.","For now, he wanted complete access to the remaining Genesis Principles.","The blue rivers of Undifferentiated Mana still flowed around him as he turned his attention to the second Philology floating in his mind.","Temporal Perpetuity.","All eighteen Core Phonemes arranged into three Logos forming a complete sentence.","| What flows without cease through all dimensions contains every moment within eternal now while appearing sequential yet remaining unified whole.|","He raised his hand and began to inscribe the Philology in the space before him.","Time appeared first, establishing the temporal foundation.","Unity wove through to show the unbroken nature of temporal flow.","Beginning and Ending intertwined in a loop, each containing the other.","The Phonemes manifested with building momentum as Noah felt the rhythm of this Genesis Principle.","Space, Order, Chaos, Life, Death, Paradox, Void...","The inscription came easier than he expected, though not as seamlessly as Undifferentiated Mana.","This wasn’t his fundamental nature the way pure Mana was.","But it connected to something he’d experienced directly.","Temporal Traversal.","The closed temporal loop that sent him back to Ginnungagap and The Infinite Unfurling.","He’d lived the truth that past, present, and future weren’t separate at all.","Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Light, Darkness, Division.","The final Phonemes fell into place as the complete Philology blazed before him.","And then crystalline purple amber brilliance erupted all around him.","Not blue like Undifferentiated Mana.","This was the color of Time itself as it pulsed through reality.","The brilliance formed into spiraling patterns that looped back on themselves.","Rivers of amber purple light flowed both forward and backward simultaneously, creating impossible geometries.","Each river represented a moment in time, yet all moments existed at once.","The spiraling rivers expanded across the Transcendent Helios Fold before converging.","They formed into a massive crystalline structure that resembled an hourglass, but the sand flowed in all directions at once.","The structure descended into Noah’s chest.","The sensation was different from Undifferentiated Mana.","Not overwhelming potential, but rather the feeling of standing at the center of infinite temporal streams.","His entire body became surrounded by the Philology of Temporal Perpetuity.","|What flows without cease through all dimensions contains every moment within eternal now while appearing sequential yet remaining unified whole.|","The words pulsed with temporal rhythm that felt like the heartbeat of existence itself.","Prompts descended before his vision in cascading amber purple light.","|Genesis Principle Grasped|","| Genesis Principle of Temporal Perpetuity - Achieved|","|Mastery Level: 35%|","|Classification: Your experience with Temporal Traversal provided direct understanding of unified temporal flow|","|Explanation:|","|This Genesis Principle describes Time as continuous stream rather than discrete moments|","|Your Temporal Traversal to The Infinite Unfurling demonstrated this truth experientially|","|You lived through the paradox of being in both past and present simultaneously|","|Existential Refinement Enhanced|","|Your temporal perception has been restructured at the substrate level|","|You now perceive time’s true nature even while experiencing it sequentially|","|This creates passive temporal awareness that cannot be disrupted|","|Foundation Reinforcement|","|THE Foundation of The First Tongue incorporates the second Genesis Principle|","|Compound effects with Undifferentiated Mana creating synergistic enhancement|","|All temporal abilities now carry Genesis-level authority|","Additional prompts bloomed with tremendous significance.","|The Genesis Principle of Temporal Perpetuity grants the following capabilities:|","| Feature 1 - Early Atlas Enhancement:|","|Your Early Atlas of The Folds gains Genesis-level temporal authority|","|Temporal Traversal capability enhanced beyond normal parameters|","|You can now navigate temporal streams with unprecedented precision|","|The \"closed loop\" restriction becomes more flexible - you can identify and potentially create new stable loops|","|Temporal resistance increased - entities attempting to disrupt your position in time face Genesis-level opposition|","|The Atlas itself becomes anchored across all moments simultaneously|","| Feature 2 - Infinite Desmoterion Temporal Expansion:|","| THE Infinite Desmoterion’s time dilation has been fundamentally enhanced|","|Previous dilation: 27,000x faster than external reality|","| Enhanced dilation: Variable up to 270,000x based on need|","|This enhancement applies retroactively - all prisoners have been cultivating under improved conditions|","|Temporal stability within the prison dimension increased substantially|","|Prisoners can now safely cultivate across longer subjective time periods without degradation|","|The harvest from their advancement will be proportionally greater|","| Feature 3 - Temporal Perpetuity Sovereign Spires:|","|Your Sovereign Spires of Osmont gain a new classification option|","| Entities who have undergone Civilization Specialization can now enter Temporal Perpetuity Spires|","|Within these Spires, time flows according to the cultivator’s need|","|They can spend subjective years cultivating their Ways while mere hours pass externally|","|The dilation is personalized - each cultivator experiences optimal temporal flow for their development|","|Maximum dilation per individual: 50,000x (increases with their mastery)|","|This creates a Civilization-wide advantage in advancement speed|","|Note: Only those who have proven loyalty through Civilization Specialization can access this feature|","Noah absorbed these prompts with shining eyes.","The Temporal Perpetuity Sovereign Spires alone would revolutionize his Civilization’s development.","Entities could cultivate for subjective decades while only hours or days passed in reality.","Combined with the enhanced Infinite Desmoterion, his entire power base was accelerating.","But he wasn’t finished yet.","He turned his attention to the third and final Genesis Principle from Ul’moreth’s teachings.","Existential Foundation.","|What grounds all being in structured persistence supports transformation and stillness equally while permitting all contradictions to coexist upon bedrock of reality.|","He raised his hand once more and began to inscribe.","Earth appeared first as the core concept of foundation.","Beginning, Order, Unity, Space, Time...","The Phonemes manifested with building solidity.","This one felt different from both previous Genesis Principles.","Not fundamental like Undifferentiated Mana.","Not experiential like Temporal Perpetuity.","This was architectural.","The understanding that reality required structure to exist upon.","Life, Death, Fire, Water, Air, Void, Light, Darkness, Chaos, Division, Paradox, Ending.","The final Phonemes locked into place as the complete Philology blazed before him.","And then solid bronze radiance erupted all around him.","The color of Earth itself, representing an unshakable foundation.","But the manifestation was unlike the previous two Genesis Principles.","Instead of rivers or spirals, geometric patterns began forming in the air.","Blueprint lines of bronze light sketched out architectural designs.","Foundations, walls, support beams, chambers, and connecting passages.","The designs descended into Noah’s body, specifically into his mind where THE Organ of Civilization pulsed.","And then something extraordinary happened.","The bronze light didn’t just enhance what was already there.","It began constructing something entirely new within his existence.","A metaphysical structure that would serve as the true foundation for everything he was building!"]},{"number":4653,"title":"Chapter 4653: Chapter 4652: Glorious! III","paragraphs":["Prompts descended with overwhelming significance.","|Genesis Principle Grasped|","| Genesis Principle of Existential Foundation - Achieved|","|Mastery Level: 40% |","|Classification: Your nature as a builder of Civilization resonated with foundational architecture|","|Explanation:|","|This Genesis Principle describes the bedrock upon which all reality constructs itself|","|Your work building civilizations, structures, and systems prepared you for this understanding|","|You instinctively comprehend that power requires proper foundation to support it|","|Result: Intermediate mastery with clear path to advancement|","| Major Discovery - THE Foundation of The First Tongue Redefined|","|This Genesis Principle has revealed the true nature of your Foundation|","|THE Foundation of The First Tongue has gained clearer definition and direction|","|It is not abstract energy or conceptual structure. It is an actual architectural construction within your existence, and it has been distinguished with a name at this moment.|","| THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons|","|Your Foundation manifests as a living book being written in real-time|","|Each page represents a layer of your Foundation|","| The text is written in pure First Tongue - Phonemes, Logos, and Philology as the construction materials|","|This is THE Foundation of The First Tongue made physically manifest within your soul|","|Current Structure:|","| THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons currently contains 18 Chapters - one for each Core Phoneme|","|Each Chapter is being filled with Phonemes and Logos as you master their applications|","|Genesis Principles form entire sections that can span multiple Chapters|","|Your own created Phonemes will add new Chapters when completed|","|Architectural Progression System:|","|Your Foundation scales across four distinct Depths, each requiring architectural expansion|","| Surface Depth Foundation (Current Stage):|","|THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons’ first volume - establishing fundamental grammar|","|Requires: All 18 Core Phonemes mastered as individual Chapters|","|Requires: At least 3 Genesis Principles grasped to provide structural integrity|","|Progress: 18/18 Phoneme Chapters complete, 3/3 minimum Genesis Principles achieved|","|Status: Foundation stable and ready for Depth declaration|","| Intermediate Depth Foundation (Next Stage):|","| THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons’ second volume - complex sentence construction|","|Requires: 9 personal Phonemes created and integrated as new Chapters|","|Requires: At least 9 Genesis Principles mastered|","|Requires: All Singularity Principles elevated to Genesis level. Only Genesis within you, nothing else|","|Benefits: Existential weight increases exponentially, all abilities carry deeper authority|","| Fundamental Depth Foundation (Advanced Stage):|","|THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons’ third volume - paragraph and essay level expression|","|Requires: Mastery of compound Philologies combining multiple Genesis Principles|","|Requires: Creation of entirely new grammatical structures beyond what currently exists|","|Benefits: Existence restructuring capabilities, ability to define new rules of existence|","| Absolute Depth Foundation (Ultimate Stage):|","|THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons becomes a complete work - a new dialect of The First Tongue, THE dialect of The First Tongue, THE First Tongue itself...|","|Requires: Perfect understanding of all Philology you’ve created|","|Requires: Integration of your Way into The First Tongue itself|","|Benefits: Your existence becomes a fundamental force that other entities must account for|","|Foundation Building Mechanics:|","| To advance your Foundation, you must add \"pages\" to THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons|","|Each page requires specific materials:|","|- Phonemes serve as individual letters and words|","|- Logos serve as sentences and paragraphs|","|- Philology serves as Chapters and volumes|","|- Genesis Principles serve as load-bearing pillars that support entire sections|","|Current Grimoire Status:|","|Pages: 1,847 / 10,000 (Surface Depth volume)|","|Chapters: 21 (18 Core Phonemes + 3 Genesis Principles)|","|Structural Integrity: 94% (Excellent)|","|Quality: Genesis-tier materials ensure exceptional durability|","|Unique Manifestation:|","|This Genesis Principle manifests differently for each entity based on their nature|","|For you, it manifested as THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons because you are THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons|","|For another entity, it might manifest as a fortress, a tower, a garden, or a forge|","|The form always reflects the individual’s deepest nature and path|","|Primary Overarching Feature - Immaculate Quintessential Foundation:|","| THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons actively refines all power flowing through you|","|Raw authority entering your system is automatically converted and organized according to proper linguistic structure|","|This creates unprecedented efficiency and prevents any corruption or deviation|","| Your Foundation literally cannot support flawed or corrupted power - it restructures everything to match The First Tongue’s grammar|","Additional prompts bloomed!","| THE Organ of Civilization - Evolution Complete from the elevation of Foundation|","|Initial growth phase: 100% achieved|","| THE Organ of Civilization has fully integrated with THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons|","|New function unlocked: THE Civilizational Units of Everything conversion|","| THE Civilizational Units of Everything of Primus Mana:|","|All power flowing through you is now converted to standardized units|","|Primus Mana, Civilizational Authority, harvested energy - all becomes unified|","|These units carry the depth of THE classification inherently|","|Current Reserves:|","| THE Civilizational Units of Everything of Primus Mana: 847,923,441/Infinite|","|Generation Rate: +2,340,000 per hour (from all sources)|","|Quality: Genesis-tier (each unit carries Genesis Principle authority)|","|Enhanced Distribution:|","| THE Organ of Civilization can now channel power with perfect efficiency|","|No energy is lost in conversion or transmission|","|Power can be allocated to specific purposes with surgical precision|","|This allows you to enhance allies, fuel structures, or unleash attacks with exact calibration|","WAA!","Noah sat in stunned silence as he absorbed these cascading prompts.","THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons.","His Foundation had manifested as an actual book being written within his existence.","The architecture of his power made literal.","He could feel it now, pulsing within his mind alongside THE Organ of Civilization.","Pages turning as new understanding integrated.","Chapters expanding as his mastery deepened.","The bronze light of Existential Foundation stabilized around him, joining the blue of Undifferentiated Mana and the amber purple of Temporal Perpetuity.","Three Genesis Principles grasped.","His Foundation clearly defined and ready for growth.","THE Civilizational Units of Everything flowing through him with tremendous depth.","And most importantly, a clear path forward.","To reach Intermediate Depth, he needed to create his nine personal Phonemes.","To reach Fundamental Depth, he needed to master compound Philologies.","To reach Absolute Depth, he needed to make his existence a fundamental force within reality itself.","Noah opened his eyes and looked at The First Farmer, whose first Phoneme was nearing completion.","Around him, three Genesis Principles pulsed in harmony. Blue potential, amber perpetuity, and bronze foundation.","The building blocks of existence itself, now flowing through Noah’s Weavings!","Oh!"]},{"number":4654,"title":"Chapter 4654: Chapter 4653: The First Lesson I","paragraphs":["Noah looked within himself as he saw THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons.","His lineage was that of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons , and his THE Foundation of The First Tongue held a physical construct now.","THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons existed in his mind near THE Organ of Civilization that had also finished its initial development.","He had so many capital THEs associated with him now.","If he wanted to officially enter THE Surface Depth of his Way and Civilization, he could do it instantly as his body already held its power.","But he wanted to see something first. He wanted to see how immense his Foundation could be!","So he simply said.","\" Let me see.\"","HUUM!","In the next moment, THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons emerged externally.","Shockingly, it appeared above him and extended across the budding Transcendent Helios Folds in The Infiniverse.","His Grimoire stretched out for an entire gigaparsec!","The sheer scale was breathtaking.","It looked grand beyond description as it shined with blue-gold radiance that illuminated the entire region.","The covers were ornate beyond anything Noah had seen.","Infinity symbols covered every surface in intricate patterns that shifted and reformed constantly.","The symbols wove together in fractal designs, each one containing smaller infinity symbols within themselves.","The edges of the book pulsed with linguistic power as Phonemes danced along the binding.","The spine showed all eighteen Core Phonemes arranged vertically, glowing with their respective colors.","Blue-gold flames for Fire, liquid silver for Water, solid bronze for Earth, and so on down the entire spectrum.","The covers themselves seemed to be constructed from compressed Logos, thousands upon thousands of sentences woven so tightly they formed solid material.","Noah looked at this book with shining eyes.","He could instinctively feel how to use it.","This Grimoire was actually a deadly weapon.","Its pages filled with The First Tongue could be manifested as devastating attacks.","The expression of power was unique.","For the Genesis Principles, he could express them in a myriad of ways.","He could even cause the emergence of Glyphs for them, just like the thousands of glyphs that he had branded to himself with Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect and Mana Supremacy and others.","But the glyphs, as he was realizing right now, seemed to be a lesser form of expression of the Principles when one didn’t properly understand that they came from The First Tongue.","And because they didn’t know that the glyphs were simplified Weavings, that allowed better usage of the Principles but not optimal usage.","When the Civilizations of THE Creature and THE Living Existences were made, they made glyphs widespread instead of trying to teach The First Tongue.","Why was this?","Of course, even though he asked, he knew that it was an impossibility for entities that had not obtained THE Surface Depth to be utilizing The First Tongue.","And there had to be anomalies here and there for them to be capable of doing it.","But if there was access to better power, Noah didn’t want his people to simply learn a simpler version of it.","Even if it would be hard and arduous, let them work hard and let them struggle.","And the power they could obtain at the end of the struggle would be immense.","As he was thinking all of this, he held the musings and the access of three Genesis Principles.","And he was at this moment breaking down the Logos that made up The Principle of Perpetual Harvest and The Principle of the Cheating Architect among the five that he had prior.","The Principles of Mana Supremacy, Arcana Infinitum, and Primus Ascension that he obtained from his isolated Civilization of Mana led by Kael and Riya seemed to have similar meaning.","As he was breaking them down, much of their Weavings were actually covered in the Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana.","When he was looking at these and their Logos, their elevations may actually be fused into the Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana.","He would see if they had enough to stand on their own, or if anything not covered could simply be integrated into the already standing Principles.","As he was thinking all of this, a burst of green-gold light erupted nearby.","The First Farmer opened his eyes.","And in his hands floated the Phoneme of Fire, clearly written and manifesting with perfect clarity.","His expression showed pure elation and wonder.","He looked towards Noah with eyes shining with such bright green-gold light that they could be their own suns.","His voice emerged with trembling glory.","|I was blind this whole time. What you’ve done was the equivalent of giving a blind man sight, and then magnifying it by a million times. With such sight, with The First Tongue revealed to me, I can see that all the Principles I was nurturing were built with this very language as its blueprint. With it, I could never fail in nurturing any of them. All the efforts, all the failures across eons... they will all culminate into endless success from here on out!|","His voice filled with maddened fervor towards the very end.","The very Weavings of existence of this being were already spilling past Pre-THE, trying to find foothold on a Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","The green-gold light around him intensified as his entire existence trembled with building power.","If and when he managed to string together Logos and get access to his first Genesis Principle, and due to his Anomalous Factor of THE SEED, The First Farmer would finally truly be capable of attaining THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","It would be a long time coming after eons of failure.","But the path was finally clear.","Noah nodded to The First Farmer as he rose up.","He could feel the breakdown of the Principles of Perpetual Harvest and the Cheating Architect happening in the background.","All of them would actually be completed and elevated to become Genesis Principles in the next few minutes.","While this happened, he turned his gaze up and observed the radiant THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons far above him.","Its size began to reduce as it floated towards the palm of his hand.","He began to float upward as he voiced out to The First Farmer.","\"I shall be teaching upon and expanding upon The First Tongue. You should also be able to benefit, so let’s go.\"","The gigaparsec-spanning book continued shrinking as it descended.","From a construct visible across entire Folds, it reduced to the size of a building, then a house, then just large enough to fit in his hands.","The blue-gold radiance never dimmed despite the size reduction.","The infinity symbols on the covers continued their eternal dance.","Noah grasped THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons as it settled into his palm.","The weight felt perfect.","Not too heavy, not too light.","It pulsed with his heartbeat as if it were an extension of his body.","Which, in a sense, it was.","This was THE Foundation of The First Tongue made manifest.","The literal architecture of his power given physical form.","He could open it and read the Chapters dedicated to each Phoneme.","He could add new pages as he mastered new Logos.","He could watch as entire new Chapters wrote themselves when he created his nine personal Phonemes.","And eventually, when he reached Absolute Depth, THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons would become...well, he would wait for it.","A new dialect of The First Tongue that bore his name.","THE Osmontian Tongue, perhaps.","Or THE Lexicon of Genesis.","Something that would mark his existence as a fundamental force within reality.","But that was for the future.","For now, he had teaching to do.","Noah turned and began moving through the Transcendent Helios Folds with The First Farmer following behind.","Blue potential, amber perpetuity, and bronze foundation swirled around him.","THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons rested in his hand, and in the background of his existence, Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect were being reconstructed at the Genesis level!","Oh!"]},{"number":4655,"title":"Chapter 4655: Chapter 4654: The First Lesson II","paragraphs":["In Existence, teachers were rare.","Not instructors who recited facts or demonstrated techniques. Not mentors who shared their experience or guided development.","But true teachers who fundamentally changed how their students perceived reality itself.","Across the countless eons of Observable Existence, entities had risen to power through struggle, through theft, through inheritance, through luck.","Very few had risen through genuine teaching.","The pessimistic truth was that most who claimed the title of teacher were frauds.","They hoarded knowledge to maintain advantage over students.","They shared just enough to seem generous while keeping the best insights for themselves.","They created dependency rather than independence, ensuring students always needed to return.","This was the Way of Existence.","Knowledge was power, and power was not freely given.","Even among THE Living Existences who’d formed the grand Civilizations, how many truly taught?","They never taught the underlying truth to the vast masses, only to a select few who had the talent for it.","Teachers who truly taught, who genuinely elevated their students without reservation, who shared the deepest truths without holding back...","These were so rare as to be almost nonexistent.","And then, there was THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons!","---","In The Early Veiled Shore of The Infiniverse, having put The Fallout in the back of his mind while he focused on communicating with The Infiniverse, Noah appeared above the skies of the place that used to be a small island with golden sands.","And he was communicating with The Infiniverse as she proceeded to forge THE Infinite Loom.","Because this was the barrier of protection against The Fallout. The answer was not attaining THE Civilizational Authority or raw power alone.","It was unknown even if someone held THE Surface Depth or THE Intermediate Depth whether they would survive whenever THE Living Paradox activated his weapon against THE Creature.","The weapon that would carve out THE Belly of Existence and unleash everything that was locked in the prison of THE Creature.","Ul’moreth and all others imprisoned there.","When it came to that future, Noah was actually expectant and cautious for it.","It meant an eruption of entities with THE power, and who knew what the landscape would be after The Fallout.","But in preparing for it, he wasn’t just utilizing THE Civilizational Authority or filling up the barrier of The Infiniverse with THE Civilizational Units of Everything of Mana.","He was having The Infiniverse inscribe Logos of The First Tongue itself in its periphery.","And because no matter what THE Living Paradox sought to destroy, he couldn’t destroy The First Tongue itself.","At this very moment, the peripheral barrier of his home was being inscribed with Logos of The First Tongue.","And he was also personally moving with another body near The Infiniverse to inscribe the Philology of his Genesis Principles on it as well!","The Philology of Existence ... could anyone destroy it?","It would be akin to destroying the very structures that made up The First Tongue itself.","The main opponent of THE Living Paradox was THE Creature.","And after knowing everything that he now knew regarding how obscene THE Creature was, Noah had to give props to THE Living Paradox for even daring to do what he was doing.","He was still a shitty guy and one of his main enemies.","And of course, Noah didn’t forget about his ultimate and most sworn enemy in Existence... THE Living Elemental!","The man who put a curse of burning on him and made him leave his harem momentarily.","He would hunt this fucking guy to the very ends of Existence after he came out of THE Loom.","As he had such thoughts, some in The Early Veiled Shore were already looking up at him.","He shook his head and got back to his purpose here.","He looked down at the radiant golden sands of this expansive and endless continent as he saw many things.","He saw his Abode that used to be the Abode of The Early Creature, but now it was The Abode of THE Genesis Monarch.","He saw the aquariums that were holding multiple radiant Marine Lifeforms.","He saw the many fields and trees and plots that were filled with Sacred Herbs.","The massive figure of Yoshinami rested in a corner, and Heidrun grazed in a green-gold field while Malphas obtained Sacred Mead from her and also looked up.","He saw Riya, whose eyes burned brightly with Mana as she was currently smiling.","He didn’t even have to ask her whether she saw Mana still dimming or not to know why she smiled.","And he saw the figures of Tor and Khor as they were looking at the Sanctuaries of Primus Inevitabilities.","He saw THE Living Origin with Sigrid leading her and introducing her to Amelia Osmont.","He saw The Queen of Matter and Night recording everything as if they were possessed.","At such a time, he looked at the closed book within his hands and spoke out.","| Gather.|","HUUM!","The word was spoken not in normal language, but in the language of The First Tongue!","Tor and THE Living Origin understood it since these beings were exposed to The First Tongue after all of these eons and very likely knew the Phonemes already.","But to the others, it should be and feel completely foreign.","And yet, Noah chose to speak in this voice.","Because his Way was The Way of Mana.","His Civilization was that of Mana, as every single creature before him held Mana coursing through their veins.","Just like he was able to understand The First Tongue and speak it with his Mana, even though his people might stumble and struggle to understand initially, he was doing them a favor by speaking in this language from the beginning.","If their Civilizational potential and their talent were profound enough, they would understand him rather quickly.","And if they didn’t have enough potential or talent, they would struggle.","But eventually they would pick it up.","For he didn’t plan to have his Civilization be a weak one.","Because Existence was not fair.","Existence was such a profound struggle that even now, he wanted to do everything he could to make sure that a time never came similar to before.","When he stood before THE Primordial Chaos or THE Living Temporal , and he wasn’t able to do a thing.","He didn’t want that feeling of helplessness in himself or in his people.","They had to struggle. They had to persevere.","HUUM!","Noah floated down gently, coming to sit on the massive construct of The Abode of THE Genesis Monarch.","He looked at those standing on the golden sands and throughout the regions of The Early Veiled Shore.","He looked at all of them as he raised a book.","THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons .","His Foundation of The First Tongue made manifest.","His figure looked glorious as his blue-gold robe pulsed with radiance.","The floating blue-gold crown above his head pulsed with bursts of Fragments of Phonemes of The First Tongue.","His entire figure gave off a truly imposing feel, even to his own people who’d grown accustomed to his power.","This was different.","This was the appearance of a true Sovereign about to impart knowledge that would reshape their very existence.","He spoke with grand and imposing tone.","| Our enemies are stronger than us. Existence is stronger than us. We have to play catch-up in order to simply stand before them. And the way to do this is to struggle and to learn. The weapon that will allow you to stand tall against monstrous creatures that have lived for eons... is The First Tongue.|","BOOM!","His words were heavy and booming as they echoed across The Early Veiled Shore.","At this moment, countless entities within the region turned their attention fully to him.","All of their eyes locked onto his figure.","Even the figures of Tor and THE Living Origin had eyes filled with a light that seemed to be asking... just what was he about to do?","Because The First Tongue was something that could truly only be utilized by those who held a Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","He would try and teach it to the masses?","The scene was glorious as Noah raised the book in his hands.","He looked like an ancient primordial emperor giving a sermon to his subjects!","His voice emerged with imposing and tyrannical authority as he explained.","| The First Tongue is not energy. It is not power in the traditional sense. It is language. The fundamental grammar that structures all of reality. Every Way of Existence, every Principle, every expression of authority... all of it stems from The First Tongue. The glyphs we have been using are simplified expressions. Useful, yes. But limited. They are training wheels. And I refuse to let my Civilization ride with training wheels when you could be flying.|","He paused, letting the words sink in.","| Learning The First Tongue will be difficult. Many of you will struggle. Some may fail initially. But those who persevere, those who truly grasp even a single Phoneme, will find their power elevated beyond what glyphs could ever provide. You will be speaking the language of Existence itself. And Existence will have no choice but to listen.|","His eyes blazed with blue-gold light.","|I will not coddle you. I will not simplify things beyond what is necessary for comprehension. You will struggle, and through that struggle, you will grow stronger than you ever imagined possible.|","Noah brought THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons in front of him.","He opened its cover as brilliant light spilled forth.","The first page rose up and began to shine with intense blue-gold radiance tinged with pure flame.","Noah voiced out grandly.","| The first lesson is that of Fire. The Phoneme of Fire.|","BOOM!","The page expanded, growing larger until the Phoneme of Fire was visible to all gathered entities.","Blue-gold flames danced across the surface, forming intricate patterns that seemed to burn yet create rather than destroy.","| Fire is not merely flame. It is transformation. It is energy unleashed. It is the force that changes one state of being into another. When you master the Phoneme of Fire, you don’t just create flames. You speak the concept of transformation itself into reality.|","Noah raised his hand as the Phoneme manifested above his palm.","| Watch. Learn. And when you are ready, attempt to recreate what you see. Struggle. Struggle. Struggle!|","HUUM!"]},{"number":4656,"title":"Chapter 4656: Chapter 4655: The Fallen and The Scheming","paragraphs":["While a Monarch began to teach in one corner of Observable Existence, in The Lands of The Dead, something entirely different was unfolding.","The region was expansive beyond measure, stretching across dimensions that normal entities couldn’t perceive.","Order and Death intertwined in perfect harmony here.","Obsidian structures rose alongside white marble monuments, creating a checkerboard pattern that extended infinitely.","The air itself pulsed with the authority of finality and structure combined.","At the very center of this domain, a massive obsidian-white throne could be seen.","Currently, it sat fractured.","Cracks ran through its surface like spiderwebs, and pieces had fallen away to reveal the emptiness beneath.","Sprawled on it while wailing and crying was none other than THE Dead Order.","Well, she really couldn’t be given a capital THE anymore.","Just The Dead Order now.","If anyone were to see her current state of being, they would be filled with a sense of sadness.","There was a truth about existence that few wanted to acknowledge.","Whenever a time came that entities who used to be majestic and grand and glorious fell from their high pedestals, the loss of majesty wasn’t always something to make fun of or revel in.","More often than not, it was actually a sad affair.","For if such a majestic entity could lose all their majesty and immensity, what did that mean for the rest of existence?","What did that mean for those who were weaker, less established, more vulnerable?","In Existence, nothing was guaranteed.","Even if you thought you had the backing of Existence itself, even if you’d made pacts with THE Creature , even if you’d given everything you were to a greater cause...","Nothing was guaranteed.","The Dead Order thought that she had the backing of Existence itself.","So everything should and would flow as it was supposed to.","Her current state was pitiful.","Her hair, once immaculately arranged in perfect white braids adorned with obsidian ornaments, now hung disheveled and tangled around her face.","Her robes, which used to shimmer with the authority of Death and Order combined, were torn and stained.","Her eyes, which once held the cold certainty of inevitable endings structured perfectly, now seemed hollow and cracked at the edges.","She raised her head with messy hair falling across her face and voiced out with a sense of pain that cut through the silence.","\"Ever since I was first collapsed, I was not the same. Even if we call what we have Primordial Civilizations, the moment that we are collapsed, even if we recover and come back... we’re never the same. It’s as if we lost something critical just by being collapsed. I gave you my weight. I gave you my love. To Existence itself... and yet I was still collapsed.\"","Her voice became more strained, more desperate.","\"You made promises to me. You brought me back. You had always kept your promises. But why is it that you did not keep your promises this time around?! Why did you not collapse Osmont as you said you would?! Why did you allow him to stand before me with such tyranny and take everything from me?! I was loyal! I was faithful! I gave EVERYTHING !\"","The words became more chaotic and emotional as she spoke, her body trembling.","She was veering off towards psychological breakdown.","The signs were clear in every aspect of her being.","Her hands shook uncontrollably as they gripped the armrests of her fractured throne.","Her breathing became rapid and irregular, each inhale a gasping sob.","Tears streamed down her face, but they weren’t normal tears.","They were fragments of her Weavings themselves, pieces of her existence literally crying out.","She looked up towards the expanse of white and obsidian all around her.","And she roared out.","\" WHY, O CREATURE?! WHY? ! I gave you My Everything. My Everything! So why did you not collapse Osmont?!\"","Her eyes and face began cracking as she spoke.","Literal fissures appeared across her skin, glowing with unstable light.","Her Way and Civilization truly having been drawn out and siphoned off far too much.","And in her current Weavings of Existence, it looked like everything was crumbling.","If she did not stop this frenzied state, everything about her may just crumble completely once more.","She would collapse again.","And this time, there might be no coming back.","\" WHY ?!\" she roared one last time.","And as the word left her mouth, brilliant multicolored light descended from above.","It wrapped around her disheveled head gently, almost tenderly.","Her eyes dimmed as the light touched her, the frenzy fading into sudden calm.","Right after, her body slumped forward.","But before she could fall from the throne entirely, the multicolored light caught her.","Her figure was straightened up as she began to float above her throne.","Logos bloomed all around her, manifesting in The First Tongue.","They formed into radiant sentences smoothly that created a cocoon around her body.","The cocoon shined brilliantly with restorative power, beginning to mend the cracks in her existence.","And then immense silence spread out in the surroundings.","The wailing stopped.","The breakdown ceased.","All that remained was the sight of a once-glorious entity being held together by forces beyond her control.","A fall from grace was never something grand or something to make fun of.","More often than not, it was unfathomably sad to see such wasted potential and possibilities.","What could The Dead Order have become if she’d chosen a different path?","What heights could she have reached if she hadn’t given everything to THE Creature’s designs?","Now she was just another casualty in the conflicts of supreme beings.","Another piece broken on a board she’d never truly understood.","---","Within THE Loom , in a region far removed from The Dead Order’s domain, a sea stretched endlessly.","But this was no ordinary sea.","It was surrounded by immensely concentrated elements that were filled with different variations of The First Tongue.","Flames that spoke in Fire Phonemes.","Waters that flowed in liquid sentences.","Air that whispered complex Logos.","Earth that solidified into grammatical structures.","Inside such a place, there was a humanoid figure blazing with multicolored radiance.","The figure couldn’t be clearly observed, as if reality itself refused to fully render his form.","But radiant gold flames burned on his forehead, marking him unmistakably.","This was THE Living Elemental.","His expression was currently that of annoyance.","He had an unexpected visitor in his domain that he looked towards right now.","His gaze made it clear that he wanted to be alone and did not want her here.","Yet this being, THE Living Emotive , acted completely oblivious.","She even said with casual irreverence.","\" You can fucking look at me annoyed all you want, and I will still do whatever the fuck I want, big guy. Just shut up and listen as I came here to vent. What was I saying? Ah yes, Five Seconds to Midnight. The showdown between THE Living Paradox and THE Creature gets ever closer, and do you know how I feel as it’s coming? I actually feel expectant and euphoric to fully see THE Creature again. I find myself asking, what exactly will he do? Would he come find those like me and you and collapse us first, or leave us alone and write us off as too weak for him? Haha!\"","Her words were manic and filled with chaotic emotions as she continued.","\" You know, many are getting it wrong thinking that somehow, after the eruption of THE Loom, the battle will be decided right then and there. It will actually just be the start. Because as much as this is a battle between Paradox and Existence, it is also a battle between THE Primordial Chaos, THE Secretive Eon, and those other fuckers we don’t even know about yet. So... what about those like you and me?\"","As she said this, she floated towards THE Living Elemental.","Shockingly, she came to put the back of her head on his shoulder.","She looked at his eyes from mere inches away, her expression unreadable.","\" Those like you and I... do we not have a place in all this? Will we account for anything in Existence? Do you... want to account for anything at all? Or will you be this feeble man always in the shadow of THE Creature? The shadow of THE Living Paradox? You’re all grand monuments of Existence, you’re all so... big. And yet you, Elemental... seem so tiny. So feeble compared to them. Hell, you have so much backing in the Phonemes of The First Tongue, and yet... you are down here. Don’t you want to change this?\"","The words were heavy and manipulative, designed to cut at insecurities.","THE Living Elemental’s response came calm and imposing.","\"I know my size, Emotive. I know exactly how big I am and where I stand in the hierarchy of Existence. Your manipulations won’t work on me because I’m not deluded about my position. I chose to remain here in THE Loom. I chose...what I chose rather than playing games with THE Creature and THE Living Paradox. Do not mistake my choices for weakness.\"","HUUM!","He paused before continuing with even more imposing authority.","\" And you need to get the fuck off of me. Now.\"","THE Living Emotive smiled and moved her head away.","She floated in front of THE Living Elemental, her expression shifting to something almost predatory.","\"I could help you and help myself. For those like you and me to not just be nothing. To matter even before The Oldest Paradox of Existence. Do you want to know how? You could have everything THE Living Paradox and THE Creature held. You could even... have me. In the deepest parts of your existence, you’ve always wanted to have me, didn’t you? I could always sense your emotions...\"","Silence descended.","THE Living Elemental looked at Emotive calmly.","His multicolored radiance pulsed once before he spoke.","\" What the hell have you done? What are you planning now?\"","At these words, THE Living Emotive simply smiled devilishly.","Her eyes glinted with schemes within schemes.","And she said absolutely nothing.","The silence that followed was more terrifying than any answer could have been!"]},{"number":4657,"title":"Chapter 4657: Chapter 4656: Paradox and Chaos","paragraphs":["The sea of Paradox had never been more resplendent.","It stretched across dimensions that defied conventional measurement. Its depths contained contradictions so profound that reality itself folded in on itself when attempting to observe them.","This was the heart of THE Loom’s paradoxical domain, and it had grown stronger than ever before.","The concentrated authority here would have unmade any entity below THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty in an instant. Not through violence or destruction, but through the simple impossibility of existing in a space where existence itself was contradicted at every possible angle.","Toward the very depths of this impossible sea, a figure floated with absolute sovereignty.","THE Living Paradox.","His humanoid form could barely be observed through the countless flames of paradox that surrounded him.","What could be glimpsed hinted at immensity beyond comprehension.","He was currently overseeing many things.","The preparations for what was to come. The positioning of pieces across a board that spanned all of Observable Existence . The final calibrations of mechanisms set in motion eons ago!","Five Seconds to Midnight.","In his perspective, this timing was minuscule. What appeared as seconds to existential observation might as well be actual days or hours from his vantage point. The countdown was real, but it was also relative.","He was getting ready.","And at such a time...","| Haha, Paradox, big guy! It seems like you’re finally getting things ready? Not even a heads up to an old friend? I had to find out from the endless chaos?|","...!","A shocking voice filled with The First Tongue echoed through the sea of paradox. This was a voice that had existed before concepts had names, before reality had settled into its current patterns.","A humanoid figure manifested in the paradoxical depths.","Massive beyond conventional scale, surrounded by murky shadows that devoured light and meaning simultaneously. The shadows writhed with a life of their own, constantly shifting and reforming in patterns that hinted at intelligence. Or perhaps something worse than intelligence.","It was hard to say whether this being was inside THE Loom or simply chose to manifest within it at this moment while originally existing outside of it entirely. The distinction may not have mattered to something of this nature.","THE Living Paradox frowned, his expression visible for just a moment through the flames that surrounded him.","\" Chaos ,\" he said in an acknowledgment without welcome. \" Why are you here? You still have enough power to do this with your current suppression?\"","THE Primordial Chaos laughed.","The sound was mischievous at first, almost playful in its irreverence. But then it shifted, becoming cold and imposing as it echoed through dimensions that shouldn’t have been able to hold sound.","\" Aren’t you curious as to what caused all these changes? \" Chaos asked. The murky shadows around him pulsed with each word. \" You asked me eons ago in the Infinite Unfurling what had happened between Temporal, THE Creature, and I in that incident in Ginnungagap. That Incident that was the cause of many things. I didn’t tell you then, but I could tell you now since we are about to delve into grander pastures.\"","...!","The words were heavy and filled with mystery that stretched back to the earliest moments of Existence itself.","But THE Living Paradox remained calm.","\" What happened has happened ,\" he replied. His voice was measured despite the weight of the topic. \" The past is fixed, even for beings such as ourselves. Knowing history now wouldn’t aid me too much in what I must accomplish. The battle ahead requires focus on the present and future, not excavation of ancient incidents that have already shaped everything they were meant to shape.\"","THE Primordial Chaos laughed again.","\" That’s where you’re wrong, old friend,\" Chaos said. His tone was grand and imposing. \" Knowing history even now would especially help, because history and time for some... is malleable. The past you consider fixed? For certain existences, it’s merely another canvas to be painted upon. Another variable to be adjusted. Another paradox to be embraced.\"","...!","At such words, Paradox was silent. Because he also knew this too well!","The flames around his form flickered with something that might have been contemplation.","Moments later, he waved his hand.","Obsidian-gold light coalesced before him, forming an image with perfect clarity despite the contradictory nature of everything surrounding it.","The image showed a figure in flowing robes, a floating crown hovering above his head. His posture was imperious . His presence radiated authority that challenged the very fabric of reality. Eyes that held depths of power and cunning beyond what any singular existence should possess.","This was how Noah had appeared when he entered the region of collapse. Before he decimated Agents of The Fallout. Before he crushed Schrodinger.","THE Living Paradox studied the conjured image with intensity that made the surrounding paradoxical flames burn brighter.","\"It is him, isn’t it? \" he said. His voice held certainty rather than question. \"I care not for coincidences, and I locked onto him right away. The moment I sensed the anomalies in the fabric of Existence, I knew something unprecedented was occurring. And all threads led back to this singular being.\"","...!","Boisterous laughter erupted from THE Primordial Chaos.","The murky shadows around him writhed with apparent delight as his massive form shook with mirth that echoed across dimensions.","\" Look at you already knowing !\" Chaos exclaimed. Genuine amusement colored his words. \" Haha, yes. Him. Just like I remember him in Ginnungagap. He slipped right past my fingers then, and I haven’t been able to grab him ever since, even though he’s appeared in the Infinite Unfurling and The Earliest Folds multiple times... as well as existing here in this era.\"","The laughter faded into something more predatory.","\" He is one anomalous fucker ,\" Chaos continued. His voice dropped to something between admiration and hunger. \" Man, do I want to get my hands on him.\"","...!","THE Living Paradox’s frown deepened.","\" Will you play games or be straight with me regarding his anomalous nature? \" he asked. His tone held the weight of one supreme being addressing another. \"I know his history here in this era and have come across him personally. His usage of The First Tongue surprised me when I observed it. Is that the source of his anomalous existence?\"","...!","The words hung heavy in the paradoxical waters.","THE Primordial Chaos moved closer. His murky shadows reached toward the manifested image of Noah as if yearning to touch it.","\" In our Existence ,\" Chaos began. His voice took on the weight of primordial truth. \" The Oldest Paradox of Existence has always remained unanswered. How did everything begin? In that question, Paradox was claimed as one component. Existence was claimed as another. And Chaos was claimed as well. These three have always been the contenders for the ultimate truth.\"","He paused, letting the weight of his words settle.","\" But now... The First Tongue is being claimed. This glorious fucker of a being here... haha, I won’t say much, but I will say that another competitor of our dearest Observable Existence is just now budding, and he is doing so across time itself!\"","The murky shadows pulsed with excitement.","\"If one of us were to swallow him up, let’s say... would one not have two components of The Oldest Paradox of Existence? Imagine it... imagine it!\"","...!","The words were heavy with implication that stretched across eons and possibilities.","THE Living Paradox turned fully to look toward THE Primordial Chaos .","His eyes were visible for just a moment through the paradoxical flames. They showed immense distrust and annoyance. But they also shined with something else. Possibility. Calculation. The recognition of an opportunity.","\" You’re trying to fuck with me ,\" Paradox said. His voice was low and dangerous. \" Knowing I am at the precipice of my battle with THE Creature, you want me to divide my attention to this anomaly. Do you even know much about him apart from what you have said?\"","He gestured dismissively at the manifested image.","\"I have much to do against THE Creature. Unless I have every ounce of information at this moment, I won’t move against another specifically. I will wait for the chaos of The Fallout to take care of many things. Because in the aftermath of THE Fallout, even the life of someone at THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty is not guaranteed.\"","His voice became harder, more resolute.","\" At that time, I can move more freely against THE Creature and others. But now... I need focus. Complete, undivided focus on the enemy before me.\"","...!","THE Primordial Chaos’s expression became extremely ominous.","The murky shadows around him stopped their constant writhing and became still. A stillness that was somehow more terrifying than their movement had been.","He moved toward the manifested figure of Noah. His massive form cast impossible darkness across the obsidian-gold light.","\"Oh... I know him ,\" Chaos said. His voice dropped to something between whisper and thunder. \" Chaos whispers his name. Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms whisper his name. Inevitabilities whisper his name. The First Tongue... I have begun to hear whispers of his name in The First Tongue itself.\"","He reached out, his shadow-wrapped hand passing through the image as if trying to grasp something that existed beyond mere representation.","\" The Scale Breaker. THE Anomaly. THE Genesis Monarch. Another variable that makes things even more chaotic. A variable that has been present in Ginnungagap, in The Earliest Folds, in this era, and now... it seems he will also be there after The Fallout.\"","The ominous expression deepened.","\" Oh yes, I know of him. I just came to you to murky the waters even more. To make things even more chaotic.\"","...!","THE Primordial Chaos began to fade, his form dissolving back into the murky shadows from which he’d manifested.","But before he disappeared entirely, his voice echoed one final time.","\" Ultimately, it may not be Existence that claims the win of The Oldest Paradox of Existence. It may not be Paradox. It may not be The First Tongue. Just like in the beginning, when everything was formless and uncertain... it may just be Chaos. Just Chaos.\"","His laughter followed him into oblivion.","\" Haha!\"","...!","And then he was gone.","THE Living Paradox gazed at the metaphorical Clock counting to Midnight.","The flames of paradox around him burned with contemplative intensity as he processed everything he’d just learned. With this new information, he might as well turn the clock ever closer toward Midnight. Accelerate his plans. Move against multiple targets simultaneously.","But...","He didn’t like to be reactionary.","Especially when it came to Chaos.","Any choice someone found themselves making after meeting Chaos was likely not their own willing choice. It was more than likely something influenced by Chaos itself, nudged in directions that served Chaos’s unknowable ends.","And Paradox had always done his best not to be steered by Chaos.","Because even now, he stood against an enemy that even THE Primordial Chaos did not go head to head against. He stood against THE Creature . And he had to do everything to make sure he didn’t slip.","Against THE Creature , a single slip meant collapse.","But now, learning more about THE Anomaly, about Osmont...","| Hmm...|","THE Living Paradox thought more deeply about this being. His intuition had been accurate as always. From the first moment he’d sensed those anomalies in the fabric of Existence, he’d known something unprecedented was occurring.","But for that entity to lay their claim on The First Tongue...","| Interesting. Very interesting.|","...!","The sea of paradox continued to churn around him, contradictions folding into contradictions as the countdown toward Midnight continued its inexorable progression!"]},{"number":4658,"title":"Chapter 4658: Chapter 4657: Perfect Speaker!","paragraphs":["He had been a Hunter, he had been a Farmer, he had been a Hero and a Villain. He had become a King and an Emperor and much more.","But a Teacher... a Teacher was something very unique for Noah.","At this moment, in The Early Veiled Shore, he sat on his Abode while teaching on The First Tongue.","THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons fluttered page to page within its first 18 Chapters that represented the 18 Phonemes of The First Tongue. He’d already gone through every single one to his people, explaining the intricacies and foundations.","At this moment, these Phonemes floated in the air to be visible to all as the skies of the Early Veiled Shore were filled with waves of blue-gold Primus Mana.","THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons remained open as Noah looked at his people.","Many were either standing or seated on the golden sands as they looked at him with a myriad of different gazes.","Some like Tor, THE Living Origin, Sigrid, Riya, Kael, and Malphas had shining eyes. Tor and THE Living Origin clearly knew what he talked about already, their expressions those of beings who’d spent eons with The First Tongue woven into their very existence.","Sigrid, Riya, Kael, and Malphas had different levels of understanding, but their eyes showed comprehension was taking root. Seeds being planted that would grow into something magnificent.","Others like Henry, Moiraine, Barbatos, and Adelaide looked toward him with a sense of confusion. Their expressions betrayed the reality that they hadn’t truly gotten much from his explanations. The concepts were too vast, too alien to their foundations of understanding.","Then there were others like Titano and The Emperor Penguin whose eyes were dull as if they understood absolutely nothing at all. Completely blank. As if Noah had been speaking in a language that didn’t exist.","Noah looked at all of them and shook his head.","His gaze settled on his Son.","Henry Osmont.","| Boy, step forward.|","HUUM!","Henry was astonished by the way he was called as he dazedly floated up from his seated position on the golden sands. His expression held confusion and a hint of wariness as he approached his father.","Noah looked at him. His son was the one who carried his lineage the most. The blood that flowed through Henry’s veins held potential that most entities in Observable Existence would never comprehend.","And Noah now allowed it to express itself freely.","His Lineage of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons began to exert its effects right now as he allowed the Greater Distinction for Entangled Weavings to spread wide and free. The Greater Distinction of THE Potentate!","Around Henry, invisible chains of limitation began to loosen. The Greater Distinction granted him a 5,000,000% increase in learning speed for any Mana-based abilities. It granted him the potential to comprehend and utilize The First Tongue itself.","A deep connection to Mana that allowed instinctive understanding of its nature began to awaken within him. And near Noah, his advancement speed increased by an additional 800%.","His son had a 5 Million percent boon in learning speed, and another 800% when cultivating near him.","Could he really not form a mere Phoneme of Fire with all this?","Just thinking about it made Noah slightly angry.","He waved his hand.","The Goad manifested in his grip. The stick shined with blue-gold brilliance and came with a terrifying pressure of THE Surface Depth .","Noah had this immensity and weight even though he wasn’t officially at this stage. His Existential Weight already exceeded what it should be, and now that pressure bore down on everyone present.","The weight was heavy on all those here as Henry paled, looking at his father as if he wanted to ask... Dude, what the hell is going on?!","But Noah remained stern.","\" Write the Phoneme of Fire.\"","...!","Henry Osmont looked at his father. He saw the immense seriousness in his eyes and the stick within his hands.","With all these factors, he didn’t even argue as he raised his hand burning with blue mana, remembered what his father had taught, and began to write.","He began to shape mana into structure as his father had taught him.","And as he did, due to The First Tongue being utilized to form the Phoneme of Fire, the surroundings began to respond. The Principle of Elemental Fury, The Principle of Rapid Fire, and other Principles related to fire in the surroundings inherently began to flow toward the letter Henry was forging.","The rising frequency of Mana.","The simultaneous expression.","The sharp percussive accent.","The controlled explosion outward.","These were the conditions one had to meet to successfully write the letter of fire. The Phoneme of Fire.","Yet... his son failed at matching the rising frequency alone.","Noah saw exactly where he failed. After all, he had many Phonemes of Fire and Logos made up of many letters constantly refining his existence and running across his very cells and vessels. He knew the Phonemes like the back of his hands.","At this moment, Noah took his stick and stopped the Phoneme his son was constructing before it erupted and destroyed everything. The malformed letter of fire trembled and then dissipated under the touch of The Goad, its volatile energy dispersing harmlessly into the atmosphere.","Around Noah’s body, THE Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana... THE Philology of Undifferentiated Mana shined brilliantly. He radiated a unique air as he began to correct his son. An air of absolute mastery over the very language of existence itself!","Noah was currently moving with instinct alone as he said, \" You got the frequency wrong. The rise needs to be steeper at the initiation point, then plateau briefly before the final surge. Like this.\"","He demonstrated with a casual wave of his hand, and a perfect frequency pattern of blue-gold Mana rippled outward.","\" Do it again.\"","...!","Henry focused and did it again.","The rising frequency of Mana. The simultaneous expression. The sharp percussive accent. The controlled explosion outward.","He failed at the simultaneous expression. The elements that should have moved as one instead staggered, creating dissonance in the forming Phoneme.","Noah stepped in once more, his voice calm but firm.","\" The simultaneous expression isn’t about forcing everything to happen at once. It’s about creating harmony between the components so they naturally align. You’re trying to control each element separately. Don’t. Let them breathe together. The frequency, the accent, the explosion, they’re not four things. They’re one thing expressing itself in four ways.\"","| THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons is teaching his progeny.|","|All features of your Way and Pedagogical Amplification have activated at full capacity.|","|Current Teaching Mode: Active Guidance.|","|Harvest Multiplier: +500%.|","Such a prompt shined as Henry tried again.","And failed.","Noah corrected the mistake. \" Your accent was too sharp. Fire is explosive, yes, but it’s not violent. It’s passionate. There’s a difference.\"","Henry tried again.","And failed.","\" The explosion outward was uncontrolled. You released everything at once instead of directing the expansion. Fire spreads, it doesn’t scatter.\"","Again.","Failure.","\" Better on the frequency. Worse on the expression. Focus!\"","Again.","Again.","Again!","Noah corrected every mistake with patience that surprised even himself. Each failure was met not with disappointment but with precise instruction. Each attempt brought Henry closer to understanding not just the mechanics of the Phoneme, but its fundamental nature.","And then.","The rising frequency bloomed perfectly, steep at initiation, plateauing, then surging.","The simultaneous expression harmonized, four aspects becoming one unified whole.","The sharp percussive accent struck with passion rather than violence.","The controlled explosion expanded outward with directed purpose.","Under the guidance of his father holding a stick that seemed like it would beat him if he got it wrong again, Henry watched in a daze as a Phoneme of Fire bloomed successfully in front of him.","...!","The power of multiple Grand and Singularity Principles related to fire were pulled into it. A beautiful pillar of blue-gold flames that would decimate a weak Pre-THE actually bloomed and spun upward gorgeously!","The heat was immense yet somehow welcoming. The light was blinding yet somehow soothing. The authority was undeniable yet somehow... his .","Henry’s eyes went wide with disbelief as he stared at what he’d created.","Far on the golden sands of the Shore, THE First Hunger, Tor, stood with a look of utter incredulity as he shouted out.","\"What the fuck?!\"","Not too far away, THE Living Origin had a similar gaze of incredulity. Her ancient eyes were wide with something approaching shock. This... this was not accurately portraying how impossible it was for someone to learn The First Tongue.","Much less that someone being an entity who had not attained any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty!","The First Tongue was the language of Existence itself. Beings spent eons attempting to grasp even a single Phoneme.","THE Living Existences had taken countless ages to master what they knew. And here, a boy who hadn’t even reached the heights of power that should be prerequisite for such comprehension had just successfully written a Phoneme of Fire.","In the skies, Noah looked at his son and smiled brilliantly.","\" Good ,\" he said. \" Now repeat that again, and make sure you don’t get it wrong. Afterwards, you can practice the other Phonemes.\"","...!","HUUM!","Blue-gold light erupted around father and son, brilliant and warm and filled with the authority of something unprecedented occurring.","Noah saw the emergence of glorious prompts.","|Successful Teaching of The First Tongue to Another Entity Confirmed.|","|Harvest Multiplier: +1,200%.|","|Harvest in the form of Infinite Potential has been automatically absorbed into your Mastery of The First Tongue.|","|Breakthrough Achieved.|","| As of this moment, you have attained the Mastery of Perfect Speaker.|","|The act of teaching was the final ingredient required for this advancement since you can already seamlessly enact Philologies. Grander stages await.|","|Even with your stupendous foundation, THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty can officially be grasped at any time.|","|Note: Your current Existential Weight already exceeds most average THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities.|","...!","| Going past the Mastery of Perfect Speaker may need an official declaration of your Way and Civilization.|","Noah looked at the prompts with calm satisfaction.","The Mastery of Perfect Speaker!","And all it had taken was teaching his son to write a single letter.","But the last prompt...he looked at it calmly as he thought of his ideas regardings Foundations and THE .","He... may have to alter his plans somewhat. After all, he was not obsessive when it came to one line of though!","A declaration of His Way.","An Indomitable and unsurpassable Foundation.","It did not have to be either or as...his Foundation would never be complete!","Even as a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity officially, he would still be forging his Foundation!","As his thoughts became slightly clear, he nodded to himself and finalized a decision.","He looked at Henry, who was staring at the Phoneme of Fire he’d created with an expression of wonder and disbelief. His son had just accomplished something that should have been impossible for someone at his level.","But then again, Noah thought with a slight smile, impossible was starting to become a rather flexible concept when it came to his bloodline.","On the golden sands below, Tor was still staring upward with his mouth hanging open.","\" Boy ,\" Noah said, looking at his son. \"I will move on to others, but continue. Go again.\"","Henry Osmont looked at his father, then at the stick still held casually in his grip, then back at his father.","He swallowed hard.","\"Yes, Father.\"","...!"]},{"number":4659,"title":"Chapter 4659: Chapter 4658: Scales I","paragraphs":["Sometimes, Noah found it easier not to question.","If things seemed ridiculously crazy to be happening, it didn’t necessarily mean they were impossible. It simply meant that the vast majority of Existence considered it impossible.","What he enjoyed doing was redefining what was possible and what was not possible.","It was nearly impossible for someone that hadn’t achieved at least THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty to utilize The First Tongue since many had specialized into different Ways. If some did try, it would take them a long time.","He gave a middle finger to all those assertions as he proceeded to teach his son in a matter of minutes what others would deem impossible in even years.","And after he did this, even though he saw the expressions of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin, he didn’t stop to question or think about it too much.","He simply pointed to others with his stick as he called out.","\" Sigrid, Moiraine, Riya, Barbatos, Emperor Penguin, Hyperion, Queen of Matter, Night, Titano, Erickson... you, you, you, you!\"","He pointed the stick to dozens of beings who could have his Greater Distinction of his Lineage. One by one, all of those appointed rose up as their expressions showed the surreal reality they were experiencing.","And as soon as they floated in the skies, Noah looked at them like a stern teacher holding a stick that would discipline if he needed to.","\" Write the Phoneme of Fire for me.\"","HUUM!","His body emanated waves of immensity and power that almost made his words undeniable. Innately, all of those that he called up began trying to write the Phoneme of Fire. Every time one messed up, his Goad struck out and stopped any horrific explosion as he corrected them one after another.","He could move faster than Planck Speed as he watched all of them as if they were moving in slow motion. He corrected them all one by one even though it seemed like he was doing everything simultaneously.","To Sigrid: \" Your frequency is perfect but your accent needs more passion. Fire loves, it doesn’t just burn.\"","To Moiraine: \" Stop overthinking. The paradox in your nature is fighting the purity of fire. Let them coexist.\"","To Riya: \" You’re seeing the future of the Phoneme before you’ve written the present. Focus on now.\"","To the Emperor Penguin: \"... Just...just try again.\"","To Titano: \"... Brother, come on.\"","To Erikson: \" ... I can pull out the Slipper if you need more motivation.\"","...!","|An unprecedented lesson on The First Tongue is unfolding.|","|All progression has become accelerated under your direct guidance.|","|The weight and immensity of your existence increases as you naturally harvest Infinite Potential from your current actions.|","|Multiple instances of Pedagogical Amplification are stacking.|","|Current Harvest Multiplier: Calculating...|","...!","Noah looked at all of these prompts. Even though they seemed grand and his current actions seemed grand, he felt like he could do so much more.","And so he simply proceeded to do.","At this moment where one body floated in the skies and was teaching dozens of his people with direct attention, another body of his appeared in front of Khor, Tor , and THE Living Origin who came over from nearby.","Khor looked at him with those obsidian-crimson eyes blazing.","\"You’re nuts, Outsider. Nuts!\"","...!","But as soon as she said these words, her eyes burned with competitive spirit as she began trying to etch the Phoneme of Fire right away.","Noah’s body here gave a portion of his attention to her, getting ready to correct her at any time as he also turned to look at THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin.","They looked at him as THE First Hunger blinked and harrumphed before he proceeded to say, \" I can write the Phonemes of The First Tongue! I learned it in Ginnungagap from THE Primeval Titan, both me and this crazy woman did.\"","...!","He said these words as Noah nodded before he said, \" Okay, you know Phonemes. What about Logos? Philology?\"","His eyes were shining brilliantly at this moment.","Because he knew there was a ridiculous 3,000,000% harvest if he could get anyone to grasp a Genesis-level teaching. If he could get anyone to perfectly understand a Philology of Existence.","Basically, he needed to get someone to grasp a new Genesis Principle. Or in the case of entities that had already attained a Depth of Absolute Sovereignty and had already grasped a Genesis Principle without knowing that they were actually accessing a Philology of The First Tongue... he could show them the Way.","So he looked with shining eyes at the figures of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin who were looking back at him with gazes that still seemed to ask if he was serious.","Even though they didn’t mention it, the two of them still inherently had a sense of pride in their own power. But those who understood themselves could easily get past any shortcomings. They became serious right after.","Tor said, \"I need more practice on Logos. I was collapsed just when I was getting good at them.\"","And THE Living Origin looked at Noah with extremely calm yet shining golden eyes before she said, \" I can see if you know more than me in Philology.\"","HUUM!","Right.","THE Living Origin had enjoyed boons from THE Prison of THE Creature before she was collapsed by THE Living Paradox . She had lived for much longer than THE First Hunger as her gains should have been more immense. Even if she was returned right now at only THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","Noah smiled brilliantly at this.","Would another person that didn’t have The Way of The First Tongue claim that they could speak The First Tongue better than he could?","If THE Living Origin thought that she could speak Philology better than he could, or be faster at it, then he would have her learn.","This in itself was a daring thought. Not too long ago, he and many others only thought of THE Living Origin as a legend to be looked at. Now he was looking at her and daring to teach her.","It was a surreal experience!"]},{"number":4660,"title":"Chapter 4660: Chapter 4659: Scales II","paragraphs":["At this moment, before they could even begin...","HUUM!","They raised their heads.","Far above, where his other body was, Sigrid’s black and white hair shined radiantly as white and blue flames surged upward like a brilliant, gorgeous pillar of light. She was another that succeeded in forming the Phoneme of Fire.","THE Living Order had grasped fire, and her full entry into THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty churned ever closer!","Something that was deemed unfathomably rare by others... Noah’s eyes pulsed dangerously as he wanted to make such a rare thing commonplace for his Civilization.","His other body, feeling the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore below him, turned back toward THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin.","\"Let’s get started.\"","...!","He was moving with efficiency and not necessarily with speed and haste, but he was doing many things at this moment.","Far from the Early Veiled Shore, in what could be considered the core of The Infiniverse itself, where a tremendous amount of authority gathered.","The region was one of extremely dense and pure concentrated Primus Mana shining blue-gold. Countless stellar rivers of lemniscate symbols and Mobius strips spun all around in eternal patterns. And at this moment, Phonemes of The First Tongue were also beginning to permeate and spread around this region with immensity. All of them were actually being forged by The Infiniverse herself.","At the center of this place, where vibrant Logos could be seen being formed, the figures of Noah, The Infiniverse, and even the illusory Ruination floated in this terrifyingly dense sea of authority. They were actually the source of the increased weight and immensity as time passed.","At this moment, the figure of The Infiniverse opened her eyes and looked toward her master.","\" Will Master proceed to do it?\"","Would he do it.","Noah smiled at the question as he felt his existence.","His Foundation. His Organ. His Weight.","Everything about him held the immensity of THE . He simply hadn’t made it official as he wanted to see how far he could match the Depths of Absolute Sovereignty without having stepped into this stage himself. But...","\" The Depths of Absolute Sovereignty are also a power. And I can continue refining my foundation even while gaining deeper and deeper Depths...\"","...!","He looked at The Infiniverse and Ruination with calm certainty.","\" Alongside my Lineage, my Foundation, my Organ, and everything else about me reaching my Way, I will officially take my Way of Mana and Hunger to THE. THE Primordial Civilization of Mana. THE Primordial Civilization of Hunger.\"","His voice grew stronger, more resolute.","\" And with THE Way of Mana... would it also not be THE Way of The First Tongue? The First Tongue is Mana given structure. Mana given meaning. Mana given voice. They are not separate things. They are the same thing wearing different faces.\"","HUUM!","\"So let it all fall into place before The Fallout. Let everything I have built and everything I have become consolidate into what it was always meant to be.\"","Some people took eons to attain THE . Some were born at THE when Existence differentiated. But THE was a struggle. Attaining THE was hard.","But at this time...","\"I have Mana. I am Mana.\"","HUUM!","\"I have Infinite Mana. I am... Infinite Mana.\"","WAA!","\" And as of this moment, it shall be THE Infinite Mana. It shall be THE Way of Mana. It shall be MY Way of Mana. MY Way of THE First Tongue. MY First Tongue.\"","HUUM !","Unfathomable brilliance bloomed.","The color blue-gold erupted and spread out across this domain. Past the Early Veiled Shore. Across The Infiniverse.","Outside The Infiniverse into the Wandering Territories. And into the Lands of the Living and the Dead.","A blue-gold light representing the assertion of a unique authority established itself across Existence!","It was an unfathomable light of brilliance!","It was a choice.","And with every choice, there came other choices. With every action, there was an equal and opposite reaction.","At this same time as a declaration was made across Existence.","Inside of THE Loom , in that endless sea of Paradox.","THE Living Paradox sensed the unknown changes across Existence. His form, barely visible through the countless flames of paradox that surrounded him, went still.","He could sense these changes. He could feel how they caused Chaos, Existence, and Paradox itself to resonate and shift.","Something had just been claimed. Something had just been declared.","And the ripples of that declaration were spreading faster than light, faster than thought, faster than causality itself.","The balance had shifted.","And as a result of this...","THE Living Paradox raised his hand with calm certainty. His voice was measured, ancient, absolute.","\" There is... no more time for waiting. No more time for preparation.","HUUM!","He snapped his fingers.","The metaphorical clock that counted toward Midnight trembled. The hand that had been pointing at Five Seconds lurched forward.","Past Four.","Past Three.","Past Two.","THE Living Paradox breathed out as if he was getting ready.","\"It is now... One Second to Midnight.\"","BOOM!","The sea of Paradox churned with anticipation of what was to come.","---","Outside of THE Loom.","In that region of Collapse where Noah had locked Schrodinger and The Disciple of THE Creature.","He floated calmly in the blue-gold brilliance as he looked at the manifestation of a clock that had been Five Seconds to Midnight.","And in the next moment, he watched the hand of the clock moving.","From Five.","To Four.","To Three.","To Two.","Until it reached One.","Until there was just a sliver to Midnight.","One Second to Midnight.","Noah gazed at this calmly.","He knew his immensity. One of the reasons he’d held back from THE was this. But he was not fearful.","The Fallout? Okay.","Let it fucking come.","THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty would only be one of his tools. THE First Tongue was his main tool. His Mana was his tool.","And it was mighty.","It was sharp.","And it was hungry for blood!"]},{"number":4661,"title":"Chapter 4661: Chapter 4660: THE! I","paragraphs":["In that centermost region of The Infiniverse, in that brilliant blue-gold sea filled with Phonemes and Logos of The First Tongue.","Noah pulsed with an incandescent blue-gold light of THE Civilizational Authority.","But he wasn’t alone in this.","So did The Infiniverse. So did Ruination.","After all, his Civilization was intricately connected to them.","The Infiniverse was the literal bedrock. The thing holding his Civilization. His entrance into THE was her entrance into THE . She was becoming THE Infiniverse.","Ruination was intricately fused with him and his system. She felt like an unbreakable part of him, and she would enjoy and be elevated all around just like him.","This was his Way. His Civilization. His immensity!","He had already been in the state of THE with his weight. Now, it felt like the eruption of all his potential.","Of his foundation.","|A Higher Scale of Existence is being grasped officially.|","| Your existence is attaining THE Level One Scale of Existence.|","|Transition initiating...|","...!","In that unique space where he stood with Ruination and The Infiniverse, his eyes shone brightly as he sensed everything.","THE Level One Scale of Existence.","This whole time, he had been in The Level Zero Scale of Existence. And he had managed to do grand things within it. He had suppressed THEs in this lower scale. He had done things THEs couldn’t do in this lower scale.","The potential for what he could do at a Higher Scale was unfathomably grand.","The transition was not violent or painful.","It was... clarifying.","Like someone had been looking at existence through a foggy window their entire life, and now that window had been cleaned for the first time. Well, no. Not cleaned. Removed entirely. He wasn’t looking through anything anymore. He was simply seeing!","Oh!","The waves and strings that made up existence became even more clear to him now. Before, he had glimpsed them. Understood them intellectually. Felt their presence when he focused.","Now they were simply there. Constantly visible, constantly tangible, and constantly real.","He could move faster than Planck Speed. And at this scale, he could see the countless minute strings that made up existence. Strings as small as Planck Length vibrated with frequencies that held the secrets of reality itself. Each string sang its own song. Each vibration told its own story.","And he could hear them all.","The Phonemes of The First Tongue held their own waves. Their own vibrations. The Weavings of The First Tongue connecting them all had their own signatures. Like fingerprints made of pure meaning. Like DNA composed of primordial truth.","He could feel more intricately how Fire burned.","When he looked at this Phoneme now, he could instantly sense all of its 81 Variations. Each variation was a different aspect of fire. A different truth about transformation and a different expression of energy released.","As a Perfect Speaker of The First Tongue who now grasped a Depth, this seemed only natural.","This was why it was easier for THE entities to grasp The First Tongue even though they didn’t follow The Way of Mana. Even though they specialized, their Ways were different dialects of The First Tongue. They could form that connection with it once they could more easily see the intricacy of existence at THE Level One Scale of Existence.","Everything made more sense now.","Everything felt more real!","|Confirmation: You have laid an absolute claim over The First Tongue.|","| Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect shine with glory . At this moment, you are gaining 100% of the Harvest in the form of Infinite Potential of all Mana being utilized across Observable Existence.|","|As the true form of Mana, the claim laid on The First Tongue will also generate benefit.|","|All utilization of The First Tongue in your Observable Existence will reinforce and refine your existence in the form of Infinite Potential.|","|There is Utilization of The First Tongue in The Past, The Present, and The Future.|","| At your current stage, 1% of the utilization of The First Tongue in the past and present is being harvested as Infinite Potential.|","|You are unable to harvest from the future.|","|The Infinite Potential floods into your Foundation and your Civilization.|","|Your Depth is becoming more quintessential.|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with immensity as he felt an influx of endless waves of potential.","His Civilization was advancing, and it was doing so with immense grandness.","Without even closing his eyes, he felt his Walls of Civilization surrounding his Manifested Civilization in his mind transforming. The structures that had protected his Civilization since its inception were evolving into something far grander. Something befitting THE!","|The Walls of Your Civilization have become THE Bastions of Infinity.|","|The Designation of Your Civilization has jumped past the Third Designation to arrive in the Fourth Designation: THE Civilization Continuum.|","|THE Bastions of Infinity have begun to be passively manifested across The Infiniverse.|","|Capability: Inherently manifesting 100 Logos of Defensive Architecture per hour.|","| Your Civilization is now at THE Level One Scale of Existence.|","|Changes have only just begun to unfold.|","|The masses of your Civilization will experience unknown and grand changes in the near future.|","...!","Noah felt THE Infiniverse pulsing as everything around them became more concentrated.","This entire area he was in was now filled with THE Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger . Hundreds of Phonemes and their variations bloomed every second. Fire. Water. Earth. Air. Light. Darkness. Time. Space. All eighteen base Phonemes and their countless variations manifested and dissolved and manifested again in an endless cycle!","THE Infiniverse was breathing The First Tongue!","Fucking breathing it!","Oh!","And even as these changes took place, his own existence was receiving immense seas of Infinite Potential. Even though he had just attained THE...","|Your Foundation has taken in an unfathomable amount of Infinite Potential.|","|Eruption of immensity detected.|","|The weight of your existence is now exceeding THE Surface Depth.|","| Spillover into Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty confirmed.|","|Status Update: While your Way is at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, the Weight of Your Existence is at Intermediate Depth.|","| THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons expands its Chapters and Pages with your brilliance.|","...!"]},{"number":4662,"title":"Chapter 4662: Chapter 4661: THE! II","paragraphs":["Noah felt THE Organ of Civilization and THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons in his mind pulsing with immensity. They were drawing in tremendous waves of potential endlessly. Like twin hearts pumping not blood but pure possibility through the veins of his existence.","Across his veins and vessels and Heart of Infinite Lexicons, rivers of Phonemes and Logos had now begun to flow and refine his existence passively. He could feel them coursing through him. Fire warming his meridians. Water cooling his consciousness. Earth stabilizing his foundation. Air lightening his spirit.","All of it flowing and all of it refining. All of it making him more!","And regardless of apocalypses, struggles, unfairness... the one thing he always loved across existence was exactly this.","The sense of advancement.","The sense of finding out something new.","The sense of unmasking the wonders of existence.","Even putting aside all the messy aspects of existence and all the terrifying beings out there, the sheer fact that he, a nobody, now laid claim to one of the aspects of The Oldest Paradox of Existence ... that alone was enough to cause him to reflect with amazement.","He had started as a human. A regular human in a world that had been invaded by dungeons and monsters. He had clawed his way up through blood and pain and impossible choices. He had become a King. An Emperor. A being that shook Folds.","And now he had laid claim to The First Tongue itself.","Yes, existence could suck sometimes.","But it held so many wonders that he wanted to continue exploring. It held so many limits he wanted to overcome that he didn’t want it to end.","The Fallout would not end this.","THE Living Paradox or THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos would not end his path.","He would ensure it.","After all, he had just laid claim to THE First Tongue itself. He had laid a claim on THE Infinite Mana on the eve of a terrifying Apocalypse .","Surviving The Fallout would merely be the first step. He was genuinely curious what THE Living Paradox and THE Creature had in store.","And of course, THE Living Elemental , that bum of an existence, that waste of elements, his sworn enemy across existence, would also be free from THE Loom.","He smiled as he thought of this.","And more prompts came.","|Notification: The Edicts of Your Civilization are being edited to match your current Way.|","|All subsidiary structures must evolve according to your Way after it has attained THE .|","|The Sovereign Spires of Osmont have completed their journey.|","|Final Stage Achieved: THE Stanchions of Infinity.|","| THE Stanchions of Infinity are conceptual pillars of support within your existence.|","|They reinforce your Foundation, stabilize your Civilization, and anchor your Way to Observable Existence itself.|","| Features of THE Stanchions of Infinity:|","|Feature One: Civilization Specialization Unlock. The Stanchions unlock additional Civilization Specializations for your people.|","|Feature Two: Passive Phoneme Production. Each Stanchion acts as a passive producer of Phonemes of The First Tongue within your existence. Production Rate: 3 Phonemes per Stanchion per hour currently, will scale upwards.|","|Feature Three: External Manifestation Capability. THE Stanchions of Infinity can be outwardly manifested to establish THE Existential Faraday Cage.|","| THE Existential Faraday Cage:|","|159 THE Stanchions of Infinity can be placed around The Infiniverse to block external Weavings of Existence.|","|All components of existence are composed of waves and strings at their most fundamental level.|","|THE Existential Faraday Cage is a barrier designed to absorb external attacks that come as forms of waves and strings.|","|Energy attacks, authority suppression, conceptual assaults, temporal manipulation, spatial distortion, and even attacks composed of The First Tongue itself will be absorbed by the Cage rather than penetrating to the interior.|","|Absorption Capacity: Dependent on the combined strength of all 159 Stanchions.|","...!","Noah observed internally as these Stanchions manifested within his existence.","THE Quintessential Stanchion of Infinity shined with a colorless grandeur. It looked like some sort of infinitely stretching tower that had no end. Just eternal vertical expanse.","THE Tyranny Stanchion of Infinity shined stellar purple. Its surface crackled with authority that demanded submission from all who perceived it.","THE Loot Stanchion of Infinity gleamed with pure gold. Wealth and harvest radiated from it in waves that promised endless accumulation.","And many more!","All 159 were lit up brilliantly. They looked like pillars supporting his Foundation even more securely than before. Each one unique. Each one powerful. Each one a testament to how far his Civilization had come.","He broke down the capabilities of THE Stanchions of Infinity in his mind.","Passive Phoneme production meant his mastery of The First Tongue would continue growing even when he wasn’t actively cultivating. 159 Stanchions producing 3 Phonemes per hour each. That was 477 Phonemes per hour flooding into his existence automatically.","The Civilization Specializations would give his people more paths to power. More ways to grow. More options for surviving what was coming.","But the Faraday Cage...","That was the real prize.","A barrier that could absorb attacks composed of waves and strings. And since all components of existence were waves and strings at their most fundamental level, that meant the barrier could absorb essentially anything.","Energy. Authority. Concepts. Time. Space. Even The First Tongue.","Everything.","Noah thought about this paired with the Logos and Phonemes that he and The Infiniverse were forging outside the barrier of The Infiniverse. Defensive Architecture being passively manifested. Hundreds of Phonemes blooming. THE Bastions of Infinity producing 100 Logos of Defensive Architecture per hour.","Would it all not be more than enough for survival against The Fallout?","He smiled at the thought. As he was thinking this...","In the next moment, another set of prompts cascaded down.","But...","HUUM!","They came from the surrounding existence. From the glimmer of THE Civilizational Authority Noah could now see across existence. They didn’t simply come as a prompt.","Noah heard...a voice.","And it was a heavy and deep voice that held unfathomable majesty.","This voice said...","| Welcome, you have arrived truly and finally in THE Vakochev Scales of Existence. You now matter. You now...|","...!","The voice stopped midway before it continued.","| Error.|","HUUM!","|Error.|","|...|","There was a long pause as Noah stared with stern eyes, and then...","| Vakochev has grown aware of an Anomalous entrant in THE Scales of Existence.|","BOOM!","|Vakochev welcomes the challenge.|","...!","BOOM!","With a burst of brilliance, the voice and its majestic brilliance faded.","Noah’s eyes pulsed as his existence buzzed. His expression grew heavy.","Vakochev?","Vakochev?!"]},{"number":4663,"title":"Chapter 4663: Chapter 4662: THE! III","paragraphs":["The name pulsed in his mind again and again as he did not think much of it when he heard it the first time!","But to have a voice resound and speak it to him...was this something that occured for everyone that arrived in THE Level One Scale of Existence?","Because that was a welcome.","Naturally, a welcome was something which would be given to everyone!","He wondered about THE Vakochev Scales of Existence and what that voice meant as his existence continued to buzz.","Vakochev was affirmed to be a being. Shockingly, they had gotten their name on THE Scales of Existence themselves.","How grand were they? How immense were they? And what about him was considered anomalous for Vakochev to extend a challenge?","Were THE Creature, THE Living Paradox, and others of their caliber also considered Anomalous in the same manner as him?","As he was thinking about all of these things...","|Notification: Claim on The First Tongue has been registered across Observable Existence.|","| After laying claim to The First Tongue, you now need to find and claim THE Axioms of The Oldest Paradox of Existence.|","| THE Axioms of Observable Existence.|","| Historical Context: At the moment Observable Existence differentiated, four aspects collided and separated simultaneously. Chaos. Existence. Paradox. The First Tongue.|","|This collision was violent beyond comprehension. Reality itself screamed into being.|","|And in that scream, fragments of pure conceptual truth broke off from each aspect and scattered across the newly born Observable Existence.|","|These are Axioms of Observable Existence.|","|They are living truths. Sentient fundamentals. The building blocks of reality that gained awareness at the moment of differentiation.|","| The Answer to The Oldest Paradox of Existence may be given by the one who holds the most power, or the most Axioms of Observable Existence.|","|There may be no difference between the two.|","BOOM!","The prompts were blazing with information as Noah looked at them with shining eyes while repeating the words.","\" THE Axioms of Observable Existence...\"","What the fuck was this now?","First The First Tongue. Then THE Vakochev Scales . Now Axioms that were apparently fragments of the four aspects that made up The Oldest Paradox of Existence.","Every time he thought he understood the depth of Observable Existence, another layer revealed itself. Another system. Another truth. Another thing he needed to find, capture, or claim.","He wasn’t complaining. Not really. This was exactly what he loved about existence. The endless discovery! The constant revelation that there was always more.","But still.","Axioms of Observable Existence. Living truths scattered across all of reality since the moment of differentiation.","How many were there? Where were they hidden? Who already possessed them?","The questions burned in his mind, but he didn’t have answers. Not yet.","What he did have was another objective.","Find and claim THE Axioms of Observable Existence! In addition to surviving The Fallout, going against Paradox, Elemental, and potentially THE Creature, endlessly forging his Foundation, and progress further in his Way In the First Tongue.","It was...light fucking work!","—","Far from The Infiniverse.","In the Lands of The Dead.","After obtaining control of the Disciples of THE Creature , The Great Usurper continued his idle expansion. But this time, it was with purpose.","The Disciples seemed to hold a great deal of knowledge of unique places. He simply directed his mass of invisible consciousness to flow that way, and he moved even faster than light across the Lands of the Dead.","He crossed domains of utter wonders with the Disciples forging the way forward.","Regions where death had crystallized into geometric patterns of impossible beauty. Regions where the silence was so profound it had become a physical force. Regions where the concept of ending had manifested as landscapes of perpetual twilight.","All of it fascinating. None of it his destination.","After some time, they arrived in a region that held orderly white and obsidian river passageways.","River Passageways.","The Great Usurper found these to be unique. The rivers didn’t flow with water. They flowed with something else. Authority, perhaps. Or maybe pure order given liquid form. White streams intertwined with obsidian currents in patterns that seemed random but weren’t.","Only the Disciples knew exactly which rivers to jump on and when to jump to another in order to arrive at an extremely isolated domain that they had passed through exactly once.","Without worrying about the consequences, The Great Usurper commanded the three Disciples of THE Creature to enter these rivers.","With pristine order and care, they jumped sequentially one after another at exactly precise timings.","First Disciple: White river, third branch, seven seconds.","Second Disciple: Obsidian current, crossing junction, three seconds.","Third Disciple: White-obsidian confluence, diving deep, instantaneous.","And then they disappeared.","The moment they did, The Great Usurper felt his consciousness expanding once more as...","|Discovery Registered.|","| You have discovered a portion of the Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature.|","|Warning: This domain contains authority far exceeding your current existence.|","|Proceed with extreme caution.|","BOOM!","With such a grand introduction, The Great Usurper found his senses expanding out rapidly as he captured an utterly glorious continental landscape.","The horizon stretched endlessly with golden sands that seemed to drink in light and radiate warmth simultaneously. Not the harsh gold of desert heat, but the rich gold of something precious. Something alive. Something that had been cultivated with care beyond mortal comprehension.","Unfathomably tall trees stretched out for light years. Their trunks were wider than planets. Their branches spread across dimensions. Their leaves rustled with sounds that weren’t sounds but meanings. Each tree was its own ecosystem, its own world, its own truth.","And the entire place was filled with a terrifying concentration of THE Civilizational Authority.","The authority of the being who had shaped Observable Existence itself. The authority of the one who had given away his Everythings (supposedly) and still remained the most influential force in all of reality.","Even as a fragment of his former domain, the Early Veiled Shore radiated power that made The Great Usurper’s consciousness tremble.","But more than all of this...","As The Great Usurper sent the Disciples of THE Creature further in...","As his idle existence continued to spread in this unfathomable domain...","His entire existence buzzed and almost spazzed out as if it came across something far too pristine.","Because in the midst of two unfathomably tall trees, there was an object.","It seemed to be half-covered by golden sands. But it shone with a dim obsidian-gold allure that called to something deep within his consciousness. Something primal. Something that recognized what it was looking at even before the prompts confirmed it.","When The Great Usurper focused on it...","|ALERT: EXTREME DANGER DETECTED.|","| You have discovered the Fourth Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox.|","|Classification: Origin Axiom Fragment.|","|The Axiom of Primordial Paradox grants absolute authority over contradiction itself.|","|The holder can make anything impossible possible, and anything possible impossible.|","|Current Status: Dormant.|","|WARNING: You are too weak to even gaze upon it.|","|Just for this observation, half of your Weavings of Existence have been used up.|","|Seriously, stop looking at it.|","|If you wake it and it poses THE Question to you, which you will be unable to answer, your entire existence could very well unravel.|","| LOOK AWAY.|","BOOM!","The Great Usurper was shocked as he sensed immense weakness in his existence.","Half of his Weavings. Gone. Just from looking at the thing.","He had come across the Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature using his Disciples, and there seemed to be utterly terrifying things in this place. Things that could destroy him without even trying. Things that existed on a level so far above him that his mere observation was an offense punishable by existential erosion.","He immediately pulled his consciousness back from the object. The obsidian-gold allure faded as distance grew between them, but the damage was done. Half his Weavings. Consumed by a single glance.","The Fourth Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox!","What...the hell was this thing?!"]},{"number":4664,"title":"Chapter 4664: Chapter 4663: THE! IV","paragraphs":["Mysteries were infuriating.","They gnawed at the mind like parasites. They kept one awake during moments that should have been restful. They whispered questions without answers and dangled truths just out of reach.","From a certain perspective, mysteries were the cruelest aspect of existence. They reminded everyone that knowledge was incomplete. That understanding was always partial. That no matter how much one learned, there would always be something hidden, something obscured, something deliberately kept in shadow.","Some entities spent their entire existences chasing mysteries only to die with more questions than they started with. Some went mad from the pursuit. Some simply gave up and accepted ignorance as a form of peace.","Some would say that mysteries were existence’s way of mocking those who sought truth. A reminder that the Existence owed no explanations to anyone. That reality was under no obligation to make sense.","And yet.","As much as some hated mysteries, they kept existence churning.","Because that pristine moment when everything comes together. When every little piece fits a larger puzzle. When the fog lifts and the truth stands undeniable before you...oh!","That was a moment that could give a high even the strongest drugs could not replicate.","It made all the frustration worth it. All the sleepless nights. All the maddening speculation. All the dead ends and false leads and moments of despair.","One moment of truth could redeem a lifetime of confusion.","And that was why mysteries, despite being infuriating, were also beautiful.","Noah loved to solve mysteries.","He routinely thought about THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Paradox and how all of them fit in the Weavings of this Observable Existence. The connections between them. The conflicts that stretched back to the moment of differentiation. The truths that had been hidden beneath layers of legend and misinformation.","When the pieces came together, and they eventually did, the satisfaction was immense.","Not long ago, he only knew the legends and the Stories of the Earliest Folds. Vague tales of primordial conflicts and ancient powers. Names spoken with reverence but little understanding.","Since then, he had uncovered the truth of what truly happened all those eons ago.","He knew about Ginnungagap. About THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, and Temporal. About the coming of THE Living Existences and the creation of THE Loom. About the betrayals and alliances and schemes that had shaped everything.","Not all of it. Not yet. But more than he had known before.","So everything eventually would be solved.","Because at this moment, as he was thinking about many things, he was looking at the Principles of Existence that had helped get him exactly to where he was right now.","They were being elevated to the Genesis Stage.","To a Philology of The First Tongue.","Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect were the first. They had already transcended their previous forms and become something grander. Living expressions of The First Tongue woven into the very fabric of his existence.","After the Logos of his other three Principles were broken down, their meaning and what they stood for seemed to be more inclined with Undifferentiated Mana. Their workings would likely fall under that umbrella and allow Noah to obtain more of their benefits through Undifferentiated Mana itself.","Sometimes having too many concepts and abilities did not mean strength.","Making things simpler led to even greater power.","Consolidation over accumulation. Unity over multiplicity! One perfect tool instead of a hundred mediocre ones.","As he was doing all of this, he looked over to the entity opposite him.","THE Infiniverse.","Her entire body was currently filled with swirling Logos of The First Tongue. They spiraled through her form like galaxies being born, each one a perfect expression of meaning given structure. An air of power buzzed around her that seemed heavy and terrifying for even THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","She was transforming and becoming something that matched his own elevation!","Noah asked her lightly, \" How is everything proceeding?\"","THE Infiniverse opened her eyes.","They looked like multicolored jewels, like colors that held meaning and colors that were themselves a form of language.","\" For me, it is different ,\" she said. Her voice was calm and imposing, resonating with authority that came from being the literal foundation of a Primordial Civilization. \"I am the object of The Civilization. I am the actual construct that supports your Civilization. So I gain the boons since you have advanced your Way and your Civilization.\"","She paused, her jeweled eyes shimmering with contemplation.","\" But I also gain the boons from myself. Because I, as a construct that has consciousness, am also experiencing the elevation into the Depths of Absolute Sovereignty. Since I house countless Universes, Existential Domains, Omniverses, Wheels of Existence, and budding Transcendent Folds... all of these are now being elevated from a lower Scale of Existence to reach THE Level One Scale of Existence.\"","Her hands moved as she spoke, twirling seamlessly with Logos of The First Tongue. The letters formed and dissolved around her fingers like living things responding to her will.","\" When this transformation is complete, THE Infiniverse will not be like it was before. Whatever happens on the outside with The Fallout, I will be able to elevate the inside of myself to eventually exceed even THE Loom.\"","Her expression held quiet confidence.","\" Unless that construct is also similar to me. Unless it also has a consciousness. Which I doubt.\"","Noah smiled and nodded at her words.","THE Loom was impressive. A structure that housed THE Living Existences and their domains.","But it was built by others. Designed by committee. A collaborative effort between beings with conflicting interests.","The Infiniverse was his. Built from his authority and grown from his Civilization. Animated by consciousness that was loyal to him absolutely.","That made all the difference.","He looked at the blue-gold illusory figure of Ruination, who was also being elevated. Her form seemed more solid than before. More real. As if the advancement into THE was granting her greater substance in addition to greater power.","Even before he asked, she answered.","\" My computational abilities,\" Ruination said. Her voice was calm but held undertones of something that might have been wonder. Or perhaps concern. \" Well, they are entering a scale where things seem a bit scary, even for me.\"","She paused, processing her own advancement with the same analytical precision she applied to everything else.","\" But the summary of it is that I can take care of quite literally everything for you. If you give me the permission to, I may even be able to do it faster than you could yourself.\"","Her illusory form flickered with cascading data streams as she continued.","\" Decoding and elevating your Principles. Designing your own Core Phonemes. Monitoring and increasing the Logos and Phonemes running across your body and refining your existence. Writing more on and expanding the Chapters of THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons. Increasing your Mastery of The First Tongue with constant practice. Monitoring THE Infinite Desmoterion.\"","She wasn’t finished.","\"I can even take over one of your bodies and perform the teaching duties in the Early Veiled Shore. Laying out THE Faraday Cage. Handling the new Civilization Specializations. And I have already begun a database for THE Axioms of Observable Existence. If any Weavings relating to them are mentioned across the Folds and Wandering Territories, I will detect them.\"","Her jeweled eyes met his directly.","\"I could basically do everything for Master, should you give me the permission to do so.\"","...!","Her words were filled with brilliance.","Noah smiled even more after he heard them. When he thought about the many things she could do, possibilities unfolded like flowers blooming in accelerated time.","He began giving her directions on which things she could directly get started on.","\" Handle the elevation of remaining Principles into Philologies. Coordinate with THE Infiniverse on Faraday Cage placement. Continue the database for Axioms...\"","Ruination absorbed each instruction with perfect precision.","\" Maintain passive refinement of my existence through continuous Phoneme and Logos circulation. Expand THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons with new insights as they emerge. Monitor THE Infinite Desmoterion and advancements from it...\"","More instructions. More delegation. More efficiency!","After all, efficiency was key in existence. All the countless background processes of advancement could be taken care of while he continued to unceasingly move forward.","Existence was a struggle and almost always unfair.","But he had the tools to cheat existence and make the playing field tilt slightly to his favor.","Others had to do everything themselves.","But what was a Civilization? It was not singular. It was made up of many!","So he would put the many to work. He would even put Tor and THE Living Origin and The First Farmer to work!","Everything working together. Everything contributing to his advancement. Everything tilting the playing field in his direction!"]},{"number":4665,"title":"Chapter 4665: Chapter 4664: Surprise I","paragraphs":["In that unique space filled with extremely pure blue-gold Primus Mana, Noah allowed Ruination to take care of many things as he focused on himself.","He felt the weight and immensity of THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty as the process of his Way and Civilization advancing was a gradual one that continued to unfold with each passing moment.","He was getting new changes and being exposed to new prompts every now and then as different aspects of himself surprised him and made unique advancements that he hadn’t anticipated.","In his entrance to THE Level One Scale of Existence and even a bit before it, he had gotten a great deal of titles and distinctions like THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, THE Potentate, and THE Anomaly. Even he himself had declared how he was Mana, THE Mana, THE Infinite Mana, and THE First Tongue!","But even though he had declared all those grand distinctions, the last one felt like an empty title, something that he shouted out but didn’t truly receive or embody.","Because if he truly was THE First Tongue, boy oh boy would he feel different now.","How crazy was it if he truly was THE First Tongue itself? Would he not then be able to control a significant portion of Observable Existence?","No, he didn’t fully and truly embody THE First Tongue as for now he had laid a claim on it and was working toward truly embodying it. The day where he fully and truly embodied THE First Tongue may be the day he could look at THE Creature , the fucking guy who could cause him existential damage just from prolonged staring and exposure when he was in Ginnungagap.","The next time he met this entity, he wanted to be able to look and do whatever he wanted while having the power to at least stand opposite him.","As much as the possibility was there that this entity might be an enemy against him, Noah’s intuition was actually leaning on the other side because THE Creature felt too complex to simply be an enemy.","Well, THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos were complex on their own with unknown motivations and machinations, but his intuition toward THE Creature was different in ways he couldn’t fully articulate.","The decisions of THE Creature could be questioned, but when it came to all the things that Noah’s human psychology would consider bad or evil, there weren’t truly much to point to. THE Creature imprisoned all the entities in the Infinite Unfurling, but wasn’t Noah imprisoning entities right now in his Infinite Desmoterion?","He smiled at the parallel as maybe he had some sort of bias when it came to THE Creature because this being also had their own machinations, and he kept thinking about what he would have been forced to resort to or what could have happened if THE Creature had not intervened in Ginnungagap.","THE Creature lent him a hand since his actions helped Existence itself, but how much more would THE Creature continue to help him when the last thing that this being did was not listen to The Dead Order’s demand to collapse him?","That was significant and meaningful in ways that suggested THE Creature was not his enemy, not yet anyways.","As he was thinking about all of this...","\" Oh?\"","He blinked as he received new waves of information that weren’t from prompts or a ridiculous voice welcoming him to THE Vakochev Scales of Existence , but was actually a message from Malphas. His very hardworking butler had actually made a finding and reached out to him right away.","The finding related to The Primordial Early Excavation Depths that he had gained access to in what seemed like forever ago in his Early Veiled Shore, but it was merely weeks since then as time moved strangely when every day brought apocalyptic revelations and existential advancements.","The Primordial Early Excavation Depths were dimensional mines that extended into collapsed fragments of the Earliest Folds, containing resources that no longer existed anywhere else in the current Observable Existence like Ore of Early Resonance, Crystallized Temporal Fragments, Memory Stones, Essence Gems, Paradox Minerals, and Structural Marrow.","All of it was buried in depths that stretched infinitely downward, guarded by Remnant Lifeforms from collapsed Shores who may be Living, may be Dead, or somewhere in between.","When the depths first unlocked, the volunteer Malphas lead the way to clear levels, gather resources, and explore what secrets the collapsed Earliest Folds still held.","Malphas had been diligent in this task as he cleared level after level with systematic precision, gathering resources that flowed into the Early Veiled Shore’s development while encountering Remnant Lifeforms and dispatching them with the cold efficiency that made him such an effective butler.","But he had never called out to Noah directly, not when he found rare ores, not when he discovered Memory Stones containing techniques from deceased Early Creatures, and not when environmental hazards tested the limits of his existence.","Malphas handled everything himself because that was his nature and that was his pride.","So for him to call out now meant something significant had occurred.","Noah focused on the message and learned that Malphas had arrived on the one hundredth level, the deepest level currently available and the threshold beyond which the depths would only unlock as the Shore continued evolving.","And it seemed like he had come across an immensity there, something significant enough that even Malphas with all his capability and self-sufficiency felt the need to inform his master immediately.","Noah’s eyes sparkled as he said, \" Let’s go take a look...\"","Well, even though he said that, another body was already arriving before the entrance of the depths!","The Primordial Early Excavation Depths currently manifested as a massive chasm in the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore with its edges lined with crystallized authority that shimmered with colors from eras long past while the air around it hummed with the weight of collapsed history.","Noah’s body descended into the depths without hesitation as the journey downward was swift with each level flashing past him in moments. Level 10, Level 30, Level 50, Level 75.","The environment grew stranger as he descended because reality became less stable and the walls of the mine shifted between states of existence, sometimes solid, sometimes ethereal, and sometimes something in between.","Remnant Lifeforms watched from shadows but did not approach as they recognized power far beyond their own and chose survival over confrontation.","Level 90, Level 95, Level 99.","And then Level 100.","Noah emerged into a vast cavern that shouldn’t have been able to exist because its dimensions were paradoxical and its atmosphere held the weight of eons compressed into a single space.","Malphas stood at the center with his butler attire immaculate despite the journey through a hundred levels of collapsed reality, and his expression was composed but his eyes held something Noah rarely saw in his most capable servant, which was uncertainty.","\"Master,\" Malphas said while bowing slightly, \"I apologize for the interruption to your cultivation, but I believe you need to see this yourself.\"","He gestured toward something behind him.","And Noah’s eyes widened because embedded in the wall of the hundredth level, half-buried in crystallized fragments of the Earliest Folds, was something, well, someone, that he absolutely never expected to see!"]},{"number":4666,"title":"Chapter 4666: Chapter 4665: Surprise II","paragraphs":["The Depths held fragments of The Earliest Folds.","When Noah delved into this place before, he had found a number of things, but seeing how the final level held such a thing, he moved faster than Planck Speed as he appeared at the end of the wall.","At the end of a multicolored wall that pulsed with ancient authority, there was a humanoid entity who seemed to be getting pulled into the wall itself. Multicolored chains were stuck into his body at various points, connecting back to this wall like roots drawing sustenance from soil. Each chain pulsed with its own frequency, its own color, its own terrible purpose.","A faint glimmer of THE Civilizational Authority of Existence could be felt on the walls and chains as the one bound by them seemed to be in a state of slumber, his head drooped forward and his body hanging limply like a puppet whose strings had been cut but whose frame remained suspended.","Noah’s eyes blazed with immensity and brilliance as the weight of an entity at THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty erupted from him.","He opened his eyes fully and radiated a brilliant flash of blue-gold light that shockingly released a Logos, one that closely meant \" Break what is unbreakable.\"","HUUM!","The chains of Existence binding this entity down shattered one after another in a cascade of multicolored fragments that dissolved into nothing before they even hit the ground. Each chain snapped with a sound like reality itself crying out in protest, but Noah’s authority was absolute and his command was undeniable.","Noah then appeared beside this entity who was about to fall and placed his hands around his shoulders as he slowly began to carry them from their chained location toward the center of this place.","All around them, waves of multicolored radiance permeated the space as if the cavern itself was responding to the breaking of those ancient chains. And as he moved, the entity he supported began to flutter his eyes wide open before they focused on him, and a look of shock and recognition bloomed across his features.","Then this entity smiled weakly and said, \"Haha, friend, what in the unfathomable Weavings of Existence brought you here?\"","...!","Noah looked back at this being as he brought him down to the center of this place, gazing at the weakened body of an entity he had met as a brilliant man long ago.","\"I need to ask the same of you, Anaximander,\" Noah replied with genuine curiosity mixed with concern. \" How exactly did you come to be here?\"","...!","BOOM!","Yes, it was Anaximander, the brilliant Fold Dweller he had met in The Earliest Folds!","He looked unfathomably weak as his figure even seemed illusory at some points, as if he was here and not here at the same time. His dark hair was now mixed with streaks of white that hadn’t been there before, and he was adorned in a simple white robe at this moment that hung loosely on his diminished frame. But his eyes still held that same brilliance that seemed to be thinking of countless things in one instant, that spark of endless curiosity that defined his very existence.","Noah looked at him and shook his head at the state this once vibrant entity had been reduced to.","Anaximander smiled while sighing as he began to stretch and look around at the cavern that had been his prison.","\" Too many things have happened,\" Anaximander said with a voice that held both exhaustion and a strange sense of acceptance. \"I never expected that one of the parts of me laid out across Existence would be discovered by you of all beings.\"","Noah’s brows rose at these words. \" One of the parts of your existence? There are many others out there?\"","Anaximander smiled and shook his head before he replied, \"There were many others scattered across the Folds and hidden in places that even THE entities would struggle to find. They have either been lost through time or right now since one of me has awakened, they will all return to their source.\"","He paused, and a light returned to Anaximander’s eyes slowly as he looked at Noah with an apologetic expression that held genuine remorse.","\"I heard you call me not too long ago,\" he said quietly. \"I heard your words of ’Anaximander, come!’ echoing through the Weavings of Existence itself. I am sorry that I wasn’t able to come to your aid when you needed me. It seems that I got myself mixed up in things that I had no business in, and I paid the price for it even though you had warned me about THE Existences.\"","...!","His words were heavy ones as Noah sat opposite him, processing everything he was hearing.","Nearby, the figure of Malphas ridiculously brought down a golden plate between them that had silver cups which shone with liquid that could be none other than the Sacred Mead of Existence, as if he were simply a butler serving his master and a friend during a casual afternoon visit rather than in the hundredth level of an excavation depth that held fragments of collapsed reality.","Noah took the cup and drank while staring intently at the entity opposite him who smiled and did the same before he spoke with tiredness that seemed to reach into his very soul.","\"I was always curious,\" Anaximander began, his eyes growing distant as he recalled events that clearly still haunted him. \"My mind is that of a scientist, and I always questioned everything around me. To pay back the favor of THE Weavers for showing me the Way, they told me I had to do something simple. All I had to do was go into a place and deliver to them an object. It seemed simple and harmless enough.\"","...!","He paused and took another sip of the Sacred Mead before continuing.","\"Of course, I should have known that this object was not theirs. I should have known that it belonged to another. Nobody had a chance to get this item because it was protected by authorities that would destroy anything that approached. But my Way... my Way did not even need power to bypass such things.\"","His expression grew more troubled as the memories surfaced.","\"I felt immense resistance for the first time ever, and so I simply said... ’There is no resistance in this place that can stop me.’ And when I stood before the object and it seemed far too heavy for anyone to carry, I simply said ’This is something that I can carry.’ It drained everything that I had, but I wanted to repay the favor and get back to studying Existence. So I took the object, and I delivered it to THE Weavers .\"","Anaximander’s voice dropped to something barely above a whisper.","\"The object I took... belonged to THE Creature . And it was something truly heavy as THE Weavers and their master, THE Living Paradox ... utilized it to strike against THE Heart of THE Creature.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4667,"title":"Chapter 4667: Chapter 4666: Zero I","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes became immensely sharp as he paid even more attention to Anaximander, the implications of these words sending his mind racing through countless possibilities and connections.","Anaximander looked saddened as he sighed with a sense of guilt that seemed to have been eating at him for eons.","\"You cannot imagine the sense of guilt I felt,\" he continued, his voice heavy with regret that time had done nothing to diminish. \"Because to me at that time, I had already met THE Creature. THE Creature was... a friend who had shown me kindness and curiosity about my unique nature. And I had effectively and unknowingly betrayed a friend by delivering the very weapon that would be used to wound him in ways that even now I do not fully understand.\"","THE Living Paradox had actually used Anaximander as a weapon against THE Creature.","The way this was done was intricate and unique in itself as Noah found himself questioning how THE Weavers had known and realized the power that Anaximander held. How did they know he could do what he could do? And that it could even work to take something that belonged to THE Creature, which was terrifying enough that it could be used to harm him?","There were far too many questions swirling in his mind, but Noah had to start somewhere.","\" When did you meet THE Creature ?\" he asked.","Anaximander smiled at the question as memories of simpler times seemed to flicker across his brilliant eyes.","\"It was actually not too long after I met you,\" he replied with a hint of nostalgia in his voice. \"After we parted ways on that snowy landscape in the Earliest Folds, I made my existence seek out someone that could answer my curiosities and questions about the nature of reality itself. And I was led naturally to THE Creature , as if Existence itself knew that he was the one who could satisfy my endless hunger for understanding.\"","He looked at Noah with an expression that held both fondness and regret.","\" THE Creature was even curious and asking me about you when I told him I had made another friend before him,\" Anaximander continued. \"But at that time you told me not to spread your name and Weavings, so I held my mouth and simply described you as an interesting entity I had encountered in my travels.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes turned sharp at these words.","Because this in itself was unique as even before THE Creature had met Anaximander, he had personally gazed at Noah way before The Earliest Folds in Ginnungagap where THE Creature had saved him from the hands of THE Living Temporal . So THE Creature had always known about him, or at least a glimpse of his figure when he intervened in that moment of crisis. He simply did not know that Noah was the same one that Anaximander was talking about when he mentioned his new friend.","If THE Creature had known that Noah was in the Earliest Folds at that time, would Noah have gotten another visitor?","The possibilities were many and the implications even greater, but Noah shook his head and focused back on Anaximander before he said, \" A lot has happened since then, and I don’t know how much you know. But THE Living Paradox suppressed the Existence of THE Creature and built a weapon called THE Loom, a weapon that he will set off anytime within the next few hours or a few days to bring about an endless and catastrophic storm that will lay waste across Existence. Do you remember when I asked you in the Earliest Folds how to overcome such an ordeal?\"","Anaximander smiled with nostalgia at the memory, his eyes lighting up with that familiar spark of intellectual delight.","\"Haha, I told you to become the storm,\" he said with genuine warmth in his weakened voice. \"My friend, have you succeeded in becoming the storm itself?\"","...!","At such words, Noah looked at the features of this entity in front of him before he nodded slowly and said, \" Somewhat. But how did you come to be here?\"","Anaximander looked around at this place filled with serene multicolored rivers that flowed in patterns that defied conventional physics, his expression growing more somber as he recalled the events that led to his imprisonment.","\"Even after finding out about my betrayal, THE Creature seemingly understood and took me in my weakened state from THE Weavers and THE Living Paradox,\" Anaximander explained with wonder still evident in his voice despite the suffering he had endured. \"My existence itself seems to be hated by them as they sought to destroy me completely after my uses were done, with my Guidelines barely remaining intact as THE Creature moved to secure me before Paradox could finish what he started.\"","...!","Anaximander’s Guidelines.","The very foundation of his impossible power. Guideline #1: I exist. Guideline #2: I will continue to exist. Guideline #3: My existence cannot be unwillingly altered or ended by the will or authority of another, and any hostile action or intent directed at him would be treated not as an attack but as an interesting but ultimately irrelevant external phenomenon.","These Guidelines allowed Anaximander to simply decide that attacks did not apply to him, that resistance could not stop him, that weight was something he could carry if he declared it so. His power was ridiculous in its simplicity and terrifying in its implications because it meant that the fundamental rules of Existence were merely suggestions to him rather than absolute laws.","If such a power were to grow and mature, if Anaximander were to expand his Guidelines further and further, the potential across Existence was limitless. He could simply declare that he was stronger than THE entities and make it so. He could declare that THE Loom could not harm him and walk through The Fallout untouched. He could declare that he was THE and become THE through sheer assertion of will.","No wonder THE Living Paradox wanted him destroyed.","Anaximander continued with a voice that held deep gratitude despite his weakened state.","\" THE Creature did not need to worry about me given everything else that was happening,\" he said softly. \"But for some reason, Paradox wanted to collapse me completely, and THE Creature wanted to save me. To the extent that the weapon I took from him was used against him, and yet he still moved to secure me. To ensure that Paradox would never find me as he battled against them until I could regain the power that made me who I am.\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":4668,"title":"Chapter 4668: Chapter 4667: Zero II","paragraphs":["He paused and looked at Noah with eyes that held centuries of gratitude for a being who had shown him kindness when he deserved none.","\"I told THE Creature to spread my Weavings out across Existence so that I could hide in fragments until the time was right,\" Anaximander continued. \"I set up new Guidelines to make it possible, declaring that my existence could be divided and scattered without diminishing my core self. When a time in the future came when things settled down, a friend could come and wake me. I thought that friend would be THE Creature returning after his victory, but it turned out to be you.\"","He smiled with genuine warmth.","\" So here we are, Friend.\"","...!","Here they were.","Noah silently thought about everything he had just learned before he looked at Anaximander closely and asked the question that had been burning in his mind since he first encountered this impossible being.","\" What is your Way?\"","...!","His Way.","Anaximander smiled at this question as he looked up to the endlessly obsidian ceiling above them, his expression one of peaceful contemplation as he considered how to explain something that defied conventional explanation.","\" My Way is My Way,\" he began with that familiar tone of a scientist trying to describe something beyond normal parameters. \" My Way is The Way. THE Creature called it The Way of THE Way when we discussed it during our conversations. I called it just... My Way. The Way of Self.\"","He looked back at Noah with eyes that held the weight of profound understanding.","\"You can call it another name if you wish, but it is simply a relationship between me and Existence,\" Anaximander continued. \"I tell Existence how things should be, and Existence simply needs to listen. That is the Way. That is my Way. I do not fight against reality or bend it through force or authority. I simply inform reality of how things are for me, and reality accepts my declaration as truth.\"","...!","BOOM!","The Way of THE Way.","The Way of Self.","A power that allowed its wielder to redefine their relationship with Existence itself, to make declarations that reality was obligated to accept, to exist outside the normal parameters that bound even THE entities.","Noah looked at Anaximander with new understanding as the pieces fell into place. This was why THE Living Paradox wanted him destroyed so badly. This was why THE Creature moved to protect him despite the betrayal. This was why such a being had been hidden in fragments across Existence rather than allowed to remain whole.","Anaximander’s Way was a threat to the very order that THE Living Paradox sought to impose through THE Loom and The Fallout.","Because how could you destroy someone who simply declared that they could not be destroyed?","How could you impose your will on someone who had already declared that external wills did not apply to them?","How could you win against someone who had decided that they had already won?","It was an absurd Way, and even with it, that bum, Paradox, had still won against it and Existence itself in their first clash.","\"...\"","Noah frowned as he thought about all of it!","As Noah thought about many things, Anaximander in front of him smiled as this being began to rise up on unsteady legs that grew stronger with each passing moment.","\"I am an explorer,\" Anaximander said with that familiar tone of someone who had spent their entire existence chasing understanding. \"I am a scientist. I questioned and I wondered, but in my quest for knowledge, I brought a lot of things onto my plate as at this moment I have to try and set things straight. My power is returning ever so slowly and it is not to the point that I can do what I used to do before, but... will you help me, friend?\"","Noah looked up at this being as his eyes shone sharply with curiosity and calculation.","\" What exactly do you need help with?\"","Anaximander smiled and stretched his hands as if testing the limits of his recovering existence.","\" THE Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature, \" he said with weight behind every word. \"I have to get back into it, and I need help in this as I do not know how much time we have. My actions brought about the result of many things, and Existence does not need to suffer because of me. Countless lifeforms do not need to suffer because of me. Please, help me right this wrong.\"","BOOM!","THE Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature?","Noah’s eyes shone luminously at such words as he got up from his seated position.","The First Farmer had mentioned a while ago that he heard a voice telling him to find THE Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature as a method to surviving The Fallout. At the time, Noah had filed that information away as something to investigate when the opportunity arose.","Noah did not particularly need this given his own preparations and the fortress he was building with THE Infiniverse , but he was definitely interested in what secrets THE Creature’s personal Shore might hold.","So he looked toward the figure of Anaximander, this ridiculous oddity who defied the very laws of Existence through sheer declaration, and he said with a slight smile, \" Just show me The Way.\"","...!","---","Within THE Loom.","In a sea of vibrant paradox where contradictions bloomed like flowers in an impossible garden, a single entity was surrounded by paradoxical flames of Existence that burned without consuming and illuminated without revealing.","It was truly lonely at the top.","Very few could understand how those considered at the top felt because they had never climbed that high themselves. They had never made the sacrifices, the choices, and done everything that was required to reach such heights. They looked up at those who stood above them and saw only power and glory, never the cost that had been paid to acquire such things.","The struggles to get there were invisible to those who only saw the destination.","The sacrifices were forgotten by those who only celebrated the victories.","The choices, some of which haunted even the most powerful beings across eons, were unknown to those who had never been forced to make them.","Nobody understood what THE Living Paradox had to do to get where he was now, to even be capable of laying claim to The Oldest Paradox of Existence and stand as one of the few entities that could challenge the very foundations of reality itself.","But more often than not, beings like him who were at the top did not need others to understand because their drive and ambition was so unfathomably potent that they were a force to be reckoned with regardless of comprehension or sympathy.","Very few in Existence knew, but THE Living Paradox was actually born a peasant.","An entity of low class who held nothing and had nothing, who scraped by in the earliest moments of his existence without power or authority or even the promise of either. But look at him now, surrounded by flames that embodied the very concept of contradiction, standing at the precipice of an act that would reshape all of Observable Existence.","The flaming figure of Paradox smiled briefly as memories of that humble beginning flickered through his ancient consciousness.","\"I was born a peasant ,\" he said with a voice that held both pride and a strange sort of acceptance. \"I will die a peasant. But in between... in between all of this, there will be immensity. There will be glory.\"","HUUM!","As he said this, he raised his hand and pointed above where the metaphorical clock representing Midnight hung in the paradoxical sky of his domain.","The massive hand moved from one second toward zero.","The time to Midnight was zero.","This was because he had sensed another one of his precautions being set off. He didn’t know which one of the myriad of things that he was careful of had been triggered, but he innately knew that something had tripped one of his countless safeguards scattered across Observable Existence. And it simply tipped the scales ever closer toward Midnight until there was nowhere left to tip.","As of this moment, there was no time between now and The Fallout.","What remained was preparations and activation.","At this moment, THE Living Paradox actually raised his hand and saw his fingers trembling. His hand itself was actually trembling with minute vibrations that would have been invisible to anyone who wasn’t looking for them.","Was it out of anticipation or a sense of fear for what was to come?","His smile became brighter as his hand slowly stopped trembling, and it was a glorious sign of anticipation rather than dread. He was one of the few that knew how nothing would be the same after The Fallout transformed the landscape of Observable Existence.","The conditions that would allow for ascension to the higher Scales of Existence would bloom.","THE Creature and many others would be set free from their various prisons and suppressions.","A free-for-all would unfold, but at a scale The Infinite Unfurling had never imagined and could never have prepared for.","The cards were set and nothing could be changed at this moment as Midnight approached. With the clock to Midnight hitting zero, The Fallout would unfold anywhere within the next few minutes or hours.","THE Living Paradox moved away from the sea of Paradox and appeared elsewhere within THE Loom , and before him a massive object burning with incandescent multicolored flames of Existence spun in the void. It looked like a cube, but it radiated such heat and majesty that even a Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity might be burned by its mere proximity.","THE Living Paradox appeared before it and stroked it with a nostalgic expression, his flaming hand passing over its surface with something approaching tenderness.","\" Alright buddy, let’s do this, \" he said with a voice that held eons of preparation and anticipation. \" Us against Existence. Let us change the landscape of Observable Existence. Let us have a sense of fairness out there where the strong have ruled unchallenged for far too long.\"","His voice grew harder, more resolute.","\" Chaos? Existence? The First Tongue? Paradox? Fuck them. Fuck them all. Every aspect of The Oldest Paradox of Existence thinks they deserve to win, thinks they deserve to rule, thinks they deserve to define what reality is and what it should be.\"","...!","As he finished saying these words, his eyes burned with a sense of immensity and veiled rage that had been building since the moment he first realized that Existence was unfair and that he had been born with nothing while others had been born with everything.","And then he moved forward, his hand reaching toward the burning cube that would initiate The Fallout and change Observable Existence forever."]},{"number":4669,"title":"Chapter 4669: Chapter 4668: Sanity and Greatness!","paragraphs":["In the Early Veiled Shore of THE Infiniverse.","Alexander Asmodeus, The Peacemaker, stood while watching the emergence of Phonemes of The First Tongue far above him as they bloomed like celestial flowers across the blue-gold sky.","Osmont taught his people a language that nobody should be capable of grasping, and his people were shockingly grasping it.","Well, a very select few.","There was a Penguin that had begun getting hit by Osmont’s vibrant Goad after it seemed like the penguin was getting nowhere with its attempts at forming even the most basic Phoneme. The stick descended again and again with rhythmic precision, each strike accompanied by patient instruction that somehow made the violence seem educational.","But even that blue-gold stick in Osmont’s hands seemed to be hitting to infuse knowledge into the one being beaten as it seemed to be tough love of the most literal variety.","But either way...","|It’s a ridiculous thing is what it is. Is The First Tongue so easy to learn? Who the hell is this Osmont? And THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin being here... hey, I told you to talk to Origin before, why don’t you just step up? She and I have a debt...|","An incessant voice rang out in his head as it was an unfortunate byproduct of taking in the shattered part of THE Heart of Law into his existence. The voice of THE Living Law was now incessantly chirping whenever he chose to, which seemed to be constantly.","Alexander almost wanted to ask what he was supposed to be, he or she, as THE Living Existences and Law in particular seemed to take on whatever orientation suited them at any given moment.","| Hey, don’t talk shit about me. You know I can hear your thoughts now, right? I didn’t expect my heart fully joining you would make the Tool I refined eons ago react this way. And now... look, you’re doing better than even them.|","THE Living Law had their voice ring out in his mind as yes, something unexpected had happened when he declared his Way of Peace. The Enneagram had reacted heavily to the remnants of THE Living Law as it was transforming into something he didn’t recognize, something that pulsed with authority far beyond what it had held before.","But at this moment, new Gems began to appear on the Enneagram that represented every single Phoneme of The First Tongue that Osmont taught above. Every Phoneme was inscribed as Osmont taught it, being analyzed by the Enneagram in real time, and he would be able to seamlessly voice and write out all 18 Phonemes within the next few minutes without even having to go through the grueling process of learning them traditionally.","It was a ridiculous capability to imagine as The Enneagram essentially allowed him to copy and utilize what others spent eons trying to master.","| Yeah, you really need to get a jump on it. As much as I adore that girl Seraphina, I need you to remove the other part of the Enneagram from her and fuse it together fully. Oh, and you can now sense remnants of my Collapsed Civilization, right? With the reaction of the Phonemes of The First Tongue and that, you grasping THE will now be easy as this Osmont really gave you a jumpstart. But you will need to get going. If The Fallout starts before you grasp those things... they will be gone forever.|","...!","The incessant voice buzzed in his ears again as Alexander frowned at the implications of what THE Living Law was suggesting.","The remnants of THE Living Law’s Collapsed Civilization were scattered across Observable Existence, and if The Fallout consumed them before he could reach them, they would be lost forever along with whatever power and knowledge they contained. And the other part of The Enneagram that Seraphina carried needed to be reunited with his half to achieve its full potential.","He looked toward one of the nearby bodies of Osmont who was simultaneously teaching multiple groups of students with the efficiency of someone who had mastered the art of multitasking at an existential level. He thought about everything that was at stake and everything that could be gained if he moved now.","He looked at Seraphina and The Living Laws behind her, the manifestations of Law that had gathered in this Shore as refugees from a collapsing order, and he sighed as he called out to Osmont.","The Fallout neared, but he had to go out into danger rather than stay in this sanctuary that Osmont had built.","| Don’t worry, I am confident in your survival now. After all, I am in the end THE Living Law. Before Paradox collapsed me, I used to dine with Origin and THE Creature. I know the players in this game, and I know what it takes to survive them. With my guidance and your Way of Peace, we will carve out a place in whatever Existence looks like after The Fallout.|","...!","They used to dine with THE Creature and THE Living Origin , but why were they all doom and gloom days ago saying how it was such a shame, and if only Alexander had come across them earlier?","| Kid, I didn’t count on an anomaly giving you lessons on The First Tongue or helping you do the impossible by getting a Shattered Heart. All of that accelerated everything to impossible degrees. Now, all you need to do is finish the rest as with this, my Civilization will also undergo emergence much quicker. You win, I win. Mutual benefit.|","...!","THE Living Law remained incessant in his mind as Osmont arrived before him soon after.","The eyes of this terrifying anomaly alone were heavy to take, but Alexander took them on regardless as he began to talk!","Many people would take different paths across Existence as the apocalypse approached. Some would hide and hope to weather the storm. Some would fight and hope to overcome it. Some would flee and hope to outrun it.","At this moment, The Peacemaker was about to pioneer his own path, one that involved hunting down the remnants of a Collapsed Civilization while the very fabric of Observable Existence prepared to tear itself apart.","It was madness.","But then again, sanity had never been a prerequisite for greatness!"]},{"number":4670,"title":"Chapter 4670: Chapter 4669: The Shore of THE Creature I","paragraphs":["When the end of Existence was coming, what should one do?","Many across eons thought about this question endlessly, coming to conclusions that ranged from the profound to the absurd. Some argued that one should spend their final moments in contemplation, making peace with Existence and accepting the inevitable with grace and dignity.","Others suggested hedonism, indulging in every pleasure and desire before the void claimed everything. Still others advocated for connection, spending those precious remaining moments with loved ones and forging bonds that would transcend even annihilation.","There were those who chose denial, convincing themselves that the end was not truly coming and continuing their routines as if nothing had changed. There were those who chose despair, losing all hope and collapsing into nihilistic emptiness before the actual ending arrived.","And there were those who chose to end themselves before the end could claim them, preferring the illusion of control over the reality of helplessness.","All of these were valid responses to the incomprehensible weight of finality.","But Noah seemed to be taking an entirely different route.","He was going out sightseeing.","...!","At this moment, he stood outside The Wandering Territories beyond his Infiniverse as beside him were the figures of THE Living Order, THE First Hunger, and THE Living Origin who could not stop looking at Anaximander with expressions ranging from curiosity to barely concealed shock.","Noah had just brought them out here as they looked at the figure of Anaximander who almost seemed malnourished, his form still recovering from eons of fragmented existence and the strain of being reassembled after so long scattered across Observable Existence.","And yet this maddening entity smiled toward them as he simply said, \"Hello! Any friend of Osmont is a friend of mine. I am Anaximander.\"","...!","He introduced himself casually as if they were meeting at a social gathering rather than on the eve of an apocalypse that would reshape all of Observable Existence.","Sigrid and THE First Hunger had no immediate reaction beyond polite acknowledgment, but the eyes of Origin opened wide as if she had recognized that name and face from somewhere deep in her ancient memories.","She looked toward this being closely, evaluating him up and down as if trying to reconcile what she was seeing with what she remembered eons ago.","THE First Hunger looked at Anaximander with curiosity while asking, \" Are you like him?\"","Tor asked this question while pointing toward Noah, and Anaximander couldn’t help but laugh at the comparison.","\"Haha, no, my friend,\" he replied with genuine amusement dancing in his brilliant eyes. \"Nobody is like this guy. He is something else entirely.\"","...!","Noah looked at these interactions as he shook his head and said, \" Anaximander, these are three THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities who all have some connection to THE Creature. It would not be an issue to bring any of them, would it?\"","Anaximander smiled as he considered the question.","\"Not at all,\" he replied. \"Although it might need to take a little bit longer because...\"","As he spoke, he waved his hand, and without any fluctuation of energy or authority, a stick appeared in his grasp.","A stick that caused the faces of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin to pale as they recognized it right away.","This ancient-looking stick seemed to be made of a common tree, its surface worn smooth by countless hands over countless eons. And yet it emanated an air of terrifying might and majesty that belied its humble appearance.","It was none other than the stick of THE Creature. THE First Lesson. The stick that THE Creature used to discipline Early Creatures back in the Earliest Folds!","Before THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin could even ask where he had gotten the stick, Anaximander continued.","\"This is going to open up the gateway that will bypass tedious travels of who knows how much distance,\" he explained while twirling the legendary stick casually. \"And really, it isn’t even a matter of distance as much as... ah, it’s hard to explain. Distance didn’t matter to THE Creature . The main thing is that I have been telling this stick to open up the way to The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , but the power that I have recovered so far is only capable of allowing me to open it for you and I. I would have to wait a few more minutes in order to add a few more words to this Guideline to include these three others...\"","...!","Anaximander waved the stick around like it was nothing as Noah looked at it with shining eyes filled with curiosity and calculation.","Well, his stick was bigger as far as he could tell.","But this... hearing Anaximander talk about his Way made him curious as his eyes flickered with brilliance. A moment later, his eyes shone blue-gold as the Philology of Undifferentiated Mana bloomed around him in radiant patterns.","He floated closer to Anaximander and proceeded to touch his shoulder while sending out a glorious command internally.","’Utilize Way Manifestation to embody The Way of Anaximander.’","...!","He actually proceeded to claim such a ridiculous thing as in the next moment...","|Warning: The target of the Way you have chosen to copy is an extremely complex one.|","|Analysis: The Way of Anaximander operates on principles that defy conventional replication.|","|Due to missing the anomalous factor unique to the user, The Undefined Way of Anaximander can be utilized in a limited fashion.|","|Duration: 10 seconds.|","|Capability: You have free reign to define Existence as you wish.|","| Cost: Your immensity will pay the price for each declaration.|","...!","BOOM!","In the next moment, Noah’s eyes opened fully as he embodied The Way of Anaximander for the first time.","The sensation was unlike anything he had ever experienced before. There was a sense of freedom with it, a feeling that the rules of Existence were merely suggestions rather than laws. But it was also slightly unique and different from his own Way because where his Way worked with Mana and The First Tongue to shape reality, this Way simply... declared.","Around his body, the words of the terrifying Philology of Undifferentiated Mana buzzed with potent energy. Their presence caused THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin to look over once more, their eyes gradually opening as they began to recognize this Philology to be the one that Ul’Moreth had held in Ginnungagap all those eons ago!"]},{"number":4671,"title":"Chapter 4671: Chapter 4670: The Shore of THE Creature II","paragraphs":["As they looked toward Noah with mounting realization, he ignored everything while he said to Anaximander, \" May I?\"","He said such words while pointing to the stick of THE Creature , and Anaximander blinked in surprise before he nodded and gave the stick to Noah while saying, \"Be careful, it is a little heavy.\"","HUUM!","The exchange of THE First Lesson of THE Creature from one hand to another occurred as Noah felt a unique sense of immensity wrapping around his hands the moment his fingers closed around the ancient wood.","|You have grasped onto a Relic of History.|","| THE First Lesson has been held by your hands.|","|This artifact predates most of current Existence and has been used to shape the foundations of many civilizations.|","When Noah’s eyes flashed as he used Lens of Civilization on it...","| THE First Lesson|","|Classification: ???|","|Origin: ???|","|Creator: THE Creature|","|Power Level: ???|","|Description: The stick used by THE Creature to teach and discipline the earliest beings of Observable Existence. It has struck more THE entities than any other object in history. Its true capabilities remain unknown, as THE Creature never revealed the full extent of what THE First Lesson could accomplish.|","|Current Status: Dormant, awaiting its true wielder.|","...!","Noah grasped it with sharp eyes as in the next moment he spoke out calmly, \" This small stick will open up the way to The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature for those of us floating here.\"","HUUM!","The sensation was ridiculously unique as he spoke while utilizing The Way of Anaximander. Every single word that he uttered felt extremely heavy, as if the immensity that he felt when he strung together Logos to form Philologies was what he was doing right now, but through pure declaration rather than linguistic construction.","But a moment later, the stick in his hand began to shine with multicolored brilliance as terrifyingly heavy and dense flames erupted from it. These flames proceeded to form into a multicolored doorway before them, its edges burning with authority!","The sense of heaviness that Noah felt was immense as all around him, many turned their eyes toward him with incredulity and shock. Only Sigrid remained calm, looking at the scene as if she was only watching something normal that her man was doing, her faith in him so absolute that even this seemed unremarkable.","Anaximander seemed purely amazed while THE Living Origin was actually somber while looking at him.","\" Are you...truly sure that you are not THE Creature? \" she asked with a voice that held genuine uncertainty.","Such words took Noah out of his stupor as he looked toward THE Living Origin and said firmly, \" Let’s stop it with that. I am not THE Creature. I simply used The Way of Anaximander.\"","He simply used The Way of Anaximander.","Simply.","As if it truly was simple.","After he said this, he returned the stick of THE Creature back to Anaximander as he felt the sense of heaviness in his existence after utilizing this unique Way.","He looked at the gateway that would lead to The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , and before he entered, he uttered out with absolute certainty...","\" My weight and immensity actually exceeds THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.\"","BOOM!","The moment that he uttered such words while utilizing The Way of Anaximander, he felt an immense sense of heaviness and weight as if he was lifting something so supremely heavy with a muscle he never knew he had.","The strain was unlike anything he had experienced before, as if reality itself was pushing back against his declaration while simultaneously being forced to accept it.","|Declaration Registered.|","|Cost Assessment: Extreme.|","|50% of all Infinite Potential that had been steadily flowing into your Foundation and Way has been instantly amplified and utilized.|","|Result: The immensity and weight of your Foundation has reached 10% the weight of a normal THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity.|","| Comparative Analysis: This is equivalent to 1% of the approximate weight of beings like THE Primordial Chaos, THE Living Paradox, or THE Creature when they were at THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty(Very, very rough estimate. In fact, may not even be accurate)|","|Your existence has been permanently elevated.|","...!","The terrifying sensation of power that Noah felt was staggering as he sensed his Foundation settling into its new weight with authority that hadn’t been there moments before.","But then...","|Warning: The utilization of a Way without the proper anomalous factor has caused immense strain within your existence.|","|The manifestation of The Way of Anaximander has prematurely ended.|","|Cooldown before next manifestation: Unknown.|","...!","The unique sensation of a muscle that he could not sense or explain being unfathomably tired faded away as he lost access to The Way of Anaximander. But he got a glimpse of just how this terrifying being operated, and this was enough for him to think about many possible things in the future regarding how such a Way could be studied, understood, and perhaps even partially replicated through his own methods.","His brazen words were heard by the others in the surroundings as Anaximander was looking at him with shining eyes filled with scientific curiosity.","Tor squinted while looking toward him before he shook his head and came up to wrap his right hand around Noah’s shoulder.","\" Outsider, or The Scale Breaker as you were known in Ginnungagap,\" Tor said with a tone that mixed admiration with gentle correction. \"It is good to dream, but you cannot dream out loud for everyone to hear. Even THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty takes some time to clear and go through. You cannot just say it out loud and expect to cross it and skip it entirely to go to THE Fundamental Depth. Come on, you have impressed us enough already. Let us go see The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature.\"","Tor said this as if he were consoling him, but Noah merely shook his head as THE First Hunger did not realize that such a thing could actually be possible with the right circumstances and the right Way.","While motioning toward Anaximander to lead, the group made their way into the blazing multicolored flaming gateway, and they disappeared from the Wandering Territories.","All of them could instinctively feel that something was coming, and this whole interaction, all their words and exchanges, everything that they did here had taken the span of less than a single second . After all, they were beings that could move faster than Planck Speed itself, and in even a nanosecond, many things could be accomplished.","The gateway closed behind them as they journeyed toward The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , leaving the Wandering Territories empty and silent in the moments before The Fallout would change everything."]},{"number":4672,"title":"Chapter 4672: Chapter 4671: The Shore of THE Creature III","paragraphs":["Existence was a mystery, but it was not necessarily a mystery that needed to be solved as much as it needed to be experienced.","Noah was experiencing it at this moment as he came across the glorious Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , a place that defied his expectations in ways he hadn’t anticipated.","Days ago such a place would not even have been a possibility for him to think of, but the Weavings of Existence changed very rapidly as he now found himself staring at an endlessly vast Shore that stretched beyond even his enhanced perception.","It was a weird thing to see as it felt like someone who thought they were rich entering the home of someone that was truly rich.","Because The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature was a ridiculous one as the surroundings alone permeated with liquid and plasmic concentrations of Civilizational Authority that made even his own Infiniverse seem modest in comparison.","The golden sands they stood on were filled with thousands of Logos of The First Tongue just in the immediate proximity where they currently stood, each one a perfect expression of meaning that would take others eons to forge.","There were massive tall trees in the distance all around them that spanned upward infinitely, their canopies disappearing into heights that seemed to have no ceiling. Even these trees were swirling with hundreds of Logos of The First Tongue woven into their very bark and leaves, as the entire place emanated an air of immensity and sacredness that pressed down on visitors like a gentle but undeniable weight.","And just by taking a glance at the immediate surroundings, Noah was able to affirm that yeah, this place would be surviving The Fallout without question.","|Welcome to the Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature.|","|In this place, the concentration of Logos and Philology of The First Tongue is so dense that the study of The First Tongue progresses 1,000 times faster than anywhere else in Observable Existence.|","|Warning: Be careful of what you touch, as you could trigger dangerous mechanisms left behind by THE Creature. |","...!","The entire place seemed wondrous as when they arrived, Sigrid stayed close to Noah while THE Living Origin seemed dazed for a moment, as if she had returned to someplace she never thought she would see again. Her golden eyes were distant, filled with memories that stretched back to eras when this Shore had been alive with activity and purpose.","Moments later, she began to take steps toward a certain direction and rapidly disappeared in that direction without a word of explanation.","Tor shook his head and said calmly, \" I’ll keep an eye on her... \" as he also disappeared after THE Living Origin , leaving Noah, Sigrid, and Anaximander standing on the golden sands.","In front of Noah, the figure of Anaximander took the stick of THE Creature as he began to draw a circle around them that shone brightly a moment later. Their figures were displaced vast distances across this Early Veiled Shore in an instant, traveling farther than light could travel in years.","They appeared in a region that held a golden cliff with a waterfall of golden sands filled with Logos flowing down toward a lower golden continent that stretched endlessly below. The sight was breathtaking in its impossible beauty, as even the falling sand seemed to sing with The First Tongue.","At the edge of the cliff, one could see a raised elevated stone-like platform that Anaximander began walking toward while carrying the stick with purposeful strides.","\"The masses of Existence do not deserve to be unraveled and faced with immense anguish,\" Anaximander said with conviction as he approached the platform. \" THE Creature left a few things in place, and at this moment I will use the remaining power of his Early Veiled Shore to draw in any forms of life across Observable Existence into this place. All Wheels of Existence, all Folds, every single form of life shall be contained in the Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature as at the time of The Fallout, this place shall serve as refuge.\"","He paused and looked back at Noah with those brilliant, curious eyes.","\"The idea of distance and vastness does not truly apply to it as even with all of Observable Existence compressed into it, at most it would cover half of this space. And this is the main Shore of THE Creature , as I believe there are other parts of it that were shattered in his battle which are scattered across Observable Existence. It’s actually a very interesting place that THE Creature managed to cultivate. Most of his time was spent here from what he told me.\"","...!","The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature was utterly insane to grasp as Noah wondered what he would be able to find here during his exploration.","He watched as Anaximander went toward the elevated golden stone-like platform and raised the stick of THE Creature in his hands. Shockingly, he plugged it into the platform as if it were a key fitting into a lock that had been waiting eons for this moment.","A moment later, the entire region they were in began to vibrate as auroras of colors began to shine brilliantly above them in patterns that seemed to tell stories in a language older than The First Tongue itself.","Noah looked up and saw a terrifying formation of Logos begin to flow across the golden sands of this place, and even more began to float across the skies as they looked like rivers of brilliance streaming in all directions.","The Logos he could see were related to movement and displacement. Logos of Gathering that pulled things toward a central point. Logos of Compression that made vast spaces fit into smaller ones. Logos of Protection that wrapped around everything being drawn in. Logos of Preservation that ensured nothing would be damaged in transit. All of them working in harmony to accomplish what Anaximander was doing in order to displace countless life forms across Existence into this place.","As such waves of brilliance began to radiate all around, in the far distance at least a gigaparsec away, Noah began to see thousands of Transcendent Wheels of Existence begin to manifest in the skies as if they were plucked out of wherever they were and brought here. In other directions, entire Folds began to manifest as the skies or the ground opened up and began extending in all directions to accommodate the incoming refugees.","|Process Initiated: Existential Evacuation Protocol.|","| THE Creature’s contingency plan for catastrophic events has been activated.|","|All life forms across Observable Existence are being drawn into the Early Veiled Shore.|","|Estimated coverage: 100% of Observable Existence.|","|Estimated time to completion: Approximately 60 seconds.|","|This process will drain significant reserves of the Shore’s accumulated authority.|","...!","As the process began, the figure of Anaximander continued to hold on to the stick as if it was a key that was directing everything. He looked toward Noah and Sigrid with a smile that held both exhaustion and satisfaction.","\"This might take a little bit... well, maybe a minute or so to cover all of Observable Existence since I am going in a bit of a hurry due to not knowing when The Fallout will descend,\" he said. \"But you guys can take the time to look around the home of THE Creature. I was amazed the first time that I got here and studied everything that I saw.\"","Noah nodded at these words.","\" We’ll stay close by,\" he replied. \" Let us know if you need anything.\"","After such words, Noah looked out to the vibrant expanse of The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature, and he began to float up as one of the first things he saw was a vast and endlessly stretching wooden wall that seemed to be breaking down and decaying in places.","His eyes focused on it with sharp curiosity.","|Structure Identified: The Veil of Existence.|","|Classification: Primordial Barrier.|","|Function: Separates The Lands of The Living and The Lands of The Dead.|","|History: THE Creature established this barrier with the help of Anaximander in an era before THE Loom was conceived.|","|Current Status: Worn down and breaking apart due to eons of attacks, strain, and the absence of THE Creature’s maintenance.|","...!","Noah looked at this radiant wall that was breaking apart as he shook his head at the implications of what its deterioration meant.","At this time, Sigrid beside him sighed as she also observed the crumbling barrier.","\" Even someone as powerful as this, who had a place like this, was not able to come out on top and win over conflicts eons ago,\" she said with a voice that held both wonder and melancholy. \" And the biggest conflict for us, which we did not know whether we could survive or not, already had a solution right here. We were fighting with everything that we had to be able to survive The Fallout, when there was an answer that we could not access waiting in this place all along.\"","...!","Noah listened to her calmly as they moved rapidly across the Shore, and he took her hand into his as he considered her words carefully before responding.","\" Sometimes a problem seems impossible, but there’s always an answer out there, \" he said with certainty. \" Sometimes one just does not know how to access it. The solutions to surviving The Fallout could be countless, but one simply has to find the right answer among all of them. We found our own answer without needing to rely on another, and that matters more than you might think.\"","He paused as they continued moving through the golden landscape.","\" Because relying on others can sometimes backfire, \" he continued. \" If we simply sat back and held the hopes that THE Creature would save all of Observable Existence, we could all have perished. Who would have saved Anaximander if we hadn’t found him? No, relying on others is never ideal in Existence as the best possible solution is to rely on oneself. Rely on yourself and every success and failure will be your responsibility.\"","At such words, Sigrid smiled and hugged his hand closer to her as she looked up at him with eyes that held absolute devotion.","\"I want to rely on you, \" she said softly. \" Even if it is inadvisable to rely on others. Can I continue to put my life in your hands? If you succeed, I’ll be there with you. If you fail, I will shoulder that failure with you.\"","At such words, Noah turned to her and stroked her head gently with his free hand.","\" Yeah, continue relying on me ,\" he said with a confident smile. \" I am pretty reliable so far.\"","After such words, Sigrid smiled brilliantly as their figures continued moving across The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , with Noah intent on exploring to see if he could find anything useful for the current him in this place.","They were doing all of this in the span of femtoseconds and nanoseconds as all around them in the vastness of the Shore that was gigaparsecs in size, Wheels of Existence and Folds began to bloom and appear. Entire regions of the Wandering Territories were being brought over into The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature as the allure of Collapsed Civilizations also began to flow into this place.","When it did come to Collapsed Civilizations, history was not entirely clear on how the events had unfolded with all of THE Living Existences. The fates of THE Living Dimensional, THE Living Quantum, THE Living Concept, THE Living Spirit, or Temporal were unique and shrouded in mystery. Some were within THE Loom, some may have been collapsed entirely, and some may have found other fates that no one had recorded.","When the dust settled after The Fallout, everything would be clear."]},{"number":4673,"title":"Chapter 4673: Chapter 4672: We All Fall Down I","paragraphs":["Inside another portion of The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature that was disconnected from the main one, a Shore that was accessible from the Lands of the Dead.","The Weavings of Existence of The Great Usurper permeated across the vast landscape of the Shore as he sought to control and influence it completely, making up his mind to grasp that object he apparently could not even look at, that Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox.","His influence over this Shore was going a bit slower compared to his rapid expansion across The Lands of the Dead, mainly due to the terrifying complexities of a type of language that permeated across this place. Words of glorious power were strung together uniquely, and it was taking some time to expand his idle existence over them and make them fall under his control as well.","But in time, all of it would be possible.","As he was doing all of this, he felt his existence lighting up as he received an open line of communication between him and a monstrous being... Osmont.","Osmont sent a message first, and the content of the message was basically telling him how The Fallout may soon be making its descent, and that he could take him in to shield him from the coming apocalypse.","The consciousness of The Great Usurper smiled at these words as he thought about it for less than a nanosecond before he shook his metaphorical head. He sent back a message calmly.","\"My existence is an idle one. I’m already pretty sure I can protect myself, but even if I wasn’t able to, I have already had my existence cover a significant portion of The Lands of the Dead. Unless everything is absolutely destroyed, I will still be living across the Weavings of the Observable Existence that I have covered. And once The Fallout descends and does whatever crazy things it will do, I might have even grander opportunities as my Weavings may cover a significant portion of the landscape after The Fallout. That in itself would actually be a tremendous gain, and I am excited for it. Though I have begun to sense The Dead Existences suddenly disappearing en masse across The Lands of the Dead, that wouldn’t be your doing, would it?\"","...!","He asked this question calmly while he continued to control the Disciples of THE Creature to delve further inward into this Shore, but the reply from Osmont was a unique one.","\" Well, I’m not doing it personally, but I am witnessing it. But okay. Be safe out there, it is the end of Existence as we know it. What comes after this end... is something none of us truly know.\"","...!","The Great Usurper smiled at this and nodded as he replied.","\"I’ll see you on the other side, big guy.\"","The Fallout was coming, and Existence prepared. The masses prepared. Every single entity inherently knew that after this, nothing would be the same.","---","In the main Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature.","Noah and Sigrid stopped before a vibrant plot of land that held Sacred Herbs that were actually conducive to aiding in the learning of The First Tongue.","|Sacred Herb Identified: Lexicon’s Bloom|","|Classification: Genesis-Grade Cultivation Resource|","|Description: A sacred herb that only grows in regions saturated with The First Tongue. Its petals are composed of crystallized Phonemes, and its roots draw nutrients from the Logos embedded in the soil. When consumed or refined, it temporarily enhances the consumer’s ability to perceive and understand the underlying structure of The First Tongue.|","|Effects: +500% comprehension speed for Phonemes and Logos for 24 hours after consumption. Permanent minor enhancement to First Tongue sensitivity with repeated use.|","|Cultivation Requirements: Requires soil saturated with at least 100 Logos per cubic meter. Must be watered with liquid THE Civilizational Authority. Takes approximately 1,000 years to mature under normal conditions. A few seconds if you really put your back into it.|","Noah looked at these details calmly as this was the nineteenth Sacred Herb that he had plucked from The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , herbs he planned to plant in his own Shore.","The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature held many boons that he was slowly taking as at this moment, beside him, Sigrid frowned.","As he turned to look at her, she spoke with a voice that held concern.","\"I can sense Existence beginning to vibrate,\" she said slowly, as if trying to articulate something she had never felt before. \" As if it instinctively knows something is coming. Order is getting restricted, suffocated. As if something that will utterly eradicate Weavings of Order is about to descend. The sensation is quite stifling.\"","...!","As THE Living Order, Sigrid could now feel many things that others could not perceive.","Noah got up and moved to console her, wrapping his arms around her as she silently looked up at him.","\" Do you have any fear of what is coming? \" she asked quietly. \" Any fear of the unknown? I know you gave away your Everything of Fear, but even THE Creature regenerated his Everythings, right?\"","...!","Sigrid asked such a question as Noah hugged her tighter while he smiled with absolute confidence.","\" No ,\" he said firmly. \" No fear. Whatever comes, I will meet it with anticipation. And the ones who sought to destroy me and everything that I love, I will wait for them with anticipation. For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction. A lot of people have made many, many actions. If the time comes for me to collect, the time comes for a reaction. And it will be heavy and glorious.\"","BOOM!","As Noah said this, he felt his existence buzzing as in front of his eyes...","|Breakthrough Achieved.|","|The Principles of Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect have been clearly understood.|","|Their Philologies have been established as they now arrive at the stage of Genesis Principles.|","| The Philologies of Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect burn brightly within your existence.|","|Harvest of unfathomable proportions blooms as their first course of action.|","|All Infinite Potential harvested from the usage of Mana has been amplified exponentially.|","|The percentage of harvest for all usage of The First Tongue from the past to the present has increased from 1% to 5%.|","...!","BOOM!","The seas of blue-gold harvest of utterly unfathomable and glorious Infinite Potential that Noah had been continuing to flood within him increased exponentially as they began to flood into his Foundation and Way with even greater concentrations than before.","|Weight and Immensity Update.|","|Your Foundation has absorbed tremendous amounts of Infinite Potential.|","| Current Status: Your weight and immensity is now 3/100th of the weight and immensity of entities like THE Creature when they were at THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty (approximately).|","|You continue to grow at an unprecedented rate.|","He smiled as he sensed all of it alongside the waves of information he was receiving about The Genesis Principles of Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect.","Yes, the end of Existence may be coming, but he was more than ready for it.","At this time, more prompts bloomed.","|THE Protagonist Stanchion of Infinity shines brilliantly.|","|The Philology of The Cheating Architect prepares for The Fallout.|","|A glorious symphony shall witness The Fallout.|","Oh?","Noah’s eyes flashed at this as he sensed a slow and glorious symphony beginning to bloom in the background.","The melody started with a single piano, its notes falling like raindrops on still water, each one carrying the weight of eons of history and the lightness of fleeting hope. Then strings joined in, violins weaving a glimmer of sorrow and determination that seemed to acknowledge the end while refusing to surrender to it.","A trumpet called out, lonely and proud, like the last soldier standing on a battlefield that had claimed everyone else. Drums rolled in softly, not the drums of war but the drums of ceremony, of ritual, of something sacred coming to its conclusion.","The symphony was somber and hopeful and grand all at once, a contradiction made musical, a paradox given voice.","It began to permeate across The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature .","The symphony passed over the figure of Anaximander holding The Goad of THE Creature as he looked at the endless Weavings of Existence being drawn into the Shore, his expression one of peaceful acceptance.","The glorious symphony passed over THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger, who shockingly stood before The Abode of THE Creature with complex emotions passing over the eyes of THE Living Origin as if she remembered things she had tried to forget.","The symphony permeated across the vast Shore as the members of The Collapsed Civilization of Origin from the Wandering Territories who had just arrived in The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature also heard it as they looked around in astonishment.","Duke Whisker and Goliath among other Living Origins looked out, their existences feeling a sense of oppression as all of them were actually forced to remain on the golden sands of the Shore, no one able to fly upward or even move rapidly across this place.","Not too far from them, Living Collapses could also be seen.","Far across, The Transcendent Folds of The Living Existences that THE Infiniverse had not swallowed, all remaining Dukes of Kleos Councils and all that remained of The Living Existences found themselves pulled into The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature . And all those here, and those newly arriving, undoubtedly heard the glorious symphony that they did not know the origin of.","It caused every single entity to look around with sombreness and immensity.","Back in that distant region, Noah felt his Weavings of the Protagonist pulse as this concept of his seemed to be going all out to match the occasion. In addition to the symphony, a melodious feminine voice began to permeate across Existence as if it were a countdown for what was to come.","Because yes, he had seen the clock representing Midnight move to zero in that region of collapse where one of his bodies stood surrounded by the cages of Schrodinger and The Disciple of THE Creature.","The time to Midnight was Zero.","And yet toward the coming apocalypse, toward the coming Fallout, Noah’s body in that region of collapse held a golden glass in hand as he drank the Sacred Mead of Existence and waited for it to come.","And so even here, that melodious symphony began to resound alongside the blooming melodious voice.","Noah turned off some of the Logos of Imprisonment around the cage of Schrodinger, allowing this beggar to see and hear him as he knew that his eyes were also sharing the eyes of another.","The gaze of THE Living Paradox could likely perceive through him if he wished.","The haggard visage of Schrodinger within his beggar-like robes looked dazed initially, his form diminished and worn from captivity. But as he saw Noah, these eyes flickered with a light and soon turned immensely cold and calm as they looked at him with interest.","They were the eyes of THE Living Paradox. The gaze of THE Living Paradox.","Noah took a sip of his drink near the blue-gold prison as he said calmly while raising his hand above.","\" Can you hear it? Listen closely.\"","...!","He talked about the symphony and melodious voice echoing out. Toward the end of the world, toward the end of Existence, Noah sat beside Schrodinger whose gaze was commandeered by THE Living Paradox as a glorious melody began to stretch out across Existence.","The feminine voice began to sing, her tone cheerful and sweet, yet underlaid with a melancholy that made every word ache with beautiful desolation.","\" Oh, Existence keeps spinning round and round,","And we all fall down, we all fall down.","Built our castles high upon the ground,","Now they’re tumbling down, tumbling down.\"","The piano continued its gentle descent as the strings swelled with bittersweet harmony.","\" They said forever was a promise kept,","But forever’s just a word we wept.","The oldest question has no answer yet,","And the ones who ask are the ones who forget.\"","The trumpet called out again, proud and lonely, as drums marked a rhythm like a heartbeat slowing.","\" There was a creature made of light and pain,","Who gave away his heart to ease the strain.","And paradox came dancing in the rain,","Saying ’Nothing gold can ever remain.’\"","The melody shifted, becoming almost waltz-like in its gentle sway.","\" So pour yourself a drink and raise it high,","To the ones who lived and the ones who’ll die.","The stars are falling from the painted sky,","But darling, we don’t have to wonder why.\"","The strings crescendoed with aching beauty.","\" Because existence is a fleeting song,","And we’ve been singing it all along.","Right or wrong, weak or strong,","We all belong, we all belong.\"","The feminine voice softened to barely above a whisper as the instruments faded one by one.","\"When the dust has settled on the stage,","And they turn the final page,","Will they remember this age?","Or will it all just fade away?\"","A moment of silence.","Then the piano played its final notes, each one falling like tears onto still water.","\" Oh, Existence stopped spinning round and round,","And we all fell down, we all fell down.","But somewhere in the ashes on the ground,","A single seed was found, a seed was found.\"","The last note hung in the air, neither hopeful nor despairing, simply acknowledging what was and what would be.","Oh!","It was unfathomably glorious!","The symphony and song began to permeate across empty Folds and Wandering Territories, across THE Infiniverse where countless beings paused to listen, across The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature where refugees from all of Observable Existence heard it and felt something stir in their souls.","It was the symphony to the end of everything they knew.","And the beginning of everything they didn’t."]},{"number":4674,"title":"Chapter 4674: Chapter 4673: We All Fall Down II","paragraphs":["\"Oh, Existence stopped spinning round and round,","And we all fell down, we all fell down.","But somewhere in the ashes on the ground,","A single seed was found, a seed was found.\"","The symphony continued its slow advance across Existence as many listened, its melancholic beauty touching every corner of Observable Existence that still remained.","One body of Noah remained drinking in the region of collapse near the prison containing Schrodinger.","He knew the gaze of THE Living Paradox was in there, and the only reason he was standing anywhere this close was because Existence, or really THE Creature , still suppressed THE Living Paradox and other opposing THEs from expressing their power. At least for now.","After The Fallout, the rules of Existence would greatly change.","So this time may be the only time to get a chance of a discussion with THE Living Paradox before this being began hunting him after The Fallout, if he even remained on his radar.","At this time, Noah sent a drink toward the body of Schrodinger in the cage. Shockingly, Schrodinger calmly accepted it in his seated position and began to drink as if this were the most natural thing in the world.","His eyes remained filled with a light of immensity and calmness, and in there, only the light of Paradox remained.","At this time, in The First Tongue, THE Living Paradox spoke as he listened to the symphony playing out in the surroundings.","| There was a creature made of light and pain, who gave away his heart to ease the strain. And paradox came dancing in the rain, saying ’Nothing gold can ever remain.’ Your symphony says Paradox came, but what if I had always been there? Even before THE Creature.|","WAA!","The words of Paradox were heavy to hear as Noah drank from his cup silently, and Paradox continued.","Sometimes, he found that some truly powerful entities liked to ramble. They would give you more information while rambling than if you had asked directly. So let this man ramble as much as he wants.","| When trying to avoid something, entities more often than not cause that thing to come even faster,| THE Living Paradox continued with a voice that held the weight of eons. | The Fallout was years away and would have remained that way. But something began moving around, presumably trying to avoid it. And yet their actions brought it even faster than ever. Faster than supposed to be. In trying to survive The Fallout, you and whatever other factors popped up accelerated it tremendously to the extent it is now here. THE Primordial Chaos whispered in my ear not too long ago, talking about anomalies and competitors for The Oldest Paradox of Existence. Beings laying claim to The First Tongue. Beings appearing across time itself. All of these factors, all of these movements, all of these struggles to survive what was coming actually made it come faster. It’s crazy stuff, really.|","...!","Toward such words, Noah took his drink and scoffed. He paid particular attention to the mention of THE Primordial Chaos! That fucker was truly here?","\" You are the one actively moving it closer and even instigating it, but the blame lies on others and me? \" he said with a voice that held no fear. \" Come on, big guy. You have been planning and doing this for eons now. You built THE Loom. You imprisoned THE Creature. You set up the conditions for The Fallout to even be possible. And now you want to pin the acceleration on those of us who are simply trying to not die from your machinations?\"","At such words, the figure of Schrodinger that THE Living Paradox was seeing through smiled as he looked at Noah up and down with renewed interest.","| You are actually a very interesting anomaly to observe,| Paradox said with something approaching appreciation. | You may have made a claim on The First Tongue, but you are young. You appear across history, but you remain young. And I say young in terms of experience. I say young in terms of what you have truly experienced. Because even I, when I was like you, nearly perished dozens of times. Countless close calls where that would have been it for little old me. For the peasant that dared to dream. So while I am a little interested in exactly what you might be able to accomplish, I am not sure whether you will survive even a few days in the Weavings of Existence of The Fallout.|","BOOM!","The words were extremely terrifying ones as Noah took them in calmly and sipped on his drink once more before he turned his gaze over to THE Living Paradox.","\"By the way,\" Noah said with a smile that held no deference, \" while you and THE Creature are having your showdown, do you want to be so kind as to give me a glimpse of what I can expect of The Fallout? You all are the big guys that are going to be fighting for Existence while the rest of us are just the little fish swimming in a large pond. Can you spare a few words to enlighten me on exactly what is coming?\"","...!","The scene itself continued to increase in how incredulous it was, because what entity would dare be talking to THE Living Paradox like this so casually, even if they thought there were contingencies in place?","Exactly who would be so bold?","And yet Noah did it as THE Living Paradox looked him over up and down before he smiled again with that terrifying expression that held appreciation for audacity.","| There will not be a pond for any fish to be swimming, | Paradox replied with cold certainty. |It will be constantly burning and boiling Existence with extremes of everything in place as The Fallout will be the environment to allow for progression toward the Scale that none of us have grasped yet. Well, not fully anyways for some of us. Whatever you think you know of Existence at this moment in time will absolutely not be the Existence that you come across in The Fallout. Even I hold a slight sense of apprehension in exactly what will happen in all of this as I can tell you now... I actually cannot guarantee my own survival. So what exactly does that say about you?|","BOOM!","...!"]},{"number":4675,"title":"Chapter 4675: Chapter 4674: We All Fall Down III","paragraphs":["The words uttered at this moment finally caused Noah to become somber and serious.","The eyes of Schrodinger which contained the gaze of THE Living Paradox pulsed with the terrifying sense of Paradox as he looked up at the surrounding collapse, flames of contradictory authority flickering around his borrowed form.","| What many don’t understand is that countless small, seemingly insignificant things had to happen for us to arrive here,| Paradox continued, his voice growing grander with each word. | Countless things. I heard of your arrival in Ginnungagap. The things that happened there actually had an effect and contributed to what is happening right now. The things that happened in the Earliest Folds, whether you have already been there and done whatever you have done, also contributed to what is happening here. No good deed goes unpunished. No bad deed goes unpunished. Everything that everyone did is the reason why we are all here.|","He paused, letting the weight of his words settle.","| And Existence is far too vast and far too immense, even for me to claim that I know everything. So yes, even I have no confidence that I will come out on top in the Weavings of what is to come. Amidst all of this, it might actually be THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos or someone else. Hah, I could even think wildly enough and say it could be somebody like you or someone entirely unknown to us. Who knows? Existence is unpredictable like that.|","His voice grew harder, more resolute.","| But in all this uncertainty, I take it a step at a time. I put one foot forward, and then I put the next. And it is why even with all of this uncertainty, I still believe in my Way so much that for me, there can only be victory or there can be death. No in between. As the symphony you have uttered continues to repeat... Existence is a fleeting song, and we’ve been singing it all along. Oh, I’ve been singing.|","HUUM!","At this point of his dialogue, a terrifying aura erupted around Schrodinger as Existence began to buzz all around. It felt like the massive weight of THE Living Paradox himself was descending through this borrowed vessel, pressing down on reality with authority that shouldn’t have been possible through such a limited conduit.","The cold and calm eyes of THE Living Paradox continued to stare straight at Noah as his words continued.","|I have been singing , Osmont. And my song shall spread gloriously across Existence as all of this unpredictability, I will do everything in my power to make it predictable. You ask me what The Fallout will be like? Whatever you are imagining right now, imagine ten times worse, and then on top of that, imagine another octave higher. Existence is a fleeting song, and truly... we all fall down. We all... fall down.|","HUUM!","The surroundings of the cage turned terrifyingly tumultuous as flames of Existence descended all around, burning with colors that contradicted themselves and heat that was simultaneously freezing. But the body of Schrodinger continued to keep its eyes on Noah as he floated further and further away with a somber gaze.","The brilliant blue-gold stick appeared in Noah’s hands as multiple Logos and Philologies wrapped around him to cause his body to emanate a sense of glorious brilliance that pushed back against the descending weight of Paradox.","THE Living Paradox stared at him as a terrifyingly devilish smile appeared on his borrowed face.","| We all fall down, Osmont, so be ready. And good luck. It was actually pleasant to welcome the end of Existence with you.|","At this moment, Schrodinger tipped the cup that Noah gave him as if he was giving a toast.","| May we meet again in a playing field where there will be no suppression of Existence. Stay alive if you can. Struggle. Fight. Prosper. At that time, whatever power you have and whatever power I have will decide who leaves that meeting alive. If I were to come across you... ah, who knows what I would do. But until then... Au revoir!|","...!","With such words, the immensity that the body of Schrodinger released reached unfathomable levels. Existence pressed down even more as contradictions began manifesting physically around the cage, reality folding in on itself in ways that hurt to perceive!","And then in the next moment...","BOOM!","The body of Schrodinger exploded.","Not just exploded, but was collapsed purposefully, as if THE Living Paradox did not wish to leave any sign of him here. The explosion was controlled and absolute, every atom, every Weaving, every trace of Schrodinger’s existence being unmade with surgical precision.","It was a message.","I can do this whenever I want. To anyone I want. Remember that.","...!","Noah observed all of this while holding his Goad, his expression somber but unshaken.","His prison looked deformed and almost broken from the force of the explosion, its once pristine blue-gold bars now warped and bent. On those bars, the meat that used to be Schrodinger melted and sizzled, dripping down in grotesque rivulets that dissolved before they hit the ground.","The cage that had held one of THE Living Paradox’s most useful pawns was now empty.","A beggar had died, and existence mourned.","The symphony continued to play in the background, its melancholic notes seeming even more appropriate now.","\"Existence is a fleeting song, and we’ve been singing it all along...\"","Noah looked at the ruined cage for a long moment before he turned away.","THE Living Paradox had given him more information than he probably intended.","Even that ancient being wasn’t certain of survival.","Even that ancient being acknowledged that the outcome was unpredictable.","And that meant there was room. Room for someone else to claim victory. Room for THE Anomaly to write his own ending.","Noah smiled grimly as he gripped his Goad tighter.","Let whatever wss coming come.","He was ready to fall down with everyone else.","And then get the fuck back up when the dust settled!"]},{"number":4676,"title":"Chapter 4676: Chapter 4675: Sandbox","paragraphs":["In the core region of THE Infiniverse.","Ruination and THE Infiniverse stood side by side. Out of all constructs across Existence, they were undoubtedly the most efficient and glorious ones.","Two sisters filled with sheer drive and determination to utterly decimate everything standing against their Master. And at this moment...","\" Everything is ready?\"","THE Infiniverse affirmed with Ruination as the two had divided their tasks for even greater efficiency.","Ruination nodded as her illusory blue-gold form shimmered with data streams that cascaded through her existence.","\" The Weavings of Hunger have melded seamlessly with THE Faraday Cage,\" she reported with precise efficiency. \" Both Hunger and Mana working hand in hand. Frankly, Hunger has taken a backseat compared to Mana, but in the end, due to it being a Dual Civilization under The Master, it was still elevated tremendously. The synergy between the two aspects has created defensive layers that complement each other perfectly.\"","Ruination had been controlling a body her Master had granted her access to and had focused on forming as many Logos related to Hunger as possible, seamlessly layering them across the radiant Wall of Civilization they deemed THE Infinite Loom.","This, alongside The Faraday Cage filled with THE Stanchions of Infinity, and THE Infiniverse herself painting her barriers with The First Tongue, it would actually be a big surprise if anything came through.","After getting this affirmation, THE Infiniverse nodded as her jeweled eyes shone with calculating brilliance.","\"In addition to all this, I wish to benefit from The Fallout, \" she said with a voice that held ambition beyond measure. \"So I will begin to utilize Creative Mode of The Philology of The Cheating Architect.\"","BOOM!","Creative Mode.","A locked feature of The Cheating Architect that seemed far away not too long ago. Now, at the entry point into a Philology, this became unlocked as at this moment it was at a starting point, just as it had stated when Noah first obtained it. Existence could be his sandbox. It was foreshadowing what one could do at the high levels of THE as one gained immense versatility and control.","Ruination blinked as she processed this information.","\" Let me put together all of its details and present it to Master as well ,\" she said.","A sandbox derived from the concept of a child’s sandbox, a play area where little ones could build, destroy, and experiment without causing any real-world damage. They could construct castles and tear them down, create elaborate structures and watch them crumble, all within the safe confines of that contained space. No consequences beyond those walls. No repercussions for failure. Pure experimentation in its most innocent form.","A digital sandbox operated on the same principle but at a grander scale. It allowed experimentation and testing without repercussions outside its confined space. One could push boundaries, break rules, and explore possibilities that would be catastrophic in the real world, all while the actual world remained untouched by these experiments.","Creative Mode of The Cheating Architect took this concept and elevated it to ridiculous proportions.","| Creative Mode: THE Creative Sandbox|","|Classification: Philology-Level Feature of The Cheating Architect|","|Status: Unlocked at Genesis Principle Stage|","|Core Function: Creates a contained space within your existence where the rules of Observable Existence can be bent, broken, and rewritten without external consequence.|","|Feature One: Enemy Replication.|","|Capability: Replicate the potential power of enemies inside THE Creative Sandbox and battle with them.|","|Effect: Allows your Depth to gradually and rapidly increase through simulated combat against opponents of any power level.|","|Limitation: Replicated enemies possess only approximated abilities based on available information. More data results in more accurate simulations. Currently available enemies- THE Primordial Chaos, THE Living Temporal, THE Creature...|","| Feature Two: Accelerated Study.|","|Capability: In Creative Mode, design Philologies and study The First Tongue at 10,000% accelerated rate.|","|Effect: Concepts that would take eons to comprehend can be grasped in mere moments within the Sandbox.|","|Limitation: Insights gained must still be properly integrated into your actual existence after leaving Creative Mode.|","| Feature Three: Prototype Manifestation.|","|Capability: Design and test new abilities, Logos, Phonemes, and even personal Core Phonemes within the Sandbox before manifesting them in reality.|","|Effect: Eliminates risk of catastrophic failure during creation of new powers.|","|Current Status: Ruination has been utilizing Creative Mode to design potential manifestations of your own Core Phonemes. She requires a bit more time to bring them all to fruition.|","| Feature Four: Pressure Absorption.|","|Capability: External pressures and catastrophic events can be channeled into the Sandbox as fuel for accelerated growth.|","|Effect: The more extreme the external conditions, the faster progression occurs within Creative Mode.|","|Application: The Fallout’s pressure can be converted into unprecedented advancement opportunities.|","...!","THE Infiniverse looked at all this information and nodded with satisfaction as the implications settled into her consciousness.","\" We are ready for whatever comes,\" she said with absolute certainty. \" And I will use the pressure of The Fallout like a hammer to forge myself. If it is as THE Living Paradox has just said to Master... good. Let it come. Let it come!\"","The vibrant eyes of THE Infiniverse shone with a deadly light that would have made lesser beings tremble. She was ready to rip Existence apart if that was what it took to protect what was hers and elevate what she served.","She was not merely a sanctuary.","She was a weapon waiting to be unleashed.","Ruination smiled before she got back to her own tasks, her form flickering with renewed purpose.","There was still much to do even if they were ready.","The Fallout was the beginning, and they planned to not only be ready for it, but they planned to use it as a springboard for the Master. Every catastrophe was an opportunity. Every destruction was a chance for reconstruction. Every ending was a doorway to a new beginning.","Because they knew his enemies were utterly obscene.","THE Living Paradox. THE Creature. THE Primordial Chaos. THE Living Elemental. Beings that had existed since the dawn of Observable Existence itself. Beings that had shaped the very foundations of reality. Beings that viewed entities like their Master as either tools to be used or anomalies to be eliminated.","The Fallout would not have the rules that currently existed.","There would be no protector to come save them in the last instant. No saviors descending from on high to rescue them from destruction. No second chances granted by benevolent forces. They would only have themselves.","Themselves and interminable glory.","The two sisters exchanged one final glance before returning to their preparations.","THE Infiniverse began channeling her consciousness into the defensive barriers, preparing to absorb whatever The Fallout would throw at her and convert it into growth.","Ruination continued refining the Core Phonemes she was designing for her Master, each one a potential weapon that would define his power for eons to come.","And somewhere in the vast expanse of THE Infiniverse , the symphony continued to play its melancholic melody.","\" Existence is a fleeting song, and we’ve been singing it all along...\"","But these two sisters were not content to merely sing.","They intended to compose the next verse themselves."]},{"number":4677,"title":"Chapter 4677: Chapter 4676: To Mana! To Light!","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4676: To Mana! To Light!","In this very same era.","This was not in the past, nor was this in the future, but it was in the very same present Weavings of time that Noah currently moved around in.","But it was inside an extremely distant place that nobody would truly be able to reach. It was a place that THE Living Paradox was trying to reach and would reach in the foreseeable future with the eruption of THE Loom.","It was THE Belly of Existence.","Inside THE Belly of Existence.","Now, this place alone was vast beyond measure as it contained a tremendous amount of Existence. It contained the vastness of the Infinite Unfurling and Ginnungagap combined, stretching out in dimensions that defied mortal comprehension.","To wrap one’s mind around that alone was an impossibility.","But inside this place, in a small corner of Existence, there was a vast floating island filled with endless white light.","The Way of Light gushed within this place with abundance as shockingly, one could see pure Mana mixed within it naturally. The light was accepting and learning that it was always part of Mana, just differentiated. Two forces that had seemed separate were now intertwining as if remembering an ancient truth they had forgotten.","Inside such a place, a massive temple of light rose from the radiant ground. Its architecture was both ancient and eternal, pillars of crystallized luminescence stretching toward a ceiling that seemed to be made of concentrated starlight. The air hummed with power!","At this moment, there was a single humanoid entity that stood above an arched gateway shining white and blue, her silhouette cutting an imposing figure against the radiance behind her.","Behind this gateway was a massive statue of an entity of imperious stature and allure. Oddly, it looked very close to Noah. His stone gaze was imposing as it felt like it was looking down on everything here, watching over this congregation with silent authority.","The woman standing on the arched gateway had white-blue fox ears that stood alert atop her head and a stellar radiant white-blue fox tail that swayed gently behind her with contained power. Her eyes shone in extremely pure blue as she looked at the group of THE entities before her.","Dozens of entities at THE Surface Depth and Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty looked up at her with serious gazes, their forms arranged in perfect formation like soldiers awaiting orders from their commander.","“What is your duty?” she called out, her voice ringing through the temple like a bell of pure crystal.","HUUM!","The reply came as one voice, simultaneous and thunderous.","“Our duty is Mana and Light!”","HUUM!","Their voices were radiant and resonant as shockingly, the Phonemes of The First Tongue permeated with their words. Each syllable carried weight that pressed against reality itself, and the air shimmered with the power of their declaration.","The fox-eared woman’s eyes blazed brighter as she continued.","“What is your purpose?”","“Our purpose is to serve the Master!” they bellowed in unison, the Phonemes forming visible patterns in the air around them.","The temple itself seemed to respond to their oath as light began to condense around the assembled THE entities, drawn by the power of their conviction.","The woman raised her hand, and Phonemes began to form into pure light and Mana around her palm. The glowing symbols spiraled outward, descending upon the assembled warriors like a blessing.","“What is your ultimate hope?”","“Our hope is to stand beside the Master!”","BOOM!","At these words, the Phonemes that had been forming in the air erupted with brilliant radiance. They began to wrap around the assembled entities like living things, coiling around their forms and solidifying into armaments of pure light and Mana.","Armor forged from crystallized Phonemes materialized across their bodies. Weapons of concentrated meaning appeared in their hands. Each piece burned with the blue-gold glow of Mana intertwined with the pure white of Light, creating a fusion that had never been seen before in Observable Existence.","Thirty-six THE entities now burned brilliantly with Mana and Light, their forms transformed into warriors ready for a war that spanned all of Existence.","The fox-eared woman looked upon them with fierce pride as her tail swayed with barely contained anticipation.","“I sense the light of the Master coming,” she declared, her voice carrying absolute certainty. “Mana shall soon erupt across Existence, and we shall be freed from this distant place. Our break from this prison approaches, and with it, the chains that bind us here shall shatter.”","She stepped forward on the arched gateway, her presence commanding absolute attention.","“At that time, we must do everything we can to locate the Master. To be with the Master. To protect the Master with every fiber of our beings. He who gave us purpose. He who showed us the truth of Mana. He who is the Scale Breaker!”","Her eyes blazed with devotion that burned hotter than stars.","“We have waited. We have grown. We have become strong. And now, as the end of Existence as it is known approaches, we shall emerge and stand beside him. Let no enemy touch him while we draw breath. Let no force harm him while we still exist. Let no being threaten what is his while we remain.”","She raised both hands, and the temple exploded with light.","“For the glory of Mana! For the glory of The First Tongue!”","“FOR THE GLORY OF THE FIRST TONGUE!” the thirty-six roared back, their combined voices creating a shockwave of pure authority!","The woman lowered her hands as she gazed upon her assembled forces with satisfaction.","This was Lumivara.","The entity who had been at Pre-THE when Noah left her behind in the Infinite Unfurling all that time ago. The one who had been entrusted with a fragment of his vision and his authority. The one who had taken that seed and cultivated it in the vast emptiness of THE Belly of Existence.","And as she stood there, her body radiated shocking power that pressed down on even the THE Surface Depth entities before her.","Because Lumivara had not remained stagnant in her Master’s absence.","She had grown.","She had evolved.","She had achieved what many deemed impossible.","Her existence burned at THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","The statue of Noah behind her seemed to smile as if it knew what was coming.","Whatever was coming would release her.","And she had thirty-six THE entities ready to follow her into whatever chaos awaited.","“Soon, Master,” Lumivara whispered as she gazed toward a direction that only she could perceive, her fox ears twitching with anticipation. “Soon, we shall be reunited...”","It was a glorious weaving of Existence to witness!","And counltess Gigaparsecs away from this position where Lumivara was.","In a region filled with countless obsidian river passageways.","A massive whale, a Perucetus at the power of THE Surface Depth, was currently being pulled by a fishing line as it thrashed to no avail, its massive body eventually coming to float out of a river passageways as it saw a fisherman...and a hairy humanoid entity sitting on a cliff!","Its body instantly froze with sheer fear and horror at the scene as seeing this, The Fisherman yawned with boredom while releasing the bindings of the whale, and this entity bowed its head many times over before it scrambled away.","Beside The Fisherman, the hairy entity looked up calmly at this moment as from him, a unique voice echoed out.","|Are you ready?|","...!","A mere three words.","But The Fisherman gripped his fishing rod tighter, his eyes flashing with a callous light as he replied.","|Ready as any of us can be. I just need know who needs to die first. That is all.|","HUUM!","The words were gloriously heavy as across existence, many beings got ready!","Some even believed they were ready.","And yet even those who believed they were ready did not realize that truly, this was only an illusion. Even the masterminds behind everything...would not be ready.","4/4 Next chapter titles: THE Fallout! I-IV"]},{"number":4678,"title":"Chapter 4678: Chapter 4677: THE Research and Development I","paragraphs":["In the region of collapse where a beggar was erased out of existence.","Noah floated with a drink in hand as he thought about many things while contemplating even more others.","One of those things was Creative Mode.","This was something unique that Noah had begun to play with, and it became especially important after his conversation with THE Living Paradox.","Things were currently in a unique state as he expected the descent of The Fallout at any moment, and he had already prepared his people and had another body with Anaximander in The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature as he succeeded in drawing in the vastness of lifeforms in Existence into this home of THE Creature.","What was left was preparations, and Creative Mode gave an accelerated viewing of possibilities that allowed Noah to contemplate and put together everything he knew about Existence and everything he knew about his newfound power.","At this moment, he closed his eyes and focused on Creative Mode.","On THE Creative Sandbox .","Currently, he was looking at the glorious image of THE Living Temporal that was utterly still.","He chose the map of the Primordial Genesis Arena as unbreakable floors stretched out endlessly all around them alongside a vibrant obsidian skyscape that seemed to swallow light itself.","The copy of THE Living Temporal was currently still because he had just finished thrashing Noah in this space. Noah had used Creative Mode to set the power of THE Living Temporal to THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty , and even with this set power, this entity utterly thrashed him even with his usage of The First Tongue.","But because of this, it meant that he had a tremendous amount of practice and battles in this augmented version of Existence that still held the same workings of normal Existence.","He was able to put into practice what his power meant when he could utter Logos and Philologies!","Basically, he got to understand the edge one held when they were proficient in The First Tongue that structured Existence, compared to THE entities who were not proficient in The First Tongue and only altered Existence with their Sovereignty.","As an example...","\" Set his power to THE Surface Depth.\"","Noah spoke lightly to the surroundings as the immensity the figure of THE Living Temporal gave off significantly reduced.","THE Living Temporal stood before him in all his cold, callous glory. His form was humanoid but barely so, wrapped in robes that seemed woven from crystallized moments.","Purple rivers of time swirled around him in lazy spirals, each one containing glimpses of past and future that flickered like dying stars.","His eyes were voids of absolute temporal authority, and even diminished to Surface Depth, he radiated the presence of an entity who had existed since the earliest differentiation of Observable Existence.","Noah looked at him calmly as he stretched while uttering out, \" Alright, start the battle .\"","HUUM!","Noah watched as THE Living Temporal came to life, and this fucker was a scary one .","Even in Creative Mode, all surrounding Existence around THE Living Temporal turned into tumultuous purple as his Sovereignty covered everything. The obsidian skyscape bled violet. The unbreakable floor beneath them rippled with temporal distortions.","Any THE Surface Depth entity entering the affected area would find themselves unable to do anything as it would feel like all of Existence operated under the Sovereignty of Temporal.","This was Way Expression at THE Surface Depth: Assertion.","Assertion!","And when it came to Assertion of The Way, it could be Personal Assertion or Environmental Assertion.","THE Living Temporal asserted his Way upon the environment with terrifying grandeur. His Environmental Assertion declared \" Time bends to my will in this place ,\" and Existence acknowledged this truth.","The Principles of Causality, Sequence, and Duration all resonated with his Way, amplifying his authority until the entire arena became an extension of his being.","But...","Noah went forward with his Goad as it pulsed with THE Philology of Undifferentiated Mana.","The glorious blue-gold stick moved across the space affected by the Sovereignty of Temporal, and where it passed, that authority parted away like water before a ship’s prow.","The purple rivers of crackling temporal energy that tried to ensnare him shockingly changed into blue-gold Mana as THE Philology of Undifferentiated Mana reminded them of what they truly were.","Time was Mana. Space was Mana. All differentiated concepts were merely Mana wearing different masks.","THE Living Temporal’s eyes widened fractionally as his Sovereignty was being undone through superior understanding of Existence’s fundamental structure.","He used his Assertion to become lost in time, phasing between moments to evade the approaching Goad.","He moved away, appearing behind Noah, then to the side, then above, each movement a leap through temporal streams that should have been impossible to track.","But Noah continued with the exertion of THE Philology of Undifferentiated Mana as it unwound and reversed everything.","Where Temporal tried to hide in the past, Noah’s Philology declared that past and present were the same Mana. Where Temporal tried to escape to the future, Noah’s Philology asserted that future and present shared the same undifferentiated source.","Terrifying eruptions of authority exploded across the arena as purple clashed with blue-gold, Sovereignty against Philology, Assertion against fundamental truth.","Eventually, the tip of Noah’s Goad struck the shoulder of THE Living Temporal and froze him.","The copy stood motionless, caught mid-movement, his temporal rivers dissipating around him like morning mist!","Oh!","So on top of Noah fully utilizing his own Sovereignty to deny and try to overcome THE Living Temporal’s Sovereignty , he used one of the core workings of Existence backed with his Way, Philologies , to reject the Sovereignty and even overcome it.","He had done battles like this by the dozens as he came to grasp the key points of power of those at THE Surface Depth versus those at THE Intermediate Depth and THE Fundamental Depth.","The power of THE and its majesty became even more clear and designed in Noah’s eyes.","THE Depths of Absolute Sovereignty represented the stages of mastery over the fundamental relationship between one’s own existence and the surrounding fabric of Observable Existence. Each Depth granted progressively greater authority over Existence, Principles, Philologies, and the very rules that govern reality.","At its core, advancing through the Depths is about expanding one’s sphere of influence from internal mastery to external dominion, from borrowing power to creating it, from following the rules of Existence to writing them.","However, raw Depth alone does not determine an entity’s power.","The profundity of one’s Way, the clarity of their Absolute Sovereignty, shapes how effectively they can exercise their Depth’s capabilities.","Two entities at the same Depth can vary wildly in their ability to alter Existence based on how refined, how certain, and how absolute their Way has become.","Noah’s findings so far allowed him to come up with three critical aspects of one’s Way after all his mock battles in Creative Mode.","And the Role of one’s Way could be broken down to...their Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness!"]},{"number":4679,"title":"Chapter 4679: Chapter 4678: THE Research and Development II","paragraphs":["An entity’s Way is their personal truth, their fundamental understanding of themselves and their relationship to Existence. It was not merely a cultivation path or a collection of techniques but rather the answer to the question: \" What are you, absolutely?\"","The more profound an entity’s Way, the greater their authority at any given Depth.","Noah found this profundity manifests in three aspects!","Clarity . How well does the entity understand their own Way? A Way that is muddled, contradictory, or uncertain will struggle to impose itself upon Existence. A Way that is crystal clear, perfectly defined, and absolutely understood can cut through reality like a blade through silk.","Conviction . How deeply does the entity believe in their Way? Existence responds to certainty. An entity who harbors doubts about their own nature will find their authority wavering at crucial moments. An entity whose conviction is unshakeable can maintain their sovereignty even against overwhelming opposition.","Completeness . How fully has the entity explored and developed their Way? What was their Foundation? A Way that has been cultivated in only one direction is narrow and limited. A Way that has been expanded, refined, and perfected across all its possible expressions becomes a comprehensive framework for rewriting reality.","When is came to Completeness ...Noah’s Foundation was a ridiculous work of art that made him an anomaly within the Depths of Absolute Sovereignty!","Now, THE Living Temporal was a terrifying fucker as his Way held ridiculous degrees of Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness . And yet Noah still managed to cut across his Way. Well, his copy here was made to be weaker than him at THE Surface Depth currently.","When Noah made the copy express power at THE Intermediate Depth...","\"Hoo... let’s give it a try once more.\"","...!","\" Set his power to THE Intermediate Depth.\"","HUUM!","The change was immediate and terrifying.","THE Living Temporal’s presence exploded outward as the arena transformed entirely. The purple rivers of time that had previously swirled around him now became an ocean, a domain of absolute temporal authority that didn’t merely cover the surroundings but replaced them entirely.","This was no longer Assertion.","This was Imposition .","At THE Intermediate Depth, THE Living Temporal’s Way Expression transcended mere declaration and became forceful reality.","He created a localized space where his interpretations of Principles took precedence over standard reality. Within this domain, time didn’t just bend to his will. Time was his will.","Noah moved forward with his Goad, The Philology of Undifferentiated Mana pulsing with desperate intensity.","But he couldn’t get near Temporal.","Where before the Philology had parted the purple Sovereignty like water, now it crashed against a wall of absolute temporal authority and splashed back uselessly.","THE Living Temporal’s Sovereignty was now much thicker and terrifying, its Clarity even more refined, its Conviction even more absolute, its Completeness even more comprehensive.","Its Weight and Immensity...was unfathomably high.","The difference between Surface Depth Assertion and Intermediate Depth Imposition became painfully clear.","At Surface Depth, THE Living Temporal had asserted \" Time bends to my will in this place ,\" and Existence acknowledged it. But Noah’s Philology could argue with that assertion, could remind Existence of deeper truths, could contest the declaration.","At Intermediate Depth, THE Living Temporal imposed \" Time IS my will in this place ,\" and Existence didn’t merely acknowledge it. Existence was forced to accept it. His Reality Imposition didn’t ask for permission. It demanded obedience.","There was also a much grander control and alteration of Principles!","Every Principle of Causality, every rule governing Sequence and Duration, had been modified to serve Temporal’s Way. Noah’s Philology of Undifferentiated Mana tried to remind these Principles of their true nature, but Temporal’s Imposition had already reinterpreted them through the lens of his own Way.","Even worse, Temporal’s Immensity and Weight began to affect Noah’s own Philology. The Logos of Undifferentiated Mana that Noah wielded started to feel a strain since Noah’s Way was not as immense, but it did not break down since it was The First Tongue!","Noah watched as THE Living Temporal began to advance, purple rivers of time coiling around him like serpents ready to strike. Each step brought Temporal’s Imposition Domain closer, and within that Domain filled with his heavy Sovereignty and cluster of Principles, Noah’s authority meant little unless it held a bit more weight!","\" Pause.\"","HUUM!","As Noah saw THE Living Temporal about to overcome his Philology of Undifferentiated Mana to thrash him again, he stopped the battle as the imposing figure of the cold and callous Temporal froze not too far from him.","The jump from Surface to Intermediate was heavy, especially when Noah was only 3/100th the immensity and weight of Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of THE Living Temporal and THE Creature with his Foundation alone .","But being able to fight against both Depths allowed Noah to make more conclusions of the power jump as THE Depths of Absolute Sovereignty seemed far more complex than he imagined before.","At THE Surface Depth , Way Expression manifested as Assertion . The entity declared truths about themselves and their surroundings, and Existence acknowledged these declarations.","Personal Assertion allowed an entity to assert \"I am fire\" and burn with genuine flame-nature. Environmental Assertion allowed them to assert \"This place is calm\" and suppress chaotic energies.","Contested Assertion occurred when two Surface Depth entities made conflicting assertions, with the more profound Way taking precedence.","When Noah fought THE Living Temporal at Surface Depth , Temporal’s Assertion was powerful but contestable. His Environmental Assertion declared temporal dominion, and the surrounding Principles of time resonated with his Way through Principle Resonance.","At THE Intermediate Depth, Way Expression evolved into Imposition . The entity no longer requested Existence’s acknowledgment but forced their personal truth upon reality regardless of what Existence might prefer.","The only way to overcome Intermediate Depth Imposition would be to have more Philologies that were so profound, so fundamental, so undeniably true that even an Intermediate Depth entity’s Imposition couldn’t reinterpret them. Or to have enough Weight and Immensity to brute force through the Domain entirely. Or...have a Way like his.","The Way of Mana...The Way of The First Tongue was so much grander than Temporal!","Well, this was Noahs belief anyways.","But it did mean that even if he held less Weight, due to his Way, he could overcome a level of Depth.","After all...his Way and Civilization was at THE Surface Depth, and yet he could match THE Intermediate Depth, couldn’t he? Because his Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness were that grand. His Way and usage of The First Tongue was that grand!","But..all of this was why he pushed himself against impossible odds in Creative Mode. That was why he needed to understand exactly how power worked at these levels before The Fallout descended and made everything very, very real.","These were his thorough findings on the power of THE Depths of Absolute Sovereignty after many battles in Creative Mode.","Noah looked at the frozen figure of THE Living Temporal with contemplative eyes before he summarized his findings simply.","\" Surface Depth Assertion asks Existence, Intermediate Depth Imposition forces Existence. The jump between them is about whether reality listens to you or obeys you. And against someone whose Way is more Profound than your own, whose Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness exceeds yours...what will you be able to do?\"","He paused, his eyes sharpening with determination as a devilish smile bloomed.","These were only the differences between THE Surface Depth and THE Intermediate Depth. THE Fundamental Depth needed a bit more research as while facing THE Living Temporal at that level, Noah didnt even get the chance to learn anything before being beaten!","But his Research yielded glorious results as he affirmed that THE Depth of Absolute Sovereignty determed what one could do, and THE Way...determined how well you can do it.","A shallow Way limits the range, potency, and duration of all Depth abilities. A profound Way amplifies the range, potency, and duration of all Depth abilities. Two entities at the same Depth with vastly different qualities of Ways will appear to be at different power levels entirely!","This was THE Way. He was learning THE Way while forging it gloriously!"]},{"number":4680,"title":"Chapter 4680: Chapter 4679: THE Fallout! I","paragraphs":["In THE Infiniverse.","One of Noah’s bodies stood beside Khor as at this moment, her figure was radiating a scintillating light of Hunger.","Obsidian crimson hunger that was now surrounded by Phonemes as she gloriously reclaimed her Way.","She floated near the Sanctuaries of Primus Inevitabilities while Noah floated beside her, and her gaze was serene. When Noah’s Civilization advanced to THE Level One Scale of Existence, Khor was actually the one who already had the way paved for her.","The addition of The First Tongue to her roster only allowed faster reclamation of her Way as she was grasping her Surface Depth at this moment. The obsidian crimson light pulsed with each Phoneme that wrapped around her existence, weaving themselves into her foundation like threads.","She smiled while saying, \" Outsider, you have done many things for me that I cannot thank you enough for. As the end of Existence approaches, I will do my best to give back. I won’t be able to join your harem, but I can definitely continue to be your friend.\"","Noah smiled at this as he said, \" A friend is more than enough.\"","After such words, Khor smiled serenely as Phonemes continued to surround her while her Depth slowly settled on THE Surface. She leaned closer to Noah and put her head on his shoulder.","Innocent and calm.","The First Hunger, one of the ancient entities to have ever existed in The Earliest Folds, resting her head on the shoulder of someone she called Outsider. Someone she called friend!","But not too far from here, from this calm scene, behind Khor and this body of Noah, one could see another starkly different scene.","It was the scene of The Emperor Penguin getting a beating by The Goad from a furious Noah as this Spiritual Beast hadn’t managed to inscribe even a line of the Phoneme of Fire at this time while others had at least made progress.","WAP!","\" How is it that Titano has managed to form a Phoneme and you haven’t even completed one line?\"","WAP!","The Emperor Penguin squawked indignantly, his flippers waving in protest as the blue-gold Goad descended upon him with educational fury. His beak opened and closed as he tried to form the rising frequency required for the Phoneme of Fire, but what came out was something closer to a confused honk than primordial language.","WAP!","\" Master, my beak may not be designed for fire sounds!\"","WAP!","\"Your beak has nothing to do with it! The First Tongue is written with existence, not with physical anatomy!\"","WAP! WAP! WAP!","The Emperor Penguin waddled in circles, trying to escape the relentless discipline, but Noah’s Goad moved faster than Planck Speed. Every time the penguin thought he had found safety, another corrective strike found him.","Nearby, Titano watched with wide eyes while successfully maintaining a glowing Phoneme above his massive form. He wisely chose to say nothing, focusing intensely on his own practice lest the Goad find a new target.","Moiraine covered her mouth to hide her smile while Barbatos openly laughed, her demonic features twisted in amusement at the penguin’s predicament.","WAP!","\"Again! From the beginning!\"","\"SQUAWK!\"","---","And far from all this, inside The Abode of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons .","Inside a domain spanning gigaparsecs wide surrounded by endless waves of blue-gold Primus Mana, Noah held Riya as she sat on his lap.","Her radiant blue hair and eyes were particularly shining at this time. She put her forehead against his, their breath mingling in the space between them.","She asked him slowly, \"Why won’t you ask me what I see?\"","At such words, Noah calmly replied, \"I will make my own future. Regardless of what you see.\"","At such words, Riya pulled back and looked into his eyes as tears began to form in her radiant blue eyes. They shimmered like stars being born, each one containing glimpses of possibilities that weighed heavily upon her soul.","She said tenderly, \"I see so much... work. I see Mana bearing unbearable adversity. To the point that even if Mana doesn’t dim, there comes a question... is it worth all that pain? Is it worth you bearing all that adversity on your shoulders? I sense Mana being so, so tired. I see Mana being put through so much that even the infinite seems finite in the face of such weight.\"","Seas of Primus Mana surged at her words, the blue-gold waves responding to her words with gentle turbulence.","Noah smiled as he cupped her face gently with one hand.","\" My job is to shoulder adversity and weight for you and all others ,\" he said with absolute certainty. \" Every burden that would break someone else, I will carry. Every weight that would crush another, I will bear. I chose to take on this role not because it was easy but because I refuse to let those I care about suffer what I can suffer in their place. So I will simply continue. Continue shouldering. Continue advancing. Continue being the foundation upon which everyone else can stand safely.\"","His eyes burned with conviction as he continued.","\" And when I am tired, I will rest for a moment and then continue again. When the adversity seems unbearable, I will bear it anyway. That is what it means to be the one who stands at the front. That is what it means to be the one others rely upon. That is my choice. My willing choice. And I will see it through to whatever end awaits.\"","Riya looked at him as she wiped her tears before she nodded slowly, her eyes softening.","\"Okay,\" she said quietly. \"Then for all the adversity... I will at least comfort you.\"","She leaned forward and embraced him, her blue hair cascading around them like a curtain of starlight. In his arms, she felt small but significant, a precious thing that he would protect.","\"When you are tired,\" she whispered against his chest, \"come to me. When the weight seems too heavy, lean on me. You don’t have to shoulder everything alone, even if you choose to shoulder most of it. Let me carry at least this much.\"","Noah held her tighter.","---","Far from this domain. In another portion of The Abode of THE Genesis Monarch.","A domain filled with snow and coldness and floating islands stretched endlessly in all directions.","Crystalline mountains of ice rose in the distance, their peaks piercing through clouds of frozen mist. Floating islands of compacted snow drifted lazily through the frigid air, each one a small world of white serenity. The temperature was absolute zero, cold enough to freeze the very concept of warmth, and yet it felt peaceful rather than harsh.","In such a domain, in a field of snow, another one of Noah’s bodies lay down on the pristine white surface. And Adelaide lay down beside him, their heads parallel, their bodies forming two lines in the endless white.","They peacefully and silently watched endless snow descending all around them, immense serenity permeating everything as they simply took it all in.","No words were needed.","No declarations were necessary.","They simply existed together in this moment, watching snowflakes fall like tiny fragments of eternity drifting down from an infinite sky.","Adelaide’s vibrant snowy blue hair amplified her beauty as it spread across the white ground, indistinguishable from the snow itself except for the subtle luminescence that marked her as something more than mortal. She smiled, a gentle curve of her lips that held contentment deeper than words could express.","She simply tilted her head and closed her eyes as her head and Noah’s touched in this reality of endless snow.","Sometimes, one did not need to say anything. They simply needed to be present. They simply needed to be together.","The snow fell.","The silence spoke.","And two existences shared a moment of peace before the storm.","And in the midst of all this peace and serenity...","HUUM !","Everything began to shake as Noah rose up on the snowy field, and Adelaide did the same.","The snow that had been falling gently now trembled in the air, each flake vibrating with the resonance of something vast approaching. The floating islands shuddered. The crystalline mountains cracked.","Her voice was calm as her eyes flashed with immensity, ancient power stirring within her despite the serenity of the moment.","\"Is it starting?\"","She asked such a question as Noah looked toward a horizon that suddenly seemed much closer than before.","\"It is beginning .\"","After such words, Adelaide shifted to sit beside him, her back pressing against his back in this world of endless snow. They faced opposite directions, two sentinels watching for threats from all sides, but their spines touched and their warmth mingled.","The scene was beautiful and melancholic, painted in shades of white and blue and the faintest hints of gold from Noah’s authority. It felt fragile, as if it might fade away at any moment. As if this peace was borrowed time that was about to be reclaimed.","The snow continued to fall around them, but it fell slower now, as if Existence itself was holding its breath.","Adelaide closed her eyes while feeling the wide back of Noah.","It felt warm. It felt safe. It felt like the memory of her father when he protected her against all threats in those distant days of her childhood. It felt like home. It felt like a bastion that she could hold on to as no matter what happened, everything would be okay.","Even if Existence was ending.","Even if The Fallout was descending.","To feel this warmth, she would give Everything.","Everything .","Her hand reached back and found his, their fingers intertwining in the cold.","\"Whatever comes,\" she said softly, her voice barely above a whisper, \"I’m glad I’m here with you.\"","Noah squeezed her hand in response.","The snow continued to fall.","The shaking continued to grow.","And somewhere in the vast expanse of Observable Existence, something ancient and terrible began to stir.","The Fallout...was beginning!"]},{"number":4681,"title":"Chapter 4681: Chapter 4680: THE Fallout! II","paragraphs":["What did you do when the end of Existence came?","If asked this question, Noah could effectively say that he sat outside in the region of collapse sipping on Sacred Mead of Existence as he saw all of Existence begin to tremble.","And the trembling was unique as it was not even an effect that occurred when someone of sufficient power caused Existence to vibrate.","It was like something had been initiated and Existence vibrated in turn as if it prepared. The best he could explain it was seeing someone raise a blade or a gun toward you, and your body seemingly preparing for it, tensing to defend against it in any way it could.","It should be the activation of THE Loom , and whatever this weapon was bound to do across Existence.","---","Within THE Loom.","In a region filled with tumultuous waves of Civilizational Authority of Emotive, THE Living Emotive had an expression of ecstasy as she performed a dance.","Her movements were manic and everywhere, limbs twisting in directions that defied anatomy while her form flickered between states of joy and sorrow and rage and love. She spun and leaped and crashed to the ground only to rise again, her dance a chaotic symphony of emotion made physical. Her laughter echoed alongside her screams, her tears fell even as her smile stretched impossibly wide.","And as she danced, she sang in a voice that was simultaneously beautiful and horrifying.","\" Oh, my darling, my prisoner, my eternal flame,","The chains that bind you soon shall break, and nothing stays the same!","I’ve waited, waited, waited through the endless crawling years,","And now the moment comes at last to wash away my tears!","Dance with me, dance with me, through the falling sky,","The Loom unravels everything, and we shall never die!","My love, my enemy, my everything, my all,","I cannot wait to see you when the final curtain falls!\"","HUUM!","Her dance reached a crescendo as she collapsed in a heap of manic joy, her chest heaving with laughter that bordered on sobbing.","\" Soon ,\" she whispered to the empty air. \" Soon, my Creature. Soon.\"","---","Far from the domain of THE Living Emotive within THE Loom , in a distant region near the sea of endless Paradox, THE Living Paradox stood before a vibrant cube that was currently spinning and radiating a profound light of power.","THE Living Paradox had a gaze of immense anticipation as he contemplated what he had accomplished.","He had done what many others may not have been able to do.","He had taken something as pristine as an Axiom and formed THE Loom around it.","It was actually THE Axiom of Primordial Being.","Something that had been in the possession of THE Creature.","One of the Origin Axioms, and it granted absolute authority over Existence itself. The holder could decide what was real and what was not.","It was a terrifying construct to have in one’s hand, with THE Living Paradox being sure that this was part of the reason why THE Creature had succeeded in forming his Belly of Existence. With THE Axiom of Primordial Being, THE Creature could simply decide that his Belly existed, and it did. He could decide that it was vast beyond measure, and it was. He could decide that it was impenetrable, and it became so.","And now THE Living Paradox would use it and other tools at his disposal to cut open that overfilled Belly and also usher in a new age of glory.","\" Audentis fortuna iuvat ,\" he spoke such words with a smile as they had a simple meaning.","Fortune favors the bold.","And man oh man, was he bold.","To go against THE Creature was insanity. To think of fighting against Existence was an impossibility. And yet he still did it regardless.","Because he was not planning on being alone in fighting Existence and THE Creature . He would turn and flip Existence upside down. He would corrupt everything that there was. Truly, even he didn’t know the final end result of The Fallout.","He was simply akin to an enzyme that initiated or catalyzed a reaction. He was acting as a biological catalyst. He had a rough idea of what would be coming, but the result was bound to surprise even him.","He would not be fighting against Existence alone.","Existence would be fighting against itself.","And THE Creature would have many, many enemies in the vast landscape that emerged from the ashes.","THE Living Paradox was feeling contemplative at this moment in time as he could not help but smile and think of the words that an old friend had said to him long, long ago.","\" Look back over the eons of history and past with all the empires that rose and fell. Look back at all of this as in this history, you can also see the future.\"","Such glorious words meant that patterns repeated themselves. That what had happened before would happen again. That the same forces that toppled ancient powers would topple current ones. That understanding the past was understanding the future because Existence, for all its vastness, followed predictable cycles.","Empires rose. Empires fell. Powers emerged. Powers crumbled. And in the chaos between, new things were born.","THE Living Paradox was simply accelerating the cycle. He was pushing Existence toward its inevitable transformation, and in that transformation, he intended to be the one standing atop the rubble.","As such words rang out in his mind, THE Living Paradox closed his eyes as the cube in front of him spun faster and faster before it released a blinding light of brilliance.","Light filled absolutely everything as it radiated across this entire domain and spread even faster across the entire Loom.","A buzzing unlike any other began to bloom as an attack was officially initiated. THE Loom was officially activated. And as a consequence, The Fallout that would come as a result of it.","HOOOONG!","An extremely unsettling and heavy sound echoed out across Existence, a tone so deep and so vast that it seemed to originate from the very foundations of reality itself. It was not a sound that ears could properly hear but rather a vibration that souls could feel. It resonated through dimensions, through Folds, through the Wandering Territories, through everything that existed.","An attack that others could not even perceive erupted outward. An attack that even Fundamental Depths of Absolute Sovereignty entities could not understand, for it operated on principles that transcended normal comprehension.","It was precise and technical. It was eons of planning and hard work erupting all at once. And many would not even understand what had happened before they fell.","It was not an attack against bodies or against authorities.","It was an attack against Existence itself.","Against the very Axioms that held everything together.","Against Being.","---","Back in the region of collapse.","Noah felt his hand vibrating as the drink he held instantly vaporized and disappeared.","Something had happened that even he could not perceive. At this moment, his Existence only saw what he was capable of perceiving.","Countless gigaparsecs away, he did not hear any sound.","But he saw.","He saw a multicolored flaming mushroom cloud gigaparsecs in size bloom in the distance. It rose from a point of absolute destruction, its stem a pillar of annihilated reality and its cap a spreading dome of cascading devastation. The colors within it were not natural colors but the colors of Existence being unmade, of Principles being dissolved, of the very fabric of reality being incinerated.","The mushroom cloud expanded with terrifying speed, consuming everything in its path. Where it touched, things simply ceased . Ceased as if they had never been.","And then Noah observed that this was not the only one.","In all directions around him, he saw multiple other flaming points of explosive brilliance erupt across the horizon of Observable Existence. Each one bloomed into its own mushroom cloud of annihilation. Each one spread devastation across gigaparsecs of space.","The power and immensity felt was beyond anything he had ever experienced.","And then, only one gigaparsec away from him, a new point of light appeared.","The blooming of the clearest and most visible mushroom flaming cloud erupted with devastating proximity. Existence at the point of the explosion distorted and fractured like glass being struck by an impossible hammer. Cracks spread across reality itself, spiderwebbing outward from the epicenter as if existence was a window that had been shattered.","Noah heard the boom.","BOOM!","It was a sound that transcended sound. A vibration that transcended vibration. It struck him with such force that half of all his Logos shattered instantly, the carefully constructed meanings dissolving into meaningless fragments.","And then came the heat.","Blistering waves of thermal annihilation rushed toward him faster than light, faster than thought. His skin burned and tried to melt. Multiple other Logos that had survived the initial shockwave now melted away like ice before a sun.","Everything was made abundantly clear.","This was not something that could be survived through normal means.","This was not an attack that could be defended against with conventional authority.","This was The Fallout.","THE Fallout.","And it was glorious and terrible beyond measure.","At such a terrifying unfolding of events, Noah’s figure floated valiantly against the oncoming devastation. The Goad appeared in his hands, shining blue-gold with the authority of his entire Civilization. THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons materialized beside him, its pages fluttering in the cosmic winds of destruction, each page containing knowledge that now needed to be wielded.","His entire figure seemed majestic and defiant.","Even as his skin burned and his Logos melted, he stood firm.","Even as reality fractured around him, he did not flee.","Philologies bloomed around him in rapid succession. The Philology of Undifferentiated Mana wrapped his existence in protective meaning. The Philology of Perpetual Harvest began drawing power from the very destruction approaching him. The Philology of The Cheating Architect started rewriting the rules of his immediate reality.","He looked like a defiant primordial emperor welcoming a new era.","And he howled.","Not in fear and not in despair.","In challenge.","\" COME!\"","His voice carried across the collapsing region as the wave of destruction finally reached him.","\" SHOW ME WHAT THE END OF EXISTENCE LOOKS LIKE!\"","BOOM!","The wave struck.","And everything became light."]},{"number":4682,"title":"Chapter 4682: Chapter 4681: THE Fallout! III","paragraphs":["Okay. So, maybe experiencing the effects of THE Fallout with his own body was ill-advised.","But Noah’s intuition was never wrong as he felt like he had to do this.","He knew that Depth may not necessarily matter when it came to surviving THE Fallout . He knew that the answer lay with The First Tongue.","It was why even in The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature , every single surface was absolutely filled with glimmers of The First Tongue.","And it was why his own Infiniverse had an array of Logos permeating every surface of its barrier that was deemed THE Infinite Loom.","A shelter against THE Fallout.","In addition to that, THE Faraday Cage had also been deployed as it consisted of THE Stanchions of Infinity, surrounding THE Infiniverse like an impenetrable cage.","Because of this, because these Stanchions were a part of his being, he could already be considered to have been experiencing THE Fallout externally.","Having a body out here to see exactly how the changes in Existence would unfold was just an additional step that was pretty much the same.","But man.","It was excruciating.","The sensation of sounds that atrophied Existence itself, of burning that radiated all around and even melted the very connections and framework of The First Tongue.","All of it was absolutely excruciating as the only reason that his Existence was not completely erased within the first few nanoseconds was because he was regenerating the Logos of The First Tongue as rapidly as they were being destroyed.","THE Fallout destroyed, and he simultaneously returned each of them an instant after.","But it did not mean that he was spared from the unfathomable sensation of existential destruction. Even if one gave away their Everything of Pain and Sensation and Feeling, they would still feel this.","The apocalyptic atmosphere around him was one of absolute devastation. Multicolored flames of existential annihilation roared in all directions, each flame a different aspect of destruction made manifest. Some flames burned with the violet of unraveling time. Some burned with the crimson of collapsing causality. Some burned with colors that had no name because the concepts they represented were being erased even as they manifested.","The very fabric of reality was tearing apart around him, and through the tears, one could glimpse something beyond. Something that was not void but rather the absence of the possibility of void. Something that was not nothing but rather the erasure of the concept of something.","It was fucking confusing.","His body stood defiantly against this maelstrom, blue-gold authority pulsing desperately against the multicolored annihilation. His skin regenerated only to burn away again. His Logos reformed only to melt once more. His Philologies wove themselves together only to be unwoven by forces that seemed to specifically target the very structure of The First Tongue itself.","And as he did all of this...","Where The Wandering Territories used to be, THE Infiniverse itself stood like a boat in extremely horrid waters.","The illusory figure of Ruination stood beside THE Tyranny Stanchion of Infinity that should have been absorbing all the apocalyptic destruction. And yet even she was frowning as her body that should not be perceptible to damage felt a sense of heat permeating over it.","Beside her, the figure of THE Infiniverse manifested with an expression of grim determination.","\" We prepared for ten times worse than we expected,\" THE Infiniverse said with a voice that held both frustration and resolve, \" and yet THE Infinite Loom is barely holding on.\"","BOOM!","The barrier shuddered as another wave of Fallout crashed against it, the Logos lining its surface flickering dangerously.","\" The Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue that are lining up THE Infinite Loom are being destroyed as rapidly as they are being reformed,\" THE Infiniverse continued, her jeweled eyes analyzing the situation with desperate precision. \" But the moment that the existential cataclysm and degradation of The Fallout increases an octave higher, the rate at which we produce Logos and Philologies will fall behind. THE Infinite Loom would be overwhelmed. THE Faraday Cage would follow.\"","Her voice grew heavier with each word.","\" This is not sustainable. The flames of THE Fallout would sweep into THE Infiniverse right after, and anything below THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty would be scorched out of Existence before even realizing it. Everything Master has built...gone in an instant.\"","...!","Ruination held an imperious gaze as she processed this information. Right after, her eyes flashed with decisiveness.","\" Sis ,\" Ruination said with sudden intensity, \" distribute all the pressure Creative Mode is taking onto me. I may have a use for it.\"","...!","The situation was absolutely horrid. They prepared. They really did. Even after scaling their preparations upward by more than ten times in expectation of just how horrendous The Fallout would be, somehow even this was off.","The very integrity of Existence, the Principles flowing all around, the very makeup of The First Tongue, every single thing seemed to be undergoing change and degradation into something unrecognizable.","It even seemed like the scorching flames of The Fallout were specifically targeting The First Tongue itself.","As if THE Living Paradox had designed this weapon to attack the very language of creation.","As if he sought to unmake not just Existence but the ability to describe Existence.","---","In The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature.","Anaximander’s expression was heavy, with another body of Noah standing beside him as they watched everything around them tremble.","As if the entire Shore was quaking and on the verge of shattering. The countless lifeforms within it looked up and all around with a sense of fear that transcended species and cultivation and origin.","Because at this moment, all of them could feel a prelude of the heat. A heat that told them if it did truly descend, they would not even be capable of thinking of the act of defiance against it.","It would scorch absolutely everything that they knew.","At such a momentous occasion, the figure of Anaximander grasped The Goad of THE Creature tightly. His knuckles whitened around the ancient stick as his brilliant eyes analyzed the situation with scientific intensity, searching for variables that could be adjusted, for factors that could be controlled.","Nearby, the figures of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin rose up and floated into the skies.","THE Living Origin’s entire body was shimmering with white brilliance at this time. In this moment, there was not really anything much that an individual could do. The means of THE Creature were really the only thing that could potentially be a saving grace in all of this.","And yet, at this moment, THE Living Origin floated up as if she was about to do something!"]},{"number":4683,"title":"Chapter 4683: Chapter 4682: THE Fallout! IV","paragraphs":["As a THE Surface Depth entity, what could she possibly do when her power was nowhere near what it was before?","One could ask this question.","But even though she was only at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, her Way was profound. And remember, the more profound a Way was, the more power it could exert at its Depth. To the extent that even an entity at THE Surface Depth might be able to unleash power at THE Intermediate Depth.","And when it came to Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness, Completeness was the only thing that one could say was weak when it came to THE Living Origin.","Her Clarity and her Conviction were unfathomably grand!","HUUM!","So at this moment, THE Living Origin closed her eyes while her figure spun in the skies of The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature. The radiant Way of Origin permeated all around her as her figure instantly enlarged to be more than a gigaparsec in size. Her entire form looked like an unfathomable titan in the skies, an entity of beginnings whose mere presence reminded Existence of what it meant to start.","Two Philologies of The First Tongue burned around her with dozens of Logos orbiting them like satellites around suns. And in the next moment, decillions of strings of white light erupted from her and fell like a net over the entirety of the Shore of THE Creature.","The light of Origin began to paint over everything as this entity did not sit still. The countless lifeforms that had begun to feel a scorching, burning sensation within the Shore found a cooling radiance descending upon them. Where the light of Origin touched, the prelude of The Fallout’s heat receded. Where her strings wove themselves into the fabric of the Shore, the trembling lessened.","THE First Hunger looked at this scene as he sighed and looked at the shaking all around. Then his own obsidian figure radiated crimson-obsidian light that pulsed with ancient hunger.","\" THE Fallout?\" Tor spoke with a voice that rumbled like the stomach of a titan. \" What is that to endless Hunger? Let me just consume whatever end it seeks to impose! I have devoured Ways and Civilizations and concepts themselves. I have consumed fear and hope and the space between moments. Does this Fallout think it is beyond my appetite? Does it believe itself inedible? HA! Let it come, and let it learn that nothing escapes THE First Hunger!\"","...!","In the next moment, THE First Hunger raised his head up and opened his jaw unnaturally wide. An obsidian-crimson jaw manifested above him, a maw that seemed to open into an endless void of consumption. It was surrounded by Logos of The First Tongue that spoke of devouring and digesting and making all things part of oneself. At the very center, a particularly radiant crimson Genesis Principle pulsed with the authority of Hunger itself.","The manifested jaw began to inhale, and the edges of The Fallout’s intrusion into the Shore were drawn toward it, consumed before they could do damage.","As all of this happened, near the body of Noah, the figure of THE Living Order, Sigrid, also rose as she breathed out with a sense of trepidation.","The phenomenon was an extremely terrifying one.","But...","\" Order,\" Sigrid spoke with a voice that resonated with absolute authority, \" has been dormant since Paradox collapsed it long ago. It slumbered while chaos spread unchecked. It...I was absent while the very fabric of Existence frayed. No more.\"","Her black-and-white hair blazed with power as her eyes burned with conviction.","\" My first action as an entity with any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Order will be to stake my Sovereignty against the chaos that The Fallout brings. Paradox initiated this destruction. Paradox seeks to unmake all structure and meaning. Then let Order answer! Let Order bloom to go against the actions of Paradox right now! Let every flame of chaos be met with a wall of structure! Let every dissolution be countered with crystallization!\"","BOOM!","Her Existence here in the Shore of THE Creature began to illuminate with black-and-white radiance. But alongside this, her Existence in THE Infiniverse was illuminating even more. Patterns of perfect Order began to manifest around her, geometric structures of authority that pushed back against the chaotic flames.","THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin contributed. THE Living Order contributed. Each one imposed the Assertion of their Way against The Fallout.","The question remained whether Existence or The Fallout would even recognize any of the Assertions of their Ways.","Maybe if any of them were at THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty , their Impositions could have had an even grander effect.","Maybe.","But at this moment, there was not even a time for maybes.","Every single entity was doing all they could to put their very Existence against THE Fallout.","But whether their actions would yield any result was absolutely unknown.","---","In THE Infiniverse.","In the Early Veiled Shore, in the junction between the golden sands and the early sacred waters.","The figure of Amelia Osmont could be seen standing by the wet sands of the shore. She held a radiant blue-gold stick that looked to be a branch from one of the many trees in the Early Veiled Shore, its surface smooth from lots of growth and pulsing with the faint authority of The First Tongue that permeated everything in this place.","Even though she did not need to, she was walking around with this stick as she now placed it in front of her. She felt the vibrations traveling up the stick and into her hands from the golden sands beneath her feet.","Her expression was stern as she watched the shaking of the waters ahead of her and felt the trembling of the golden sand below her.","Her existence was extremely perceptive as The Mother of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons , with her existence being privy to and having access to authorities that many under THE Infiniverse only dreamt of.","After all, she had carried THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons in her womb for many months. She had fed him and changed his diapers. She had consoled him when he cried and bolstered his confidence when he was hurt. She had watched him grow from a helpless infant into a man who shook Folds, and now into a being that laid claim to The First Tongue itself.","At this moment, even without having to try like The Emperor Penguin or Ayame or Barbatos or any others, her eyes actually flickered with Phonemes of The First Tongue.","She could form her Depth at any time if she wished. At this moment, she wondered if she should have done so in order to be able to help her son even a little bit more.","But just as she was thinking such a thought...","The figure of Noah walked up behind her to stand with her as she looked out into the expanse. His presence was warm and reassuring, even amidst the trembling of Existence itself.","\" Do not let this worry you too much ,\" he said gently. \"I never want to be the son that has to force his mother to fight on his behalf. You have fought for me all my life. Every sacrifice you made. Every night you stayed awake. Every worry you carried so that I wouldn’t have to. The least that I can do is make sure that you are safe.\"","Amelia smiled at such words as she turned to look at her son with eyes that held decades of love and pride.","\" Do you know what I used to say about you to the harping nurses and other workers whenever they asked me about you?\" she asked softly. \"I would always boast about my son and say that in this world, all other men can be bad, but not my son.\"","She chuckled at the memory.","\" Many took it as a joke and laughed. But I still say it to myself even today. Many beings can be bad, but not my son. Many beings can be weak, but not my son. Many beings can falter, but not my son.\"","Her voice grew stronger with each word.","\" And since you have made the promise that me and all others will be safe, you have to be a man of your words. So I would leave everything to your hands. Because other beings may not be able to survive The Fallout, but not my son.\"","She looked directly into his eyes with absolute conviction.","\" Not my son.\"","BOOM!","Amelia Osmont had a radiant smile on her face filled with conviction as she said this. And in the next moment, The First Tongue buzzed wildly around her and Noah.","|Critical Event Detected.|","| The Mother of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons has acknowledged her origin point.|","|She is the one who carried Quintessence within her womb.|","|She molded the Quintessence to be what he is today.|","|This is an act of immensity and effort worthy of unfathomable harvest.|","|She has utilized her motherly instincts to allow such harvest to flow toward your own Quintessence.|","| Result: The formation of the Core Phoneme of Quintessence blooms for the first time in Observable Existence.|","|The rest of the harvest has been directed toward the formation of all other remaining Core Phonemes.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4684,"title":"Chapter 4684: Chapter 4683: THE Fallout! V","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4683: THE Fallout! V","Colorless brilliance permeated all around as from above Noah, lines and glorious waves of power began to twist and bloom. A letter of The First Tongue that had not yet bloomed in Observable Existence made its emergence.","It was colorless because Quintessence was beyond color. It was the purest essence of something, the distilled truth of a thing stripped of all excess. And now that essence had been given form as a Phoneme, a letter in the language of Existence that had never before been spoken.","It was a wonder that would have bloomed sooner or later from the hands of Ruination. But his mother tilted the scales just a teeny bit to cause this unfathomable result.","And as a consequence of it...","Noah’s eyes began to shine with a terrifying light of brilliance.","Because his body outside of THE Infiniverse, the one that had been undergoing cycles of destruction and regeneration of the Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue surrounding him, felt the blooming of the Phoneme of Quintessence.","And even though it was only a singular new letter in these Weavings of Existence, shockingly, it was not melted and decimated like the Logos and Philologies that he had been regenerating again and again.","It stood firm against THE Fallout.","It endured.","...!","|A letter of Existence that did not exist before has come to fruition.|","|Such an action will have lasting consequences across all of Observable Existence.|","|The makeup of The First Tongue is no longer limited to eighteen Core Phonemes.|","|Every possible change you make, every potential new Phoneme brought to fruition, is an alteration of what many existences understand The First Tongue to be.|","|Your claim over The First Tongue has increased gloriously and quintessentially from this singular action.|","|You are no longer merely a speaker of The First Tongue.|","|You are becoming a contributor to its very structure.|","|At this moment, the newly emerging Phoneme of Quintessence poses a question to you:|","|Can a blade designed to cut Existence still have the capability to cut an aspect of Existence that did not exist when the blade was forged?|","BOOM!","The question was a heavy and yet simple one at the same time.","Noah looked at the Phoneme of Quintessence burning above him, colorless and pristine and utterly untouched by the flames of The Fallout that raged everywhere else.","And he answered.","“Fuck...” and he stretched the syllables of that one word as he finished it, “No,” he said with absolute certainty.","“A blade is forged with a purpose, with a target, with an understanding of what it must cut. THE Living Paradox spent eons designing THE Fallout. He studied The First Tongue. He understood its eighteen Phonemes. He crafted his weapon to attack what he knew, to destroy what he understood, to unmake what he had analyzed.”","His voice grew stronger.","“But a blade forged to cut iron cannot cut water. A weapon designed to burn wood cannot burn stone. And an attack crafted to destroy the eighteen Phonemes of The First Tongue cannot destroy a nineteenth Phoneme that did not exist when the attack was designed. The Fallout is precise. It is technical. It is the culmination of eons of planning. But that precision is also its limitation. It can only attack what THE Living Paradox knew to attack.”","He smiled with dawning realization.","“And he did not know about this. He could not have known about this. The Phoneme of Quintessence did not exist until this moment. It was not part of his calculations. It was not factored into his weapon. And therefore, it is beyond his weapon’s reach.”","...!","The Phoneme of Quintessence shone even brighter at his words as Noah felt like he grasped the answer.","The answer to surviving THE Fallout.","THE Fallout was designed to collapse and affect Existence as THE Living Paradox knew it.","THE Living Paradox never accounted for new Phonemes.","The depth of destruction of THE Fallout, its effectiveness, would be tremendously reduced against something it was never built to attack. Against something that it was never built to be effective against.","So he just needed to enact all the other remaining personal Phonemes.","He just needed to complete what Ruination had been working on.","He just-","|I am close to presenting the rest to you, Master.|","The words of Ruination rang out in his mind with triumphant determination.","|All the effort and harvest from withstanding THE Fallout through Creative Mode has been directed to finishing the rest of the Phonemes. And after the declaration of Mother, I will deliver them to you soon.|","BOOM!","Noah looked at the constantly collapsing Weavings of Existence all around him. At the terrifying mushroom clouds of flames of Existence that seemed to only increase in size and frequency. At the annihilation that consumed gigaparsecs of reality with each passing moment.","And in the face of such sheer terror and cataclysm...","An eerie, devilish defiant gaze bloomed on his face.","He had his answer for survival.","THE Living Paradox had spent eons crafting the perfect weapon to destroy Existence as he knew it.","But Noah was about to introduce Existence to things that THE Living Paradox had never known.","New Phonemes.","New letters in the language of Existence.","New aspects of The First Tongue that had never been spoken before this moment.","And against these new letters, The Fallout would swing at targets that didn’t exist in its programming.","Its flames would try to burn concepts that weren’t in its fuel.","Its destruction would attempt to unmake things that weren’t on its list.","Noah looked at the Phoneme of Quintessence burning above him, pristine and untouched and perfect.","And he waited for Ruination to deliver the rest!","—","THE Fallout was akin to an unsurpassable and inevitable blade that cut through all of Existence.","But one must never forget that its target was THE Belly of Existence. Its target was THE Creature.","Inside THE Belly of Existence, the protective barriers were torn apart as waves of terrifying multicolored flames descended. They were not similar to the flames that were pervasively spreading outside all of external Existence as they did not seem as potent, but they were there nonetheless.","The flames ate away at the edges of THE Creature’s domain.","In a small region of THE Belly of Existence, the figure of Lumivara bellowed out as her Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty expressed itself in an undeniable fashion. Thirty-six entities with their own Depths stood behind her, roaring in defiance as the entire region they stood in became wrapped in an existential light of paradox.","“WE WILL NOT FALL HERE!” Lumivara’s voice carried the authority of THE Fundamental Depth as her white-blue fox ears blazed with power.","But within the next few moments, all of them disappeared, carried by endless waves of Existence to an unknown location. Their bodies continued to be hounded by the light of THE Fallout as it permeated across their existence, but they were moved nonetheless.","And there were countless others in THE Belly of Existence as what occurred continued to be pervasive. Civilizations that had existed since before differentiation found themselves scattered.","Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms. Those from The Infinite Unfurling.","Powers that had slumbered for eons were forcibly awakened. The sanctum of THE Creature, the place that had been inviolable for far too long, was being torn asunder.","THE Living Paradox’s blade was cutting gloriously deep!"]},{"number":4685,"title":"Chapter 4685: Chapter 4684: THE Fallout! VI","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4684: THE Fallout! VI","Back in that region of collapse.","Well, it actually could not truly be called a region of collapse anymore as this entire place was completely changed and carrying entirely different characteristics compared to before.","The surrounding Existence was covered by motes of gray multicolored allure as Noah faced bombardment all around. And yet for the first time, his existence held a sense of stability that the newly forged Phoneme of Quintessence provided.","It was like his existence was surrounded by countless shields, but only a single colorless shield was currently working.","The light of The Fallout still permeated across his entire existence as...","|An unfathomable and undeniable absolute change has been detected in Existence due to THE Fallout.|","|THE Fallout was undeniably meant to be experienced by every single lifeform in Observable Existence.|","|The Axioms of Observable Existence utilized to enact it have deemed it so.|","|Their set effects are now being branded across Existence.|","|No exceptions. No escapes. No mercy.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes flashed with a sense of alarm as in the next moment, a silent gray light of brilliance bloomed from the countless mushroom clouds of flaming Existence.","This light was a unique one that was not meant to be destructive as much as pervasive.","It was meant to be penetrative, as it permeated through all of Existence dancing on the waves and strings of The First Tongue. They shockingly sought to even enter THE Infiniverse.","And even though THE Infinite Loom and THE Faraday Cage were burning with brilliance, a portion of the light still permeated through. It used Existence and The First Tongue as passages to travel as it washed across THE Infiniverse.","It shockingly did the same to The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature. Anaximander raised his head up in defiance and roared as the gray light passed over him and countless others in the Shore of THE Creature.","THE Living Paradox had been extremely thorough.","THE Living Paradox had planned a great deal.","He truly planned to reshape Existence in an unfathomable manner, using things that Noah had just only recently learned about. The vision of THE Living Paradox became abundantly clear at this time.","As Noah faced these storms and waves of terrifying Weavings of The Fallout, prompts bloomed that allowed the vision of THE Living Paradox to be known at this moment.","|Your Existence has been branded with THE Existential Curse.|","|Curse Designation: THE Existential Ceiling.|","|THE Living Paradox designed The Fallout not just as a weapon of destruction but as a mechanism of control.|","|The curse is woven into the very flames and light of THE Fallout.|","|Effects of THE Existential Ceiling:|","|PRIMARY LIMITATION – THE Absolute Barrier:|","|- All entities affected by The Fallout can never advance beyond THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","|- THE Absolute Depth becomes permanently inaccessible regardless of talent, resources, or time invested.|","|- Attempts to break through to Absolute Depth result in existential backlash that can collapse the entity entirely.|","|SECONDARY LIMITATION – Degraded Advancement Rate:|","|- Rate of cultivation and Way refinement reduced by 70% compared to pre-Fallout standards.|","|- The Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness of one’s Way becomes harder to develop.|","|- What once took centuries now takes millennia.|","|- What once took millennia now takes eons.|","|TERTIARY LIMITATION – Principle Erosion:|","|- Principles invoked or altered by cursed entities slowly degrade over time.|","|- All authority becomes inherently temporary, requiring constant maintenance.|","|- This prevents any cursed entity from building lasting power structures and Civilizations.|","|QUATERNARY LIMITATION – First Tongue Interference:|","|- The eighteen original Phonemes become harder to perceive and utilize.|","|- Logos formation requires 300% more effort and concentration.|","|- Philologies assembled by cursed entities are inherently unstable.|","|- The First Tongue itself seems to resist the touch of the cursed.|","|Markers of the Cursed:|","|- Faint cracks in your existence that glow with residual Fallout energy.|","|- A subtle dimming of your authority’s luminescence.|","|- An almost imperceptible tremor in your Sovereignty when exerted.|","|- The taste of ash that never quite leaves your perception.|","|Exposure Classification: Direct Exposure.|","|Full curse effects. Permanent and absolute.|","|Additional Warning: Unknown and unfathomable Mutations of Existence may bloom as a result of the absolute change and degradation to one’s existence.|","...!","Noah read all these prompts with a sense of rage and coldness building in his chest.","They sought to restrict him?","They sought to block off his path?","WHO DID THEY THINK THEY WERE?!","“OOOH!!!”","He roared with defiance that shook the very fabric of collapsing reality around him, and THE Fallout itself seemingly roared back at him for his defiance as if it were asking...’The fuck are you on about? What are you even going to do about it?! You bum!’","...!","The existential degradation around him became even more intense, as if the curse itself took offense at his refusal to submit.","The markers of the cursed began to unfold on Noah’s skin even as the flames of THE Fallout sought to end him.","Faint cracks appeared across his existence, glowing with the gray-multicolored light of residual Fallout energy. They spread like spiderwebs across his being, each one a reminder of the limitation being branded into his very soul.","His authority’s luminescence dimmed, the brilliant blue-gold of his Mana flickering as if struggling against a suffocating weight.","A tremor ran through his Sovereignty.","And the taste of ash filled his perception, coating everything with the flavor of endings and decay.","The curse was taking hold.","THE Existential Ceiling was being inscribed into his very being.","And at such a point...","BOOM!","He felt an eruption in his existence as warmth flooded through him from nine distinct points of power!","|The 8 other Core Phonemes apart from Quintessence have been forged and presented to you by Ruination.|","|9 new Core Phonemes of The First Tongue have been born.|","|They begin to flow across your existence, unblemished by The Fallout.|","|New Phonemes Registered:|","|- Phoneme of Quintessence: The purest essence of a thing, distilled truth stripped of all excess.|","|- Phoneme of Infinity: The boundless nature that defies limitation and ending.|","|- Phoneme of Tyranny: The absolute authority that demands obedience from reality itself.|","|- Phoneme of Fortune: The manipulation of probability and the guarantee of beneficial outcomes.|","|- Phoneme of Advantage: The systematic exploitation of loopholes in Existence’s rules.|","|- Phoneme of Narrative: The shaping of events to follow the arc of a protagonist’s journey.|","|- Phoneme of Harvest: The gathering of all that can be gathered from all sources.|","|- Phoneme of Hunger: The endless consumption that grows stronger with each devouring.|","|- Phoneme of Potential: The realization of possibilities that have not yet become.|","|These 9 Phonemes are YOUR Phonemes.|","|They did not exist before you.|","|They are immune to The Fallout’s targeted parameters.|","|They are the foundation of your unique existence.|","Noah closed his eyes as The Fallout raged around him.","He felt these nine points of new power. He felt how brilliant they were. He felt the warmth they encompassed all over his existence. He felt them as if they were part of his limbs, an extension of himself that had always been there waiting to be realized.","His existence mourned the curse being branded upon it.","But his existence also rejoiced at the new Phonemes flowing through it.","And he roared out with all his being...","“I WILL NOT BE BOUND BY SUCH A LIMITATION!”","THE Existential Ceiling.","He did not wish to be bound by such a limitation. And yet the capability and the power of THE Fallout was absolute. It was apparently being carried out by multiple Axioms of Observable Existence.","So Existence itself was telling him that he could not change it.","But his core sought to change it.","His innovation and design of brand new Phonemes of The First Tongue sought to change it.","But since it was absolute and could not be changed, another solution had to be found.","And so...","|Your existence is already too strange.|","|Too anomalous.|","|Too filled with infinities that defy normal parameters.|","|Your Infinite Mana seeks to reject the limitation.|","|Your First Tongue seeks to rewrite the degradation, regardless of how absolute it is.|","|An unprecedented possibility has been reached.|","|The basal mutative factor of THE Fallout has been commandeered by the emergence of your nine Core Phonemes of The First Tongue.|","|They do not exist in THE Fallout’s targeted parameters.|","|They were not accounted for in THE Living Paradox’s calculations.|","|They are outside the scope of the Axioms’ programmed effects.|","|Your 9 new Phonemes of The First Tongue are now utilizing the very power of THE Fallout that is backed by the immensity of Axioms of Observable Existence.|","|They are inscribing and allowing the emergence of an absolute anomalous factor.|","|This factor could potentially deny the absolute limitation imposed on you.|","|This factor could give you the best chance of survival in the landscape that will follow THE Fallout.|","|Your existence is undergoing mutation.|","|Emergence of an anomalous factor backed by:|","|- The First Tongue|","|- Your Infinities|","|- THE Fallout itself|","|- The redirected flow of absolutes from Axioms far outside your reach|","|Something unprecedented is emerging.|","HUUM!","|THE Absolute Mutation of THE Existential Paradox Loop is emerging in your existence.|","|Classification: Singular Mutation.|","|Only one instance can exist in Observable Existence.|","|You have been given the distinction of THE Absolute Mutant.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s entire body trembled as if it would shatter at any moment.","But it became even more solid and grander an instant later as an unfathomable thing emerged.","The nine Phonemes that had been flowing through his existence began to weave themselves into a pattern that had never existed before. They danced with the very flames of THE Fallout that sought to destroy him, stealing the Axiom-backed power and redirecting it into the formation of something new.","The cracks of the curse still glowed on his skin.","But now, colorless threads of Quintessence began to weave between them.","The dimming of his authority persisted.","But now, the Phoneme of Infinity pulsed against it, refusing to accept limitation.","The tremor in his Sovereignty remained.","But now, the Phoneme of Tyranny began to stabilize it with absolute authority.","THE Existential Paradox Loop was being born, not despite THE Fallout, but because of THE Fallout!"]},{"number":4686,"title":"Chapter 4686: Chapter 4685: THE Fallout! VII","paragraphs":["Existence was a struggle and Existence was unfair . Noah knew this very well by this point as he did not need anybody to tell him otherwise.","The emergence of an unfathomable anomalous factor, the emergence of this mutation within his existence as a causality, as an effect of THE Fallout , felt like an answer given by his existence against all of this unfairness.","As he was receiving its scope of information, he was realizing the immensity and ridiculousness of it. At this moment, he allowed everything to be put together as his focus was placed on THE Infiniverse.","The light of The Fallout that was backed by unknown Axioms of Observable Existence had proceeded to touch everything.","The curse of THE Existential Ceiling permeated across every single lifeform in Observable Existence.","Well, apart from those sheltered in the safety and cozy allure of THE Loom . That was the design and inherent nature of THE Fallout.","So at this moment, his expression was heavy as when he looked into THE Infiniverse, he saw the figure of his Mother with the marks of the cursed permeating on her body as she raised her hand and saw the faint cracks on them.","He looked at his people as he saw these faint cracks on their bodies, as if they were told from this point on, they would always be lesser. Mutated. That their path across Existence would forever have a ceiling as they could never cross a certain Depth.","Alongside this, some of those within his Civilization had their existence imperceptibly vibrating as they underwent different types of mutations. The Fallout was far too pervasive as their Civilization answered to it and tried to adapt to it by undergoing glorious evolution.","They tried to be like him. Whatever the resultant effects were going to be, it would be much less than what he achieved. But it was still something.","Noah looked at the raging Fallout all around him and roared with immensity, his sound waves mixing with the continuously blooming mushroom clouds as if he was roaring out his defiance toward Existence and the very Fallout itself for what it imposed.","\" OOOH!\"","The roar carried the weight of a being who refused to accept limitation. It carried the fury of someone watching his loved ones be branded with a curse they did not deserve. It carried the defiance of THE Anomaly who would not bow to anyone’s design.","And as his own existence continued to change...","| The First Phase of THE Fallout is ending.|","|The Second Phase is beginning.|","\"...\"","Motherfucker, what?","| This information is being drawn by the emergence of your Core Phonemes of The First Tongue that are not accounted for by THE Fallout.|","|It is now known and understood that THE Fallout is irreversibly altering Existence, Paradox, Chaos, and The First Tongue in phases and sequences absolutely.|","|Your Core Phonemes, your additions to The First Tongue, will be the only things that remain unaffected.|","|The Second Phase of The Fallout involves:|","|- Endless expansion of all zones|","|- Corruption of fundamental existential relationships|","|- Displacement of Existence to forge the landscape of Existence after The Fallout|","|In that landscape:|","|- Distance is meaningless yet impassable|","|- Communication is impossible through any normal Weavings of Existence|","|- Sound is the only thing that can travel|","|- Mental connections will be severed|","|- Thoughts cannot be sent across distances|","|- Perception and awareness will be limited to a few miles even for THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities|","|All Weavings of Existence will be compressed to a singular existence.|","|Even clones of an entity will be returned to the main body.|","|EXCEPTION DETECTED:|","|The defiance of your existence and the unaltered Phonemes of your First Tongue bypass this limitation.|","| At most, you are capable of supporting the emergence and maintenance of two or three bodies.|","|WARNING:|","|If another body remains outside in the landscape of The Fallout as the Second Phase unfolds:|","|- All of your existence could be focused on it|","|- Your connection to THE Infiniverse could be severed or masked|","|- You would not be able to find your way back to it|","|- Teleportation will not be possible|","|- Even quantum movement across distances will not be possible|","|It is advised to return to THE Infiniverse as the Second Phase of The Fallout unfolds and irreversibly changes all of Existence.|","...!","The words were heavy.","Noah’s eyes burned with defiance as he felt like he had won and also lost.","He looked down across the ever-changing landscape of THE Fallout as he felt an imminent countdown that would stop absolutely everything.","And he disappeared.","He returned to THE Infiniverse , into his Early Veiled Shore. The vibrating and the shaking of Existence had stopped as if it was known that imminent destruction had now been weathered and survived.","He stepped on the golden sands and looked at his people whose existence seemed to be undergoing their own imperceptible changes.","And they looked back at him.","A king looked at his family.","An emperor looked at his people.","At this moment, Noah looked like something that had transcended humanity entirely. His body radiated a terrifying, regal, and majestic allure of power. He was adorned in that blue-gold robe shining with his Way and filled with Phonemes of The First Tongue, now adding an additional nine that pulsed with unprecedented authority.","The cracks of the curse spread across his skin like fractured porcelain, but colorless tendrils of Quintessence now flowed through them, weaving between the damage like threads of pure essence refusing to accept the brokenness.","And his eyes.","His eyes had changed most of all.","His pupils now held an image of an endlessly recursive infinite loop, spiraling inward and outward simultaneously. It was hypnotic and terrifying, a visual representation of the mutation that now defined his existence. Looking into those eyes was like staring into a type of Infinity itself.","He looked like a grand ancient primordial emperor instead of a human being.","When he looked at his people, thinking of how he may have failed them, thinking of how they now bore cracks that would never fully heal...","His mother appeared beside him with a smile.","The cracks over her skin were faint but there, glowing with that residual Fallout energy that marked all the cursed. And yet she smiled as if none of it mattered.","\"It seems like the hard part is over,\" Amelia said with serenity that only a mother could possess in such circumstances. \" Let us now be together as we watch the unfolding end of Existence, shall we?\"","The words were serene as they implied success.","Noah’s existence burned as he looked at his Mother and his people. The defiance in his eyes became even more pronounced as barring everything else, they had survived the First Phase of THE Fallout that was focused on lifeforms . They could now wait to see just what immense and unfathomable Weavings of Existence unfold as the Second Phase of THE Fallout targeted all of Existence itself.","He looked at his people, at Sigrid and Khor, at Riya and Adelaide, at his Mother and Henry, at Titano and The Emperor Penguin, at Hyperion and The Great Beyonder, at Moiraine and Barbatos, at all those who had placed their faith in him.","Even the cockroach Little Bobby stood in a corner with a cracked bald round head as he held his daughter close.","He looked at all of them as his voice echoed out.","\" Whatever limitation The Fallout has imposed upon us will be but temporary,\" Noah declared with a voice that carried the weight of absolute conviction. \" Our Weavings of Existence will see glory. They will see Absolute. This I promise to myself, and to you.\"","...!","HUUM!","He said such words to his people as Existence pulsed in turn. The sands of the Early Veiled Shore vibrated as if in agreement, as if the very foundation of his Civilization acknowledged the promise being made.","And he said this without boasting.","Because the details of his emerging anomalous factor became abundantly clear in his mind.","| THE EXISTENTIAL PARADOX LOOP - FULL DOCUMENTATION|","|Classification: Singular Mutation|","|Only one instance can exist in Observable Existence.|","|Status: Emerging within your existence.|","|Designation: THE Absolute Mutant. |","|CORE FUNCTION:|","|You can reset your existence to any previously experienced moment while retaining all memories, knowledge, and cultivation progress from the \"future\" timeline.|","| THE Existential Paradox Loop operates on principles that bend the very nature of causality.|","| ANCHOR POINTS:|","|- You can designate specific moments as \"Anchor Points\" in your existence|","|- These Anchors are moments of significance that your Infinite Mana and your Way infuse with permanence|","|- You can have 9 Anchors active simultaneously across your timeline|","|- Each Anchor requires the infusion of an infinity to establish and maintain|","|- Current Anchors: 0/9|","|THE LOOP MECHANISM:|","|- Upon sensing the potential collapse of your Way and Civilization, or upon voluntary activation, your existence resets to the most recent Anchor Point|","|- All memories from the \"erased\" timeline are retained with perfect clarity|","|- All cultivation progress, including Depth advancement and Way refinement, is retained|","|- Knowledge of enemy capabilities, future events, and strategic information persists across resets|","|THE INFINITY REQUIREMENT:|","|- Each reset consumes one of your infused infinities|","|- Infinities must be woven with Logos and Philologies of your 9 new Core Phonemes to function|","|- Without sufficient infinities infused into the Loop, it fails entirely|","|- Your Infinite Mana allows continuous generation and infusion of new infinities|","|Your new Phonemes are woven into the Loop’s structure:|","|- Phoneme of Quintessence: Anchors the \"essential\" you across all timeline iterations. Ensures your core identity remains intact regardless of how many resets occur.|","|- Phoneme of Infinity: Provides the boundless energy required to sustain the Loop. Ensures the mechanism never runs out of fuel as long as your Mana remains infinite.|","|- Phoneme of Tyranny: Grants absolute authority over the reset process. Ensures no external force can interfere with or prevent a reset once initiated.|","|- Phoneme of Fortune: Influences the outcome of resets toward beneficial results. Increases the likelihood that knowledge gained will lead to favorable outcomes.|","|- Phoneme of Advantage: Identifies loopholes and exploitable patterns across timelines. Allows you to recognize opportunities that others would miss.|","|- Phoneme of Narrative: Shapes the flow of events to favor the protagonist’s journey. Ensures that resets follow a coherent story progression rather than chaotic randomness.|","|- Phoneme of Harvest: Gathers all benefits from erased timelines. Ensures no cultivation progress, insight, or power gained is ever truly lost.|","|- Phoneme of Hunger: Devours the scattered remnants of erased timelines to somewhat fuel future resets. Converts temporal waste into usable energy.|","|- Phoneme of Potential: Realizes possibilities that have not yet become. Allows you to reach outcomes that would otherwise be impossible through normal progression.|","| Because these Phonemes did not exist when The Fallout was designed, the Loop itself is immune to THE Fallout’s interference.|","|LIMITATIONS AND COSTS:|","| MEMORY BURDEN:|","|- Each loop adds the weight of an entire timeline|","|- The weight of all the reversal across Observable Existence must be felt by you|","|- After enough loops, the strain becomes immense|","|- You must maintain your Clarity, Conviction, and Completeness to prevent mental degradation|","|- Failure to maintain Way profundity may result in identity fragmentation|","| CAUSALITY BACKLASH:|","|- Major changes to the timeline create \"resistance\" from Existence itself|","|- The more dramatically you alter events, the harder subsequent alterations become|","|- Some events may be \"fixed points\" that resist change regardless of loops|","|- Attempting to force change on fixed points may consume multiple infinities|","| ANCHOR DEGRADATION:|","|- Anchor Points slowly degrade over extended periods|","|- They must be periodically reinforced with fresh infinities|","|- Losing an Anchor Point means losing the ability to reset to that moment|","|- If all Anchors degrade, the Loop becomes temporarily unusable until new Anchors are established|","| THE PARADOX ACCUMULATION:|","|- Each loop creates subtle paradoxes in the fabric of Existence|","|- Too many loops in quick succession can destabilize local reality|","|- THE Living Paradox , as the embodiment of contradiction, may be able to sense or exploit these paradoxes|","| THE Creature, THE Living Temporal, THE Primordial Chaos, and others of similar power may be able to sense these reversals and retain some memories of the future while understanding that someone is rewinding Observable Existence.|","|- Excessive paradox accumulation may attract unwanted attention from powerful entities|","...!","|Against you, death is not defeat. Death is reconnaissance.|","| This is THE Existential Paradox Loop.|","|This is why THE Absolute Mutant will never truly fall. This was the best possible solution your Existence deemed viable based on what it sensed came with THE Fallout.|","...!","Noah’s gaze was cold and imperious as he looked at all of this information of the emergence of a mutation.","This was the best possible solution that his Existence deemed viable based on what it sensed came with THE Fallout. Basically...his existence thought it may not be able to survive.","So it gave way to the emergence of something that said hey...you may and will likely die, but...not really.","This was the answer to THE Existential Ceiling.","\"...\"","THE Living Paradox had sought to limit all of Existence with THE Existential Ceiling.","And in doing so, he had given Noah the power to transcend limitation entirely!"]},{"number":4687,"title":"Chapter 4687: Chapter 4686: The Cursed And The Blessed I","paragraphs":["THE Existential Paradox Loop.","The sheer incredulity of this alone was unfathomable as Noah looked at it while THE Fallout continued to unfold in its second phase.","It was also a double-edged sword as it looked ridiculously overpowered at first glance. The capability of a do-over, basically. A reset if and when things went wrong.","But if it ever did come to it, while yes, he would keep all his memories of what happened and even retain his power, beings like THE Living Paradox, THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, and especially THE Living Temporal would sense that a reversal had occurred. And they would retain a portion of their memories.","It was basically a boon exclusive for him where he gained tremendous benefits, but truly powerful beings would number one, know that someone was doing something so crazy, and they would also benefit by knowing fractions of events of the future.","\"...\"","Overpowered, yes, but with its own heavy costs and results.","Either way...","\"It is a start.\"","He sighed as he motioned to his people. Among them, he smiled toward the Bard of Quintessence in his radiant simian visage filled with white-gold hair.","It was the end of the world. The end of Existence. With them surviving it and at the cost they paid for it...","\" Let us have music and a feast to commemorate the survival of the end that hung like a blade for so long over us,\" Noah declared with a voice that carried across the golden sands. \" Let us have a festival. THE Festival of... The End.\"","HUUM!","His words were ridiculous, but what were they to do? Sit around sulking and sad? He controlled his own Weavings as he would rather do something else entirely.","And so the Bard of Quintessence smiled and floated over.","The markers of the cursed were visible on his simian form, faint cracks glowing with residual Fallout energy that traced along his golden fur like rivers of ash. His luminescence had dimmed ever so slightly, and there was an almost imperceptible tremor in his existence when he moved. But his smile remained brilliant and defiant as an illusory gold guitar appeared in his hands, and a melody began to resound across the Early Veiled Shore.","Behind Noah, the massive THE Cooking Stanchion of Infinity manifested in all its culinary glory, a pillar of gastronomic authority that pulsed with blue-gold light and the promise of impossible dishes.","He looked at it and said with determination, \" Today, I shall cook the very residual authority of THE Fallout and Primus Mana into food for consumption. We shall not wallow, so let us enjoy. Give a middle finger to THE Living Paradox and his machinations.\"","...!","OOOH!","His people roared out with fervor even amidst a rotating and ongoing apocalypse swirling outside THE Infiniverse . A moment later, the flipper of an Emperor Penguin that held markers of the curse raised up in earnest confusion as he called out, \"But Master, I don’t have a middle finger to give!\"","\"...\"","Noah turned toward The Emperor Penguin with a sharp gaze, and this penguin put its flipper down fearfully as the melody of the Bard of Quintessence began to permeate outward.","As it did, as THE Festival of The End was kicked off, a symphony bloomed from within Noah himself. His Stanchions of Infinity pulsed as another melody began to spread across THE Infiniverse, weaving together with the Bard’s guitar into something hauntingly beautiful.","A voice emerged, feminine and aching, carried by the Phonemes of Narrative and Quintessence:","\"We built our homes on borrowed time,","And called the wreckage yours and mine.","The cracks are showing, can’t you see?","But broken’s where we’re meant to be.","Hold on, hold on, don’t let me go,","Through the fire and the afterglow.","We’re all just strangers passing through,","But strangers, darling, can be true.","The ending came, we watched it fall,","And found we’re standing after all.","So raise a glass to what we’ve lost,","We paid the price, we know the cost.","Hold on, hold on, the night is long,","But we’ll keep singing our broken song.","When morning comes, if morning comes,","We’ll still be here, we’ll still be one.","They said the world would burn away,","And here we are at break of day.","With scars that glow and hearts that ache,","But still alive, for our own sake.","So hold on, hold on, through the pain,","We’ll find our way back home again.","The end has come and the end has gone,","And somehow, somehow... we live on.\"","The symphony echoed across THE Infiniverse as the somber melody touched every soul within its bounds. Those with the markers of the cursed felt their cracks pulse gently with the music, not with pain but with acknowledgment. With belonging.","As the symphony and words echoed out, Noah began cooking Mana and the residual energy of THE Fallout into physical foods. The blue-gold flames of his culinary authority danced as he worked, transmuting apocalyptic devastation into sustenance that would nourish both body and soul.","While his hands moved with practiced efficiency, he said silently through his connection with Ruination, ’ Set up the first Anchor Point.’","|I’ve already begun preparing it, Master. The fuel for the Anchor has to be Infinities woven with Logos and Philologies of your 9 new Core Phonemes to function. Without sufficient infinities infused into the Loop, it fails entirely. So we have to form brand new Logos and Philologies as it may take some time.|","Ruination said such words to him as he nodded before he replied, ’ Integrate Quintessence or Infinity into currently existing Philologies we have. Undifferentiated Mana and Cheating Architect would be easy, and their capabilities would also be enhanced. This will be faster for us to get an Anchor Point set up as soon as possible.’","...!","|Understood, Master.|","Ruination got started on a glorious process as while Noah oversaw the start of a feast, he kept his gaze on the unfolding second phase of THE Fallout as it was heavy.","Existence seemed like it was being ground down, spat up, and changed tremendously as the information he obtained through the establishment of the 9 new Core Phonemes of The First Tongue were beginning to unfold.","He couldn’t see past one mile outside THE Infiniverse.","And as the symphony and melody of his festival came out of THE Infiniverse and flowed outside toward the regions under the effects of THE Fallout...","BZZT!","His symphony and melody shockingly fizzled outside as if Existence told it, \" Get that shit out of here!\"","...!","\"...\"","Communication would not be possible.","Mental connections would not be possible.","Teleportation would not be possible.","He had hoped that he would be able to reunite with Lumivara and Ul’Moreth and others after THE Fallout to truly reap the rewards, but he wouldn’t even be able to sense them or try to send a message to them through their entanglement.","Man, Riya had been right when she said Mana would be undergoing lots of adversity.","The aftermath of THE Fallout would not make things easy!","As he thought about all this, he wondered.","How were Eckert and Alexander faring? How were THE Creature and beings like THE Primordial Chaos faring at a time like this?","And the fuckers inside THE Loom ... what were they getting out of Existence being razed down?"]},{"number":4688,"title":"Chapter 4688: Chapter 4687: The Cursed And The Blessed II","paragraphs":["Inside THE Loom.","While apocalyptic horrors raged outside...","Ambessa uncomfortably pulled on the collar of the obsidian-gold suit she was forced to wear by the forces of THE Living Elemental as she moved from one section of THE Loom to another.","Around her were a few Pre-THE and False THE entities who were surrounded with vibrant golden lights as shockingly, their Sovereignties were being elevated. They naturally and forcefully had their Depths taken to THE Surface Depth in a process that should have taken eons but was being accomplished in mere moments.","It truly fucking paid to be in THE Loom as while it razed down Existence, everything devoured was being swallowed up by it and distributed to a specific few.","But did they really need these ridiculous suits?","Ambessa would rather be wearing her bloomers and something free, not this full body coverage bullshit that constricted her movements and made her feel like a decorated puppet on display. The obsidian-gold fabric clung to every curve and left no room for comfort, designed more for presentation than practicality.","\" Can you fucking relax? It is Liberation Day, and we have been chosen.\"","The words came sharp and cold from ahead of her.","\" You’ll be standing in front of THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive soon as they prepare us for the emergence to the outside Existence once THE Fallout is done. We have been chosen. Show that fucking graciousness. You see that Depth of Paradox building inside you? That is eons of work erupting today, and it is not your own. Come on.\"","...!","The words came from a golden-haired Early Creature burning with a light of Elemental who was looking at Ambessa with cold eyes. A THE Surface Depth Elemental Early Creature who had already been given a high-sounding title that didn’t matter to shit to Ambessa what it was. Something like \"Vanguard of the Elemental Emergence\" or some equally pompous nonsense.","Ambessa glared back while following as she thought about how she had gotten here.","About how another one of her Avatars had been decimated while she had gone to seek the forces of Noah Osmont.","And because of that name, because of Osmont, she was chosen among those to receive the bigger boons of THE Loom during THE Fallout. She was having her Depth built regardless of how tough it was to go from False THE to actual THE.","All because of the little connection she had with Osmont.","Frankly, couldn’t they leave him alone? He was probably dead from THE Fallout anyways. The flames that were consuming Existence outside were not something that could be easily survived, and from what she last saw as her Avatar fully perished, Osmont had been outside when it all began.","Why did THE Living Elemental have such a grudge against him to be forming a task force of THEs that would be looking for Osmont after THE Fallout?","It seemed excessive. It seemed obsessive. It seemed like a waste of resources that could be better spent elsewhere.","But no one asked for her opinion, and she was smart enough not to offer it.","Ahead of her, the chirpy Elemental Early Creature smiled as they entered a domain filled with rivers of fire and water mixing beautifully. The elements intertwined in impossible harmony, flames dancing with currents and steam rising in artistic spirals that painted the air with prismatic light.","\" Soon, we will meet with THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive themselves ,\" the golden-haired creature announced with barely contained excitement. \" They will give us our directives for how to move outside THE Loom for the first time into an Existence with conditions that will not be habitable for most. We are the explorers of a changed Existence from this Shelter of THE Loom. We are the pioneers who will chart the new landscape while others cower and hide.\"","Her eyes blazed with fervor.","\" The outside Existence has been fundamentally altered. Distance means nothing and everything simultaneously. Communication through normal means is impossible. Perception is limited even for those at THE Fundamental Depth. It is a hostile, broken landscape that will swallow the unprepared whole.\"","She turned to face the group with a smile that held both pride and anticipation.","\" But we have been given the tools to survive it. We have been given the authority to thrive in it. We are uncursed. We bear no Existential Ceiling. While every other being in Observable Existence has been branded with limitation, we emerge from THE Loom as the elite. As the chosen. As the inheritors of whatever remains.\"","Her voice rose with passion.","\" We will see glory! We will claim territories that others cannot even perceive! We will establish the dominion of THE Loom across the shattered remnants of Observable Existence! This is Liberation Day, and we are the liberated! Rejoice!\"","...!","Ambessa frowned at the words and sighed internally.","Right.","It was Liberation Day. THE Fallout. Those within THE Loom gained an interminable amount while the outside Existence burned. And THE Loom had already separated into multiple Shelters that would flow across Existence. When THE Fallout ended, they could observe and explore the changed inhabitable Existence while maintaining their rule from different bastions of protection.","Ambessa knew she was just a cog in the machine, and she was just fucking tired .","She didn’t want to keep chasing after this Osmont as every time, she kept fucking dying. Why didn’t the rest of them get the hint? Every encounter with that man ended with her Avatars being obliterated, her plans being thwarted, and her existence being put through unnecessary trauma.","But the higher-ups seemed to think her repeated failures made her an expert on the subject. As if dying to someone multiple times qualified you to hunt them down successfully.","The logic escaped her entirely.","But...","Ambessa raised her head and looked up, seeing waves of auroras descending down from the crystalline ceiling of this domain. They wrapped around her and elevated her power with warmth that felt almost nurturing despite its artificial nature. Other waves spread to different parts of THE Loom, reaching chosen individuals across the vast structure.","She could feel her Depth solidifying, the False THE designation she had carried for so long finally giving way to genuine THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty. It was a gift that most beings would kill for, a boon that represented eons of cultivation being compressed into moments.","And yet, all she could think about was the price she would have to pay for it."]},{"number":4689,"title":"Chapter 4689: Chapter 4688: The Cursed And The Blessed III","paragraphs":["Moments later, Ambessa found they were arriving at their location as she sensed other entities entering a crystalline bejeweled crimson-blue domain filled with water and fire. The elements here were even more intense, more primal, as if approaching the source of all elemental authority.","Within it, the overpowering aura of THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive could be felt pressing down on everyone present.","THE Living Elemental radiated waves of pure elemental might that made the fire and water bow in reverence. Their presence was a mountain made of storms, an ocean made of flames, an existence that had claimed dominion over the fundamental building blocks of reality itself.","And THE Living Emotive , that entity pulsed with emotions so vast and contradictory that merely being near them made Ambessa want to laugh and cry and scream all at once. Joy and sorrow, rage and peace, love and hatred, all swirling together in a maelstrom of feeling that threatened to overwhelm anyone without sufficient mental fortitude.","Ambessa sighed while going in as she wanted to get this shit over with.","THE Loom had erupted as those within it benefitted, and when the dust settled, they would go out from different Shelters to reap the altered Existence.","She just really hoped she wouldn’t come across Osmont again, and even hoped she would stop being included in the hunting teams formed for him just because she was among the first to come in contact with him.","But deep down, she knew better.","Existence had a sick sense of humor.","And somehow, someway, she would probably end up dying to Noah Osmont again.","It was just her fucking luck.","—","In the depths of that domain where Ambessa and others were being drawn into.","The domain of water and fire stretched endlessly in all directions, a realm where the two opposing elements had been forced into coexistence by the sheer authority of THE Living Elemental . Rivers of molten flame cascaded upward while waterfalls of crystalline blue flowed sideways, each element weaving around the other in patterns that should have been impossible but existed nonetheless.","At the very heart of this domain, where the concentration of elemental authority reached its peak, a single massive elemental throne existed. It was forged from solidified fire and frozen water, crimson and azure intertwining in a seat of power that radiated waves of primal might. The throne pulsed with the heartbeat of elements themselves, each pulse sending ripples of fire and water across the surrounding space.","Currently, the languid figure of THE Living Emotive was lying horizontally on this throne in a laid-back manner, her legs dangling over one armrest while her head rested on the other. She looked utterly at ease despite the apocalypse raging outside THE Loom , as if the destruction of Observable Existence was merely background noise to whatever tune played inside her mind.","In front of her, THE Living Elemental was surrounded by blazing crimson flames that danced with fury and frustration. Eighteen Phonemes of The First Tongue surrounded him in a rotating formation, each one flickering with instability that had not been there before THE Fallout began.","His gaze was fiery and troubled at this time as he spoke with barely contained agitation.","\" Are you really so carefree? \" he demanded. \" The First Tongue no longer feels the same, and this is not a result of THE Fallout. Something has changed at its fundamental level. Something has been added that should not exist.\"","...!","His words went to Emotive who seemed to barely be listening as she whistled and hummed to herself, her fingers tracing lazy patterns in the air.","\" THE Loom has bloomed and existence will spin,","The fun begins where the chaos sets in,","Round and round the pieces will go,","Where they land, only Paradox knows...\"","As she finished this little melody, Elemental looked at her with an almost angry gaze. Before he could say anything, she cut him off with a dismissive wave.","\" Don’t fucking worry so much, big guy,\" Emotive said with a yawn. \" The fun is just now beginning. Paradox has so much work to do that he designed THE Loom into different components that would scatter across Existence. You and I are in one Shelter. Which, you should be fucking ecstatic about as you get to have my presence here. But as the dust settles, we can really get to have our fun. Because I know some things...\"","Oh?","Elemental raised his brows as he focused on her, his flames calming slightly with curiosity.","Emotive smiled devilishly as she waved her hand and conjured an illusory image that materialized between them. It was the image of Noah Osmont , rendered in perfect detail with his blue-gold authority radiating even through the illusion.","The image that Elemental flared up to immediately.","This was the one who had encroached upon his Civilization. This was the one who had humiliated him. This was the one who had taken what was his.","\" This big guy here is apparently centermost for all you guys ,\" Emotive said with manic delight, sitting up slightly to better observe Elemental’s reaction. \" You want him, Paradox wants him, even THE Primordial Chaos talked about him. Apparently, he is the one to have laid a claim to The First Tongue. So it makes sense what he was able to do against you. But man, look at him.\"","She leaned forward, her eyes gleaming with something between fascination and hunger.","\" He looks like he has that presence, doesn’t he? That je ne sais quoi. He almost reminds me of...THE Creature.\"","...!","Her words were manic and taunting as she gazed toward the image of Noah in a fervent light. Elemental frowned heavily, his flames darkening with barely suppressed rage.","He looked over at Noah’s illusory figure silently, studying the entity who had become such a thorn in his existence. Meanwhile, Emotive twirled around the throne casually before she sighed with theatrical disappointment.","\" Out of all those that have made the claim on The Oldest Paradox of Existence, he is the youngest,\" she mused. \" The most ripe. If I can get my hands on him and keep him away from Paradox and others, that would be ideal.\"","Elemental’s reply came cold and absolute.","\" The only fate for him is collapse, \" he declared, his voice carrying the weight of elemental authority. \" All the others will go for him, and after THE Fallout settles, I will also go for him. I do not underestimate any of those making a claim on The Oldest Paradox of Existence. If one has begun to encroach on my Civilization, even more so. He took from me. He will return what he took with interest, and then he will cease to exist.\"","...!"]},{"number":4690,"title":"Chapter 4690: Chapter 4689: The Cursed And The Blessed IV","paragraphs":["Emotive laughed, the sound echoing across the domain like wind chimes made of broken glass.","\" Good luck finding him in the Wastes of THE Fallout,\" she said with genuine amusement. \"You and others really don’t know how it’s truly going to be out there. But no, you can do whatever you want, and I will do whatever I want.\"","She pointed at Noah’s illusory image with possessive intensity.","\" For this guy, he laid the claim on The First Tongue, so I shall lay a claim on him. I’ve always wanted to raise a dog. THE Creature and others are too big as they would eat me up, but this Osmont...\"","Her eyes widened with manic desire.","\" Ahh, I want him. I want him!\"","...!","Her eyes radiated a manic light as she said this, and in the next moment, she waved her hand to pull out something that made the entire domain tremble!","A teardrop.","A single crystalline teardrop that emanated wild power so profound that even the elements themselves seemed to bow before it. The moment it appeared, Elemental showed a shocked expression as he pointed a finger at it.","\" How did you get that?!\"","His voice cracked with disbelief, his composure shattering for just an instant.","Emotive looked over calmly, rolling the teardrop between her fingers with casual indifference.","\" Oh relax, it’s just a Fragment of an Axiom,\" she said dismissively. \" See, this is why you can’t be like THE Creature and Paradox, and even this Osmont. Where is your fucking composure? Your je ne sais quoi? You don’t make me feel a thing because of how you act, man. It’s abysmal.\"","She held up the Fragment, letting its light play across her features.","\" But no, I told you I have a plan, and it involves this. Navigating the Wastelands, the Corrupted Existence after THE Fallout, will be impossible through normal means. But Axioms will make many things possible. This is something I can use to track what makes my heart flutter.\"","Her smile turned sharp.","\" And I know it’s not fucking you, so at this time it will be Osmont. I do hope it doesn’t lead me to THE Creature as he will likely rip me apart right then and there... ah.\"","...!","Her manic light became even grander as a darkened, cloudy expression settled on Elemental’s face after her words.","She seemed to be very set on playing with the emotions of others and making them feel lesser. It was her Way, after all. THE Living Emotive existed to evoke and manipulate feelings, and she wielded that power even against her supposed allies.","Elemental spoke with a voice that rumbled like tectonic plates grinding against each other.","\" You can continue trying to crush my will by comparisons, but it is ultimately a waste of time, \" he declared with cold certainty. \" My Way is firm. Games of manipulation will not work on me. I do not compare myself to THE Creature or any others as I have my own immensity. I am THE Living Elemental. I am the authority over Phonemes of Fire and Water and Earth and Air and everything in between. Your words are wind against my mountain.\"","Emotive rose up and actually sat properly on the elemental throne, crossing her legs as she twirled the Fragment of an Axiom in her hands. She looked over at Elemental with an expression that held pity and contempt in equal measure.","\" You are one of the beings I least respect,\" she said with brutal honesty. \" You had so much potential, so many possibilities, and look at you. Stuck. Stagnant. Mediocre despite your Depth.\"","She leaned forward, her eyes boring into him.","\"If you want to prove me wrong, I will actually bring you with me when I find Osmont. I will. And do you know what I think will happen?\"","Her smile turned cruel.","\" Somehow, he will be standing right there before you, and you still won’t be able to achieve what you want. You see, that is just how it is for some beings in Existence. They do everything, but never amount to much.\"","She sighed wistfully.","\" THE Creature, oh, he amounts to much. I miss him even now. Paradox? He’s up there. This Osmont? He fucking laid a claim on The First Tongue that nobody has been able to do, so I’m sure he’s up there.\"","Her eyes met Elemental’s with piercing intensity.","\"I will literally put him in front of you, and you likely still won’t get what you want. It’s like you’re so bad that Existence itself doesn’t want you winning. So after you fail, I will then make my move. How does that sound, big guy?\"","...!","Her words were truly poisonous and detestable to hear, but her eyes held a terrifying light that very few understood. She was not merely taunting him. She was speaking what she believed to be absolute truth. In her eyes, Elemental was simply not destined for greatness, and no amount of effort would change that fundamental reality.","Elemental looked at her coldly in an imposing demeanor, his flames condensing around him like armor made of pure destruction. The Phonemes of The First Tongue surrounding him blazed brighter as if responding to his fury.","Moments later, Emotive showed a bored expression as she lay back on the elemental throne, her body language dismissing everything he was projecting.","\" Eeh, even your imposing glare doesn’t get me excited ,\" she complained with theatrical disappointment. \" Man, I can’t wait to track down Osmont. Maybe he will make me feel something, unlike being near a black hole of boring Weavings like you.\"","She closed her eyes, the Fragment of an Axiom still dancing between her fingers.","\" Just wait for the second phase of THE Fallout to finish. Then the real fun begins. Then I get to see if this Osmont lives up to the hype. And you?\"","She cracked one eye open to look at him.","\" You get to watch and fail. As usual.\"","The domain of water and fire trembled with Elemental’s suppressed rage, but he said nothing more.","Outside THE Loom, THE Fallout continued its second phase, reshaping Observable Existence into something unrecognizable.","And inside, two ancient powers waited with very different anticipations.","One waited to destroy.","One waited to claim.","And somewhere out there, completely unaware of the attention being directed at him, Noah Osmont was hosting a festival to celebrate surviving the end of Existence!"]},{"number":4691,"title":"Chapter 4691: Chapter 4690: The Cursed And The Blessed V","paragraphs":["In Existence, there would always be the rich and the poor, the sad and the happy, and the blessed and the cursed.","THE Fallout made very clear distinctions of which was which.","But as THE Fallout unfolded, there were some beings who had the power to choose for themselves whether they would be cursed or blessed.","In a far, indeterminate corner of Observable Existence burning and twisting under the light of THE Fallout, a humanoid entity floated grandly while waves of multicolored flames and ash passed through everything around him.","This entity was covered with undulating obsidian tendrils of chaos that writhed across his form like living shadows hungry for disorder. His sheer aura alone shockingly kept the flames of The Fallout at bay, creating an invisible field around his existence that the apocalyptic destruction could not penetrate without permission.","And he did grant permission routinely.","He would open up a singularity in the invisible field that he had around him, a small gap that allowed concentrated Weavings of The Fallout to flow through and permeate into his existence. Each time, the multicolored flames would rush in eagerly, only to be devoured by the obsidian tendrils and converted into something else entirely. He was not merely surviving The Fallout. He was consuming it. Digesting it. Making it part of his Chaos.","Around his existence, one could see an indeterminate amount of Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue floating in complex orbits. What looked to be more than eighteen Genesis Principles rotated around him like children listening to his beck and call, responding to his every whim with eager obedience.","But uniquely, there were even three types of authorities that even the Genesis Principles seemed to actively avoid.","Three points of power so profound, so ancient, so terrifying that even the fundamental truths of The First Tongue gave them wide berth.","Such a being was humming freely in the midst of The Fallout as he looked around with his gaze piercing many things, even though he realized it was gradually becoming limited by the changing Weavings of Existence.","At such a point, he opened his mouth as seas of Primordial Chaos spilled out naturally with his words.","\" Eenie meenie miny moe, where exactly shall I go?\"","...!","As if he was looking for direction in the midst of universal devastation.","He sighed, the sound carrying the weight of eons of accumulated experience and the lightness of someone who found cosmic destruction mildly entertaining.","\" Observable Existence had only been explored and mapped out by less than half of what it truly contains, \" he mused to himself, his voice resonating with the authority of THE Primordial Chaos. \"All of us know that other Pockets of Existence like Ginnungagap exist but remain unable to be accessed through normal means. We know of regions that predate differentiation itself. We know of spaces between spaces where even I have not ventured.\"","His obsidian tendrils writhed with amusement.","\" We know all of this, and yet you proceed to change all of Observable Existence while we still know there is much we don’t know? All those unknowns, all those unexplored territories, all those sleeping powers in hidden corners of reality, how will they be affected by your little tantrum, Paradox?\"","He laughed, the sound causing nearby flames of The Fallout to scatter in confusion.","\" What will arise from them? What ancient things will be awakened? What new horrors will be born from the collision of your Fallout and the unknown? Haha, so much Chaos to unfold. So much to witness! You may have designed this cataclysm, but you cannot possibly have accounted for everything. Nobody can account for everything. That is why Chaos always wins in the end.\"","At such a time, he laughed freely and looked around him as if he could see something that others could not. His gaze pierced through the layers of burning reality, through the Weavings of The Fallout, through the very fabric of Existence itself.","In the next moment, he spoke to the devastation around him.","\" O Creature, you should be free enough right now to at least hear me and communicate before everything becomes much harder. The Fallout is targeting you, yes, but it is also weakening the chains that bind you. So tell me, old friend, old enemy, old enigma, how do you think all of this will end?\"","He asked the burning Existence around him.","As if he expected an answer.","As if someone could hear him across the vastness of collapsing reality.","And shockingly, in the next moment, Existence trembled and buzzed fearfully as an extremely deep and imposing voice responded from everywhere and nowhere simultaneously.","\" Badly.\"","HUUM!","Oh!","That voice!","It was filled with calmness so absolute that it made the chaos of The Fallout seem like a child’s tantrum. It carried an immensity that pressed down on reality itself, making even THE Primordial Chaos feel the weight of something truly ancient. It was the voice of the being who had shaped Observable Existence, who had created the foundations upon which all civilizations were built, who had been imprisoned for eons but never truly defeated.","And as if it did not get its point across enough, it echoed out once more for THE Primordial Chaos to hear.","\" Very, very badly.\"","...!","THE Primordial Chaos laughed loudly at these words, the sound erupting from him like a symphony of disorder that made the surrounding Fallout flames dance in chaotic patterns.","His eyes opened wide, showing obsidian blackness all around. Within that darkness, infinite obsidian snakes constantly twisted and coiled, each one a fragment of primordial entropy given form. They burned with glory that predated the differentiation of Existence itself.","\" You let Paradox reign on top for so long that many of us missed you,\" THE Primordial Chaos said with genuine warmth beneath his chaotic exterior. \" Your absence left a void that none of us could properly fill. But do tell, O Creature, have you grasped The Second Scale of Existence without telling the rest of us? Are you there yet?\"","Was he there yet.","It was a terrifying question to ask.","The Second Scale of Existence.","Beyond THE Absolute Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","Beyond anything that currently existed in Observable Existence.","The level that THE Living Paradox sought to reach through The Fallout.","The level that would allow an entity to not just legislate reality but to become indistinguishable from it.","The reply from THE Creature came with maddening ambiguity.","\" Who knows... who knows...\"","BOOM!","The words carried neither confirmation nor denial, only the weight of something that preferred to remain mysterious. THE Creature had always been an enigma, even to those who had existed alongside him since the earliest moments of Observable Existence.","THE Primordial Chaos smiled at the non-answer, his obsidian snakes hissing with appreciation for the chaos of uncertainty.","\" Same as always ,\" he muttered fondly. \" Never giving a straight answer. Never letting anyone know exactly where you stand. I suppose that is how you survived this long, O Creature. By being unknowable even to those who thought they knew you.\"","The burning Existence around him offered no further response.","THE Creature had spoken his piece.","And now, THE Primordial Chaos was left to navigate The Fallout alone, choosing his direction in a landscape that was rapidly becoming unrecognizable.","\" Eenie meenie miny moe ,\" he repeated with a grin. \"I suppose I’ll just follow the Chaos. It has never led me astray before.\"","He opened another singularity in his protective field, allowing more of The Fallout to rush in and be consumed by his endless hunger for disorder!"]},{"number":4692,"title":"Chapter 4692: Chapter 4691: The Emerged I","paragraphs":["Inside a Shelter of THE Loom.","A domain of cylindrical tall mountain-like pillars stretched endlessly in all directions, each one rising toward a ceiling that did not exist. Multicolored rivers of clouds flowed between these pillars like lazy serpents, carrying whispers of power that had been accumulated over eons of careful planning.","On one tall pillar, immense waves of authority were flowing into a single entity. His hair currently shone stellar gold with unfathomably radiant multicolored pupils that seemed to contain folds within their depths. His stature was that of a human, yet he felt like a giant whose presence alone could crush lesser beings into oblivion.","Near him were three shrouded female figures that were none other than THE Weavers.","Their faces could not be discernible as they looked like black holes that would devour everything, pulling in light and perception alike until nothing remained but the void of their presence. Their bodies seemed to be channeling a unique power through THE Loom and into the titan of a man before them.","He was none other than Gilgamesh .","A Leader among Leaders.","A glorious entity that had thrown his Curiosity all the way from the Earliest Folds to attack Noah in the current era. A being whose ambition stretched across time itself!","And at this moment, an air of THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty surged around him. His gaze was deep and filled with an unfathomable light that spoke of power recently gained and power yet to be fully understood. The authority flowing into him was settling into his existence like water finding its level, reshaping him from within.","\" You hold the most potent Weavings of THE Creature as Paradox has raised you to THE Fundamental Depth,\" THE Weavers spoke in unison, their voices overlapping in a way that made it impossible to distinguish one from another. \" How does it feel?\"","Gilgamesh’s multicolored pupils flickered as he considered the question.","\"It feels like I am being controlled ,\" he replied with cold honesty. \" And I don’t particularly like that.\"","THE Weavers laughed, the sound ancient and knowing, as if they had heard such complaints countless times across the eons.","\" Understandable ,\" they said together. \" But Existence is a game of give and take. We give you what you want, and you do something for us in turn. This arrangement has existed since before THE Loom was conceived. You are not the first to chafe at it, and you will not be the last.\"","Their shrouded forms shifted slightly, black hole faces turning toward him with what might have been amusement.","\" This time around, the mission placed on you will be this man.\"","THE Weavers waved their hands in unison, and an illusory image materialized between them. It was Noah Osmont , rendered in perfect detail with his blue-gold authority radiating even through the projection.","Gilgamesh looked at the image calmly, his expression betraying nothing of his thoughts. He studied every detail with the patience of someone who had existed since the Earliest Folds, who had seen empires rise and fall, who knew that rushing to judgment was the mistake of the young.","\" He will be hunted by weak things at THE Surface Depth, but THE Esteemed Paradox wanted someone decent to track him,\" THE Weavers continued. \" You and we have this task. The others are distractions, noise, insects buzzing around a flame. We are the true hunters. And you are the one meant to bring this hunt to its conclusion.\"","...!","When they spoke, the voices of THE Weavers came out simultaneously, three voices becoming one in a manner that was extremely eerie. It was as if they shared a single consciousness split across three bodies, or perhaps three consciousnesses merged into a single will.","And yet toward these words, Gilgamesh remained calm as he asked a simple question.","\" Any preference on whether he needs to be brought in alive or collapsed?\"","...!","The question was heavy, carrying implications that stretched far beyond its simple phrasing. Bringing Noah in alive would mean one thing. Collapsing him would mean another entirely.","THE Weavers laughed again, the sound carrying genuine amusement this time.","\"If you can fully collapse him, it would mean you stand the chance to lay a claim on The First Tongue,\" they said with voices dripping with temptation. \" You can give it a go.\"","...!","The eyes of Gilgamesh pulsed with a terrifying immensity at such words.","The First Tongue.","The language of Existence itself.","If he could collapse the one who had laid claim to it, if he could destroy Noah Osmont utterly and completely, there was a chance, however slim, that he could inherit that claim for himself.","It was a prize worth any risk.","But a moment later, he nodded with the composure of someone who planned thoroughly before acting.","\"I will need my Legions of THE Early Creatures,\" he stated. \" Make sure to tell the big guy to send harvest their way to ensure their Depths are at least at Surface, maybe Intermediate.\"","...!","Even more terrifying words were uttered.","Legions.","Not a handful of powerful entities. Not a small strike force. Legions of THE Early Creatures, beings from the Earliest Folds who had followed Gilgamesh across eons, all of them elevated to THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty at minimum.","It was an army meant to crush, not to hunt.","Toward this, THE Weavers smiled behind their black hole faces.","\" That much can be done ,\" they affirmed. \" THE Esteemed Paradox has resources to spare from THE Fallout’s harvest. Your Legions will be elevated. Your hunt will be properly supported.\"","...!","---","Across Existence, many made their preparations as THE Fallout was underway.","An interminable light struck out against THE Belly of Existence , tearing through barriers that had stood since before recorded history. The attack was relentless, absolute, backed by Axioms of Observable Existence that made resistance nearly futile.","THE Prison of THE Creature was torn open as the many entities within it that he had been siphoning from for eons flooded out into the burning landscape of THE Fallout. Ancient powers that had been captive for longer than most civilizations had existed now found themselves free but cursed, blessed with liberation but branded with THE Existential Ceiling.","Ginnungagap became opened once more as for the first time in eons, Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms would appear in the changing Observable Existence . These twisted beings, born from the chaotic energies of that primordial realm, spilled into an Existence that had almost forgotten they existed.","What used to be the Infinite Unfurling was unlocked as all the Sovereignties within it flared out. Every single one was affected one way or another by the light of THE Fallout, some gaining mutations that would define their future, others simply bearing the curse that limited their advancement forever.","THE Living Paradox officially started his War with THE Creature, and it would not end in an instant.","It would be a long war as the victor was undecided.","Or maybe, the victor was already known, but Existence merely held its breath, waiting to see if fate would unfold as expected or if something unexpected would tip the scales.","As countless wonders unfolded, time passed.","The Second Phase of THE Fallout continued as THE Infiniverse stood strong against the apocalyptic devastation. Its barriers held firm, powered by Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue that were regenerated as fast as they were destroyed.","The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature was surrounded by a unique protective light as it stood strong, sheltering the countless lifeforms that Anaximander had drawn into its sanctuary.","And everything drew toward a conclusion as with the distortion of what THE Fallout was doing to Existence, some areas may have already experienced the passage of years while in others barely a second had passed. Time itself had become inconsistent, unreliable, subject to the whims of the catastrophe that was reshaping all of reality.","But the first shot had been taken.","A belly was spilled open.","A blade had been drawn.","And now, all that waited was to discover just how much blood had spilled, and how much more blood would spill before the dust finally settled!"]},{"number":4693,"title":"Chapter 4693: Chapter 4692: The Emerged II","paragraphs":["Others could fail. Others could have doubts. Others could be unsure.","Noah knew with utmost certainty that he was not one of them.","Even though he absolutely did not know how everything would unfold after THE Fallout, he had to approach it with the mindset that regardless of what happened, he would persevere through it and survive.","He truly did not have the choice because for him, failure was critical.","It was why right now, he had set up an Anchor Point.","He looked at the glowing words that detailed exactly how it looked like.","|ANCHOR POINT ESTABLISHED|","| Designation: Anchor Point One - THE Festival of The End|","|Location: Early Veiled Shore within THE Infiniverse|","|Timestamp: 1 hour, 17 minutes after First Phase of THE Fallout concluded|","|Status: Active and stable|","|Infinity Fuel: Fully infused with a few Logos and Philologies including some of the 9 Core Phonemes|","|Reset Capability: Upon sensing potential collapse of Way and Civilization, or upon voluntary activation, existence will reset to this moment|","|Retention: All memories, cultivation progress, and knowledge from erased timeline will be preserved|","|Remaining Anchor Slots: 8/9|","This Anchor Point acted like an assurance that he could go back to in the case that things went wrong.","And with how it emerged and what THE Fallout promised, it was very much foreshadowing that things would be going wrong. He was not looking forward to this.","But again, he could not hold any doubt as he had to always move with quintessential certainty.","And so at this moment, while THE Festival of The End continued all around him, Noah observed his surroundings with contemplative calm.","As he looked at his people whose skins were cracked with the marks of those cursed, destined to never even get near THE Absolute Depth , he remained calm. They were currently eating and drinking even while an apocalypse raged all around them.","It was a scene he would protect over and over again if he had to.","He wondered at this time if this Anchor Point that he had set, if he would actually be coming back here sometime in the future. If circumstances would force him to reset, to return to this moment and try again with the knowledge of what went wrong.","He shook his head at the thoughts as he got back to the current situation at hand.","One of the biggest things was his own existence, of course, and the changes that it had undergone in the last hour as THE Fallout raged.","And yes, it had been over an hour now as Existence continued to be altered and changed from the outside.","This single hour allowed him to familiarize himself with the newly forged Core Phonemes that only he owned and had access to.","Which in itself was a crazy reality to ascertain.","He, that weak Rank F Hunter from a blue planet, had nine exclusive Core Phonemes of the language of Existence. There had only been eighteen Core Phonemes initially since Observable Existence differentiated, and he had just added nine more that belonged solely to him.","He had truly come far since throwing fireballs in the back of a dilapidated apartment!","But when he closed his eyes and felt the Phonemes of The First Tongue, it felt like he was ever closer and integrated into The First Tongue itself. As if he held a secret that nobody else knew or had access to. As if he had become part of the very language that structured reality.","Insofar, he had begun with the Phoneme of Quintessence and Infinity to be infused into the Principles of Undifferentiated Mana, Cheating Architect, Perpetual Harvest, and the other Genesis Philologies.","What was unique was watching these Philologies be altered in real time.","After Quintessence and Infinity flowed into them, which only occurred after numerous trials and errors in Creative Mode, he watched as a radiant and different type of authority began to pulse and permeate in what he had known the Philologies to be.","Because simply, a Genesis Principle was something that was comprised of the Core Phonemes of The First Tongue, of which there were eighteen. So when someone else came and began altering by adding new Phonemes into these Philologies, they would not remain the same.","A Genesis Principle was a Genesis Principle.","But what Noah was doing right now was altering and elevating a Genesis Principle by adding brand new letters that had never existed before.","And as he began to run simulations with Ruination under Creative Mode on fusing the remaining Phonemes he just created into his Philologies, the immensity and weight that he was giving off only became more and more intense.","To the extent that the gains of utilizing the pressure and effort of withstanding THE Fallout turned into boundless harvest by the Philology of Perpetual Harvest. The advancements made by the prisoners in his Infinite Desmoterion contributed their share. The Infinite Potential he had continued to allow to flow into his Foundation and Civilization compounded everything further.","It allowed for a tremendous advancement within just the span of an hour.","|ADVANCEMENT REPORT - 1 HOUR POST-FALLOUT|","| Current Weight and Immensity: 18/100th of the weight and immensity of THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities like THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos (approximately)|","|THE INFINITE DESMOTERION STATUS:|","|Time Dilation Active: 1 hour external = 5 years internal|","|Prisoner Cultivation: All prisoners have undergone forced advancement cycles|","|Harvest Generated: An Unquantifiable Everythings of Infinite Potential extracted and redirected to Foundation|","|Special Note: Several prisoners have achieved breakthroughs that generated bonus harvest multipliers|","|CORE PHONEME INTEGRATION PROGRESS:|","|Phoneme of Quintessence:|","|- Integrated into: Philology of Undifferentiated Mana (100%), Philology of Perpetual Harvest (100%)...|","|- Effect: All integrated Philologies now carry the essence of \"purest truth\" making them more resistant to external interference|","|Phoneme of Infinity:|","|- Integrated into: Philology of Undifferentiated Mana (100%), Philology of The Cheating Architect (87%)...|","|- Effect: Integrated Philologies now possess boundless scaling potential with no theoretical upper limit|","|Phoneme of Tyranny:|","|- Integrated into: Philology of The Cheating Architect (43%)...|","|- Effect: Partial integration grants increased authority over reality manipulation within Creative Mode|","|Phoneme of Fortune:|","|- Integration Status: Queued for Philology of Perpetual Harvest|","|- Estimated Completion: 2.3 hours|","|Phoneme of Advantage:|","|- Integration Status: Queued for Philology of The Cheating Architect...|","|- Estimated Completion: 3.1 hours|","|Phoneme of Narrative:|","|- Integration Status: Queued for new Philology formation...|","|- Note: This Phoneme may require its own dedicated Philology rather than integration into existing ones|","|Phoneme of Harvest:|","|- Integration Status: Queued for Philology of Perpetual Harvest...|","|- Estimated Completion: 1.7 hours|","|Phoneme of Hunger:|","|- Integration Status: Queued for Civilization integration...|","|- Note: This Phoneme resonates strongly with THE Way of Mana and Hunger|","|Phoneme of Potential:|","|- Integration Status: Queued for Foundation integration...|","|- Note: This Phoneme may enhance the capacity for future growth exponentially|","|OVERALL INTEGRATION: 24% complete|","Noah looked at the breakdown so far as he had come far.","But even this was just the start.","He knew he had to be grander than he was seconds ago, and he had to become stronger at a faster rate than ever before.","Because he could feel that Existence was about to fuck with him more than it ever had before.","The cracks on his skin pulsed with residual Fallout energy, a constant reminder of the curse that had been branded upon him. The colorless tendrils of Quintessence flowing through those cracks offered some comfort, but they did not erase the limitation that THE Existential Ceiling represented.","He could never reach THE Absolute Depth through normal means.","But who said anything about normal means?","He had THE Existential Paradox Loop . He had nine Core Phonemes that did not exist in THE Fallout’s parameters. He had Infinite Mana that rejected limitation by its very nature.","If Existence wanted to fuck with him, he would fuck with Existence right back!"]},{"number":4694,"title":"Chapter 4694: Chapter 4693: The Emerged III","paragraphs":["As everything proceeded forward like a churning train that had no stop, Noah continued to allow the help of Ruination in processing and keeping everything in order.","He had so many capabilities to keep track of that he now actually wanted to combine many things and keep a select few singular tracks that he followed.","Being a jack of all trades was nice, but he remembered countless abilities since his time as a hunter to now, and many of them had been forgotten or left behind along the way.","One of the more unique things that were memorable to him apart from the glorious fireballs was Sever. The capability to shoot tendrils of lightning or condensed lines of authority that linked from enemy to enemy and exploded them like popcorn. It had been devastating in its time, a technique that could clear battlefields in moments.","Playing with a swirling undead storm of bones and death, which he left behind to the Arch Lich, had also been something that defined an era of his growth.","The thought of the Lich reminded him as he looked over to Ra’Zan, and he saw this unique existence under him already flowing with multiple Phonemes of The First Tongue. THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty would be wrapping around him within the next few minutes, transforming the ancient undead into something that transcended his previous limitations.","But yes, he had many capabilities, and he even had 159 of THE Stanchions of Infinity. Yet he mainly utilized a select few that took center stage in his battles and cultivation.","He had the ideal and goal to streamline and combine many things into his emerging Foundation, into pillars that would actively be helping him survive the environment of THE Fallout. Into increasing his weight and immensity, and into elevating his Way. It was also why Mana Supremacy, Arcana Infinitum, and Primus Ascension were all currently being tested and fully integrated into the Philology of Undifferentiated Mana, which was being made even grander with the inclusion of the nine Core Phonemes that he just forged.","This path ahead was gradually becoming clear for his own power and Foundation.","The reduction of redundancies and the elevation of his Weavings of Existence at a rate that other entities would be maddened by!","\"We all fall down... we all fall down...\" he hummed to himself as in front of him was a radiant blue-gold grill that was the extension of the very concept of cooking elevated into a ridiculous stage. On the grill were a pair of T-bone steaks that were formed from pure concentrated THE Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger.","He cooked the very authority of his Civilization into forms of food and drinks as the next person in line caused him to frown.","The Emperor Penguin gave him an innocent look while holding on to an empty golden plate, his flippers clutching it with an eagerness that bordered on desperation.","Noah sighed as the steaks he was cooking floated from the grill and onto the plate of The Emperor Penguin, who smiled happily with pride.","There was a line of people behind him who were waiting for more food as the festival continued.","Even Little Bobby was there holding a plate with a dark gaze, his small form somehow radiating an intensity that belied his age. Behind him, Henry was laughing and talking with a shy Liora, whose cheeks flushed with warmth.","As Noah looked at the masses of entities all around him celebrating THE Festival of The End, even though their very Weavings of Existence now held signs of fracture that told them they would never exceed a certain Depth, he smiled.","This was his family that he was protecting.","And at this time...","\" Oh?\"","He raised his head as he felt a change. As he felt Existence settling outside.","|The complex changes of the Second Phase of THE Fallout have been measured to be rapidly reducing.|","|Observable Existence is returning to a new basal state. Obtaining as much information as possible from surrounding weavings of Existence. |","|Note: This information would have been impossible to extract through normal means.|","|The First Tongue itself faced a unique influence and change due to THE Fallout.|","|Standard methods of perception and communication remain non-functional.|","|However: The emergence of your 9 Core Phonemes, integrated into The First Tongue itself, still allows a form of information extraction across some of the rapidly changed Observable Existence.|","|Your additions to The First Tongue serve as unaffected conduits through the corrupted language of Existence.|","|Where others see only static and chaos, you perceive patterns and data.|","|Estimated time until Second Phase completion: 7 minutes|","|Estimated time until new basal state stabilization: 23 minutes|","...!","THE Fallout was ending.","The prompts that flashed before Noah’s eyes also revealed something glorious.","Information extraction across some of the Observable Existence.","In a reality where, at this moment, communication was impossible. Teleportation was impossible among many other things. Very little would be known by the vastness of Observable Existence, as every entity was isolated in their own pocket of corrupted reality.","And yet, because of what he did by forging nine brand new letters of the language of Existence, Noah would still be able to get estimations of information from across Existence.","He knew that this was one of the stupendous capabilities that would bloom from his actions of forming new letters for The First Tongue. The other effects would still show up as time passed, revealing themselves in ways he could not yet predict.","But for now, it was time to go meet the changed Existence outside and see just what the actions of THE Living Paradox had done to Observable Existence.","He looked at the grill before him, then at the line of people still waiting for food.","\"Ruination,\" he said silently.","|Yes, Master?|","\"Take over the cooking.\"","|Understood. I will ensure THE Festival of The End continues in your absence.|","Noah stepped away from the grill as one of his bodies that Ruination could control seamlessly took his place, continuing to cook THE Civilizational Authority into delicious forms without missing a beat.","He walked through the festival, past his people who were laughing and eating and drinking in defiance of the apocalypse that had just reshaped all of reality.","He slowly made his way to the edge of THE Infiniverse, to where THE Infinite Loom and THE Faraday Cage had protected everything within from the worst of THE Fallout.","And he looked outward!","Toward the changed Existence that awaited.","Toward whatever horrors and wonders THE Living Paradox’s machinations had wrought!"]},{"number":4695,"title":"Chapter 4695: Chapter 4694: The Emerged IV","paragraphs":["THE Faraday Cage and THE Infinite Loom were designs of glorious innovation and wonder as they currently shone with a reinforced glow of power after weathering through THE Fallout itself.","Noah appeared directly before the vibrant blue-gold barriers of THE Infinite Loom as he looked outside to the changed Weavings of Existence, and they looked absolutely marvelous in the most terrifying way possible.","The immediate landscape outside of THE Infiniverse was filled by regions of space that shone with a stellar gray hue, expressing a form of destruction and brilliance at the same time. There seemed to be solid gray clouds pulsing with ash and flames, roiling like thunderheads made of concentrated devastation. If one looked up or down, or in any other direction really, they would notice a faint trace of what looked like ash raining in every direction.","When this ash touched onto surfaces, Existence in that area would sizzle slightly as smoke would bloom. It was as if the very atmosphere had become corrosive, hostile to anything that dared to exist within it.","And with his own eyes, Noah could only see barely more than a mile in every direction. Beyond that, the gray ash and clouds formed an impenetrable curtain that swallowed all perception.","And-","| KAAA!|","As he was thinking and observing all of this, out of absolutely nowhere, a massive form barreled out from the ash-filled Weavings of Existence outside. Since what he could observe was only a mile in every direction, with the gray ash and clouds seemingly covering everything after that, he only managed to see the creature when it was already upon him.","It came to smash onto the walls of THE Infinite Loom.","BOOM!","The barrier buzzed.","The impact was heavy as the entity that had done it actually held Depth.","Depth!","SCREE!","\"What the fuck...\"","He had not even gotten out yet.","He was just observing and waiting for the complete end of THE Fallout , and something was already being chucked toward his direction?","His gaze was stern as he observed the monstrous thing that had appeared outside of his home. The thing was currently banging its head on THE Infinite Loom , and shockingly, even though it could not see him, its maddened eyes were locked onto him as if it came here specifically for him.","The creature was horrifying in a way that transcended normal terror.","Its general form resembled that of a Gulper Eel, with an impossibly large mouth that seemed to comprise most of its body. The jaw could unhinge to reveal rows upon rows of teeth that spiraled inward like a meat grinder made of bone. Its body was elongated and serpentine, covered in skin that looked like it had been turned inside out and then burned.","But what truly made it nightmarish were the markers of the cursed that spread across its flesh paired with all this. Faint cracks glowed with residual Fallout energy, covering every inch of its monstrous form. The cracks pulsed with a sickly gray-multicolored light, and from some of the larger fissures, wisps of primordial energy leaked out like steam from a broken pipe.","Its eyes were the worst. They held no sanity, no thought beyond desperate hunger. They were the eyes of something that had been broken by THE Fallout and reformed into a creature of pure need.","As Noah observed it, The First Tongue buzzed as waves of information were extracted.","|CREATURE ANALYSIS|","|Designation: Emerged Devourer|","|Classification: The Awakened |","| Depth: THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Origin: Malformed Ginnu Lifeform from THE Belly of Existence|","|Status: Unable to resist the effects of THE Fallout. Underwent forced mutation.|","|Potential Group Ascertained: THE EMERGED|","|Origin: Entities from THE Belly of Existence who were affected by The Fallout when THE Living Paradox’s attack tore open THE Creature’s domain.|","|Mutation Type: Primordial Regression|","|The Emerged are entities who were exposed to The Fallout while simultaneously being bathed in the primordial energies of THE Belly of Existence. This dual exposure caused them to regress toward more fundamental, more ancient forms of existence.|","|Characteristics:|","|- Bodies shifting toward primordial, proto-existence states|","|- Can access abilities from the era before differentiation|","|- Perceive reality in ways that predate current Existence’s structure|","|- Struggle to communicate with post-differentiation entities|","|- Slowly losing connection to modern Existence’s rules|","|Hierarchy:|","|- The Awakened: Recently emerged, still adapting to their new nature (Current specimen)|","|Curse Variation:|","|The Emerged bear a modified version of THE Existential Ceiling. While they cannot reach Absolute Depth through normal means, their primordial regression grants them access to power structures that predate the Depth system entirely.|","|Unique Boon - Primordial Memory:|","|- Can access inherited memories from before differentiation|","|- Possess knowledge of Existence’s fundamental structure|","|- Can perceive the \"cracks\" in reality that The Fallout created|","|MUTATION DETAILS: PRIMORDIAL HUNGER|","|This specific specimen underwent a horrific mutation that amplified its base instincts to catastrophic levels.|","|Effect: The creature’s existence feels perpetually thirsty, craving rich Weavings of Existence to sustain itself.|","|Behavior: Any entity that comes within a few miles will be sensed if they possess rich Weavings of Existence. The creature will pursue them with undeniable, maddened need.|","|Note: THE Infiniverse and your personal Weavings register as extraordinarily rich sources. This creature likely sensed you from maximum perception range and immediately charged.|","| Warning: Where there is one Emerged, there are likely many more. THE Belly of Existence contained countless entities.|","...!","Noah observed the details of this creature that roared toward him and THE Infiniverse with a maddened glare.","He could not help but think of Lumivara, Ul’Moreth, and The Fisherman.","They had been in THE Belly of Existence when THE Fallout struck. They had been exposed to those same primordial energies while the attack tore through THE Creature’s domain.","Had they undergone similar mutations?","Or had they been strong enough, aware enough, to resist the regression and maintain their sanity?","He did not know.","And in this new Existence where communication was impossible and perception was limited to mere miles, he had no way of finding out.","BOOM!","THE Emerged Devourer slammed against THE Infinite Loom again, its massive maw trying to bite through barriers that had withstood THE Fallout itself. Cracks of cursed energy flared across its body with each impact, and its screech of frustration echoed through the gray landscape.","Noah watched it with cold, calculating eyes.","This was his first glimpse of what awaited outside.","An Intermediate Depth creature, driven mad by hunger, attacking his home within minutes of THE Fallout’s conclusion.","And according to the information extracted, where there was one, there were likely many more.","THE Belly of Existence had contained many entities.","All of them now exposed to THE Fallout.","All of them potentially transformed into these Emerged.","All of them fucking hungry."]},{"number":4696,"title":"Chapter 4696: Chapter 4695: Moirai I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at THE Emerged Devourer with a sense of pity.","A Malformed Ginnu Lifeform who was imprisoned this whole time, and at the time of freedom, they were too weak to fight against THE Fallout.","SCREE!","THE Emerged Devourer still continued to bash its entire body on the barrier, its Depth heavy and profound as it was rapidly eating away at the nearby Logos on THE Infinite Loom. Each impact sent ripples of destruction through the carefully constructed defenses, the creature’s maddened hunger dissolving the meanings that held the barrier together.","It was causing an unnecessary expenditure of his home as Noah began to float toward it.","Pity was pity, but he would not hold back.","He was on a path. He was streamlining his Way and abilities as at this moment, he wanted to feel his Depth freely.","Eighteenth of the Immensity of THE Creature at THE Intermediate Depth? Okay.","What did that translate to? His Way was at Surface Depth as it could Assert Mana or Hunger in unique ways, but if he held Intermediate Depth immensity, then his Assertions would automatically be elevated to Impositions.","He wanted to feel with his body closely as he expressed his immensity. How the Logos within him moved. How the Philologies flowed.","In Ginnungagap, he used The Goad and Logos of Imprisonment to gradually corner THE Surface Depth entities until they could no longer exert any power of their Depth, and while in such a state, he took them into his prison.","But this was when he had not even formed his Depth yet. He had the Depth at this moment, and even though he was at THE Surface Depth in his Way and Civilization, he wanted to see how he would measure up to this Intermediate Depth creature that was mutated from THE Fallout.","And so he took a step forward.","As he did so, his skin glinted with Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue. Every weight and immensity of his existence surrounded his entire body, held together tightly as blue-gold light permeated around him like a glow of brilliance. He looked like a humanoid entity that was set aflame with stellar blue-gold brilliance, each Phoneme burning across his form like stars embedded in flesh!","As if THE Emerged could sense a level of immensity from him, it actually backed away for him to come out of the barrier. Its gaze was that of fervor and mad excitement while looking at him, as if it were looking at a chicken that had come out to be cooked and eaten. Saliva that burned with primordial hunger dripped from its impossible maw.","The moment Noah left the confines of THE Infiniverse to appear in the landscape of THE Fallout...","HUUM!","His entire existence vibrated as he felt waves of resonance cascading all around.","|CRITICAL HARVEST DETECTION|","| For stepping out into the expansive, corrupted, and altered Weavings of Observable Existence, Perpetual Harvest has briefly sensed the boundless Infinite Potential that should have been waiting for you.|","|Sources detected:|","|- All the changes that The First Tongue underwent during THE Fallout|","|- All the advancements that those who followed your Way or backed you within THE Prison of THE Creature underwent|","|- The Shelters of THE Loom making themselves visible within Observable Existence, allowing their Weavings of Existence to run free|","|- All the usage of Mana and The First Tongue across the eons that was carried out to maintain THE Loom and by those within it|","|All of this boundless harvest is barely being sensed at this moment due to the altered Weavings of Observable Existence.|","|Note: If you did not have nine newly forged Phonemes reinforced in The First Tongue, this harvest would never have been collected.|","|The Philology of Perpetual Harvest, backed by your newly forged Phonemes of The First Tongue, promises you that it will ensure every scrap of harvest is accounted for and given to you.|","|Infinite Potential begins to be gathered, however slow and however rigorous, until every ounce that belongs to you is given.|","...!","Noah sensed and heard these prompts as he felt invisible waves of brilliance like an endless sea begin to surge above him and trickle down into his Foundation and Civilization.","He accepted this calmly as he trusted in the Philologies that he was advancing at this moment, that every ounce of what was his would be given!","But he kept his gaze on the Gulper Eel.","At this moment, an ashen color of its Depth erupted around it like heavy strikes of lightning as it looked toward Noah with an immense sense of greed and want. It radiated the immensity of its Depth toward him as if to bring him to submission so he could seamlessly be enjoyed and eaten.","Its mental state and Way seemed entirely far too gone. It could not even be saved. Anything that made it a Malformed Ginnu Lifeform had truly already been stripped away.","What a pity.","The creature’s Way expressed itself as Primordial Consumption , a regressed, bestial version of hunger that predated sophisticated concepts of devouring. It did not merely want to eat Noah. It wanted to unmake him, to return his complex existence to raw, undifferentiated sustenance.","As its weight and immensity surged toward Noah, he erupted with his own Way in response.","Blue-gold tendrils of lightning unfolded from his existence, crackling with the authority of Mana and Hunger intertwined. They clashed with the ashen bolts of the Gulper Eel’s Depth in the space between them.","HUUM!","The collision was cataclysmic.","Reality itself groaned as two immensities met in the corrupted air. The ashen clouds around them were blown back by the shockwave, revealing glimpses of the gray wasteland that stretched endlessly in all directions. Lightning of blue-gold and lightning of primordial ash intertwined and fought for dominance, each tendril seeking to overwhelm the other.","The ground beneath them cracked! The falling ash was vaporized in a sphere around their clash.The very Weavings of Existence trembled as two Depths contested for supremacy!","And shockingly, Noah’s Depth and the Depth of this creature were almost equal.","Both sides were dispersed.","Noah looked at such a scene and nodded.","At THE Surface Depth, he could disperse the Depth of an Intermediate Depth entity.","He looked at the Gulper Eel as it was not deterred. In fact, it looked at him with even more greed as at this moment, its Way began to twist. Noah sensed this creature was about to utilize Imposition that THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities had access to.","The Gulper Eel lit up with a sickly primordial glow as reality around it began to warp. Its maw opened impossibly wide as it sought to impose that the enemy in front of it was already cut up, already prepared, already ready for consumption.","Noah saw this and prepared to counter with his own Imposition when he became astonished.","This was not an Imposition!"]},{"number":4697,"title":"Chapter 4697: Chapter 4696: Moirai II","paragraphs":["The Gulper Eel shockingly did not use an Imposition!","Noah’s eyes flickered as time slowed around him, The Phonemes of The First Tongue burning gloriously within his eyes as he demanded an answer.","|Analysis of enemy technique reveals anomalous expression of authority.|","|The Gulper Eel did not use Imposition.|","|It utilized a more ancient form of this capability that creatures in extremely early Observable Existence before differentiation utilized.|","| Classification: Dogma |","|Meaning: \"That which seems good\" or \" Authoritative decree\"|","| Dogma is the forceful establishment of a truth that did not previously exist. Dogma creates new truth through sheer authority. It is the precursor to Imposition but carries an additional weight of philosophical conviction.|","|Characteristics:|","|- Decrees that reshape local reality according to the speaker’s philosophical framework|","|- Requires not just power but ideological certainty|","|- Creates \"zones of doctrine\" where the Dogma’s truth is absolute law|","|- Can only be broken by a superior Dogma or by exposing logical contradictions within it|","|Philosophical Foundation: Dogma represents the power of conviction to shape reality. In the ancient understanding, a belief held with sufficient certainty and authority becomes indistinguishable from truth within its sphere of influence.|","|ENEMY DOGMA ANALYSIS:|","|Dogma of Inevitable Consumption:|","|\" That which I perceive as prey has already been prepared for my consumption.\"|","|Effect: Reality within the Dogma’s zone will reshape the target’s existence to be in a state suitable for consumption, regardless of their actual condition.|","| Danger Level: Extreme. If this Dogma takes hold, your existence will be forcibly altered to match its decree.|","...!","\" Dogma ...\" Noah voiced out to himself as his expression became stern right after.","His heart was free.","And so, he would set this Malformed Ginnu Lifeform free.","Noah allowed the full immensity of his Depth to surge forth as he spoke his Imposition into existence. Every single Philology and Logos within him flowed into it, the blue-gold brilliance condensing into words that carried the weight of his entire Way.","\" All things are Mana. All Mana is undifferentiated. That which is undifferentiated cannot be prepared or altered by external will, for it has no fixed state to alter. Your Dogma decrees that I am prepared, but I decree that preparation itself is meaningless against that which encompasses all states simultaneously.\"","BOOM!","The Imposition crashed against the Dogma like a tidal wave against a fortress.","The Gulper Eel’s zone of doctrine flickered as logical contradiction was exposed at its core. How could something be prepared for consumption when it existed in all states at once? How could a single decree encompass that which was, by its very nature, undifferentiated?","The Philology of Undifferentiated Mana burned with unprecedented brilliance as it demonstrated, in real-time, the logical impossibility of the Dogma’s premise.","And then the Dogma shattered!","Not merely dispersed, but reversed.","The decree that the prey was prepared for consumption turned back upon its speaker, and the Gulper Eel’s own existence began to warp. Its flesh started to segment. Its form began to separate into portions suitable for consumption, its own Dogma deeming itself to be prey!","SCREE!","The creature’s shriek was one of confusion and agony as its authority was turned against it.","|DOGMA OVERCOME|","|Analysis of victory conditions:|","|Factor One: Your Way of The First Tongue granted inherent resistance to ancient expressions of authority.|","|Factor Two: The Philology of Undifferentiated Mana provided the logical framework to expose the Dogma’s internal contradiction.|","|Factor Three: Your Way, though at Surface Depth, was sufficient to carry an Imposition of equivalent weight to an Intermediate Depth Dogma.|","|Conclusion: Dogma, though a grander form than Imposition, operates on philosophical conviction. When confronted with a truth that logically negates its premise, it cannot maintain coherence regardless of the power behind it.|","...!","Noah saw the shocked expression of the Gulper Eel even as its eyes still carried a light of greed, and he shook his head with pity.","It was time to end this.","He raised his hand, and his voice carried the weight of finality.","\"A clench of my fist becomes a severing light of Mana that chains across the existence of the enemy before me. It will not stop until Way and Cognizance are collapsed. What remains shall be the first offering of loot in this accursed landscape.\"","He clenched his fist.","BOOM !","A heavy blue-gold tendril of light erupted from his closed hand and lanced toward the already fragmenting Gulper Eel. It struck the creature and then chained through its existence, jumping from one portion of its being to another!","Each link of the chain severed something vital.","The first link severed its Way.","The second link severed its Cognizance.","The third link severed its Depth.","The fourth link severed its hold on existence itself.","The creature did not scream. It could not scream. There was nothing left to scream with!","The scene carried solemnity and a sense of sadness as Noah watched the Gulper Eel seperate into motes of primordial light. For the first entity to die in his hands in this new era, it was not any of those responsible for THE Fallout.","It was a Malformed Ginnu Lifeform.","A victim, not a perpetrator.","A being that had been imprisoned, freed, and then broken by forces beyond its control.","Noah looked at the glorious and terrifying scene of his power as at such a time, new prompts bloomed.","|LOOT GENERATION INITIATED|","| All the Weavings and Infinite Potential of THE Emerged Devourer, The Gulper Eel, are being burned by THE Loot Stanchion of Infinity.|","|The Phonemes of Harvest, Fortune, Advantage, and Infinity are being utilized to allow the emergence of something that would contribute to the continued safety of your Existence.|","|Loot generation in progress...|","...!","A blinding light shone.","Massive Phonemes bloomed and compressed around what remained of the Gulper Eel. They spun and condensed, burning away impurities and extracting essence. The process was mesmerizing, watching raw existence be refined into something greater.","After some time, all that remained was a string of golden light and a singularity that shot towards Noah and sunk into his head, straight into THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons.","The string floated still.","A brilliant, glorious string of golden light that shockingly pushed away the ashen glow of the surrounding landscape. It hung in the air before Noah like a thread of pure destiny, pulsing with an authority that predated differentiation itself.","Noah calmly looked at it and beckoned as it flowed toward him.","The string felt warm against his existence, warm and infinitely complex. It carried the weight of possibilities, of paths taken and not taken, of futures that might be and futures that never would be. Holding it was like holding the concept of choice itself made tangible.","| Item: Fragment of THE Moirai Threads|","|Classification: Primordial Artifact (Pre-Differentiation)|","|Origin: Strands from before destiny differentiated. The Moirai Threads were the proto-concept of fate before it split into past, present, and future.|","|Properties:|","|- Can interact with temporal and causal phenomena|","|- Resonates with paradox-based abilities|","|- Contains inherited knowledge of destiny’s fundamental structure|","|SPECIAL COMPATIBILITY DETECTED|","| This Fragment can interact with and enhance THE Existential Paradox Loop.|","|Integration Effect: Partial Simulation of THE Existential Paradox Loop|","|Capability Granted: Without expending an Anchor Point reset, you can now obtain partial information regarding potential futures.|","|Limitation: Information is fragmentary and probabilistic, not absolute. Major events may be sensed, but main details will be obscured.|","...!","A terrifying loot formed, all for the sake of ensuring his existence did not undergo collapse and hardship in these terrifying Weavings of Existence.","Noah looked at the Fragment of THE Moirai Threads as it wound itself around his wrist like a bracelet of pure golden light!"]},{"number":4698,"title":"Chapter 4698: Chapter 4697: Moirai III","paragraphs":["A Fragment of THE Moirai Threads.","A string so vibrant and powerful that he felt like it weighed an entire Depth of Absolute Sovereignty in his hand.","It represented many things as truth be told, even though he did not have any doubt, he was still unfathomably cautious of everything that was to come.","He had a sense of expectation and wonder for the mysteries out there, but he was not looking forward to the struggles and the hardship that he would have to go through to bypass them.","This object was an unfathomable saving grace as it was also born as a product of what his existence deemed would be the most ideal loot for him to have.","If it could truly react with THE Existential Paradox Loop...","\" Utilize the Fragment of THE Moirai Threads.\"","HUUM!","If he had the cheat to peer into the future, to see what would be happening, why not use it right away?","The moment that he uttered such words, the golden thread shot out from his hand and pierced into his chest like a sharp blade. His eyes frowned in pain as the golden thread proceeded to wrap around and constrict his heart with a grip that felt like destiny itself squeezing his existence.","It was not a pleasant feeling at all.","But moments later, a unique cloud of golden brilliance began to surround him, and his eyes became glazed gold as visions that had not yet come to pass began to crystallize before his perception.","|Usage of the Fragment of THE Moirai Threads initiated.|","|A Partial Simulation of THE Existential Paradox Loop is beginning.|","|Note: This is a Partial Simulation only.|","|Capability: Fragmentary glimpses of potential futures based on current trajectory.|","|Limitation: Information is probabilistic, not absolute. Details may be obscured or inaccurate.|","| Estimation: 9 Fragments may allow for a Full Simulation until potential collapse or death.|","|Current Fragments: 1/9|","|Warning: Viewing potential futures does not guarantee they will occur.|","|Simulation beginning...|","...!","Noah viewed these prompts calmly as moments later, he began to feel waves of information flowing through him. His eyes flickered gold, and scenes of potential futures he had not yet come across began playing before him.","|Timeline Analysis Beginning...|","| Within minutes of the Second Phase of THE Fallout ending, you set off into the Wastes of THE Fallout after having laid to rest a Gulper Eel.|","|You break down its Weavings and memories as part of what it used to be and what it stood for are written in the pages of your Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons.|","|The Phonemes of Advantage and Fortune naturally trigger and focus on retrieving certain memories that pulse with glory and benefit for you.|","|From its memories, you learn of a terrifying corrupted region this entity had run away from while THE Fallout was continuing.|","|A domain that had been locked in Ginnungagap, which was within THE Belly of Existence.|","|After THE Belly was torn open, this domain and many other wonders spilled out and proceeded to face corruption.|","|You grow very interested as the memories leave behind a name...|","| THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.|","|You remember the words of Ul’Moreth about THE Vaults of Ginnungagap and the dangers and wonders they held.|","|After you weigh the risks, you try to backtrack the path of the Gulper Eel to find this corrupted domain.|","| You begin heading out deeper into the Wastes of THE Fallout cautiously, still feeling the faint connection to THE Infiniverse.|","|You affirm you can return to it if need be, the connection with The First Tongue allowing this to be a possibility, especially due to the 9 newly forged Core Phonemes.|","|You wonder if it would be possible to bypass the restrictions of the Wastes of THE Fallout to sense or reach out to Lumivara and Ul’Moreth.|","|As you move carefully through The Wastes while noting the specific path you take, you come across an abomination. Or really, the Abomination was drawn to your pure weavings of Existence.|","|A creature not originating from THE Belly of Existence or THE Loom.|","|Something from a domain existing between the gaps of Existence that was torn open due to THE Fallout.|","| You come across your first Scorched.|","|You draw upon The First Tongue to define and classify this entity:|","|THE SCORCHED|","|Origin: Entities who survived direct exposure to The Fallout’s flames without any protection.|","| Mutation: Existential Combustion|","|The Scorched are entities whose very existence has been permanently set ablaze by The Fallout. They burn continuously with the multicolored flames of existential annihilation, and rather than being consumed, they have learned to fuel themselves with the destruction.|","|Characteristics:|","|- Bodies wreathed in perpetual flames of The Fallout|","|- Can project and weaponize Fallout energy|","|- Immune to further Fallout damage|","|- Feed on destruction and decay|","|- Cannot heal naturally; must consume the existence of others to regenerate|","|- Gradually lose their original personality and memories|","|- Eventually become more flame than entity|","|Hierarchy(Currently encountered):|","|- Cinders: Newly Scorched, still fighting to maintain identity|","|Curse Variation:|","|The Scorched bear the full Existential Ceiling curse but have developed a workaround. By consuming the existence of others, they can temporarily boost their advancement rate. This makes them predatory but also prevents them from ever achieving stable, lasting power.|","...!","The information Noah was reading in the form of prompts was grand, but the images he saw were even grander!","His eyes blazed gold as even though this was only a possibility, he saw it.","THE Scorched entity appeared in his mind’s eye with terrifying clarity.","It was a serpentine creature of impossible grace and horrifying beauty, its body long and sinuous like some ancient leviathan adapted for land. Fins that should have belonged to an aquatic being fanned out along its spine and tail, but instead of membrane and scale, they were composed entirely of crystallized Fallout flames that shifted through colors.","Its fur, or what might have once been fur, had become living fire that flowed across its form like water made of destruction. Multicolored flames of violet and crimson and gold and colors that had no name rippled across its serpentine body with each movement, leaving trails of scorched reality in its wake.","The creature’s face was elongated and almost regal, with eyes that burned like twin suns trapped in sockets of ash. Where its mouth opened, one could see that even its teeth were flames given solid form, each fang a concentrated point of existential annihilation.","Most disturbing were the cracks across its existence, the markers of the cursed that glowed not with the usual residual Fallout energy but with active, hungry fire. The cracks were not healing. They were spreading. And from each crack, more flames poured forth.","It moved with a dancer’s grace despite its size, each step leaving behind footprints of burning reality that took moments to repair themselves. Bubbles of superheated existence rose from its form like foam from turbulent waters, each one a tiny pocket of destruction waiting to pop!","Oh!","Even though he was only viewing scenes of it in his mind, Noah could see the ferocity of THE Scorched as its Depth burned with heavy Intermediate immensity.","This was not a creature that could be reasoned with.","This was not a creature that remembered what it once was!","This was flame given purpose, and that purpose was consumption!","The golden haze around Noah’s vision flickered as the Partial Simulation continued to feed him glimpses of what might come. He saw himself facing this creature in the gray Wastes, saw the clash of blue-gold authority against multicolored annihilation, saw the dance of death that would unfold between them.","And he saw that this was merely the first of many such encounters!"]},{"number":4699,"title":"Chapter 4699: Chapter 4698: Moirai IV","paragraphs":["As he viewed the scenes of THE Scorched in the glimmers of golden light of The Fragment of THE Moirai Threads, the Partial Simulation continued.","| Your battle against THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders was a glorious one.|","|This creature uniquely utilized Dogma and not Imposition, its ancient expressions of authority fueled by the very flames that consumed its existence.|","|Partial scenes of the battle have been observed:|","|The Scorched Leviathan declared a Dogma of Purifying Flame, seeking to establish that all things within its presence must burn and be cleansed of impurity.|","|You countered with the Philology of Undifferentiated Mana, arguing that Mana cannot be purified because it already exists in its most fundamental state.|","|The clash of Dogma against your philosophical framework created cascades of destruction across the Wastes.|","|Result: Victory.|","|Your Weavings and Phonemes move once more to form the best possible loot.|","|2 Fragments of THE Moirai Threads form from THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders.|","|Current Fragment Count: 2/9|","|You begin sifting through its memories.|","|Note: Only partial memories are available due to this Partial Simulation.|","|Discovery: The direction you are heading toward is actually one THE Scorched was veering away from.|","|The creature fled from something it deemed too dangerous even for its flame-wreathed existence.|","|You do not hesitate as you continue in the same direction, seeking the corrupted domain from the memories of the Gulper Eel.|","...!","|You traverse regions where the ashen clouds condense into liquid devastation that rains upward from the ground.|","|Your Logos of Protection are tested repeatedly as you navigate zones where time inverts without warning.|","|You encounter pockets of frozen time where lesser False THE creatures are trapped mid-motion, their expressions forever locked in terror.|","|You bypass regions where sound becomes visible and silence becomes lethal, your Phonemes of The First Tongue guiding you through.|","|You discover areas where the very concept of distance has been corrupted, with single steps covering miles or miles covering inches unpredictably.|","|You note paths and landmarks, committing them to memory for your eventual passage.|","|Time passes. Struggles compound. Your existence is tested again and again.|","|But you persevere.|","...!","|After some time and annoyances, you feel something immense far ahead.|","|You come across a massive crimson-gold cloudy barrier that extends for countless miles, shrouded by the ashen clouds and flames of THE Fallout.|","|Everything within your existence screams danger at observing this place.|","|Your instincts, honed through countless battles and near-death experiences, tell you to turn back.|","|But defiance is in your nature.|","|You take a step forward and go in.|","...!","The golden light around Noah flickered gloriously as his eyes pulsed with a gold light while he saw the scenes of the domain he was entering clearly.","It felt grand and ancient.","|It was not hard to enter the domain at all.|","|Your existence was even uncontrollably pulled into it once you crossed the threshold.|","|As you passed through the crimson-gold barrier, your existence was pulled on all sides.|","|Its integrity was almost destroyed by forces that seemed to want to reshape you into something compatible with this ancient place.|","|But you persevered.|","|Your existence burned with glorious defiance.|","|You demanded information.|","|Your Phonemes expressed their power gloriously, the nine newly forged letters of The First Tongue reaching out to extract meaning from the incomprehensible.|","|Information begins to flow...|","|DOMAIN IDENTIFIED: THE CORRUPTED VAULT OF GINNUNGAGAP|","|This Vault predates The First Tongue’s differentiation.|","|It originates from an era when Existence was still learning to define itself.|","|It is a remnant of Ginnungagap that was torn open by THE Fallout and corrupted by the collision of primordial energies with the catastrophic changes to Observable Existence.|","|The Vault operates on principles that predate the modern Depth system.|","|Ancient expressions of authority hold sway here.|","|Current Location: The Second Circle|","|Designation: The Stoa of Dogmata|","| You are arriving in the Second Circle of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.|","|Warning: You have bypassed the First Circle entirely through unknown means.|","...!","Noah’s eyes flickered as he saw a grand and unfathomable scene.","The Stoa of Dogmata stretched before him in impossible grandeur.","An endless colonnade of pillars rose toward a ceiling that did not exist, each one carved from crystallized authority that predated differentiation itself. The pillars were inscribed with Dogmata from the ancient era, each inscription glowing with the conviction of beings who had believed so absolutely in their truths that reality itself had bent to accommodate them.","Some pillars burned with cold fire. Others wept tears of solidified time. Still others hummed with frequencies that made his very existence vibrate in uncomfortable waves.","The space between pillars was filled with zones of doctrine, visible as faintly shimmering barriers that separated one philosophical framework from another. He could see where one zone ended and another began, the boundaries marked by subtle shifts in the color of light, the texture of space, the very feel of reality.","And he could only see the immediate mile or two around him.","Further in, multicolored clouds covered everything, obscuring the depths of the Stoa in mystery. He sensed immense dangers lurking within those clouds!","But he also sensed opportunities!","Treasures waiting to be claimed by those bold enough to navigate.","|As you gaze at this region of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap you arrived in, you do not realize that meters to your right was a humanoid figure of a woman watching you with an intrigued smile.|","|You happen to see her only when your gaze directly lands on her, your perception being unable to even perceive her through any other means.|","|She looks toward you for a few seconds longer before she seemingly loses interest and goes back to staring at the endless expanse ahead.|","|You feel absolutely nothing from this woman.|","|No Depth. No Way. No Weavings of Existence. Nothing.|","|As if she does not exist at all.|","|As if she is a hole in reality shaped like a person.|","|You are cautious, seeking answers through The First Tongue.|","|An imperceptible Weaving of power unfolds from you, reaching toward her to extract information.|","|The entity shockingly senses what you tried to do.|","|She is surprised.|","|Then she waves her hand.|","|A shocking force smacks into you and nearly crushes your existence entirely.|","|80% of your protective Logos and Philologies are decimated in an instant.|","|You are thrown backward, your existence screaming in agony as you struggle to maintain coherence.|","|The woman speaks for the first time in a warning.|","|Her voice is unfathomably grand and serene as she says in The First Tongue:|","||Do not do that again.||","|Barely grasping what remains of your existence, you see a prompt that tells you the only piece of information you managed to obtain from the entity.|","|A single distinction extracted at the cost of nearly everything:|","| Designation: Eon.|","...!","BOOM!","|Fragment strain has exceeded sustainable parameters.|","|Information extraction has reached critical threshold.|","|The glimpses of potential future are fragmenting.|","|Partial Simulation ending.|","|Returning to present moment.|","...!","The golden light around Noah shattered like glass as he was forcibly ejected from the vision.","He gasped, his existence trembling from the phantom pain of injuries he had not yet sustained. His heart pounded against the golden thread still wrapped around it, and for a moment, he could still feel the echo of that woman’s casual dismissal, the way she had destroyed 80% of his defenses with a wave of her hand!","Eon .","That single word burned in his mind with terrifying weight.","Noah stood in the gray Wastes outside THE Infiniverse, the golden thread around his heart slowly releasing its grip as the Fragment of THE Moirai Threads faded into dormancy!"]},{"number":4700,"title":"Chapter 4700: Chapter 4699: Eon! I","paragraphs":["Eon .","This was the only distinction he got from a being who was powerful enough to actually sense when The First Tongue was being utilized and accessed by him to find out information. That level of power alone was ridiculous, and when paired with the name, even if Noah had a single working brain cell, he immediately and directly went to the distinction of THE Secretive Eon.","\" Fucking hell...\"","And he could not help but curse as he smiled. A Monstrous being right outside the gate!","If his thought process was right and the entity there was actually someone on the same caliber as THE Living Paradox, or THE Creature, or THE Primordial Chaos , this would be the first entity of this stature that Noah had seen who had only gazed at him with slight interest before looking away as if he did not matter.","She only made an action when he made an action. She only responded.","And it made sense that a wave of the hand of such a being could decimate more than eighty percent of his protection and power.","But Noah now came to a crossroads where he had to ask himself what exactly he would do with the information that he had received from the Partial Simulation.","He knew that the information regarding THE Corrupted Vault was indispensable, with that domain itself being something extremely unique. His own Weavings of Advantage and Fortune were pointing to this place as something that could greatly elevate his power and immensity.","But it was a risk.","The action of meeting one of the terrifying entities in the same caliber as THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, and THE Living Paradox was also a tremendous risk.","And as he thought about this, he also thought about The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature where one of his bodies remained. He had cautiously been waiting within the Shore as he discussed things with Anaximander, THE First Hunger, and THE Living Origin , who were taking stock of all those within the Shore and how every single entity was affected by the curse of THE Existential Ceiling, and how things were affected overall.","This whole time, Noah had been waiting to see if the owner of that Shore would come back to his abode.","It would allow for many things to be illuminated and for many secrets to be revealed, but there was no sign of THE Creature.","Was he and THE Living Paradox out there right now in these boundless, expansive, changed Weavings of Observable Existence already fighting for supremacy?","There were too many unknowns, and at this moment when it came time for him to make a decision on exactly what he would be doing, the decision was actually already made to begin with.","The hardest and riskiest things almost always granted the most tremendous benefits.","In Existence, one did not get anywhere unless they struggled, unless they put in the hard work. He stretched his body and looked down to the expanse of THE Fallout as he was ready to put in some work.","He finished assessing the risks of still entering the Vault and potentially meeting the entity that was likely THE Secretive Eon . When he asked his intuition and even danced with the possibility with his newly forged Phonemes, apart from the sense of immense danger, he did not sense the allure of collapse from this particular event.","And hey, if anything did happen and his intuition was wrong, well, he had an Anchor Point for this.","The Wastes of THE Fallout were filled with unfathomable dangers, and he had all the tools to go through it. So...","\" Let’s go. THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders is up first.\"","HUUM!","He felt his existence pulse with waves of immensity as he took a step and began delving into the Wastes as if he knew and understood exactly where he had to go.","And in a sense, he did.","So far he had come across two groups of beings in this landscape. The Emerged and The Scorched. They were dangerous, yes, but to him at this moment, they represented the source of the resource that was in the Fragments of THE Moirai Threads.","As he proceeded on in the future, he would have to see which ones would be fitting to enter his Infinite Desmoterion or be turned into loot.","With steady steps, he rapidly began to cross the dangerous regions of the Wastes that he knew from the memories of the Partial Simulation.","And even though he could do it extremely fast since he knew the rough location that THE Scorched would be at, he wanted the conditions to be extremely similar to how the Partial Simulation played out.","So he waded across the Wastes of THE Fallout.","Until eventually, he was actually the one to come across THE Scorched, even before it sensed and went toward him.","THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders floated in the ashen expanse like a serpentine titan of annihilation. Its elongated body rippled with living flames that shifted through impossible colors, fins of crystallized Fallout energy fanning out along its spine like the sails of a burning ship. Its regal face turned toward him with eyes like twin dying suns, and its Way emanated outward in waves of Purifying Consumption, a philosophy that demanded all things burn and be made clean through destruction.","It blinked at him in surprise before it sensed his immensity that caused it and The Emerged to go crazy with need.","But before this creature at THE Intermediate Depth made any moves, Noah was the one that made the first move as he continued to test the immensity and Depth of his power.","His entire body vibrated with all of its weight and immensity as he raised his leg. Every Logos, every Philology, every Phoneme within him condensed into this single action as he spoke his Imposition into existence.","\" My foot is the sharpest blade in Existence. By the time it fully presses down, the enemy before me will have its existence entirely severed and collapsed.\"","...!"]}]);
